::: {.transliteration}
Qadrī tafakkur kun kih hamīn kalimiy-i amthāl-i tu chih qadr ʿaẓīm ast va chigūnih khurshīd-i nūrānī rā dar fikr uftādih-īd kih bi-ḥujubāt-i nafs va havā mastūr dārīd va aʿmālash rā ḍāyiʿ kunīd. Nah va-Allāh, juz amthāl-i tu aḥadī bi-īn kalimāt iltifāt nanamāyad chih kih kull fiʿl-i Ḥaqq rā bi-baṣar-i khud dīdih-and. Yawmī az ayyām farmūdand kih aʿẓam az īn balāyā dar surādiq-i qaḍā mastūr ast va bāyad nāzil shavad chunānchih khwābī dar ʿIrāq dīdih-am va az ān chunīn mustafād mīshavad. Qāla wa-qawluhu al-ḥaqq: Kuntu nāʾiman fī laylatin balmāʾ baʿda ʿafrāʾ idhan raʾaytu bi-an ijtamaʿat fī ḥawlī al-nabiyyūna wa-l-mursalūn wa-hum qad jalasū fī aṭrāfī wa-kulluhum yanūḥūna wa-yabkūna wa-yaṣrukhūna wa-yaḍijjūn wa-innī taḥayyartu fī nafsī fa-saʾaltu ʿanhum idhan ishtadda bukāʾuhum wa-ṣarīkhuhum wa-qālū li-nafsika yā sirr al-aʿẓam wa-yā haykal al-qidam wa-bakaw ʿalā shaʾnin bakaytu bi-bukāʾihim wa-
:::

::: {.translation}
Reflect a little on how grave this very statement by people like you is, and how you have conceived the idea of concealing the radiant Sun behind the veils of self and desire and rendering His deeds fruitless. No, by God, no one but people like you would pay attention to such words, for all have seen the deeds of the True One with their own eyes. One day He said that afflictions greater than these lay concealed in the tabernacle of destiny and must descend, as He had seen a dream in Iraq from which this could be understood. He said—and His word is truth—“I was asleep on a dark night following a bright one, when I saw that the Prophets and Messengers had gathered around Me. They were seated on every side of Me, and all were lamenting, weeping, crying out, and wailing. I was bewildered within Myself and questioned them. Then their weeping and cries intensified, and they said, ‘For You, O Most Great Mystery, O Temple of Eternity!’ They wept so much that I wept at their weeping, and
:::

### 620

::: {.original lang="ar"}
اذا سمعت بكاء اهل ملأ الأعلی و فى تلك الحالة خاطبونى و قالوا قد عظم بلائك يا سدرة المنتهى و كبر قضائك يا سرّ الآخرة و الأولی عليك بالصّبر يا آية الكبرى و ظهور نقطة الأولی ثمّ عليك بالصّبر يا شجرة القصوى و ظهور القضآء فى ملكوت الامضآء فسوف ترى بعينك ما لا رءاه احد من المعشر النّبيّين و تشهد ما لا شهده احد من العالمين و تسمع ما لا سمعه اذن الأصفیآء و الأودّاء فصبراً صبراً يا سرّ اللّه المكنون و رمز المخزون و كلمته المحتوم و كتابه المختوم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Idhā samiʿtu bukāʾa ahl-i malaʾ-i aʿlā wa-fī tilka al-ḥālati khāṭabūnī wa-qālū qad ʿaẓuma balāʾuka yā sidrat al-muntahā wa-kabura qaḍāʾuka yā sirr al-ākhirati wa-l-ūlā ʿalayka bi-l-ṣabr yā āyat al-kubrā wa-ẓuhūr nuqṭat al-ūlā thumma ʿalayka bi-l-ṣabr yā shajarat al-quṣwā wa-ẓuhūr al-qaḍāʾ fī malakūt al-imḍāʾ fa-sawfa tarā bi-ʿaynika mā lā raʾāhu aḥadun min al-maʿshar al-nabiyyīn wa-tashhadu mā lā shahidahu aḥadun min al-ʿālamīn wa-tasmaʿu mā lā samiʿahu udhun al-aṣfiyāʾ wa-l-awiddāʾ fa-ṣabran ṣabran yā sirr Allāh al-maknūn wa-ramz al-makhzūn wa-kalimatuhu al-maḥtūm wa-kitābuhu al-makhtūm.
:::

::: {.translation}
when I heard the weeping of the people of the Supreme Concourse, in that state they addressed Me and said, ‘Great indeed is Your affliction, O Tree beyond which there is no passing, and momentous is Your destiny, O Mystery of the next world and this one. Be patient, O Most Great Sign and Manifestation of the Primal Point. Again, be patient, O Uttermost Tree and Manifestation of the Decree in the kingdom of its fulfillment. You will see with Your own eyes what none of the company of Prophets has seen, witness what no one in all the worlds has witnessed, and hear what the ears of the chosen ones and the beloved have never heard. Be patient, be patient, O hidden Mystery of God, His treasured Symbol, His irrevocable Word, and His sealed Book.’
:::

### 621

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و كنت معهم فى تلك الليلة خاطبتهم و خاطبونى الى ان قرب الفجر و ارفعت رأسى عن النّوم و كنت متفكّراً فى نفسى ما بلآء الّذى ما شهده احد فى الابداع و ما حكيته عند احد الى ان حضر تلقآء الوجه احد من علمآء العراق الّذى سمّى بعبد السّلام افندى فلمّا حضر القيناه و اخبرناه و قصصنا له ما ارانى اللّه فى المنام و هو حزن تلقآء الوجه بحزن عظيم كذلك كان الأمر و لكن النّاس هم فى غفلة مبين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-kuntu maʿahum fī tilka al-laylati khāṭabtuhum wa-khāṭabūnī ilā an qaruba al-fajr wa-arfaʿtu raʾsī ʿan al-nawm wa-kuntu mutafakkiran fī nafsī mā balāʾ alladhī mā shahidahu aḥadun fī al-ibdāʿ wa-mā ḥakaytuhu ʿinda aḥadin ilā an ḥaḍara tilqāʾa al-wajh aḥadun min ʿulamāʾ al-ʿIrāq alladhī summiya bi-ʿAbd al-Salām Afandī fa-lammā ḥaḍara alqaynāhu wa-akhbarnāhu wa-qaṣaṣnā lahu mā arānī Allāhu fī al-manām wa-huwa ḥazina tilqāʾa al-wajh bi-ḥuznin ʿaẓīm kadhālika kāna al-amr wa-lākinna al-nāsa hum fī ghaflatin mubīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
“I was with them that night, speaking to them and hearing them speak to Me, until dawn drew near and I raised My head from sleep. I wondered within Myself what this affliction could be that no one in creation had witnessed. I told no one of it until one of the scholars of Iraq, named ʿAbd al-Salām Afandī, came into My presence. When he arrived, We related it to him, informed him, and recounted to him what God had shown Me in the dream. He was deeply saddened in Our presence. Such was the matter, yet the people are in manifest heedlessness.”
:::

### 622

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اين رؤيائى است كه در عراق مشاهده فرموده و ذكر فرموده‌اند و در اين ایّام بعضى از آن تعبير شده چنانچه شنيده‌ايم از اقوال شما آنچه را كه احدى از قبل نشنيده و دیده‌ايم آنچه را نفسى نديده و فرمودند در كلّ احوال صابر و شاكريم و جميع مقصود آن نفوس اينست كه چرا حقّ ظاهر شده فو‌اللّه هذا لم يكن من عندى بل من لدن من ارسلنى بالحقّ و جعلنى رحمة على العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Īn ruʾyāʾī ast kih dar ʿIrāq mushāhidih farmūdih va dhikr farmūdih-and va dar īn ayyām baʿḍī az ān taʿbīr shudih chunānchih shinīdih-īm az aqvāl-i shumā ānchih rā kih aḥadī az qabl nashnīdih va dīdih-īm ānchih rā nafsī nadīdih va farmūdand dar kull-i aḥvāl ṣābir va shākirīm va jamīʿ-i maqṣūd-i ān nufūs īnast kih chirā Ḥaqq ẓāhir shudih. Fa-wa-Allāh hādhā lam yakun min ʿindī bal min ladun man ar salanī bi-l-ḥaqq wa-jaʿalanī raḥmatan ʿalā al-ʿālamīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
This is a dream that He saw in Iraq and recounted, and in these days part of it has been fulfilled: We have heard from your utterances what no one has ever heard before and have seen what no one has seen. He said, “In every circumstance We are patient and thankful.” The entire concern of those souls is why the True One has appeared. By God, this did not originate with Me, but with Him who sent Me with the truth and made Me a mercy to all the worlds.
:::

### 623

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قوله كبر غلّه مذكور نموده‌ بوديد كه زن در سرايه فرستاده عرض نموده‌اند اوّلا آنكه ظلم موجب زياده از اين خواهد بود علاوه مرحبا از شما كه با ادّعاى حقّیّت شما و زيركى زير آب‌كشى ديگر از انبیاء و اولیاء نموديد آيا بجهت فدك حضرت فاطمه دست حسنين را نگرفته و بدر مهاجر و انصار نبرده آفرين بر شما انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qawluhu, kabura ghilluhu: Madhkūr namūdih būdīd kih zan dar sarāyih firistādih ʿarḍ namūdih-and. Avvalan ānkih ẓulm mūjib-i ziyādih az īn khwāhad būd. ʿAlāvih marḥabā az shumā kih bā iddiʿā-yi ḥaqqiyyat-i shumā va zīrakī zīr-āb-kashī-yi dīgar az anbiyā va awliyā namūdīd. Āyā bi-jahat-i Fadak Ḥaḍrat-i Fāṭimih dast-i Ḥasanayn rā nagiriftih va bi-dar-i Muhājir va Anṣār naburdih? Āfarīn bar shumā. Intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
His words—great is his rancor: “You mentioned that they had sent a woman to the government residence to present a petition. First, oppression will lead to more than this. Moreover, bravo to you! With your claim to being in the right and your cleverness, you have made yet another attempt to undermine the Prophets and holy ones. Did not Her Holiness Fāṭimih, for the sake of Fadak, take Ḥasan and Ḥusayn by the hand and bring them to the doors of the Emigrants and the Helpers? Well done!” End of quotation.
:::

### 624

::: {.original lang="ar"}
صه لسانك يا ايّها الكافر باللّه ثمّ صه لسانك يا ايّها المشرك باللّه ثمّ صه لسانك يا ايّها المحارب باللّه
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ṣah lisānaka yā ayyuhā al-kāfir bi-Allāh thumma ṣah lisānaka yā ayyuhā al-mushrik bi-Allāh thumma ṣah lisānaka yā ayyuhā al-muḥārib bi-Allāh.
:::

::: {.translation}
Silence your tongue, you who disbelieve in God! Again, silence your tongue, you who associate partners with God! Again, silence your tongue, you who wage war against God!
:::

### 625

::: {.original lang="ar"}
ولو اكررّ تلك الكلمة من حینئذ الى آخر الّذى لا آخر له لتكون مستحقّاً بها بل لا تذكر عند ما ارتكبت فى جنب اللّه يا ايّها الغافل عن امر اللّه و المستكبر على نفس اللّه
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-law ukarrir tilka al-kalimata min ḥīniʾidhin ilā ākhir alladhī lā ākhira lahu la-takūna mustaḥiqqan bihā bal lā tudhkaru ʿinda mā irtakabta fī janb Allāh yā ayyuhā al-ghāfil ʿan amr Allāh wa-l-mustakbir ʿalā nafs Allāh.
:::

::: {.translation}
Even if I repeated those words from this moment until the end that has no end, you would deserve them. Indeed, they are nothing beside what you have committed against God, you who are heedless of the Cause of God and arrogant toward God Himself.
:::

### 626

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بعد از ورود اين ارض جمال مبارك و حضرت كليم و ميرزا يحيى هر يك در بيت عليحدّه مقرّ داشتند و اين ارض محلّى نيست كه نفسى بنفسى ظلم نمايد و ظلمى را كه مشرك باللّه ارتكاب نمود در وقتى بود كه تفريق كبرى واقع نشده بود و بعد از ظهور ما فى صدره تفصيل و تفريق واقع چنانچه ذكر شد و ابداً ديگر ملاقات نشده و گفتگوى لسانى هم بميان نيامده فاسئل من اهل تلك الأرض لكى تجد الى الصّدق سبيل
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Baʿd az vurūd-i īn arḍ Jamāl-i Mubārak va Ḥaḍrat-i Kalīm va Mīrzā Yaḥyā har yak dar bayt-i ʿalāḥaddih maqarr dāshtand va īn arḍ maḥallī nīst kih nafsī bi-nafsī ẓulm namāyad va ẓulmī rā kih mushrik bi-Allāh irtikāb namūd dar vaqtī būd kih tafrīq-i kubrā vāqiʿ nashudih būd va baʿd az ẓuhūr-i mā fī ṣadrihi tafṣīl va tafrīq vāqiʿ chunānchih dhikr shud va abadan dīgar mulāqāt nashudih va guftugū-yi lisānī ham bi-miyān nayāmadih. Fa-sʾal min ahl tilka al-arḍ li-kay tajida ilā al-ṣidq sabīl.
:::

::: {.translation}
After arriving in this land, the Blessed Beauty, His Holiness Kalīm, and Mīrzā Yaḥyā each resided in a separate house. This land is not a place where one person can oppress another. The wrong committed by the one who associates partners with God took place before the Most Great Separation had occurred. After what lay within his breast was revealed, the division and separation took place, as has been mentioned. Since then there has never been another meeting, nor has any spoken exchange taken place. Ask the people of that land, so that you may find a path to the truth.
:::

### 627

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ديگر آنكه مملكت مال دولت عليّه و در اين ارض جميع مسجون و غريب و بعد از اظهار ما فى سرّه احدى معاشرت ننموده‌جز درويش صدقعلى كه بجهت خدمات او مراوده مينمود و هم‌چنين يك نفر در خدمت جمال اقدس و يكنفر هم خدمت حضرت كليم و باقى اصحاب كلّ در منزلهاى عليحدّه متفرّق ديگر اين ظلم چه بوده و از چه رو وارد شده با آنكه جميع ذرّات ميدانند كه سبب ظلم آن ظالم بود كه ايشان بافتضاح خود راضى شدند و تفريق فرمودند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va dīgar ānkih mamlakat māl-i Dawlat-i ʿAliyyih va dar īn arḍ jamīʿ masjūn va gharīb va baʿd az iẓhār-i mā fī sirrihi aḥadī muʿāsharat nanamūdih juz Darvīsh Ṣidqʿalī kih bi-jahat-i khadamāt-i ū murāvadih mīnamūd va hamchunīn yak nafar dar khidmat-i Jamāl-i Aqdas va yak nafar ham khidmat-i Ḥaḍrat-i Kalīm va bāqī aṣḥāb kull dar manzilhā-yi ʿalāḥaddih mutafarriq. Dīgar īn ẓulm chih būdih va az chih rū vārid shudih bā ānkih jamīʿ-i dharrāt mīdānand kih sabab-i ẓulm ān ẓālim būd kih īshān bi-iftiḍāḥ-i khud rāḍī shudand va tafrīq farmūdand.
:::

::: {.translation}
Moreover, the country belongs to the Ottoman government, and in this land all are prisoners and strangers. After he disclosed what lay hidden within him, no one associated with him except Darvīsh Ṣidqʿalī, who visited him to attend to his needs. Likewise, one person served the Most Holy Beauty and one served His Holiness Kalīm, while all the other companions were dispersed in separate dwellings. What, then, was this oppression, and how did it come about? Every atom knows that the cause of the wrongdoing was that oppressor, who consented to his own disgrace and brought about the separation.
:::

### 628

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و مع‌ذلك تقول ما لا تشعر اصل شجره ظلم را عدل شمرده و شجره فضل و عدل را ظالم دانسته هذا مكر منك و منهم فى امر اللّه آنقدر درايت ندارى كه سخنى استماع نمودى تفكّر كنى در همان ایّام كه زنش بسرايه رفته فو‌اللّه كه در اوّل ماه مخصوص او از آن زخرفيكه در هر شهر مياوردند مع يك بقچه اسباب درويش كه مباشر او بود الآن موجود است برده و چند نفر هم مجدّد در اين ارض وارد شده بودند كلّ مطّلع از جمله جناب ميرزا حيدر على و سلمان و استاد عبد الكريم از اهل صاد و مع‌ذلك مخصوصاً زن بسرايه فرستاده و بهمين لفظ گفته نسبت بجمال ابهى كه ما را آورده و نان و لباس بما نميدهد و افتضاحى در اين ارض برپاشد كه يكى از قنصلهاى اين ارض بسيار تعجّب نموده ‌بشخصى ذكر نمود كه امروز امر عجبی‌ واقع شده و جميع اعجام بشماتت برخواستند كه در اين طايفه عصمت و عفّت نيست
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va maʿa dhālik taqūlu mā lā tashʿur. Aṣl-i shajariy-i ẓulm rā ʿadl shumurdih va shajariy-i faḍl va ʿadl rā ẓālim dānistih. Hādhā makrun minka wa-minhum fī amr Allāh. Ānqadr dirāyat nadārī kih sukhanī istimāʿ namūdī tafakkur kunī dar hamān ayyām kih zanash bi-sarāyih raftih. Fa-wa-Allāh kih dar avval-i māh makhṣūṣ-i ū az ān zukhrufī kih dar har shahr mīāvardand maʿ yak buqchih asbāb Darvīsh kih mubāshir-i ū būd al-ān mawjūd ast burdih va chand nafar ham mujaddad dar īn arḍ vārid shudih būdand kull muṭṭaliʿ az jumlih Jināb-i Mīrzā Ḥaydar ʿAlī va Salmān va Ustād ʿAbd al-Karīm az ahl-i Ṣād va maʿa dhālik makhṣūṣan zan bi-sarāyih firistādih va bi-hamīn lafẓ guftih nisbat bi-Jamāl-i Abhā kih mā rā āvardih va nān va libās bi-mā namīdihad va iftiḍāḥī dar īn arḍ bar-pā shud kih yakī az qunṣulhā-yi īn arḍ bisyār taʿajjub namūdih bi-shakhṣī dhikr namūd kih imrūz amr-i ʿajabī vāqiʿ shudih va jamīʿ-i aʿjām bi-shamātat bar-khāstand kih dar īn ṭāʾifih ʿiṣmat va ʿiffat nīst.
:::

::: {.translation}
Yet you say what you do not understand. You have accounted the very root of the tree of oppression to be justice, and have judged the tree of grace and justice to be oppressive. This is a plot by you and them against the Cause of God. You do not have enough discernment to reflect on something you have heard. In those very days when his wife went to the government residence—by God—at the beginning of the month, Darvīsh, who acted as his agent and is still alive, had taken his allotted portion of the money brought in each city, together with a bundle of belongings. Several people had also newly arrived in this land, and all knew of it, including Jināb-i Mīrzā Ḥaydar ʿAlī, Salmān, and Ustād ʿAbd al-Karīm of the people of Ṣād. Yet he deliberately sent his wife to the government residence, and she said these very words about the All-Glorious Beauty: “He has brought us here and gives us neither bread nor clothing.” Such a scandal arose in this land that one of its consuls was greatly astonished and remarked to someone, “A strange thing has happened today.” All the Persians began to gloat, saying that this community had neither chastity nor decency.
:::

### 629

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و خود نفس غافلت آنقدر دانسته كه اگر يهود بر ايشان وارد شود بقدر مقدور زخرف فانيه از او منع نميشود مع‌ذلك نوشتى آنچه نوشتى و فدك را كثيف نمودى و لكن مطمئنّ باش كه در هر ارضى يك سيّدة النّسائى دارى و از آن رشته مراياى تام واحداً بعد واحد هم بسيار و در هر ارضى موجود دوازده سنه جمال ابهى در عراق تشريف داشتند و احدى از ايشان امرى كه فى‌الجمله مغاير و مخالف باشد نديده از جميع اهل عراق سؤال كن حال از آن رشته مراياى تام واحداً بعد واحد يكى در عراق است بايد از اهل عراق احوال او را پرسيد باو نوشته انّا جعلناك على العالمين نوراً منيراً و هم‌چنين هو النّور فى النّور و انّ مثل نوره كنور نور من نور اللّه و بامّ الفواحش اين آيهء مباركه قرآن را بعينه نوشته يا مريم اقنتى لربّك و اسجدى و اركعى مع الرّاكعين انّ اللّه طهّرك و اصطفاك على نسآء العالمين حال حظّ كن از آن سيّدة النّسآء و از آن مرآت تام كاش آنجا هم ميرفتى و يك سجده مينمودى لعن اللّه الّذين تحرّفوا كلمة اللّه عن موضعها و اعرضوا عن جماله و اتّخذوا لانفسهم عجلاً من دونه فما لهؤلآء لا يكادون يفقهون ذكراً من اللّه العلىّ العظيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va khud nafs-i ghāfilat ānqadr dānistih kih agar Yahūd bar īshān vārid shavad bi-qadr-i maqdūr zukhruf-i fāniyih az ū manʿ namīshavad. Maʿa dhālik nivishtī ānchih nivishtī va Fadak rā kathīf namūdī va lākin muṭmaʾinn bāsh kih dar har arḍī yak Sayyidat al-Nisāʾī dārī va az ān rishtih marāyā-yi tāmm wāḥidan baʿda wāḥid ham bisyār va dar har arḍī mawjūd. Davāzdah sanih Jamāl-i Abhā dar ʿIrāq tashrīf dāshtand va aḥadī az īshān amrī kih fī-l-jumlih mughāyir va mukhālif bāshad nadīdih. Az jamīʿ-i ahl-i ʿIrāq suʾāl kun. Ḥāl az ān rishtih marāyā-yi tāmm wāḥidan baʿda wāḥid yakī dar ʿIrāq ast bāyad az ahl-i ʿIrāq aḥvāl-i ū rā pursīd. Bi-ū nivishtih innā jaʿalnāka ʿalā al-ʿālamīn nūran munīran va hamchunīn huwa al-nūr fī al-nūr wa-inna mathala nūrihi ka-nūri nūrin min nūr Allāh va bi-Umm al-Favāḥish īn āyiy-i mubārakiy-i Qurʾān rā bi-ʿaynihi nivishtih yā Maryam uqnutī li-rabbiki wa-sjudī wa-rkaʿī maʿa al-rākiʿīn inna Allāha ṭahharaki wa-ṣṭafāki ʿalā nisāʾ al-ʿālamīn. Ḥāl ḥaẓẓ kun az ān Sayyidat al-Nisāʾ va az ān mirʾāt-i tāmm. Kāsh ānjā ham mīraftī va yak sajdih mīnamūdī. Laʿana Allāhu alladhīna taḥarrafū kalimat Allāh ʿan mawḍiʿihā wa-aʿraḍū ʿan jamālihi wa-ttakhadhū li-anfusihim ʿijlan min dūnihi fa-mā li-hāʾulāʾ lā yakādūna yafqahūna dhikran min Allāh al-ʿAliyy al-ʿAẓīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
Your own heedless self knows at least this much: if a Jew came to Him, such perishable wealth as was available would not be withheld from him. Yet you wrote what you wrote and sullied Fadak. But rest assured that in every land you have a “Mistress of Women,” and many of that succession of “perfect mirrors, one after another,” are to be found in every land. The All-Glorious Beauty resided in Iraq for twelve years, and no one saw Him do anything even remotely improper or contrary to what is right. Ask all the people of Iraq. Now, one of that succession of “perfect mirrors, one after another,” is in Iraq: you should ask the people of Iraq about him. He wrote to him, “We have made you a shining light to all the worlds,” and likewise, “He is the light within the light, and the likeness of his light is as the light of a light from the light of God.” To the Mother of Obscenities he wrote this blessed verse of the Quran, word for word: “O Mary, be devoutly obedient to your Lord, prostrate yourself, and bow with those who bow. God has purified you and chosen you above the women of all the worlds.” Now take pleasure in that “Mistress of Women” and that “perfect mirror”! If only you had gone there too and performed a prostration! May God curse those who have displaced the word of God from its proper place, turned away from His Beauty, and taken a calf for themselves in His stead. What is wrong with these people that they can scarcely understand a word from God, the Most High, the Almighty?
:::

### 630

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اللّه ناله مينمايم و اين كلمات مينويسم چه كه امر بجائى رسيده كه بايد بچنين اذكار مشغول شد قد ضيّعتم حرمة اللّه و حرمة انفسكم قلب را از كثافات اوهام مشركين طاهر نما و ذكر انبیاء و مرسلين را باذكار انفس مشركين مقترن منما چه كه جميع آن طلعات رحمن جان در سبيل محبوب داده و براى نان بكلّ من على الأرض اعتنا نفرموده‌اند حال انصاف ده تو از اهل قياسى با اين عباد كه چگونه فعلى را بچه فعلى قياس نموده ‌فانصف لتنصف ثمّ ارحم امر الّذى سفك فى سبيله دمآء المقرّبين و عباد اللّه المخلصين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va-Allāh nālih mīnamāyam va īn kalimāt mīnivīsam chih kih amr bi-jāʾī rasīdih kih bāyad bi-chunīn adhkār mashghūl shud. Qad ḍayyaʿtum ḥurmat Allāh wa-ḥurmat anfusikum. Qalb rā az kathāfāt-i awhām-i mushrikīn ṭāhir namā va dhikr-i anbiyā va mursalīn rā bi-adhkār-i anfus-i mushrikīn muqtarin manamā chih kih jamīʿ-i ān ṭalaʿāt-i Raḥmān jān dar sabīl-i Maḥbūb dādih va barā-yi nān bi-kull-i man ʿalā al-arḍ iʿtinā nafarmūdih-and. Ḥāl inṣāf dih tu az ahl-i qiyāsī bā īn ʿibād kih chigūnih fiʿlī rā bi-chih fiʿlī qiyās namūdih. Fa-anṣif li-tunṣaf thumma irḥam amr alladhī sufika fī sabīlihi dimāʾ al-muqarrabīn wa-ʿibād Allāh al-mukhliṣīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, I lament as I write these words, for matters have reached a point where such things must be discussed. You have dishonored God and yourselves. Purify your heart of the filth of the delusions of those who associate partners with God, and do not link mention of the Prophets and Messengers with accounts of those souls who associate partners with Him. All those Countenances of the All-Merciful gave their lives in the path of the Beloved and paid no heed to anyone on earth for the sake of bread. Now judge fairly: you are one who draws comparisons with these servants—what sort of deed have you compared to what other deed? Be fair, that you may be treated fairly, and have mercy on the Cause of Him in whose path the blood of those brought near and of God’s sincere servants has been shed.
:::

### 631

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قوله عظم كذبه عرض ديگر آنكه در باب آمدن حاجى سيّد محمّد در اسلامبول و خودم همه را مطّلعم و حضور داشتم شب اوّل آمده در سفارت جناب مشير الدّوله بودند و سركار حاجى ميرزا صفى و بنده و بس و مشير الدّوله باو گفت كه چرا آمده گفت بجهت استخلاص خود و عرض حال عالى پاشا را هم من ديدم تا آنكه رسولان ايشان آمدند و آغاز بدگوئى نمودند و او هم بجهت اين بدگوئيها بقدر لازم گفت انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qawluhu, ʿaẓuma kadhibuhu: ʿArḍ-i dīgar ānkih dar bāb-i āmadan-i Ḥājī Siyyid Muḥammad dar Islambūl va khudam hamih rā muṭṭaliʿam va ḥuḍūr dāshtam. Shab-i avval āmadih dar sifārat Jināb-i Mushīr al-Dawlih būdand va Sarkār Ḥājī Mīrzā Ṣafī va bandih va bas va Mushīr al-Dawlih bi-ū guft kih chirā āmadih guft bi-jahat-i istikhlāṣ-i khud va ʿarḍ-i ḥāl-i ʿĀlī Pāshā rā ham man dīdam tā ānkih rasūlān-i īshān āmadand va āghāz-i badgūʾī namūdand va ū ham bi-jahat-i īn badgūʾīhā bi-qadr-i lāzim guft. Intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
His words—great is his falsehood: “Another point I submit concerns the arrival of Ḥājī Siyyid Muḥammad in Istanbul. I myself know all about it and was present. On the first night he came to the embassy, Jināb-i Mushīr al-Dawlih was there, together with His Honor Ḥājī Mīrzā Ṣafī and myself, and no one else. Mushīr al-Dawlih asked him why he had come. He said, ‘To secure my release.’ I also saw the petition to ʿĀlī Pāshā. Then their messengers came and began to speak ill of him, and in response to this disparagement he too said as much as was necessary.” End of quotation.
:::

### 632

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قد سوّد اللّه وجه الكاذب اگر مخصوص استخلاص آمده سياهه نفوس را كه احدى مطّلع نبوده كه داده هشت نفر بودند بقلم داده بيست و يك نفريم و شش ماه معطّل شده تا آنكه بهزار تدليس وصل الى مقصوده و مقصود صاحبه باعوا يوسف الأمر بدراهم معدودة فافّ لهم و لوفائهم تاللّه بفعلهم ضيع امر اللّه بين النّاس
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qad sawwada Allāhu wajh al-kādhib. Agar makhṣūṣ-i istikhlāṣ āmadih siyāhiy-i nufūs rā kih aḥadī muṭṭaliʿ nabūdih kih dādih? Hasht nafar būdand bi-qalam dādih bīst va yak nafarīm va shash māh muʿaṭṭal shudih tā ānkih bi-hizār tadlīs waṣala ilā maqṣūdihi wa-maqṣūd ṣāḥibihi. Bāʿū Yūsuf al-amr bi-darāhima maʿdūdah fa-uffin lahum wa-li-wafāʾihim ta-Allāh bi-fiʿlihim ḍuyyiʿa amr Allāh bayna al-nās.
:::

::: {.translation}
God has blackened the face of the liar. If he came solely to secure his release, who supplied the list of people, of which no one had any knowledge? There were eight of them, but he submitted in writing, “We are twenty-one.” He spent six months waiting until, through a thousand deceptions, he attained his own purpose and that of his companion. They sold the Joseph of the Cause for a few dirhams. Shame on them and their faithfulness! By God, through their actions the Cause of God was dishonored among the people.
:::

### 633

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و امرنامه كه از استامبول آمده نوشته‌اند كه بعضى از همرهان ايشان آمده و شكايت نموده‌اند كه ايشان بما نان نميدهند و الان آن امرنامه موجود مع‌ذلك نوشته آنچه را نوشته لعن اللّه الّذين بدّلوا حرمة اللّه بزخارف الدّنيا و اذا خلوا الى الشّياطين يتبرّئون من اللّه و امره ثمّ يكتبون الى الحمقآء من امثالهم انّا رؤسآء الأمر و مرایاء العباد و اثمار التّوحيد و اوراق التّجريد و لكن الّذين جعل اللّه بصرهم حديداً يشهدون و يطلعون بما ارتكبوا فى الحيوة الباطلة و لايشتبه عليهم لانّهم يجدون عن كلّ فعل من افعالهم روايح الكذب و النّفاق و التّزوير و الشّقاق و انّهم من جواهر الخلق بين عباد اللّه و بريّته و عليهم ذكر اللّه و ثنائه فى كلّ حين و بعد حين و حين حين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va amr-nāme ke az Estāmbol āmade neveshte-and ke baʿżī az hamrahān-e īshān āmade va shekāyat namūde-and ke īshān be mā nān nemīdahand va al-ān ān amr-nāme mawjūd maʿa-dhālek neveshte ānche rā neveshte. Laʿana Allāhu alladhīna baddalū ḥurmata Allāhi bi-zakhārifi al-dunyā wa idhā khalaw ilā al-shayāṭīni yatabarraʾūna min Allāhi wa amrihi thumma yaktubūna ilā al-ḥumaqāʾi min amthālihim innā ruʾasāʾu al-amri wa marāyāʾu al-ʿibādi wa athmāru al-tawḥīdi wa awrāqu al-tajrīdi wa lākinna alladhīna jaʿala Allāhu baṣarahum ḥadīdan yashhadūna wa yaṭṭaliʿūna bi-mā irtakabū fī al-ḥayāti al-bāṭilati wa lā yashtabihu ʿalayhim li-annahum yajidūna ʿan kulli fiʿlin min afʿālihim rawāʾiḥa al-kadhibi wa al-nifāqi wa al-tazwīri wa al-shiqāqi wa innahum min jawāhiri al-khalqi bayna ʿibādi Allāhi wa bariyyatihi wa ʿalayhim dhikru Allāhi wa thanāʾuhu fī kulli ḥīnin wa baʿda ḥīnin wa ḥīna ḥīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
In the official order that came from Istanbul, they wrote that some of his companions had come and complained, “He does not give us bread.” That order is still in existence, yet he has written what he has written. May God curse those who have bartered the honor of God for the vanities of this world, and who, when alone with the devils, disavow God and His Cause, then write to fools like themselves, “We are the leaders of the Cause, the mirrors of the servants, the fruits of divine unity, and the leaves of detachment.” But those whose sight God has made keen witness and perceive what they have committed in this vain life. They are not deceived, for in every one of their actions they detect the odors of falsehood, hypocrisy, deceit, and dissension. They are among the gems of creation amid the servants of God and His creatures. May God’s remembrance and praise rest upon them at every moment, time after time, and at all times.
:::

### 634

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اللّه خوب مريدى هستى و خوب بستر فحشا مشغول شده بعد از شهود و لكن بر بصير خبير امر پوشيده نيست و مطّلعيم كه چه افتراها گفته و چگونه كمر قتل بسته حتّى گفته‌اند كه ايشان مخصوص آدم به طهران فرستاده‌اند بجهت امر شنيع لعنة اللّه على المفترين و الكاذبين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va Allāh khūb morīdī hastī va khūb be satr-e faḥshā mashghūl shode baʿd az shohūd va lāken bar baṣīr-e khabīr amr pūshīde nīst va moṭṭaleʿīm ke che efterāhā gofte va chegūne kamar-e qatl baste ḥattā gofte-and ke īshān makhṣūṣ ādam be Ṭehrān ferestāde-and be jahat-e amr-e shanīʿ. Laʿnatu Allāhi ʿalā al-muftarīna wa al-kādhibīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, what a fine disciple you are, and how diligently you have occupied yourself with concealing indecency after witnessing it! But the matter is not hidden from the All-Seeing, the All-Informed. We know what slanders he has uttered and how he has resolved upon murder. They have even said that He sent someone to Tehran expressly to carry out a shameful deed. May God’s curse be upon the slanderers and liars.
:::

### 635

::: {.original lang="fa"}
حال فعل حقّ را مشاهده كن كه بهمان مدينه وارد شدند و ابدا بكسى مراوده نفرمودند و در امر اللّه با نفسى مداهنه نشد و چون آن خبيث ديده كه سفير ايران مكدّر است از ايشان محض خدعه و تلبيس و نفاق با حقّ بآن مقرّ وارد و التجا نموده‌و گفته آنچه گفته اگر او استخلاص ميخواست كسى باو حرف نداشت او از حاجى ميرزا احمد معروف‌تر نبوده بهيچوجه و از سايرين كه رفته‌اند معتبرتر نه بلكه نزد بعضى ذكر نداشته فو‌اللّه كه مخصوص شهريه آمده چنانچه اين ارض هم عرايضى كه او و ميرزا يحيى بباب مشير نوشته‌اند موجود و
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ḥāl feʿl-e Ḥaqq rā moshāhede kon ke be hamān madīne vāred shodand va abadan be kasī morāvede nafarmūdand va dar amr-e Allāh bā nafsī modāhane nashod va chon ān khabīth dīde ke safīr-e Īrān mokaddar ast az īshān maḥż-e khodʿe va talbīs va nefāq bā Ḥaqq be ān maqarr vāred va eltejā namūde va gofte ānche gofte agar ū estekhlāṣ mīkhāst kasī bā ū ḥarf nadāsht ū az Ḥājī Mīrzā Aḥmad maʿrūf-tar nabūde be hīch vajh va az sāyerīn ke rafte-and moʿtabar-tar na balke nazd-e baʿżī dhekr nadāshte fa-wa-Allāh ke makhṣūṣ-e shahrīye āmade chenānche īn arż ham ʿarāyeżī ke ū va Mīrzā Yaḥyā be bāb-e moshīr neveshte-and mawjūd va
:::

::: {.translation}
Now observe the conduct of the True One: He entered that same city and had no dealings with anyone, and no compromise was made with anyone concerning the Cause of God. But when that wicked man saw that the Persian ambassador was displeased with Him, he went to that residence and sought refuge there, solely to deceive, dissemble, and act hypocritically toward the True One, and said what he said. If he had wanted his release, no one would have objected. He was by no means better known than Ḥājī Mīrzā Aḥmad, nor more esteemed than the others who left; indeed, some had never even heard of him. By God, he came expressly for a stipend, as the petitions that he and Mīrzā Yaḥyā wrote to the office of the Mushīr are also here in this land, and
:::

### 636

::: {.original lang="fa"}
از استامبول جميع امور را از اينجا استفسار نمودند كه او ميگويد هفت نفر رفته‌اند و باقى بكسب مشغولند و من و ميرزا يحيى بيست و يكنفريم و شهريّه نداريم سركار والى مخصوص فرستاده و استفسار نموده‌كه باب عالى همچه ذكر نموده‌اند و تو مينويسى كه بجهت استخلاص بوده حال كه بمنتهى مراد خود رسيدند ايكاش كه ديگر باطراف ننويسند كه نان نداريم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Az Estāmbol jamīʿ-e omūr rā az īnjā estefsār namūdand ke ū mīgūyad haft nafar rafte-and va bāqī be kasb mashghūland va man va Mīrzā Yaḥyā bīst-o yek nafarīm va shahrīye nadārīm sarkār-e vālī makhṣūṣ ferestāde va estefsār namūde ke bāb-e ʿālī hamche dhekr namūde-and va to mīnevīsī ke be jahat-e estekhlāṣ būde ḥāl ke be montahā-ye morād-e khod resīdand ey kāsh ke dīgar be aṭrāf nanevīsand ke nān nadārīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
From Istanbul they inquired here about all these matters, saying, “He says that seven people have left and the rest are occupied in earning a living, while Mīrzā Yaḥyā and I number twenty-one and have no stipend.” His Excellency the Governor sent someone expressly to inquire, saying that the Sublime Porte had reported this. Yet you write that it was to secure his release. Now that they have attained the utmost of their desire, if only they would stop writing far and wide that they have no bread!
:::

### 637

::: {.original lang="fa"}
حال انصاف ده آن فعل حقّ و اين فعل اين گروه از كدام رايحه حقّ استشمام ميشود و اللّه چنين رؤسا از براى امثال شما بسيار خوبند و همچه مدان كه سفير ايران غافلند لا و اللّه يومى آيد كه خود ايشان تصديق بر فعل حقّ نمايند و منكر فعل آن نفوس شوند و اگر هم بر تو مشتبه شود بر ايشان مشتبه نخواهد شد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ḥāl enṣāf deh ān feʿl-e Ḥaqq va īn feʿl-e īn gorūh az kodām rāyeḥe-ye Ḥaqq esteshamām mīshavad va Allāh chonīn roʾasā az barā-ye amthāl-e shomā besyār khūband va hamche madān ke safīr-e Īrān ghāfeland lā va Allāh yawmī āyad ke khod-e īshān taṣdīq bar feʿl-e Ḥaqq namāyand va monker-e feʿl-e ān nofūs shavand va agar ham bar to moshtabeh shavad bar īshān moshtabeh nakhwāhad shod.
:::

::: {.translation}
Now judge fairly: that is the conduct of the True One, and this is the conduct of this group. From which can the fragrance of truth be perceived? By God, such leaders are very well suited to people like you. Do not imagine that the Persian ambassador is unaware. No, by God! A day will come when he himself will affirm the conduct of the True One and repudiate the conduct of those people. Even if you are deceived, he will not be.
:::

### 638

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ديگر رسولان را ندانستم كه را گفته اگر مقصود جناب عبد حاضر لدى الوجه بوده و اللّه مخصوص امرى آمده در آن مدينه كه هيچ دخلى باو نداشته چنانچه نزد احدى نرفته جميع شاهد و گواهند كه آن نفس خبيث در اين ارض جميع افعال شنيعه قبيحه را بحقّ نسبت داده و ذر آن ارض هم گفته‌اند آنچه را كه احدى در حقّ احدى نگفته عبد حاضر لدى الوجه حال ميگويد خود نفس كاذبت نيامدى و مذكور ننمودى كه سيّد محمّد چنين و چنان ميگويد و چه مقدار كلمات نالايقه در حقّ ايشان ذكر نمودى كه او ميگويد حتّى مذكور نمودى كه از براى شهريه خوب نيست حرف گفته شود هر قسم هست اصلاح شود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va dīgar rasūlān rā nadānestam ke rā gofte agar maqṣūd janāb-e ʿabd-e ḥāżer ladā al-wajh būde va Allāh makhṣūṣ-e amrī āmade dar ān madīne ke hīch dakhlī bā ū nadāshte chenānche nazd-e aḥadī narafte jamīʿ shāhed va govāhand ke ān nafs-e khabīth dar īn arż jamīʿ-e afʿāl-e shanīʿe-ye qabīḥe rā be Ḥaqq nesbat dāde va \[corrupted text\] ān arż ham gofte-and ānche rā ke aḥadī dar ḥaqq-e aḥadī nagofte ʿabd-e ḥāżer ladā al-wajh ḥāl mīgūyad khod-e nafs-e kādhebat nayāmadī va madhkūr nanamūdī ke Siyyid Moḥammad chonīn va chonān mīgūyad va che meqdār kalemāt-e nālāyeqe dar ḥaqq-e īshān dhekr namūdī ke ū mīgūyad ḥattā madhkūr namūdī ke az barā-ye shahrīye khūb nīst ḥarf gofte shavad har qesm hast eṣlāḥ shavad.
:::

::: {.translation}
As for the messengers, I do not know whom he meant. If he meant His Honor, the servant present before the Face, by God, he came to that city for a particular matter that had nothing to do with him, and he visited no one. All are witnesses and can testify that in this land that wicked man attributed every shameful and vile deed to the True One, and \[corrupted original text\] that land too they have said what no one has ever said of anyone. The servant present before the Face now says: “Did you not come yourself, liar that you are, and report that Siyyid Muḥammad was saying such and such? How many unseemly statements about Him did you repeat, saying that he was uttering them! You even said that it was not good for talk to arise over the stipend and that the matter should be settled somehow.”
:::

### 639

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و من در جواب گفتم كه معارضه نبوده و نخواهد بود اعراض از آن نفوس لامر اللّه واقع شده نه لاجل امور ظاهره جميع شهريه را واگذارند بآن نفوس مشركه جنگى و جدالى نبوده و در مجالس متعدّده از تو خواستم كه در يك مقرّ با او مجتمع شويم تا بر تو ثابت گردد كه آنچه گفته بافتراى محض نسبت داده آمدى گفتى كه قبول نميكند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va man dar javāb goftam ke moʿāreże nabūde va nakhwāhad būd eʿrāż az ān nofūs li-amri Allāh vāqeʿ shode na li-ajl-e omūr-e ẓāhere jamīʿ-e shahrīye rā vāgod hārand be ān nofūs-e moshreke jangī va jedālī nabūde va dar majāles-e motaʿaddede az to khwāstam ke dar yek maqarr bā ū mojtameʿ shavīm tā bar to thābet gardad ke ānche gofte be efterā-ye maḥż nesbat dāde āmadī goftī ke qabūl nemīkonad.
:::

::: {.translation}
“I replied that there had been no dispute and would be none. Our turning away from those people was for the sake of the Cause of God, not for outward concerns. Let them give the entire stipend to those idolatrous souls; there has been no quarrel or contention. On several occasions I asked you to arrange for us to meet with him in one place, so that it would become clear to you that everything he had said was sheer slander. You came back and said that he would not agree.”
:::

### 640

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فو‌اللّه كلّ وجود متحيّرند از كذب شما و افتراى ما اى بی‌‌درايت سالها اين ميرزا يحيى در خدمت ايشان بوده آيا هيچ شنيده كه نفسى از منتسبين ايشان حرف بد و يا مكروهى نسبت باو گفته باشد هر جاهلى ميداند كه آنچه واقع شود افتضاح امر بوده و خواهد بود و اللّه كه هميشه فرموده‌اند كه راضى بودم هزار مرتبه شهيد شوم و اين امور بين ناس ذكر نشود كه يكى از منتسبين ايشان براى نان شكايت نموده‌و بشهرها عريضه فرستاده لعن اللّه الّذين ارتكبوا ما ناح به كلّ شیء و احترقت عنه اكباد المقرّبين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-Allāh koll-e vojūd motaḥayyerand az kedhb-e shomā va efterā-ye mā ey bī-derāyat sālhā īn Mīrzā Yaḥyā dar khedmat-e īshān būde āyā hīch shenīde ke nafsī az montasebīn-e īshān ḥarf-e bad va yā makrūhī nesbat be ū gofte bāshad har jāhelī mīdānad ke ānche vāqeʿ shavad efteżāḥ-e amr būde va khwāhad būd va Allāh ke hamīshe farmūde-and ke rāżī būdam hezār martabe shahīd shavam va īn omūr beyn-e nās dhekr nashavad ke yekī az montasebīn-e īshān barā-ye nān shekāyat namūde va be shahrhā ʿarīże ferestāde laʿana Allāhu alladhīna irtakabū mā nāḥa bihi kullu shayʾin wa iḥtaraqat ʿanhu akbādu al-muqarrabīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, all existence is bewildered by your lies and our fabrications! You who lack understanding! For years this Mīrzā Yaḥyā was in His service. Has he ever heard anyone associated with Him say anything bad or offensive about him? Even an ignorant person knows that whatever happens has brought, and will bring, disgrace upon the Cause. By God, He has always said, “I would willingly be martyred a thousand times rather than have these matters spoken of among the people—that one of those associated with Him has complained about bread and sent petitions to the cities.” May God curse those who have committed what has caused all things to lament and the hearts of those brought near to Him to burn.
:::

### 641

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فو‌اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو كه جميع اين عباد راضى بوديم كه كشته شويم و اين حرفها بميان نيايد آنچه حال ميگوئيم مكلّفيم چه كه مشاهده ميشود كه جمعى كمر بسته‌اند در هتك حرمت امر اللّه چه كه متديّن بدينى نبوده و نيستند و لاجل رياست خود را بمهلكه انداخته و مياندازند قريب پنج سنه در اين ارض توقّف شده و ابدا نفسى بباب عالى نفرستاده‌اند و مطلبی‌ اظهار نشده و آنچه وارد شده حرمة لأمر اللّه صبر نموده‌ايم و لكن آن خبيث مرتكب شده امرى را كه نفسى از قبل مرتكب نشده اميدواريم كه بمقصود خود نرسند چنانچه حرمت يك سلسله را تمام نمود او كه شأنى نداشته و نخواهد داشت
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-Allāhi alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa ke jamīʿ-e īn ʿebād rāżī būdīm ke koshte shavīm va īn ḥarfhā be miyān nayāyad ānche ḥāl mīgūyīm mokallafīm che ke moshāhede mīshavad ke jamʿī kamar baste-and dar hatk-e ḥormat-e amr-e Allāh che ke motadayyen be dīnī nabūde va nīstand va li-ajl-e reyāsat khod rā be mahlake andākhte va mīandāzand qarīb-e panj sane dar īn arż tavaqqof shode va abadan nafsī be bāb-e ʿālī naferestāde-and va maṭlabī eẓhār nashode va ānche vāred shode ḥurmatan li-amri Allāh ṣabr namūde-īm va lāken ān khabīth mortakeb shode amrī rā ke nafsī az qabl mortakeb nashode omīdvārīm ke be maqṣūd-e khod narasand chenānche ḥormat-e yek selsele rā tamām namūd ū ke shaʾnī nadāshte va nakhwāhad dāsht.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, besides whom there is no god, all of us servants would willingly have been killed rather than have such things brought up. We are duty-bound to say what we now say, for we see that a group has resolved to violate the honor of the Cause of God. They have never adhered to any religion and still do not, and for the sake of leadership they have cast themselves, and continue to cast themselves, into destruction. We have resided in this land for nearly five years, and He has never sent anyone to the Sublime Porte, nor has any request been made. Whatever has befallen us, we have borne patiently out of reverence for the Cause of God. But that wicked man has committed what no one has ever committed before. We hope they will not attain their aim, for he has utterly destroyed the honor of an entire community. He himself has never had, and will never have, any standing.
:::

### 642

::: {.original lang="fa"}
خود انصاف ده اسم او در كجا مذكور بوده اولياى دولت عليه كجا او را ميشناخته‌اند بسبب كه معروف شده خود تو ميدانى و لكن بغضآء للّه ستر مينمائى و انت من الّذين غطّيت عيوب المشركين و ما ارتكبوا لتّضييع حرمة اللّه كذلك جرى الأمر حینئذ من هذا القلم المتكلّم الصّادق الأمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Khod enṣāf deh esm-e ū dar kojā madhkūr būde awliyā-ye dawlat-e ʿalīye kojā ū rā mīshenākhte-and be sabab-e ke maʿrūf shode khod-e to mīdānī va lāken bughḍan li-llāh satr mīnamāʾī wa anta mina alladhīna ghaṭṭayta ʿuyūba al-mushrikīna wa mā irtakabū li-taḍyīʿi ḥurmati Allāhi kadhālika jarā al-amru ḥīnaʾidhin min hādhā al-qalami al-mutakallimi al-ṣādiqi al-amīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Judge fairly yourself: where had his name ever been mentioned? How had the officials of the exalted government ever known him? You yourself know through whom he became known, but out of hatred for God you conceal it. You are among those who have covered up the faults of the idolaters and what they have committed to dishonor God. Thus has the matter now issued from this speaking Pen, the truthful, the trustworthy.
:::

### 643

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قوله كبر حمقه خيلى خيلى عجب است از شما كه قريب بيست سال است ميرزا يحيى را بخدائى پرستيديد كه خود مطّلعم در اصفهان در نزد خودم اقرار نموديد حال مردود شده به آقا ميرزا محمّد على و ميرزا ابوالحسن و ديگران و ميرزا حسين ورزنه چه جواب بگويم كه فلانيها هر روز بيكى ميچسبند و يكى را حقّ ميدانند و بعد باطل مينمايند اين از عدم تميز آنها است بجهت آنكه حقّ باطل نميشود و اين تناقض است دين اينها بوالهوسى است چنانچه ميرزا ابوالحسن در طهران بمن گفت حيف از شما بچه دليل اوّل حقّ بود و خدا و حال باطل است و عبد كافر اى به به عجب يك انصاف از شما ميپرسم شما را بخدا اين است در بعضى مقامات با شما در وقتى حركت كرده كه در عرض هم بوديم حالا را هر يك بديگرى نميتوانيم برترى نمائيم اگر چه هر قدر كامل شده باشيم انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qawluhu kabura ḥumquhu kheylī kheylī ʿajab ast az shomā ke qarīb-e bīst sāl ast Mīrzā Yaḥyā rā be khodāʾī parastīdīd ke khod moṭṭaleʿam dar Eṣfahān dar nazd-e khodam eqrār namūdīd ḥāl mardūd shode be Āqā Mīrzā Moḥammad ʿAlī va Mīrzā Abu’l-Ḥasan va dīgarān va Mīrzā Ḥoseyn-e Varzane che javāb begūyam ke folānīhā har rūz be yekī mīchasband va yekī rā ḥaqq mīdānand va baʿd bāṭel mīnamāyand īn az ʿadam-e tamīz-e ānhā ast be jahat-e ānke ḥaqq bāṭel nemīshavad va īn tanāqoż ast dīn-e īnhā bū’l-havasī ast chenānche Mīrzā Abu’l-Ḥasan dar Ṭehrān be man goft ḥeyf az shomā be che dalīl avval ḥaqq būd va khodā va ḥāl bāṭel ast va ʿabd-e kāfer ey bah bah ʿajab yek enṣāf az shomā mīporsam shomā rā be khodā īn ast dar baʿżī maqāmāt bā shomā dar vaqtī ḥarakat karde ke dar ʿarż-e ham būdīm ḥālā rā har yek be dīgarī nemītavānīm bartarī namāʾīm agar che har qadr kāmel shode bāshīm intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
His words—great is his folly: “It is very, very astonishing that for nearly twenty years you worshipped Mīrzā Yaḥyā as God. I know this myself, for you admitted it in my own presence in Isfahan. Now he has been rejected. What answer should I give Āqā Mīrzā Muḥammad ʿAlī, Mīrzā Abu’l-Ḥasan, the others, and Mīrzā Ḥusayn of Varzanih, who say that these people attach themselves to someone new every day, consider someone to be the truth, and then declare him false? This is due to their lack of discernment, because truth does not become falsehood, and this is a contradiction. Their religion is caprice. As Mīrzā Abu’l-Ḥasan said to me in Tehran, ‘What a pity for you! On what grounds was he at first the truth and God, and now false and an unbelieving servant?’ Oh, bravo! How astonishing! I ask you for just one fair judgment, for God’s sake! This is someone who, on certain occasions, associated with you at a time when we were on an equal footing. At present neither of us can claim superiority over the other, however much we may have advanced in perfection.” End of quotation.
:::

### 644

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اوّلا اين بحث بر شما و امثال شما وارد چه كه سالها نفوسى را پيشوا ميدانستيد كه اخبث از آن نفوس در ابداع نيامده چنانچه بحكم آن نفوس مظهر نفس الهى را بتمام ظلم شهيد نمودند و ثانياً اينكه اين عباد باو خلوص داشته‌ايم و مقرّيم چه كه در كلمات حضرت ابهى بعضى اوصاف مشاهده ميشد و همچه گمان مينموديم كه مرجع آن اوصاف نفس موهوم است الى ان كشف اللّه لنا ما كشف و اطّلعنا من افعاله ما لا فعله النّمرود و لا الفرعون و لذا كسّرنا صنم الوهم و عرفنا ما هو المقصود فى كلماته الابدع البديع ثمّ اطّلعنا به و باصل امره ما كان مقنوعا عنك و عن مثلائك و انّك لو تعرف لتفرّ منه و تشقّ سبحات الجلال و تتوجّه الى مشرق الجمال و تكون من الموقنين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Avvalan īn baḥth bar shomā va amthāl-e shomā vāred che ke sālhā nofūsī rā pīshvā mīdānestīd ke akhbath az ān nofūs dar ebdāʿ nayāmade chenānche be ḥokm-e ān nofūs maẓhar-e nafs-e elāhī rā be tamām-e ẓolm shahīd namūdand va thāniyan īnke īn ʿebād bā ū kholūṣ dāshte-īm va moqerrīm che ke dar kalemāt-e Ḥażrat-e Abhā baʿżī awṣāf moshāhede mīshod va hamche gomān mīnamūdīm ke marjaʿ-e ān awṣāf nafs-e mawhūm ast ilā an kashafa Allāhu lanā mā kashafa wa iṭṭalaʿnā min afʿālihi mā lā faʿalahu al-Nimrūdu wa lā al-Firʿawnu wa li-dhā kassar nā ṣanama al-wahmi wa ʿarafnā mā huwa al-maqṣūdu fī kalimātihi al-abdaʿi al-badīʿi thumma iṭṭalaʿnā bihi wa bi-aṣli amrihi mā kāna maqnūʿan ʿanka wa ʿan muthalāʾika wa innaka law taʿrifu la-tafirru minhu wa tashuqqu subuḥāti al-jalāli wa tatawajjahu ilā mashriqi al-jamāli wa takūnu mina al-mūqinīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
First, this objection applies to you and those like you, for years you regarded as leaders people more wicked than any who have ever appeared in creation. It was at their command that the Manifestation of the divine Self was martyred with the utmost cruelty. Second, we admit that we servants were sincerely devoted to him, for certain descriptions appeared in the words of His Most Glorious Presence, and we supposed that those descriptions referred to that imagined person, until God revealed to us what He revealed, and we learned of deeds of his that neither Nimrod nor Pharaoh had committed. Therefore we shattered the idol of delusion and recognized what was intended in His most wondrous and incomparable words. Then we learned about him and the true nature of his affair what had been concealed from you and those like you. If you knew, you would flee from him, tear through the veils of glory, turn toward the Dawning-Place of Beauty, and be among those who are certain.
:::

### 645

::: {.original lang="fa"}
حمد ميكنيم خدا را كه ببازوى توكّل و انقطاع صنم وهم را شكستيم و بشريعه يقين وارد شديم و كاش تو هم ميبودى و ببصر خود مشاهده مينمودى نحمد اللّه بذلك و نشكره فى كلّ حين فو‌اللّه اگر ذرّه انصاف در تو ميبود هرآينه بايد ليل و نهار باوصاف اين عباد متكلّم شوى چه كه فعل ما بر دين ما گواهى است صادق و شاهدى است واضح و آشكار چه كه سلاسل تقليد را شكستيم و بحقّ فايز گشتيم و از وهميكه جميع قلوب را اخذ نموده ‌بود فارغ شديم اى فقير بی‌‌بضاعت بسيار بسيار در وهم مستغرقى فيا ليت رايته و عرفته و اطلعت بما عنده كاش ملاقات شده بود و از عرفانيكه در مجالس ذكر مينمود مذكور ميامد و مطّلع ميشدى از آنچه اين ایّام از او محتجبی‌
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ḥamd mīkonīm Khodā rā ke be bāzū-ye tavakkol va enqeṭāʿ ṣanam-e vahm rā shekastīm va be sharīʿe-ye yaqīn vāred shodīm va kāsh to ham mībūdī va be baṣar-e khod moshāhede mīnamūdī naḥmadu Allāha bi-dhālika wa nashkuruhu fī kulli ḥīn fa-wa-Allāh agar dharre enṣāf dar to mībūd har-āyene bāyad leyl va nahār be awṣāf-e īn ʿebād motakallem shavī che ke feʿl-e mā bar dīn-e mā govāhī ast ṣādeq va shāhedī ast vāżeḥ va āshkār che ke salāsel-e taqlīd rā shekastīm va be Ḥaqq fāyez gashtīm va az vahmī ke jamīʿ-e qolūb rā akhdh namūde būd fāregh shodīm ey faqīr-e bī-beżāʿat besyār besyār dar vahm mostaghraqī fa-yā layta raʾaytahu wa ʿaraftahu wa iṭṭalaʿta bi-mā ʿindahu kāsh molāqāt shode būd va az ʿerfānī ke dar majāles dhekr mīnamūd madhkūr mīāmad va moṭṭaleʿ mīshodī az ānche īn ayyām az ū moḥtajebī.
:::

::: {.translation}
We praise God that, through the strength of trust in Him and detachment, we shattered the idol of delusion and reached the waters of certainty. Would that you too had been there and seen with your own eyes! We praise God for this and thank Him at all times. By God, if you had a particle of fairness, you would surely speak day and night of the qualities of these servants, for our conduct is a truthful testimony to our faith and a clear and evident witness. We broke the chains of imitation, attained the True One, and freed ourselves from the delusion that had seized every heart. You poor, destitute one! You are deeply, deeply immersed in delusion. If only you had seen him, known him, and learned what he possessed! Would that a meeting had taken place, that the spiritual knowledge of which he spoke in gatherings had been discussed, and that you had learned what remains veiled from you concerning him in these days.
:::

### 646

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انّك ان لاتعرفنا نحن نعرفك انفسنا لتطلع و تكون من العالمين نحن عباد الّذين جعل اللّه ابصارنا حديداً و عرفناه بنفسه و انقطعنا عن العالمين و ما منعنا منع مانع و لا مكر ماكر و لاخدع خادع و لاريب قلوب المغلّين نحمد اللّه بما عرفنا نفسه الّذى كان موعوداً فى الواحه المقدّس المحكم البديع و ما منعنا عن عرفانه حجبات الّذينهم كفروا باللّه ثمّ سبحات الّذينهم اشركوا بنفسه الواحد الفرد العزيز الحميد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-innaka in lā taʿrifunā naḥnu nuʿarrifuka anfusanā li-taṭṭaliʿa wa-takūna mina al-ʿālimīn. Naḥnu ʿibād alladhīna jaʿala Allāhu abṣāranā ḥadīdan wa-ʿarafnāhu bi-nafsihi wa-inqaṭaʿnā ʿani al-ʿālamīn. Wa-mā manaʿanā manʿu māniʿ wa-lā makru mākir wa-lā khidʿu khādiʿ wa-lā raybu qulūbi al-mughillīn. Naḥmadu Allāha bi-mā ʿarrafanā nafsahu alladhī kāna mawʿūdan fī alwāḥihi al-muqaddasi al-muḥkami al-badīʿ. Wa-mā manaʿanā ʿan ʿirfānihi ḥujubātu alladhīnahum kafarū bi-Allāh thumma subuḥātu alladhīnahum ashrakū bi-nafsihi al-Wāḥidi al-Fardi al-ʿAzīzi al-Ḥamīd.
:::

::: {.translation}
If you do not know us, we will make ourselves known to you, so that you may understand and be among those who know. We are servants whose sight God has made keen; we have recognized Him through Himself and detached ourselves from all the worlds. No obstruction by anyone, no schemer’s plotting, no deceiver’s deception, and no doubt in the hearts of the malicious have held us back. We praise God for making known to us His own Self, who was promised in His holy, firmly established, wondrous Tablets. Neither the veils of those who disbelieved in God nor the veils of glory of those who associated partners with His Self, the One, the Unique, the Almighty, the All-Praised, prevented us from recognizing Him.
:::

### 647

::: {.original lang="fa"}
عجب است كه باينگونه تحقيقات مشغول شده اذا ظهر الشّطّ هل يليق لأحد ان يلتفت الى مآء الغدير اذا فانصف يا ايّها الحمير و اذا اشرقت الشّمس هل ينبغى لأحد ان يستضئ بالسّراج و لو كان سراجاً حقيقيّاً فانصف يا ايّها الغافل الّذى بغفلتك ناح كلّ شیء و لو انّك انت فى حجبات غليظ و اذا تموّج بحر الأعظم هل يتوجّه العاقل الى سراب بقيعة لا فو‌ربّنا الرّحمن الرّحيم و لكن انت لن تجد ما نذكر لانّ قلبك صار محروماً من نفحات اللّه المقتدر العلىّ الحكيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
ʿAjab ast kih bi-īn-gūnih taḥqīqāt mashghūl shudih. Idhā ẓahara al-shaṭṭu hal yalīqu li-aḥadin an yaltafita ilā māʾi al-ghadīr? Idhan fa-anṣif yā ayyuhā al-ḥamīr. Wa-idhā ashraqati al-shamsu hal yanbaghī li-aḥadin an yastaḍīʾa bi-al-sirāj wa-law kāna sirājan ḥaqīqiyyan? Fa-anṣif yā ayyuhā al-ghāfil alladhī bi-ghaflatika nāḥa kullu shayʾ wa-law innaka anta fī ḥujubātin ghalīẓ. Wa-idhā tamawwaja baḥru al-Aʿẓam hal yatawajjahu al-ʿāqilu ilā sarābin bi-qīʿah? Lā fa-wa-Rabbinā al-Raḥmāni al-Raḥīm. Wa-lākin anta lan tajida mā nadhkuru li-anna qalbaka ṣāra maḥrūman min nafaḥāti Allāhi al-Muqtadiri al-ʿAliyyi al-Ḥakīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
It is astonishing that you have occupied yourself with investigations of this kind. When the great river has appeared, is it fitting for anyone to turn toward the water of a pool? Be fair, then, you ass! When the sun has risen, should anyone seek illumination from a lamp, even if it is a real lamp? Be fair, heedless one, through whose heedlessness all things have lamented, though you remain within thick veils. When the Most Great Ocean surges, would a rational person turn toward a mirage on a plain? No, by our Lord, the All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful! Yet you will never grasp what We recount, for your heart has been deprived of the breezes of God, the All-Powerful, the Most High, the All-Wise.
:::

### 648

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اللّه نسوان ننگ دارند از ادلّه تو شيطان در هر آسمانى باسمى معروف و معلّم ملكوت بوده و زياده از الف سنه بكلّ اسماء موسوم و بعد يكمرتبه رجيم شده اين امور از بدايع قدرت الهى است هل تنكرها و انّك لو تنكر يصدقها عباده الموقنين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va-Allāh nisvān nang dārand az adillih-yi tu. Shayṭān dar har āsmānī bi-ismī maʿrūf va muʿallim-i malakūt būdih va ziyādih az alf sanih bi-kull-i asmāʾ mawsūm va baʿd yik-martabih rajīm shudih. Īn umūr az badāyiʿ-i qudrat-i ilāhī ast. Hal tunkiruhā wa-innaka law tunkir yuṣaddiquhā ʿibāduhu al-mūqinīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, women are ashamed of your arguments. Satan was known by a name in every heaven and was a teacher of the Kingdom. For more than a thousand years he bore every name, and then, all at once, he was cast out. These things are among the wonders of divine power. Do you deny them? Even if you deny them, His servants who are certain affirm them.
:::

### 649

::: {.original lang="fa"}
آيا نشنيده يهوداى اسخريوطى يكى از حروفات اثنا عشريّه انجيل بوده و بعد بشقاوتى ظاهر كه كلمة اللّه را تسليم يهود نمود و كاش رئيس شما بفعل او ارتكاب مينمود چه كه او بعد از آن عمل شنيع نادم شده و لكن مرشدت نقطه بيان و كلّ انبیاء و مرسلين و حرمة اللّه جميع را بزخارف ارض مبادله نموده‌ و فروخته چنانچه ذكر شد و تو بجميع مطّلعى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Āyā nashanīdih Yahūdā-yi Iskharīyūṭī yikī az ḥurūfāt-i ithnā-ʿasharīyyih-yi Injīl būdih va baʿd bi-shiqāvatī ẓāhir kih Kalimat Allāh rā taslīm-i Yahūd namūd? Va kāsh raʾīs-i shumā bi-fiʿl-i ū irtikāb mīnamūd, chih kih ū baʿd az ān ʿamal-i shanīʿ nādim shudih, va lākin murshidat Nuqṭih-yi Bayān va kull-i anbiyā va mursalīn va ḥurmat-i Allāh jamīʿ rā bi-zakhārif-i arḍ mubādilih namūdih va furūkhtih, chunānchih dhikr shud, va tu bi-jamīʿ muṭṭaliʿī.
:::

::: {.translation}
Have you not heard that Judas Iscariot was one of the twelve Letters of the Gospel, and afterward displayed such wickedness that he delivered the Word of God into the hands of the Jews? Would that your leader had committed his deed, for Judas repented after that heinous act. Your guide, however, has exchanged and sold the Point of the Bayán, all the Prophets and Messengers, and the sanctity of God for earthly vanities, as has been recounted, and you are aware of it all.
:::

### 650

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ديگر در اسمعيل بن حضرت صادق چه ميگوئى بعد از آنكه بجميع ولايات نوشته كه او بعد از من امام است و پيشواى خلق بعد از مدّتى امورى از او ظاهر شد و حضرت او را عزل فرمودند كه مخصوص زراده و بعضى از اصحاب عرض كردند يا ابن رسول اللّه اين امر بزرگى است چگونه ميشود شخصى امام خلق باشد و حقّ و بعد باطل شود حضرت ذكر بدا فرمود برو و روايت كلينى را ببين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va dīgar dar Ismaʿīl ibn-i Ḥaḍrat-i Ṣādiq chih mīgūʾī? Baʿd az ānkih bi-jamīʿ-i vilāyāt nivishtih kih ū baʿd az man imām ast va pīshvā-yi khalq, baʿd az muddatī umūrī az ū ẓāhir shud va Ḥaḍrat ū rā ʿazl farmūdand, kih makhṣūṣ Zarādih va baʿḍī az aṣḥāb ʿarḍ kardand: Yā ibn-i Rasūl-i Allāh, īn amr-i buzurgī ast, chigūnih mīshavad shakhṣī imām-i khalq bāshad va ḥaqq va baʿd bāṭil shavad? Ḥaḍrat dhikr-i badā farmūd. Biraw va rivāyat-i Kulaynī rā bibīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
And what do you say about Ismaʿil, the son of His Holiness Ṣádiq? After he had written to all the provinces that Ismaʿil would be the Imam and leader of the people after him, certain things appeared from Ismaʿil after a time, and His Holiness dismissed him. In particular, Zarádih and some of the companions submitted: “O son of the Messenger of God, this is a weighty matter. How can someone be the Imam of the people and be true, and then become false?” His Holiness spoke of badá. Go and read Kulayní’s account.
:::

### 651

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اى فقير از هيچ امرى خبر ندارى نه از بيان و نه از فرقان و نه از تورية و نه از انجيل و در ظهور اين امر انقلابات بسيار شده و اين عبد نظر باختصار ذكر ننمود و در كتب خود شما مذكور است چنانچه حال هم بعضى از اطراف اسمعيل را امام ميدانند كتب ظاهره را هم نديده و مطّلع نيستى شان شما اينست كه بحرفهاى ّ تكلّم نمائيد و باينگونه ادلّه مستدلّ شويد بر بصير خبير مشتبه نشده و نميشود و بسا از امور كه واقع شده و احدى مطّلع نه چه كه حقّ از قبل ستر فرموده ايكاش كه از هوى ميگذشتى و چندى للّه در كوى دوست مقرّ ميگزيدى تا بعضى از امور مستوره بر تو كشف ميشد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ay faqīr, az hīch amrī khabar nadārī, nah az Bayān va nah az Furqān va nah az Tawrāt va nah az Injīl. Va dar ẓuhūr-i īn amr inqilābāt-i bisyār shudih va īn ʿabd naẓar bi-ikhtiṣār dhikr nanamūd, va dar kutub-i khud-i shumā madhkūr ast, chunānchih ḥāl ham baʿḍī az aṭrāf Ismaʿīl rā imām mīdānand. Kutub-i ẓāhirih rā ham nadīdih va muṭṭaliʿ nīstī. Shaʾn-i shumā īnast kih bi-ḥarfhā-yi \[corrupted text\] takallum namāyīd va bi-īn-gūnih adillih mustadill shavīd. Bar baṣīr-i khabīr mushtabih nashudih va namīshavad. Va basā az umūr kih vāqiʿ shudih va aḥadī muṭṭaliʿ nah, chih kih Ḥaqq az qabl satr farmūdih. Ay kāsh kih az havā mīgudhashtī va chandī li-llāh dar kūy-i Dūst maqarr mīguzīdī tā baʿḍī az umūr-i mastūrih bar tu kashf mīshud.
:::

::: {.translation}
You poor man, you know nothing of any matter—neither of the Bayán, nor of the Qur’an, nor of the Torah, nor of the Gospel. Many reversals have occurred in the unfolding of this matter, and this servant has not recounted them for the sake of brevity. They are recorded in your own books; even now, people in some regions regard Ismaʿil as the Imam. You have not even seen the readily available books and are uninformed. Your way is to utter words of \[corrupted original text\] and to argue with proofs of this kind. The discerning and well-informed have not been misled, nor will they be. Many things have happened of which no one is aware, for God concealed them in the past. If only you would abandon your desires and dwell for a time, for God’s sake, in the Beloved’s neighborhood, so that some hidden matters might be disclosed to you.
:::

### 652

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ديگر از بلعم باعور اطّلاع ندارى كه بسيار از رئيس شما مشهورتر بود ولايتش كه مسلّم بوده مع‌ذلك بعد از ظهور شمس كليم من افق ربّك الرّحمن الرّحيم فعل ما فعل و بذلك بدّل اللّه نوره بالنّار و انّه لعلى كلّ شیء قدير كاش از رئيس خود اطّلاع ميداشتى فو‌اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو انّ يد القدرة و القوّة قد اخذ كفّا من التّراب و نفخ فيه روحاً من ارواح الّتى خلقت بمشيّته فلمّا اهتزّ و قام البسه بقميص الأسماء بين الأرض و السّمآء لحكمة الّتى ما اطّلع بها احد الّا نفسه العليم الخبير زياده از اين نبوده و نخواهد بود فلمّا عاد على اللّه عاد اللّه عليه كما عاد كذلك يجزى عباده المعتدين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va dīgar az Balʿam-i Bāʿūr iṭṭilāʿ nadārī kih bisyār az raʾīs-i shumā mashhūrtar būd. Vilāyatash kih musallam būdih, maʿa-dhālik baʿd az ẓuhūr-i shams-i Kalīm min ufuqi Rabbika al-Raḥmāni al-Raḥīm faʿala mā faʿala wa-bi-dhālika baddala Allāhu nūrahu bi-al-nār wa-innahu la-ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr. Kāsh az raʾīs-i khud iṭṭilāʿ mīdāshtī. Fa-wa-Allāhi alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa inna yada al-qudrati wa-al-quwwati qad akhadha kaffan mina al-turāb wa-nafakha fīhi rūḥan min arwāḥi allatī khuliqat bi-mashīʾatihi fa-lammā ihtazza wa-qāma albasahu bi-qamīṣi al-asmāʾ bayna al-arḍi wa-al-samāʾ li-ḥikmati allatī mā iṭṭalaʿa bihā aḥad illā nafsuhu al-ʿAlīmu al-Khabīr. Ziyādih az īn nabūdih va nakhvāhad būd. Fa-lammā ʿāda ʿalā Allāh ʿāda Allāhu ʿalayhi ka-mā ʿād. Kadhālika yajzī ʿibādahu al-muʿtadīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Nor do you know about Balaam son of Beor, who was far more renowned than your leader. His spiritual authority was acknowledged; nevertheless, after the sun of Moses rose from the horizon of your Lord, the All-Merciful, the Ever-Merciful, he did what he did, and through this God changed his light into fire. He indeed has power over all things. Would that you knew about your own leader! By God, besides whom there is no other god, the hand of power and might took a handful of dust and breathed into it a spirit from among the spirits created by His will. When it stirred and stood upright, He clothed it in the garment of names between earth and heaven, for a wisdom known to no one but His own Self, the All-Knowing, the All-Informed. It has never been, nor will it ever be, more than this. Then, when he turned against God, God turned against him as he had turned. Thus does He recompense His transgressing servants.
:::

### 653

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بشنو سخن اين عبد را سبب وهم ناس مشو رحم كن بر امر اللّه و برناس در هر عصر نفوس متوهّمه مجتمع شده و ناس را از شاطى بحر احديّه محروم نموده‌اند قدرى تفكّر نما كه چه مقدار توهّمات در ما بين ملأ فرقان بود از ظهور قائم و ظهور قيامت و ظهور ساعت و بعد از ظهور نقطه اولى روح ما سواه فداه معلوم شد كه جميع خاطى بوده‌اند و بقطره از بحر علم مشروب نه و آن جمال قدم بزحمت تمام كسر اصنام وهم و هوى نموده ‌تازه امثال آن نفوس اراده نموده‌اند ناس را باوهام جديد مبتلا نمايند بگو بترسيد از خداوند يكتا و مرتكب مشويد امري را كه از چشم مقرّبين بجاى اشك خون جارى شود حقّ را باطل مدانيد و باطل را حقّ مشمريد بلى حقّ لم‌يزل حقّ بوده و لكن تو آن حقّ را نشناخته
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bishnaw sukhan-i īn ʿabd rā, sabab-i vahm-i nās mashaw. Raḥm kun bar Amr-i Allāh va bar nās. Dar har ʿaṣr nufūs-i mutavahhimih mujtamiʿ shudih va nās rā az shāṭī-yi baḥr-i aḥadīyyih maḥrūm namūdih-and. Qadrī tafakkur namā kih chih miqdār tavahhumāt dar mā bayn-i malaʾ-i Furqān būd az ẓuhūr-i Qāʾim va ẓuhūr-i qiyāmat va ẓuhūr-i sāʿat, va baʿd az ẓuhūr-i Nuqṭih-yi Ūlā, rūḥ-i mā sivāh fidāh, maʿlūm shud kih jamīʿ khāṭī būdih-and va bi-qaṭrih az baḥr-i ʿilm mashrūb nah. Va ān Jamāl-i Qidam bi-zaḥmat-i tamām kasr-i aṣnām-i vahm va havā namūdih, tāzih amthāl-i ān nufūs irādih namūdih-and nās rā bi-avhām-i jadīd mubtalā namāyand. Bigū bitarsīd az Khudāvand-i yiktā va murtakib mashavīd amrī rā kih az chashm-i muqarrabīn bi-jā-yi ashk khūn jārī shavad. Ḥaqq rā bāṭil madānīd va bāṭil rā ḥaqq mashmurīd. Balī Ḥaqq lam-yazal ḥaqq būdih va lākin tu ān Ḥaqq rā nashnākhtih.
:::

::: {.translation}
Listen to the words of this servant, and do not cause people to fall into delusion. Have mercy on the Cause of God and on the people. In every age, deluded souls have gathered together and deprived people of the shore of the ocean of oneness. Reflect a little on how many misconceptions existed among the people of the Qur’an concerning the appearance of the Qá’im, the advent of the Resurrection, and the coming of the Hour. After the appearance of the Primal Point—may the souls of all besides Him be sacrificed for Him—it became clear that they had all been mistaken and had not drunk a single drop from the ocean of knowledge. That Ancient Beauty shattered the idols of delusion and desire with immense difficulty, and now others like those souls have set out to afflict people with new delusions. Say: Fear the one God, and do not commit a deed that would cause blood rather than tears to flow from the eyes of those near to Him. Do not regard truth as falsehood, or reckon falsehood as truth. Yes, the True One has always been true, but you have not recognized that True One.
:::

### 654

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اين مسلّم بوده كه بعد از نقطه حقّ منحصر است در حروفات حىّ چه كه كلّ خلق بيان در ظلّ واحد اوّل خلق شده و ميشوند و حقّ هر ذى حقّى باين نفوس ثابت و هم‌چنين كلّ صفات و اسماء حسنى و مع‌ذلك خطاب ميفرمايد بيكى از حروفات حىّ كه از ظهور بعد سؤال نموده ‌ميفرمايد اگر بدانم كه تو در يوم اشراق نيّر معانى بايمان باو فايز نميشوى حال حكم دون ايمان در حقّ تو جارى مينمايم و اگر بدانم يكى از نصارى در يوم ظهور مؤمن باو ميشود حال حكم ايمان درباره او ميفرمودم مع آنكه مؤمن نيست و فعل محبوبی‌ از او ظاهر نشده قدرى تفكر نما و حقّ را بشناس
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īn musallam būdih kih baʿd az Nuqṭih ḥaqq munḥaṣir ast dar Ḥurūfāt-i Ḥayy, chih kih kull-i khalq-i Bayān dar ẓill-i Vāḥid-i Avval khalq shudih va mīshavand, va ḥaqq-i har dhī-ḥaqqī bi-īn nufūs thābit va ham-chunīn kull-i ṣifāt va asmāʾ-i ḥusnā. Va maʿa-dhālik khiṭāb mīfarmāyad bi-yikī az Ḥurūfāt-i Ḥayy kih az ẓuhūr-i baʿd suʾāl namūdih, mīfarmāyad: Agar bidānam kih tu dar yawm-i ishrāq-i nayyir-i maʿānī bi-īmān bi-ū fāʾiz namīshavī, ḥāl ḥukm-i dūn-i īmān dar ḥaqq-i tu jārī mīnamāyam, va agar bidānam yikī az Naṣārā dar yawm-i ẓuhūr muʾmin bi-ū mīshavad, ḥāl ḥukm-i īmān dar bārih-yi ū mīfarmūdam, maʿa ānkih muʾmin nīst va fiʿl-i maḥbūbī az ū ẓāhir nashudih. Qadrī tafakkur namā va Ḥaqq rā bishnās.
:::

::: {.translation}
It has been acknowledged that, after the Point, truth is confined to the Letters of the Living, for the entire creation of the Bayán has been and continues to be created beneath the shadow of the First Váḥid. The right of everyone possessing a right is established through these souls, as are all the attributes and most beautiful names. Nevertheless, addressing one of the Letters of the Living who had asked about the next Revelation, He says: “If I know that, on the day when the Luminary of inner meanings rises, you will not attain faith in Him, I pronounce upon you now the judgment of unbelief. And if I know that one of the Christians will believe in Him on the day of His Revelation, I would pronounce upon him now the judgment of faith, even though he is not a believer and no pleasing deed has appeared from him.” Reflect a little and recognize the True One.
:::

### 655

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اين نفوس حقّند ماداميكه در ظلّ حقّ باشند چه كه در آنوقت ديده نميشود در آن نفوس مگر حقّ و بعد از توقّف دام الملك فى الملك و رجع المخلوق الى شكله و مثله آن حقّيكه لم‌يزل باطل نشده و نخواهد شد آن شجره حقيقت است فاعرف لو تكون من العارفين كذلك فصّل الأمر من لدن منزل قديم تفكّر يا عبد لعلّ تكون من المهتدين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Īn nufūs ḥaqq-and mādāmīkih dar ẓill-i Ḥaqq bāshand, chih kih dar ān vaqt dīdih namīshavad dar ān nufūs magar Ḥaqq. Va baʿd az tavaqquf dāma al-mulku fī al-mulk wa-rajaʿa al-makhlūqu ilā shaklihi wa-mithlihi. Ān Ḥaqqīkih lam-yazal bāṭil nashudih va nakhvāhad shud ān Shajarih-yi Ḥaqīqat ast. Fa-iʿrif law takūnu mina al-ʿārifīn. Kadhālika fuṣṣila al-amru min ladun Munzilin Qadīm. Tafakkar yā ʿabd laʿalla takūnu mina al-muhtadīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
These souls are true as long as they remain beneath the shadow of the True One, for at that time nothing is seen in them but the True One. After they hesitate, sovereignty remains within sovereignty, and the creature returns to its own kind and likeness. That True One who has never become false, nor ever will, is the Tree of Reality. Recognize this, if you are among those who know. Thus has the matter been expounded by the Ancient Revealer. Reflect, O servant, so that you may be among the rightly guided.
:::

### 656

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اى غافل غير بالغ بدانكه در بعث مراتب ما لانهايه بوده و خواهد بود و بعث اسماء را از دونش تميز ده بسا نفوس كه اسماء مبعوثند من غير رسم ذلك لحكمة لن يعرفها احد و لو تريد ان تعرفها فاسئل عن اللّه ربّك بخضوع و خشوع و انابة مبين ليعلّمك ما عنده و انّه لهو العليم الخبير در الواح قبل در اينمقام از قلم امر فى الجمله نازل شده اگر اراده نمائى در آن الواح نظر كن شايد بهمان قدر قناعت نمائى و مقصود از اين ذكر آنكه باسماء از منزل آن محتجب نمانى اگر چه بشأنى محتجب مانده كه ابداً گمان نميرود كه خرق شود الّا بارادة اللّه و مشيّته
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ay ghāfil-i ghayr-i bāligh, bidānkih dar baʿth marātib-i mā lā nihāyih būdih va khvāhad būd va baʿth-i asmāʾ rā az dūnash tamyīz dih. Basā nufūs kih asmāʾ mabʿūthand min ghayri rasm. Dhālika li-ḥikmatin lan yaʿrifahā aḥad. Wa-law turīdu an taʿrifahā fa-isʾal ʿan Allāhi Rabbika bi-khuḍūʿin wa-khushūʿin wa-inābatin mubīn li-yuʿallimaka mā ʿindahu wa-innahu la-huwa al-ʿAlīmu al-Khabīr. Dar alvāḥ-i qabl dar īn maqām az Qalam-i Amr fī al-jumlih nāzil shudih. Agar irādih namāʾī dar ān alvāḥ naẓar kun, shāyad bi-hamān qadr qanāʿat namāʾī. Va maqṣūd az īn dhikr ānkih bi-asmāʾ az Munzil-i ān muḥtajib namānī, agar-chih bi-shaʾnī muḥtajib māndih kih abadan gumān namīravad kih kharq shavad illā bi-irādati Allāhi wa-mashīʾatihi.
:::

::: {.translation}
O heedless, immature one! Know that resurrection has had and will have limitless degrees, and distinguish the resurrection of names from other kinds. Many are the souls whose names have been raised without any outward trace. This is for a wisdom that no one will know. If you wish to know it, ask God your Lord with humility, reverence, and manifest repentance, so that He may teach you what is with Him. He is indeed the All-Knowing, the All-Informed. In earlier Tablets, something on this subject has been revealed by the Pen of the Cause. If you wish, consult those Tablets; perhaps you will be content with that much. The purpose of this mention is that you should not remain veiled by the names from the One who reveals them, although you have remained so veiled that it is inconceivable that the veil should ever be torn away except through God’s purpose and will.
:::

### 657

::: {.original lang="fa"}
نقطه بيان جلّت عظمته در تبديل كينونات هم ذكر فرموده‌اند تا چه رسد باسماء چنانچه بعضى از آن از قبل ذكر شد و هم‌چنين ميفرمايد قوله جلّ ذكره فانّ عند كلّ ظهور ادلّآء اثباتها يبدّلنّ بالنّفى و لكن اللّه فى ذلك الظّهور يثبت امره و يتقن صنعه لانّ فيه لايبدّلنّ النّور بالنّار الّا فى ظهور اللّه فانّ حزنى على كلّ من فى البيان من يؤمئذ انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Nuqṭih-yi Bayān, jallat ʿaẓamatuhu, dar tabdīl-i kaynūnāt ham dhikr farmūdih-and tā chih rasad bi-asmāʾ, chunānchih baʿḍī az ān az qabl dhikr shud. Va ham-chunīn mīfarmāyad, qawluhu jalla dhikruhu: Fa-inna ʿinda kulli ẓuhūrin adillāʾa ithbātihā yubaddalunna bi-al-nafy wa-lākinna Allāha fī dhālika al-ẓuhūri yuthbitu amrahu wa-yutqinu ṣunʿahu li-anna fīhi lā yubaddalunna al-nūru bi-al-nār illā fī ẓuhūri Allāh fa-inna ḥuznī ʿalā kulli man fī al-Bayān min \[corrupted text\]. Intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
The Point of the Bayán—exalted be His grandeur—has spoken even of the transformation of essential realities, let alone names, as some of this has already been mentioned. He also says—His words, exalted be His mention: “At every Revelation, the exponents of its affirmation are changed into negation. Yet in that Revelation God establishes His Cause and perfects His handiwork, for in it light is not changed into fire except at the Revelation of God. My sorrow is indeed for everyone in the Bayán from \[corrupted original text\].” End of quotation.
:::

### 658

::: {.original lang="fa"}
ملاحظه نمائيد كه صريح ميفرمايند نور مبدّل بنار ميشود چنانچه نورى كه شما آن را نور فرض گرفته‌ايد كينونتش بنار تبديل شده و لكن شاعر نيست و در كمال غفلت مشغول بتحريف كلمات الهيّه بوده و هست و اينكه ميفرمايند الّا فى ظهور اللّه همچه ندانيد كه قبل از ظهور تبديل نور نميشود بلى فو‌نفسه الحقّ غير از نفس ظهور كلّ تبديل شده و ميشوند و اين مسائل موهومه نزد ناس بوده و تا اين ظهور كشف نشده فلمّا خرقتم حجاب حرمة اللّه لذا خرق ستر حجابكم بأنامل القدرة و القوّة
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Mulāḥiẓih namāyīd kih ṣarīḥ mīfarmāyand nūr mubaddal bi-nār mīshavad, chunānchih nūrī kih shumā ān rā nūr farḍ giriftih-īd kaynūnatash bi-nār tabdīl shudih va lākin shāʿir nīst, va dar kamāl-i ghaflat mashghūl bi-taḥrīf-i kalimāt-i ilāhīyyih būdih va hast. Va īnkih mīfarmāyand illā fī ẓuhūri Allāh hamchih nadānīd kih qabl az ẓuhūr tabdīl-i nūr namīshavad. Balī fa-wa-nafsihi al-Ḥaqq ghayr az nafs-i Ẓuhūr kull tabdīl shudih va mīshavand. Va īn masāʾil-i mawhūmih nazd-i nās būdih va tā īn ẓuhūr kashf nashudih. Fa-lammā kharaqtum ḥijāba ḥurmati Allāh li-dhā kharaqa sitra ḥijābikum bi-anāmili al-qudrati wa-al-quwwah.
:::

::: {.translation}
Observe that He explicitly says that light is changed into fire. Thus the light you have assumed to be light has had its essential reality changed into fire, yet he is unaware, and in utter heedlessness has been and remains occupied with distorting the divine words. Do not understand His statement, “except at the Revelation of God,” to mean that light is not transformed before the Revelation. Yes, by His own Self, the True One, all except the Manifestation Himself have been and continue to be transformed. These imaginary notions existed among the people, and the matter had not been disclosed until this Revelation. But when you tore through the veil of God’s sanctity, He therefore tore away the covering of your veil with the fingers of power and might.
:::

### 659

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فرق اينست كه در حين ارتقاء مظهر احديّه برفيق اعلى الى ظهور بعد مشيّت ظاهره مشهود نه تا حكم نمايد اگر چه لازال انّه هو حىّ فى الأفق الأبهی و لكن چون بر حسب ظاهر احدى بر او عارف نه و كلّ نفوس از لقا ممنوع لذا حكم تبديل مستور تا حين ظهور چه كه در آن حين اگر نور اقلّ من آن توقّف نمايد در قول بلى حكم نار از منبع علم لدنّى الهى در حقّ او جارى چنانچه در ظهور قبل مشاهده شد و در اين ظهور هم ببصر ظاهر و باطن ديده ميشود كه نفوسى كه خود را نور ميناميدند عند اللّه حكم نار در حقّ آن نفوس جارى و لكن خود من غير شعور حركت مينمايند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Farq īnast kih dar ḥīn-i irtiqā-yi Maẓhar-i Aḥadīyyih bi-Rafīq-i Aʿlā ilā ẓuhūr-i baʿd Mashīyyat-i Ẓāhirih mashhūd nah tā ḥukm namāyad, agar-chih lā-zāl innahu huwa ḥayyun fī al-ufuq-i al-Abhā. Va lākin chūn bar ḥasab-i ẓāhir aḥadī bar ū ʿārif nah va kull-i nufūs az liqā mamnūʿ, li-dhā ḥukm-i tabdīl mastūr tā ḥīn-i ẓuhūr, chih kih dar ān ḥīn agar nūr aqall min ān tavaqquf namāyad dar qawl-i balā ḥukm-i nār az manbaʿ-i ʿilm-i ladunnī-yi ilāhī dar ḥaqq-i ū jārī, chunānchih dar ẓuhūr-i qabl mushāhidih shud va dar īn ẓuhūr ham bi-baṣar-i ẓāhir va bāṭin dīdih mīshavad kih nufūsī kih khud rā nūr mīnāmīdand ʿinda Allāh ḥukm-i nār dar ḥaqq-i ān nufūs jārī va lākin khud min ghayr-i shuʿūr ḥarakat mīnamāyand.
:::

::: {.translation}
The difference is that, from the time when the Manifestation of Oneness ascends to the Companion on high until the next Revelation, the manifest Will is not visibly present to pronounce judgment, although He is ever alive in the All-Glorious Horizon. But since outwardly no one knows Him and all souls are denied access to His presence, the judgment of transformation remains concealed until the time of the Revelation. At that time, if a light hesitates for less than an instant to say “Yes,” the judgment of fire is pronounced upon it from the source of innate divine knowledge. This was witnessed in the previous Revelation, and in this Revelation too it is seen with both the outward and the inward eye that souls who called themselves light are judged as fire in God’s sight, yet they themselves go about unaware.
:::

### 660

::: {.original lang="fa"}
در كلّ حين پناه بخدا برده كه از نفس ظهور محتجب نمانى چه كه مقصود بالذّات او بوده و خواهد بود او است آيه ليس كمثله شیء و او است آيه لم يلد و لم يولد بل مظاهر لم يلد و لم يولد خلق عنده ان انتم توقنون و لكن اينمقام را هر نفسى ادراك ننمايد الّا المنقطعون و هم فى عرفان منيع
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Dar koll-e ḥīn panāh be-Khodā borde ke az nafs-e ẓohūr moḥtajeb namānī, che ke maqṣūd be-dh-dhāt ū būde va khwāhad būd. Ū ast āye-ye laysa ka-mithlihi shayʾ, va ū ast āye-ye lam yalid wa-lam yūlad. Bal maẓāhir-i lam yalid wa-lam yūlad khalqun ʿindahu in antum tūqinūn. Va lāken īn maqām rā har nafsī edrāk nanamāyad illā al-munqaṭiʿūn wa-hum fī ʿirfānin manīʿ.
:::

::: {.translation}
At every moment, seek refuge in God, that you may not remain veiled from the Manifestation Himself, for He has always been and will ever be the One sought in His own right. He is the verse, “Nothing is like Him,” and He is the verse, “He neither begets nor is begotten.” Indeed, the manifestations of “He neither begets nor is begotten” are created beings in His sight, if you are certain. Yet not every soul can comprehend this station, but only those who are detached, who dwell in exalted understanding.
:::

### 661

::: {.original lang="fa"}
از اين جهت است كه نقطه مشيّت اوّلیّه روح ما سواه فداه در مقام ذكر حروفات و مرايا و نور و امثالها من اعلى مراتب الأسماء و الصّفات الى ان ينتهى الى ادنى رتبة الأشیآء ميفرمايند اينها از خود تحقّقى نداشته چون بشمس حقيقى مقابل شده‌اند اشراق تجلّيات لانهايه بر آنها شده در اينمقام ديده نميشود در آن مظاهر الّا اللّه ميفرمايد شما ناظر باسماء نباشيد بل بما يقوم به الأسماء ناظر شويد و هم‌چنين ما يقوم به الصّفات چه كه كلّ باقبالهم الى اللّه و بايمانهم باللّه باثواب بديعه منيعه اسماء مزيّن شده و ميشوند جمعى از حروفات ناميده ميشوند و جمعى از مرايا و جمعى از ادلّاء نوريّه وهم‌چنين از مظاهر جمال و جلال و حىّ و قديم و امثال آن از اسماء اللّه الحسنى تختلف ظهورات التّجلّى باعتباراتهم و استعداداتهم و الّا انّ التّجلّى واحد و المجلّى واحد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Az īn jahat ast ke Noqṭe-ye Mashiyyat-e Avvaliyye, rūḥ-e mā sevāh fedāh, dar maqām-e dhekr-e ḥorūfāt va marāyā va nūr va amthāl-e ānhā, min aʿlā marātib al-asmāʾ wa-l-ṣifāt ilā an yantahī ilā adnā rutbat al-ashyāʾ, mīfarmāyand īnhā az khod taḥaqqoqī nadāshte, chon be-shams-e ḥaqīqī moqābel shode-and eshrāq-e tajalliyāt-e lā-nehāye bar ānhā shode. Dar īn maqām dīde nemīshavad dar ān maẓāher illā Allāh. Mīfarmāyad shomā nāẓer be-asmā nabāshīd bal be-mā yaqūmu bihi al-asmāʾ nāẓer shavīd va ham-chenīn mā yaqūmu bihi al-ṣifāt, che ke koll bi-iqbālihim ilā Allāh va bi-īmānihim bi-Allāh be-athvāb-e badīʿe-ye manīʿe-ye asmā mozayyan shode va mīshavand. Jamʿī az ḥorūfāt nāmīde mīshavand va jamʿī az marāyā va jamʿī az adellā-ye nūriyye va ham-chenīn az maẓāher-e jamāl va jalāl va ḥayy va qadīm va amthāl-e ān az asmāʾ Allāh al-ḥusnā. Takhtalifu ẓuhūrāt al-tajallī bi-iʿtibārātihim wa-istiʿdādātihim wa-illā inna al-tajallī wāḥid wa-l-mujallī wāḥid.
:::

::: {.translation}
For this reason, the Point of the Primal Will—may the spirit of all besides Him be sacrificed for Him—when speaking of the Letters, the Mirrors, the Light, and the like, from the highest degrees of the names and attributes down to the lowest rank of things, states that these had no independent reality of their own. When they faced the true Sun, the radiance of infinite revelations shone upon them. In this station, nothing is seen in those manifestations but God. He says that you should look not to the names, but to that through which the names subsist, and likewise to that through which the attributes subsist. For all, through their turning to God and their faith in God, have been and are adorned with the wondrous, exalted robes of the names. Some are called Letters, some Mirrors, and some luminous Guides, and likewise manifestations of Beauty, Majesty, the Living, the Ancient, and other such most beautiful names of God. The manifestations of the revelation differ according to their respective conditions and capacities; otherwise, the revelation is one, and the One who reveals it is one.
:::

### 662

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و بصير خبير ادراك مينمايد كه كلّ اين اسماء نظر بآن ايمانى است كه در آنها بوده و هست وهم را بگذار ملاحظه در اوّل من آمن كن و هم‌چنين ثانى من آمن كه هيچ نفسى را بيان ازيد از اين دو نفس و ساير حروفات حىّ وصف نفرموده‌اند چنانچه در زيارتشان يا ساذج اللّه و يا كينونة اللّه و يا ذات اللّه و بامثال اين كلمات ذكر فرموده‌اند حال اگر اوّل من آمن نفس مذكور نبود و نفس ديگر بود البتّه اينمقام باو عنايت ميشد اگر در اين بحر متغمّس شوى ادراك مينمائى بعضى از اسرار محجّبه مقنّعه مستوره را و فرق شمس معانى را از ظلّش تميز ميدهى و مرتكب نميشوى آنچه را كه كلّ ذرّات بنوحه مشغولند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va baṣīr-e khabīr edrāk mīnamāyad ke koll-e īn asmā naẓar be-ān īmānī ast ke dar ānhā būde va hast. Vahm rā begoẕār, molāḥeẓe dar avval-e man āmana kon va ham-chenīn thānī-ye man āmana, ke hīch nafsī rā Bayān azyad az īn do nafs va sāyer-e Ḥorūfāt-e Ḥayy vaṣf nafarmūde-and, chenānche dar ziyārat-e shān yā sādhij Allāh va yā kaynūnat Allāh va yā dhāt Allāh va be-amthāl-e īn kalemāt dhekr farmūde-and. Ḥāl agar avval-e man āmana nafs-e madhkūr nabūd va nafs-e dīgar būd albatte īn maqām be-ū ʿenāyat mīshod. Agar dar īn baḥr motaghamm es shavī edrāk mīnamāʾī baʿẓī az asrār-e moḥajjabe-ye moqannaʿe-ye mastūre rā va farq-e shams-e maʿānī rā az ẓell-ash tamīz mīdehī va mortakeb nemīshavī ānche rā ke koll-e dharrāt be-nawḥe mashghūl-and.
:::

::: {.translation}
One who is discerning and well informed understands that all these names refer to the faith that has existed and continues to exist within them. Set aside illusion and consider the first to believe, and likewise the second to believe, for the Bayán has praised no souls more highly than these two and the other Letters of the Living. Thus, in their visitation prayers, He has addressed them as “O pure Essence of God,” “O Being of God,” and “O Essence of God,” and in similar words. Now, if the first to believe had not been the person in question, but someone else, this station would assuredly have been bestowed upon that other person. If you immerse yourself in this ocean, you will comprehend some of the veiled, shrouded, hidden mysteries, distinguish the Sun of inner meanings from its shadow, and refrain from committing that over which every atom is lamenting.
:::

### 663

::: {.original lang="fa"}
مثلا ملاحظه كن اگر ترابی‌ بيد مبارك اخذ فرمايد و بفرمايد كه اين قبضه خاك مسجود عالمين است حقّ لاريب فيه و هم‌چنين اگر صد قبضه خاك ديگر بردارد و درباره كلّ همين حكم را فرمايد جارى بوده و خواهد بود چه كه در اينمقام نظر بامر است كه از مصدر امر ظاهر شده نه بشىء من حيث هو شیء
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Mathalan molāḥeẓe kon agar torābī be-yad-e mobārak akhdh farmāyad va befarmāyad ke īn qabẓe khāk masjūd-e ʿālamīn ast, ḥaqqun lā rayba fīh. Va ham-chenīn agar ṣad qabẓe khāk-e dīgar bardārad va dar bāre-ye koll hamīn ḥokm rā farmāyad jārī būde va khwāhad būd, che ke dar īn maqām naẓar be-amr ast ke az maṣdar-e amr ẓāher shode na be-shayʾ min ḥaythu huwa shayʾ.
:::

::: {.translation}
Consider, for example: if He takes some dust in His blessed hand and declares that this handful of earth is the object before which all worlds bow down, it is true beyond any doubt. Likewise, if He takes a hundred other handfuls of earth and pronounces the same decree concerning them all, it has been and will remain in force. For in this station, regard is given to the command that has issued from the Source of command, not to a thing considered merely as a thing.
:::

### 664

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اينكه امثال آن نفوس محتجبه بذكر وصايت از ما يقوم به الوصىّ و فوقه من الولاية و النّبوّة و الرّسالة و الرّبوبيّة غافل شده‌اند اوّلا بدان فو‌اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو كه ابداً نقطه اولى بچنين كلمه مخصوص نفسى در بيان تكلّم نفرموده بلى يك توقيعى بميرزا سليمان التفات فرموده بودند در صدر آن توقيع كلمه بود كه جميع از خواندن آن عاجز شدند خود ميرزا سليمان در ایّام مراجعت از ماكو ميگفت اين لفظ وصايت است و بمن نوشته‌اند و او در سرّ سرّ اين ادّعاى اين رتبه مينمود و ايكاش شما باو متشبّث ميشديد در اين امر اوعندالله سزاوارتر است از اين نفسى كه باو تمسّك جسته‌ايد و ديگر همچه ذكرى ابداً نبوده مگر آنكه بعضى الواح نوشته‌اند و باسم نقطه اولى شهرت داده‌اند كلّها كذب بربّ البهآء
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īnke amthāl-e ān nofūs-e moḥtajebe be-dhekr-e veṣāyat az mā yaqūmu bihi al-waṣī wa-fawqahu min al-wilāya wa-l-nubuwwa wa-l-risāla wa-l-rubūbiyya ghāfel shode-and, avvalan bedān fa-wa-Allāh alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa ke abadan Noqṭe-ye Ūlā be-chenīn kaleme makhṣūṣ-e nafsī dar Bayān takallom nafarmūde. Balī yek tawqīʿī be-Mīrzā Solaymān eltefāt farmūde būdand. Dar ṣadr-e ān tawqīʿ kaleme būd ke jamīʿ az khwāndan-e ān ʿājez shodand. Khod-e Mīrzā Solaymān dar ayyām-e morājaʿat az Mākū mīgoft īn lafẓ veṣāyat ast va be-man neveshte-and va ū dar serr-e serr īn eddeʿā-ye īn rotbe mīnamūd. Va ey kāsh shomā be-ū motashabbeth mīshodīd dar īn amr. Ū ʿinda Allāh sazāvārtar ast az īn nafsī ke be-ū tamassok joste-īd. Va dīgar hamche dhekrī abadan nabūde magar ānke baʿẓī alvāḥ neveshte-and va be-nām-e Noqṭe-ye Ūlā shohrat dāde-and. Kulluhā kadhib bi-Rabb al-Bahāʾ.
:::

::: {.translation}
As for such veiled souls becoming heedless, through mention of successorship, of that through which the successor subsists, and of the higher degrees of guardianship, prophethood, messengership, and lordship: first, know—by God, besides whom there is no god—that the Primal Point never spoke such a word in the Bayán specifically concerning any individual. He did, however, graciously send a Tablet to Mírzá Sulaymán. At the beginning of that Tablet was a word that everyone was unable to read. Mírzá Sulaymán himself, during his return from Mákú, would say, “This word is ‘successorship,’ and He has written it to me.” In the utmost secrecy, he laid claim to this rank. Would that you had held fast to him in this matter! In God's sight, he is more deserving than the person to whom you have attached yourselves. There has never been any other such mention, except that some Tablets have been written and circulated in the name of the Primal Point. They are all false, by the Lord of Bahá!
:::

### 665

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ثانيا اين رتبه رتبه نيست كه بخواهيم از نفسى سلب نمائيم يا اثبات نمائيم چه كه آنچه فخر وصى است ان ما يقوم به الوصايه بوده و خواهد بود و بعد از انقطاع عند اللّه ذكر نداشته و نخواهد داشت چنانچه نقطهء اولى روح ما سواه فداه در اينمقام ميفرمايد قوله عزّ ذكره زيرا كه جوهر كلّ همان است كه آن محتجب مانده از چيزيكه وصىّ بآن وصىّ است نه اينست كه اين شأن وصايت را هم بشأن خاصّ نظر كنى بلكه ناظر شو بما يقوم به كه امر شجره حقيقت باشد كه اگر فرضا رسول خدا باسم وصايت نصب نميفرمود امروز ذكر بغير وصايت ميشد كلّ اينها از براى اين است كه در يوم ظهور باسماء محتجب نمانى بلكه نظر كنى بما يقوم به الأسماء من كلّ شیء حتّى ذكر النّبی‌ انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va thāniyan īn rotbe rotbe nīst ke bekhwāhīm az nafsī salb namāʾīm yā ethbāt namāʾīm, che ke ānche fakhr-e vaṣī ast inna mā yaqūmu bihi al-waṣāya būde va khwāhad būd va baʿd az enqeṭāʿ ʿinda Allāh dhekr nadāshte va nakhwāhad dāsht. Chenānche Noqṭe-ye Ūlā rūḥ-e mā sevāh fedāh dar īn maqām mīfarmāyad, qawluhu ʿazza dhikruhu: zīrā ke jawhar-e koll hamān ast ke ān moḥtajeb mānde az chīzī ke vaṣī be-ān vaṣī ast. Na īn ast ke īn shaʾn-e veṣāyat rā ham be-shaʾn-e khāṣṣ naẓar konī balke nāẓer shaw be-mā yaqūmu bihi ke amr-e Shajare-ye Ḥaqīqat bāshad, ke agar farẓan Rasūl-e Khodā be-nām-e veṣāyat naṣb nemīfarmūd emrūz dhekr be-ghayr-e veṣāyat mīshod. Koll-e īnhā az barā-ye īn ast ke dar yawm-e ẓohūr be-asmā moḥtajeb namānī balke naẓar konī be-mā yaqūmu bihi al-asmāʾ min kulli shayʾ ḥattā dhikr al-Nabī. Intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
Second, this rank is not a rank that We would wish either to take away from someone or to affirm for someone. For the glory of the successor has always been and will ever be that through which successorship subsists; once severed from it, he has had and will have no standing before God. Thus the Primal Point—may the spirit of all besides Him be sacrificed for Him—states in this connection, His words, exalted be His mention: “For the essence of the whole matter is precisely this: he has remained veiled from that by which the successor is a successor. It is not that you should regard even this station of successorship as a special distinction; rather, look to that through which it subsists, which is the command of the Tree of Truth. For if, hypothetically, the Messenger of God had not appointed him under the name of successorship, today he would be spoken of by a name other than successorship. All this is so that, on the Day of Manifestation, you may not remain veiled by names, but may instead look to that through which the names of all things subsist, even the designation ‘Prophet.’” End of quotation.
:::

### 666

::: {.original lang="fa"}
حال قدرى تفكّر نما تا عارف شوى كه كلّ بامر او معزّزند و بذكر او مفتخر و اين شأن صادق است ماداميكه از حدّ خود تجاوز ننمايند و در حين بعث امر اوّلیّه كلّ اين اسامى از مسمّيات خود خارج و بملكوت راجع اگر ثانيا امر مبرم نازل يصدق عليهم كلّ الأسماء من اسماء اللّه الحسنى و الّا يرجعن الى مقرّهم قبل ان يقول لم او بم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ḥāl qadrī tafakkor namā tā ʿāref shavī ke koll be-amr-e ū moʿazzaz-and va be-dhekr-e ū moftakher va īn shaʾn ṣādeq ast mādāmī ke az ḥadd-e khod tajāvoz nanamāyand. Va dar ḥīn-e baʿth-e amr-e avvaliyye koll-e īn asāmī az mosammayāt-e khod khārej va be-malakūt rājeʿ. Agar thāniyan amr-e mobram nāzel, yaṣduqu ʿalayhim kull al-asmāʾ min asmāʾ Allāh al-ḥusnā, wa-illā yarjiʿna ilā maqarrihim qabla an yaqūla lima aw bima.
:::

::: {.translation}
Now reflect a little, that you may recognize that all are exalted through His command and honored through His mention. This condition holds true so long as they do not overstep their bounds. At the raising up of the primal Cause, all these names are withdrawn from those who bear them and return to the Kingdom. If a binding command descends anew, all the most beautiful names of God apply to them; otherwise, they return to their abode before one can say “Why?” or “By what?”
:::

### 667

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بارى نظر از اين تحديدات بردار و بآن نقطه ساريه در كلّشیء ناظر شو و آن نقطه را موهوم مدان چنانچه از قبل كلّ عباد بتوهّمات مانده و الى حين عارف نشده و نخواهند شد الّا من شآء ربّك و همين ميرزا يحيى كه بواسطه او از حقّ معرض شده بين يدى مثل يكى از خدّام حاضر بوده و القاى كلمات اللّه بر او ميشد چنانچه حال جمعى تلقاء وجه حاضرند بهمان قسم بر ايشان القاء ميشود در كلّ ليالى و ایّام و لكن فرق است كه آن نفس مغرور چون دو كلمه از لسانش جارى شد ارتكب ما لا ارتكب مظاهر النّفى كلّها و لكن اين نفوس حاضره تلقاء وجه بابدع كلمات ناطق و مع‌ذلك ليس لهم من امر الّا بعد اذنه كذلك كان الأمر ان انت من العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bārī naẓar az īn taḥdīdāt bardār va be-ān noqṭe-ye sāriye dar koll-e shayʾ nāẓer shaw va ān noqṭe rā mawhūm madān, chenānche az qabl koll-e ʿebād be-tavahhomāt mānde va ilā ḥīn ʿāref nashode va nakhwāhand shod illā man shāʾa Rabbuka. Va hamīn Mīrzā Yaḥyā ke be-vāseṭe-ye ū az Ḥaqq moʿreẓ shode, bayna yaday mithl-e yekī az khoddām ḥāẓer būde va elqā-ye kalemāt-e Allāh bar ū mīshod, chenānche ḥāl jamʿī telqāʾ-e vajh ḥāẓer-and, be-hamān qesm bar īshān elqā mīshavad dar koll-e layālī va ayyām. Va lāken farq ast ke ān nafs-e maghrūr chon do kaleme az lesān-ash jārī shod irtakaba mā lā irtakaba maẓāhir al-nafy kulluhā, va lāken īn nofūs-e ḥāẓere telqāʾ-e vajh be-abdaʿ-e kalemāt nāṭeq va maʿa dhālik laysa lahum min amrin illā baʿda idhnihi. Kadhālika kāna al-amr in anta min al-ʿālimīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
In short, turn your gaze away from these limitations and look to that Point which pervades all things. Do not regard that Point as imaginary, as all the servants of former times remained caught in imaginings and, to this day, have not attained recognition and never will, except those whom your Lord wills. This very Mírzá Yaḥyá, on whose account you have turned away from the True One, used to stand in My presence like one of the attendants, and the words of God were imparted to him, just as a number of people now stand before My face and receive them in the same manner every night and day. The difference, however, is that when a mere two words flowed from the tongue of that deluded soul, he committed what all the manifestations of negation had never committed. These souls now present before My face, by contrast, utter the most wondrous words, yet undertake nothing without His permission. Such has been the matter, if you are among those who know.
:::

### 668

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اگرچه كلمات مشركين در قلبت مقرّ گرفته و محو آن مشكل مگر آنكه از اين سلسبيل عنايت كه در عيون كلمات بنفس كلمات جارى و سارى است بياشامى كذلك نبّأناك و اخبرناك و قصصناك ما كنت محتجباً عنه لعلّ تخرق الأحجاب بقدرة ربّك العزيز الوهّاب و تشهد ما لا شهدته من قبل و تعرف ما كنت غافلاً عنه و لكن لن توفّق بذلك الّا بأن تنقطع عما خلق بين السّموات و الأرض و تتوجّه الى اللّه الملك المقتدر العزيز المختار
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Agarche kalemāt-e moshrekīn dar qalb-at maqarr gerefte va maḥv-e ān moshkel magar ānke az īn salsabīl-e ʿenāyat ke dar ʿoyūn-e kalemāt be-nafs-e kalemāt jārī va sārī ast biyāshāmī. Kadhālika nabbaʾnāka wa-akhbarnāka wa-qaṣaṣnāka mā kunta muḥtajiban ʿanhu laʿalla takhruqa al-aḥjāb bi-qudrati Rabbika al-ʿAzīz al-Wahhāb wa-tashhada mā lā shahidtahu min qablu wa-taʿrifa mā kunta ghāfilan ʿanhu. Wa-lākin lan tuwaffaqa bi-dhālika illā bi-an tanqaṭiʿa ʿammā khuliqa bayna al-samāwāt wa-l-arḍ wa-tatawajjaha ilā Allāh al-Malik al-Muqtadir al-ʿAzīz al-Mukhtār.
:::

::: {.translation}
Although the words of those who associate partners with God have lodged in your heart, and it is difficult to efface them unless you drink from this Salsabíl of loving-kindness that flows and courses through the wellsprings of the words by means of the words themselves. Thus have We told you, informed you, and recounted to you what you were veiled from, that you may rend the veils through the power of your Lord, the Almighty, the All-Bountiful, witness what you have never witnessed before, and recognize what you were heedless of. Yet you will not succeed in this unless you detach yourself from all that has been created between the heavens and the earth and turn toward God, the King, the All-Powerful, the Almighty, the One who chooses.
:::

### 669

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اى عباد در عرفان اين ظهور بكلمات و اشارات معرضين و تصديق و تكذيب آن نفوس متمسّك نشويد و باصل امر ناظر شويد چه كه اكثرى از ناس لم‌يزل و لايزال محتجب و متوهّم مشاهده شده و ميشوند و رؤساى عصر نظر باستحكام رياست خود ناس را از شطر احديّه و عرفان آيات اللّه ممنوع و مأيوس نموده ‌و خواهند نمود مثلاً ملاحظه در ظهور نقطه فرقان نما كه آنحضرت بآيات اللّه ظاهر شدند و در فرقان حجّت و برهان جز آيات نازل نشده مع‌ذلك بعد از ارتقاى نقطه فرقان برفيق اعلى و انقطاع روايح رحمن امر بدست علماء افتاد و آن نفوس بالمرّه ناس را از عرفان آيات منع نموده‌كه شما آيات اللّه را ادراك نمينمائيد و علم آن نزد ما است باينجهت حجّيت آيات از ميان رفت و زمام خلق بدست آن نفوس آمد و ناس را باوهامى تربيت نمودند كه ذكر آن ممكن نه چنانچه ديده و شنيده‌ايد و آياتيكه در ظهور بعد و قيامت و امثال آن نازل شده جميع را بهواى خود تفسير نمودند و ناس هم متابعت آن نفوس را من حيث لايشعر نموده ‌تا آنكه امر بمقامى رسيد كه ضرّ آن اوهام جميع بشجره ظهور بعد وارد شد و
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ey ʿebād, dar ʿerfān-e īn ẓohūr be-kalemāt va eshārāt-e moʿreẓīn va taṣdīq va takdhīb-e ān nofūs motamassek nashavīd va be-aṣl-e amr nāẓer shavīd, che ke aktharī az nās lam-yazal va lā-yazāl moḥtajeb va motavahhem moshāhede shode va mīshavand va roʾasā-ye ʿaṣr naẓar be-esteḥkām-e reyāsat-e khod nās rā az shaṭr-e aḥadiyye va ʿerfān-e āyāt-e Allāh mamnūʿ va maʾyūs namūde va khwāhand namūd. Mathalan molāḥeẓe dar ẓohūr-e Noqṭe-ye Forqān namā ke ān Ḥaẓrat be-āyāt-e Allāh ẓāher shodand va dar Forqān ḥojjat va borhān joz āyāt nāzel nashode. Maʿa dhālik baʿd az erteqā-ye Noqṭe-ye Forqān be-Rafīq-e Aʿlā va enqeṭāʿ-e ravāyeḥ-e Raḥmān amr be-dast-e ʿolamā oftād va ān nofūs be-l-marre nās rā az ʿerfān-e āyāt manʿ namūde ke shomā āyāt-e Allāh rā edrāk nemīnamāʾīd va ʿelm-e ān nazd-e mā ast. Be-īn jahat ḥojjiyyat-e āyāt az miyān raft va zemām-e khalq be-dast-e ān nofūs āmad va nās rā be-awhāmī tarbiyat namūdand ke dhekr-e ān momken na, chenānche dīde va shenīde-īd. Va āyātī ke dar ẓohūr-e baʿd va qiyāmat va amthāl-e ān nāzel shode jamīʿ rā be-havā-ye khod tafsīr namūdand va nās ham motābaʿat-e ān nofūs rā min ḥaythu lā yashʿur namūde tā ānke amr be-maqāmī resīd ke ẓorr-e ān awhām jamīʿ be-Shajare-ye Ẓohūr-e baʿd vāred shod va
:::

::: {.translation}
O servants! In seeking to recognize this Revelation, do not cling to the words and allusions of those who turn away, or to those souls' affirmations and denials. Look instead to the foundation of the Cause itself, for most people have always been and continue to be seen veiled and deluded. The leaders of the age, intent on consolidating their own authority, have barred people from the realm of oneness and the recognition of God's verses, and have deprived them of hope, and will continue to do so. Consider, for example, the Revelation of the Point of the Qur'an: He appeared with the verses of God, and in the Qur'an no proof or testimony was revealed other than the verses. Nevertheless, after the Point of the Qur'an ascended to the Companion on high and the fragrances of the All-Merciful ceased, the matter fell into the hands of the learned. Those souls completely barred people from recognizing the verses, saying, “You cannot comprehend the verses of God; knowledge of them rests with us.” Thus the evidentiary authority of the verses disappeared, the reins of the people passed into those souls' hands, and they instructed people in imaginings that cannot be recounted, as you have seen and heard. They interpreted all the verses revealed concerning the next Manifestation, the Resurrection, and the like according to their own desires. The people, too, followed those souls unawares, until matters reached the point where all the harm of those imaginings befell the Tree of the next Revelation, and
:::

### 670

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بعد از ظهور موعود در سنه ستّين مجدّدا ارياح فضل وزيد و سموات علم مرتفع شد و ارض عرفان منبسط و آيات اللّه از سماء مشيّت نازل و لكن نظر باوهام قبل ناس در حجيّت آيات توقّف نموده‌كه ما ادراك نمينمائيم و حال آنكه حقّ جلّ ذكره اعظم و اكرم و ارحم از آن است كه مظهر نفس خود را بفرستد و جميع را بعرفان او كه نفس عرفان اللّه است امر فرمايد و مع‌ذلك حجّتى بفرستد فوق ادراك ناس سبحانه عن ذلك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Baʿd az ẓohūr-e Mawʿūd dar sane-ye settīn mojaddadan aryāḥ-e faẓl vazīd va samavāt-e ʿelm mortafeʿ shod va arẓ-e ʿerfān monbaseṭ va āyāt-e Allāh az samā-ye mashiyyat nāzel. Va lāken naẓar be-awhām-e qabl nās dar ḥojjiyyat-e āyāt tavaqqof namūde ke mā edrāk nemīnamāʾīm, va ḥāl ānke Ḥaqq jalla dhikruhu aʿẓam va akram va arḥam az ān ast ke maẓhar-e nafs-e khod rā beferestad va jamīʿ rā be-ʿerfān-e ū ke nafs-e ʿerfān-e Allāh ast amr farmāyad va maʿa dhālik ḥojjatī beferestad fawq-e edrāk-e nās. Subḥānahu ʿan dhālik.
:::

::: {.translation}
After the appearance of the Promised One in the year sixty, the winds of grace blew anew, the heavens of knowledge were raised, the earth of recognition was spread out, and the verses of God descended from the heaven of His will. Yet, because of their former imaginings, people hesitated to acknowledge the evidentiary authority of the verses, saying, “We do not comprehend them.” The True One—exalted be His mention—is, however, far too great, generous, and merciful to send the Manifestation of His own Self, command everyone to recognize Him, which is itself the recognition of God, and yet send a proof beyond people's comprehension. Far exalted is He above such a thing!
:::

### 671

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بالأخرة باوهام انفس خود مشغول و محجوب بشأنيكه بآيات اللّه كفايت ننموده‌مع آنكه نصّ فرقان است او لم يكفهم انّا انزلنا عليك الكتاب و جميع مستدلّ باينكه ادراك آيات فوق عقول و عرفان ما است امر ديگر بايد ظاهر شود قد غيّروا نعمة اللّه و حجّته و ارادوا بغير ما اراد اللّه لذا اكثر اعراض نموده‌ بهاويه راجع شدند و هر چه اعراض مشركين شدّت نمود آن شمس معانى محكم‌تر حجّيت آيات را نازل فرمودند بشأنيكه كلّ حجّت و برهان را منحصر بآيات نمودند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Be-l-ākhare be-awhām-e anfos-e khod mashghūl va maḥjūb be-shaʾnī ke be-āyāt-e Allāh kefāyat nanamūde, maʿa ānke naṣṣ-e Forqān ast a-wa-lam yakfihim annā anzalnā ʿalayka al-kitāb, va jamīʿ mostadell be-īnke edrāk-e āyāt fawq-e ʿoqūl va ʿerfān-e mā ast, amr-e dīgar bāyad ẓāher shavad. Qad ghayyarū niʿmata Allāh wa-ḥujjatahu wa-arādū bi-ghayri mā arāda Allāh. Le-dhā akthar eʿrāẓ namūde be-hāviye rājeʿ shodand va har che eʿrāẓ-e moshrekīn sheddat namūd ān Shams-e Maʿānī moḥkamtar ḥojjiyyat-e āyāt rā nāzel farmūdand be-shaʾnī ke koll-e ḥojjat va borhān rā monḥaṣer be-āyāt namūdand.
:::

::: {.translation}
In the end, they were so absorbed in and veiled by their own imaginings that they did not regard the verses of God as sufficient, even though the explicit text of the Qur'an states, “Is it not enough for them that We have sent down to you the Book?” All argued, “Comprehension of the verses is beyond our reason and understanding; something else must appear.” They altered God's blessing and His proof, and desired something other than what God desired. Thus most turned away and returned to the abyss. The more fiercely those who associated partners with God turned away, the more firmly that Sun of inner meanings revealed the evidentiary authority of the verses, to the point that He confined all proof and testimony to the verses alone.
:::

### 672

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و رغماً لأنف المشركين اين آيه از سماء احديّة نازل لو ارادت نملة ان يتصرّف فى القرآن و باطنه و باطن باطنه فى حكم سواد عينيها لتقدر لانّ سرّ الصّمدانيّة و تجلّى الأحدانيّة قد تلجلجت فى كلّ شیء و اين آيه نازل كه جميع مستشعر شوند كه ابواب رحمت و عنايت مسدود نيست هر نفسى مقبل شود و الى اللّه توجّه نمايد حجيّت آيات اللّه را بنفس آيه ادراك مينمايد و ادراك آن مقام بعلوم ظاهره منوط نبوده و نخواهد بود بلكه بنفوس زكيّه و قلوب طاهره مقبله منوط طوبی‌ للمقبلين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va raghman li-anfi l-mushrikīn īn āyih az samā-yi aḥadiyyat nāzil: law arādat namlatun an yataṣarrafa fī l-Qurʾān wa-bāṭinihi wa-bāṭini bāṭinihi fī ḥukmi sawādi ʿaynayhā la-taqdiru li-anna sirra l-ṣamadāniyya wa-tajalliya l-aḥadāniyya qad talajlajat fī kulli shayʾ. Va īn āyih nāzil kih jamīʿ mustashʿir shavand kih abvāb-i raḥmat va ʿināyat masdūd nīst. Har nafsī muqbil shavad va ila Allāh tavajjuh namāyad ḥujjiyyat-i āyāt-i Allāh rā bi-nafs-i āyih idrāk mīnamāyad va idrāk-i ān maqām bi-ʿulūm-i ẓāhirih manūṭ nabūdih va nakhvāhad būd balkih bi-nufūs-i zakiyyih va qulūb-i ṭāhirih-yi muqbilih manūṭ. Ṭūbā li-l-muqbilīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
And despite those who associate partners with God, this verse descended from the heaven of oneness: “If an ant wished to exercise power over the Qur’an, its inner meaning, and the inner meaning of its inner meaning, as over the black of its own eyes, it would be able to do so, for the mystery of self-sufficiency and the revelation of oneness have stirred within every thing.” This verse was revealed so that all might realize that the doors of mercy and loving care are not closed. Whoever turns toward God perceives the evidentiary authority of the verses of God through the verse itself. Understanding this station has never depended, nor will it ever depend, on outward learning; rather, it depends on pure souls and unsullied hearts turned toward Him. Blessed are those who turn toward Him.
:::

### 673

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و هم‌چنين آن ساذج معانى حجبات و اوهاميكه از قبل بود و ناس بآن محتجب و متوهّم جميع را خرق نمودند و بافق انّنى انا حىّ فى الأفق الأبهی راجع شدند حال جمعى انفس موهومه لاثبات رياست و حفظ آن اراده نموده‌اند اوّلا حجيّت آيات را از بيان محو نمايند و در اين فقره بسيار سعى نموده‌ و مينمايند و بتمام مكر و حيله در اين امر مشغولند و لكن ابی‌ اللّه الّا ان يثبت آياته بالحقّ و لو تنكرها المشركون و حال در نفاق بمقامى رسيده‌اند كه اگر نفسى بحجيّت آيات متكلّم شود باو استهزاء و سخريه مينمايند بعينه مثل ملل قبل بل هؤلآء اشدّ جهلا و اكبر نفاقاً لو انتم تعرفون
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va ham-chunīn ān sādhij-i maʿānī ḥujubāt va avhāmī kih az qabl būd va nās bi-ān muḥtajib va mutavahhim jamīʿ rā kharq namūdand va bi-ufuq-i innanī anā ḥayyun fī l-ufuqi l-abhā rājiʿ shudand. Ḥāl jamʿī anfus-i mawhūmih li-ithbāt-i riyāsat va ḥifẓ-i ān irādih namūdih-and avvalan ḥujjiyyat-i āyāt rā az Bayān maḥv namāyand va dar īn fiqrih bisyār saʿy namūdih va mīnamāyand va bi-tamām-i makr va ḥīlih dar īn amr mashghūland va lākin abā Allāhu illā an yuthbita āyātihi bi-l-ḥaqq wa-law tunkiruhā l-mushrikūn. Va ḥāl dar nifāq bi-maqāmī rasīdih-and kih agar nafsī bi-ḥujjiyyat-i āyāt mutakallim shavad bi-ū istihzā va sukhriyyih mīnamāyand bi-ʿaynih mithl-i milal-i qabl bal hāʾulāʾi ashaddu jahlan va akbaru nifāqan law antum taʿrifūn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Likewise, that Quintessence of meanings tore through all the veils and imaginings that had existed before and by which people had been veiled and deluded, and returned to the horizon of “Indeed, I am alive in the all-glorious horizon.” Now a number of deluded souls, intent on establishing and preserving their leadership, have resolved first to erase from the Bayán the evidentiary authority of the verses. They have striven greatly in this matter and continue to do so, employing every trick and stratagem. But God refuses to do anything other than establish His verses in truth, even though those who associate partners with Him deny them. Their hypocrisy has now reached such a degree that if anyone speaks of the evidentiary authority of the verses, they ridicule and mock him, exactly like the religious communities of the past. Indeed, these people are more ignorant and greater in hypocrisy, if you only knew.
:::

### 674

::: {.original lang="fa"}
لازال عرفان منبسطه الهيّه را نفوس محتجبه محدود نموده‌اند و باين جهت اكثر عباد از فيوضات رحمانى و عنايات ربّانى محروم مانده‌اند چنانچه نفس ملقى يومى از ایّام استهزاء على نقطة البيان ذكر مينمود كه فرموده‌اند كه احدى بر اتيان يك آيه قادر نه و حال آنكه مى بينيم كه بعضى نفوس قادرند كه دو كلمه آيات تكلّم نمايند پس از اين قرار اين نفوس هم حقّ خواهند بود فو‌اللّه من وجد رايحة رضوان المعانى ليعرف من هذه الكلمة كفره و نفاقه و بغيه و اعتراضه على كلّ النّبيين و المرسلين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Lāzāl ʿirfān-i munbasiṭih-yi ilāhiyyih rā nufūs-i muḥtajibih maḥdūd namūdih-and va bi-īn jihat akthar-i ʿibād az fuyūḍāt-i raḥmānī va ʿināyāt-i rabbānī maḥrūm māndih-and. Chunānchih nafs-i mulqī yawmī az ayyām istihzāʾan ʿalā Nuqṭati l-Bayān dhikr mīnamūd kih farmūdih-and kih aḥadī bar ityān-i yik āyih qādir nah va ḥāl ānkih mībīnīm kih baʿḍī nufūs qādirand kih du kalimih āyāt takallum namāyand pas az īn qarār īn nufūs ham Ḥaqq khvāhand būd. Fa-wa-Allāhi man wajada rāʾiḥata Riḍwāni l-maʿānī la-yaʿrifu min hādhihi l-kalimati kufrahu wa-nifāqahu wa-baghyahu wa-iʿtirāḍahu ʿalā kulli l-nabiyyīn wa-l-mursalīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Veiled souls have always confined the all-embracing knowledge of God, and for this reason most people have remained deprived of the outpourings of the All-Merciful and the loving care of the Lord. Thus, one day, the very person who put this notion forward said in mockery of the Point of the Bayán: “He has stated that no one is capable of producing a single verse, yet we see that some people are able to utter two words of verses. On this basis, these people too would be the True One.” By God, anyone who has caught the fragrance of the paradise of meanings will recognize from this statement his unbelief, hypocrisy, rebellion, and opposition to all the Prophets and Messengers.
:::

### 675

::: {.original lang="fa"}
مشاهده شد كه ابداً از كوثر معانى مرزوق نشده و از رضوان معنوى الهى بغايت محروم مانده چه كه اين بسى واضح است كه مقصود حضرت از اين بيان چه بوده و كلمه حقّ اگر چه بحرفين باشد سلطان كلمات اهل ارض بوده وخواهد بود و اللّه از نفحات همان كلمه وحده عارفين نفحات حقّ را مييابند و برضوانش توجّه مينمايند ملاحظه نما كه اگر از شطّ عذب فرات كاسى اخذ شود صاحبان ذايقه ادراك مينمايند كه اين ماء از كدام منبع بوده و از عذوبت او پى‌برند بمنبع او و حال آنكه بحسب ظاهر يك كاس ماء بوده و چون منبع علم و عرفان و عنايت و مكرمت و فضل و قدرت و جلال و عظمت جارى و سارى است لذا از آن كلمه مخلصين و مقرّبين ادراك مينمايند و بمنبع آن پى‌ميبرند كذلك فصّل لك لعلّ تهتدى بهدى اللّه ربّك و لاتلتفت الى جنود الشّياطين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Mushāhidih shud kih abadan az kawthar-i maʿānī marzūq nashudih va az Riḍvān-i maʿnavī-yi ilāhī bi-ghāyat maḥrūm māndih chih kih īn basī vāḍiḥ ast kih maqṣūd-i Ḥaḍrat az īn bayān chih būdih va kalimih-yi Ḥaqq agar chih bi-ḥarfayn bāshad sulṭān-i kalimāt-i ahl-i arḍ būdih va khvāhad būd. Va-Allāh az nafaḥāt-i hamān kalimih vaḥdih ʿārifīn nafaḥāt-i Ḥaqq rā mīyāband va bi-Riḍvānash tavajjuh mīnamāyand. Mulāḥiẓih namā kih agar az shaṭṭ-i ʿadhb-i furāt kāsī akhdh shavad ṣāḥibān-i dhāʾiqih idrāk mīnamāyand kih īn māʾ az kudām manbaʿ būdih va az ʿudhūbat-i ū pay barand bi-manbaʿ-i ū va ḥāl ānkih bi-ḥasab-i ẓāhir yik kās-i māʾ būdih va chūn manbaʿ-i ʿilm va ʿirfān va ʿināyat va makramat va faḍl va qudrat va jalāl va ʿaẓamat jārī va sārī ast lidhā az ān kalimih mukhliṣīn va muqarrabīn idrāk mīnamāyand va bi-manbaʿ-i ān pay mībarand. Kadhālika faṣṣala laka laʿalla tahtadī bi-hudā Allāhi rabbika wa-lā taltafit ilā junūdi l-shayāṭīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
It became evident that he had never been nourished by the heavenly waters of meanings and had remained utterly deprived of the divine paradise of spiritual understanding, for what His Holiness intended by this statement is abundantly clear. The word of the True One, even if it consists of only two letters, has always been and will always be sovereign over the words of the people of the earth. By God, from the fragrance of that word alone, those endowed with understanding perceive the fragrances of the True One and turn toward His paradise. Consider: if a cup is drawn from a sweet, refreshing river, those with a sense of taste perceive the source of this water and recognize its source from its sweetness, although outwardly it is only a cup of water. And since the wellspring of knowledge, recognition, loving care, generosity, grace, power, glory, and grandeur flows and pervades all things, the sincere and those brought near perceive through that word and recognize its source. Thus He has explained it to you, so that you may be guided by the guidance of God, your Lord, and pay no heed to the hosts of devils.
:::

### 676

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اگر نفسى دو كلمه بگويد و در كلمه سيّم معطّل ماند مبرهن است كه از اين منبع جاريه ساريه نبوده و نخواهد بود فو‌اللّه يا عبد حقّ بجميع شئونش از دونش ممتاز بوده و خواهد بود بر خود مشتبه مكن ميخواهى تجربه كن بين يدى حاضر شو و يك آيه از آيات اللّه سؤال نما اذا تطّلع ببحر الّذى يتموّج بذاته لذاته و لم يكن لامواجه من نفاد و تطّلع بمكمن المعانى و العرفان و مخزن العلم و الحكمة و تكون من الموقنين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va agar nafsī du kalimih bigūyad va dar kalimih-yi siyyum muʿaṭṭal mānad mubarhan ast kih az īn manbaʿ-i jāriyih-yi sāriyih nabūdih va nakhvāhad būd. Fa-wa-Allāh yā ʿAbd Ḥaqq bi-jamīʿ-i shuʾūnash az dūnash mumtāz būdih va khvāhad būd. Bar khud mushtabih makun mīkhvāhī tajribih kun bayna yaday ḥāḍir shaw va yik āyih az āyāt-i Allāh suʾāl namā. Idhan taṭṭaliʿ bi-baḥri lladhī yatamawwaju bi-dhātihi li-dhātihi wa-lam yakun li-amwājihi min nafād wa-taṭṭaliʿ bi-makmani l-maʿānī wa-l-ʿirfān wa-makhzani l-ʿilmi wa-l-ḥikma wa-takūnu mina l-mūqinīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
If someone utters two words but is at a loss for a third, it is evident that these have not come, nor will they ever come, from this flowing, all-pervading wellspring. By God, O servant, the True One has always been and will always be distinguished from all others in every aspect of His being. Do not confuse the matter for yourself. If you wish, put it to the test: enter My presence and ask for a single verse of the verses of God. Then you will behold the ocean that surges of itself and for itself, whose waves have no end, and you will discover the sanctuary of meanings and recognition and the treasury of knowledge and wisdom, and be among those who are certain.
:::

### 677

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اين ظهور اعظم را چون نقطه بيان جلّ كبريائه مخصوص در جميع بيان فرموده بآيات ظاهر ميشود لذا بآيات ظاهر شده و الّا كلّ ما ظهر من عنده حجّة على العالمين در اين ظهور اعظم جميع آيات قدرتيّه و آفاقيّه و انفسيّه مشاهده شده و لاينكرها الّا كلّ مغلّ مكّار
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īn Ẓuhūr-i Aʿẓam rā chūn Nuqṭih-yi Bayān jalla kibriyāʾuhu makhṣūṣ dar jamīʿ-i Bayān farmūdih bi-āyāt ẓāhir mīshavad lidhā bi-āyāt ẓāhir shudih va illā kullu mā ẓahara min ʿindihi ḥujjatun ʿalā l-ʿālamīn. Dar īn Ẓuhūr-i Aʿẓam jamīʿ-i āyāt-i qudratiyyih va āfāqiyyih va anfusiyyih mushāhidih shudih va-lā yunkiruhā illā kullu mughillin makkār.
:::

::: {.translation}
Since the Point of the Bayán—exalted be His majesty—specifically stated throughout the Bayán that this Most Great Revelation would appear through verses, it has therefore appeared through verses. Otherwise, everything that has appeared from Him is a proof to all the worlds. In this Most Great Revelation, all the signs of power, all the signs in the world and within human souls, have been witnessed, and none denies them except the treacherous and deceitful.
:::

### 678

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بر هر نفسى اليوم لازم كه از انفس خبيثه مشركه اجتناب نمايد چه كه بمكرى ظاهر شده‌اند كه در ابداع شبه آن ممكن نه چنانچه از ارض صاد بجناب اسم اللّه آقاسيّد مهدى عليه بهآء اللّه نوشته‌اند كه امّ الفواحش و الخطيئات مكتوبی‌ باين ارض فرستاده مضمون آنكه در بيت ايشان لوحى مدفون بوده از خطّ حضرت اعلى و من آن لوح را بيرون آورده‌ام و در آن لوح عباراتى مسطور و نسبت بنقطه اولى داده كه بطلعت ابهى در سفارش ميرزا يحيى نوشته‌‌اند فو‌اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو كلّ متحيّر مانديم از جعل اين نفوس و مكر اين قوم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bar har nafsī al-yawm lāzim kih az anfus-i khabīthih-yi mushrikih ijtināb namāyad chih kih bi-makrī ẓāhir shudih-and kih dar ibdāʿ shibh-i ān mumkin nah. Chunānchih az arḍ-i Ṣād bi-janāb-i Ismuʾllāh Āqā Siyyid Mahdī ʿalayhi Bahāʾuʾllāh nivishtih-and kih Umm-i l-Fawāḥish va-l-Khaṭīʾāt maktūbī bi-īn arḍ firistādih maḍmūn ānkih dar bayt-i īshān lawḥī madfūn būdih az khaṭṭ-i Ḥaḍrat-i Aʿlā va man ān lawḥ rā bīrūn āvardih-am va dar ān lawḥ ʿibārātī masṭūr va nisbat bi-Nuqṭih-yi Ūlā dādih kih bi-Ṭalʿat-i Abhā dar sifārish-i Mīrzā Yaḥyā nivishtih-and. Fa-wa-Allāhi lladhī lā ilāha illā huwa kull mutaḥayyir māndīm az jaʿl-i īn nufūs va makr-i īn qawm.
:::

::: {.translation}
Today everyone must avoid these wicked souls who associate partners with God, for they have appeared with a deceit whose like is impossible in creation. Thus, a letter has been written from the land of Ṣád to His Honor Ismu’lláh, Áqá Siyyid Mahdí—may the glory of God rest upon him—reporting that the Mother of Abominations and Sins has sent a letter to that land. Its purport is that a Tablet in the handwriting of His Holiness the Most Exalted had been buried in their house, and that “I have brought that Tablet out.” In that Tablet, certain passages are inscribed and attributed to the Primal Point, purportedly written to the All-Glorious Beauty in commendation of Mírzá Yaḥyá. By God, besides whom there is no other god, we were all astonished at the fabrications of these souls and the deceit of these people.
:::

### 679

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و بعد از مصدر امر حكم شده كه بروند و باو بگويند كه آن لوح را از كدام محلّ بيت بيرون آورده و بنما لعلّ تتنبّه فى نفسها و تكون من التّائبات باين شدّت بر افترا قيام نموده‌اند و اين امور دستور‌العملى است كه ميرزا يحيى از اينجا مينويسد و ميفرستد لعنة اللّه على الكاذبين و المفترين اذا يتبرّء منهم نقطة البيان فى عرش الجنان و يقول خسرانا لكم يا ملأ المشركين و نارا عليكم يا ملأ المغرضين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va baʿd az maṣdar-i amr ḥukm shudih kih biravand va bi-ū bigūyand kih ān lawḥ rā az kudām maḥall-i bayt bīrūn āvardih va binamā laʿalla tatanabbahu fī nafsihā va takūnu mina l-tāʾibāt. Bi-īn shiddat bar iftirā qiyām namūdih-and va īn umūr dastūr al-ʿamalī ast kih Mīrzā Yaḥyā az īnjā mīnivīsad va mīfiristad. Laʿnatu Allāhi ʿalā l-kādhibīn wa-l-muftarīn. Idhan yatabarraʾu minhum Nuqṭatu l-Bayān fī ʿarshi l-jinān wa-yaqūlu khusrānan lakum yā malaʾa l-mushrikīn va nāran ʿalaykum yā malaʾa l-mughriḍīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Afterward, the Source of authority commanded that they go and ask her from which part of the house she had brought out that Tablet, and tell her, “Show it,” so that she might come to her senses and be among those who repent. They have risen to fabricate falsehoods with such vehemence. These actions follow instructions that Mírzá Yaḥyá writes and sends from here. May God’s curse rest upon the liars and fabricators. Thereupon the Point of the Bayán, on the throne of paradise, disavows them and says: “Ruin upon you, you who associate partners with God! Fire upon you, you people of malice!”
:::

### 680

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اليوم بايد بصر را حديد نمود و قلب را طاهر و صدر را منزّه تا انسان خود را از دونش بشناسد و تميز دهد و اين رتبه اگر چه بسيار بلند و عظيم است ولكن نزد منصفين بسيار سهل و يسير اگرچه حال اهل بيان بمقامى رسيده‌اند و بامورى بر حقّ اعتراض نموده‌اند كه از اوّل ابداع تا حين احدى در مثل آن امور بر حقّ اعتراض ننموده ‌جميع اين عباد سالها است طايف حول بوده‌ايم و اللّه العظيم كه هرگز نزدشان از زخرف دنيا شيئى نبوده و اگر هم بوده جميع شريك بوده‌ايم و هر نفسى ببيت اعظم وارد گويا خود صاحب بيت است كمال عنايت درباره او مبذول و مع‌ذلك اهل بيان اعتراضا على اللّه بكلّ ما ظهر من الحقّ اعتراض نموده‌اند حتّى شرب چاى و همچنين در لباس و امثال آن افّ لهم و لحيائهم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Al-yawm bāyad baṣar rā ḥadīd namūd va qalb rā ṭāhir va ṣadr rā munazzah tā insān khud rā az dūnash bishināsad va tamyīz dihad va īn rutbih agar chih bisyār buland va ʿaẓīm ast va lākin nazd-i munṣifīn bisyār sahl va yasīr. Agarchih ḥāl ahl-i Bayān bi-maqāmī rasīdih-and va bi-umūrī bar Ḥaqq iʿtirāḍ namūdih-and kih az avval-i ibdāʿ tā ḥīn aḥadī dar mithl-i ān umūr bar Ḥaqq iʿtirāḍ nanamūdih. Jamīʿ-i īn ʿibād sālhā ast ṭāʾif-i ḥawl būdih-īm va-Allāhu l-ʿaẓīm kih hargiz nazdishān az zukhruf-i dunyā shayʾī nabūdih va agar ham būdih jamīʿ sharīk būdih-īm va har nafsī bi-Bayt-i Aʿẓam vārid gūyā khud ṣāḥib-i bayt ast kamāl-i ʿināyat dar bārih-yi ū mabdhūl va maʿa dhālik ahl-i Bayān iʿtirāḍan ʿalā Allāh bi-kulli mā ẓahara mina l-Ḥaqq iʿtirāḍ namūdih-and ḥattā shurb-i chāy va hamchunīn dar libās va amthāl-i ān. Uffin lahum va li-ḥayāʾihim.
:::

::: {.translation}
Today one must sharpen one’s sight, purify one’s heart, and sanctify one’s breast, so that a person may recognize and distinguish himself from others. Although this rank is very lofty and great, it is very easy and simple for the fair-minded. Yet the people of the Bayán have now reached such a state, and have objected to the True One over such matters, that from the beginning of creation until now no one has objected to the True One over anything like them. All of us servants have circled around Him for years. By God the Almighty, He has never possessed anything of this world’s finery, and if there has been anything, we have all shared in it. Anyone who enters the Most Great House is treated as though he himself were its owner, and the utmost loving care is lavished upon him. Nevertheless, the people of the Bayán, in opposition to God, have objected to everything that has appeared from the True One, even the drinking of tea, and likewise to His clothing and similar things. Shame on them and their sense of shame!
:::

### 681

::: {.original lang="fa"}
نميدانم چه شده كه هر نفسى در عقبه واقف و مبتلى لوحى در اين ایّام از مشرق مشيّت رحمن مخصوص يكى از احبّا مشرق و نازل در اينمقام لاجل تنبّه ذكر ميشود شايد متنبّه شوند و بشنوند قول نقطه اولى را در كرّه اخرى از لسان ابدع ابهى و از ضجيج و حنين و ناله آن حضرت شرم نمايند و بآنچه عامل شده كفايت كنند و هذه صورة ما نزل من جبروت اللّه العلىّ العظيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Namīdānam chih shudih kih har nafsī dar ʿaqabih vāqif va mubtalā. Lawḥī dar īn ayyām az mashriq-i mashiyyat-i Raḥmān makhṣūṣ-i yikī az aḥibbā mushriq va nāzil. Dar īn maqām li-ajl-i tanabbuh dhikr mīshavad shāyad mutanabbih shavand va bishinavand qawl-i Nuqṭih-yi Ūlā rā dar karrih-yi ukhrā az lisān-i abdaʿ-i abhā va az ḍajīj va ḥanīn va nālih-yi ān Ḥaḍrat sharm namāyand va bi-ānchih ʿāmil shudih kifāyat kunand. Va hādhihi ṣūratu mā nazala min jabarūti Allāhi l-ʿAliyyi l-ʿAẓīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
I do not know what has happened that every soul has halted at the mountain pass and become afflicted. In these days a Tablet has dawned and descended from the dayspring of the will of the All-Merciful, addressed specifically to one of the loved ones. It is quoted here to awaken them, so that they may perhaps come to their senses and hear once again the words of the Primal Point from a wondrous, all-glorious tongue, feel ashamed at His cries, lamentations, and weeping, and content themselves with what they have already done. This is the text of what descended from the dominion of God, the Most High, the Almighty.
:::

### 682

::: {.original lang="ar"}
بسم اللّه الأقدس العلىّ الأعلی
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bi-smi Allāhi l-Aqdasi l-ʿAliyyi l-Aʿlā.
:::

::: {.translation}
In the name of God, the Most Holy, the High, the Most Exalted.
:::

### 683

::: {.original lang="ar"}
هذا كتاب نقطة الأولی الى الّذينهم آمنوا باللّه الواحد الفرد العزيز العليم و فيه يخاطب الّذينهم توقّفوا فى هذا الأمر من ملأ البيانييّن لعلّ يستشعرن ببدايع كلمات اللّه و يقومن عن رقد الغفلة فى هذا الفجر المشرق المنير قل انّا امرناكم فى الكتاب بأن لاتقدموا طايفة الّتى يظهر منها محبوب العارفين و مقصود من فى السّموات و الأرضين و امرناكم ان ادركتم لقآء اللّه قوموا تلقآء الوجه ثمّ انطقوا من قبلى بهذه الكلمة العزيز المنيع عليك يا بهآء اللّه و ذوى قرابتك ذكر اللّه و ثنآء كلّ شیء فى كلّ حين و قبل حين و بعد حين و جعلنا هذه الكلمة عزّاً لاهل البيان لعلّ بها يرتقون الى معارج القدس و يكوننّ من الفائزين و انّهم تركوا ما امروا به بحيث ما ظهر احد تلقآء الوجه بما امرناهم فى الواح عزّ عظيم بل رموا نحوه من كلّ الآفاق رمى النّفاق و بذلك بكيت و بكت اهل جبروت العظمة ثمّ روح الأمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Hādhā kitābu Nuqṭati l-Ūlā ilā lladhīnahum āmanū bi-Allāhi l-Wāḥidi l-Fardi l-ʿAzīzi l-ʿAlīm wa-fīhi yukhāṭibu lladhīnahum tawaqqafū fī hādhā l-amri min malaʾi l-bayāniyyīn laʿalla yastashʿirna bi-badāʾiʿi kalimāti Allāhi wa-yaqūmna ʿan raqdi l-ghaflati fī hādhā l-fajri l-mushriqi l-munīr. Qul innā amarnākum fī l-kitābi bi-an lā taqdamū ṭāʾifata llatī yaẓharu minhā maḥbūbu l-ʿārifīn wa-maqṣūdu man fī l-samāwāti wa-l-arḍīn wa-amarnākum in adraktum liqāʾa Allāhi qūmū tilqāʾa l-wajhi thumma nṭiqū min qiblī bi-hādhihi l-kalimati l-ʿazīzi l-manīʿ: ʿalayka yā Bahāʾa Allāhi wa-dhawī qarābatika dhikru Allāhi wa-thanāʾu kulli shayʾin fī kulli ḥīnin wa-qabla ḥīnin wa-baʿda ḥīn. Wa-jaʿalnā hādhihi l-kalimata ʿizzan li-ahli l-Bayāni laʿalla bihā yartaqūna ilā maʿāriji l-qudsi wa-yakūnanna mina l-fāʾizīn. Wa-innahum tarakū mā umirū bihi bi-ḥaythu mā ẓahara aḥadun tilqāʾa l-wajhi bi-mā amarnāhum fī alwāḥi ʿizzin ʿaẓīm bal ramaw naḥwahu min kulli l-āfāqi ramya l-nifāqi wa-bi-dhālika bakaytu wa-bakat ahlu jabarūti l-ʿaẓamati thumma Rūḥu l-Amīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
This is the Book of the Primal Point to those who have believed in God, the One, the Unique, the Almighty, the All-Knowing. In it He addresses those among the people of the Bayán who have hesitated in this Cause, so that they may become aware of the wonders of God’s words and rise from the sleep of heedlessness in this radiant, luminous dawn. Say: We commanded you in the Book not to take precedence over the community from which would appear the Beloved of those endowed with understanding and the Desire of all who are in the heavens and on earth. We commanded you, should you attain the presence of God, to stand before His face and then utter on My behalf these mighty, exalted words: “Upon You, O Bahá’u’lláh, and upon Your kindred, be the remembrance of God and the praise of every thing, at every moment, before every moment, and after every moment.” We made these words an honor for the people of the Bayán, so that through them they might ascend to the heights of holiness and be among those who attain their goal. Yet they abandoned what they were commanded, so that no one appeared before His face with what We had enjoined upon them in Tablets of great glory. Instead, from every horizon they hurled the shafts of hypocrisy at Him. At this I wept, and the inhabitants of the dominion of grandeur wept, and then the faithful Spirit.
:::

### 684

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قل يا قوم فاستحيوا عن جمالى انّ الّذى قد ظهر بالحقّ انّه لبهآء العالمين لو انتم من العارفين و انّه لبهآء اللّه و عليه ذكر اللّه و ثنائه ثم ثنآء اهل ملأ الأعلی و ثنآء اهل جبروت البقآء و ثنآء كلّ شیء فى كلّ حين ایّاکم ان تحتجبوا بما خلق بين الأرض و السّمآء ان اسرعوا الى رضوان رضائه و لا تكوننّ من الرّاقدين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul yā qawmi fa-staḥyū ʿan jamālī inna lladhī qad ẓahara bi-l-ḥaqqi innahu la-Bahāʾu l-ʿālamīn law antum mina l-ʿārifīn wa-innahu la-Bahāʾu Allāhi wa-ʿalayhi dhikru Allāhi wa-thanāʾuhu thumma thanāʾu ahli malaʾi l-aʿlā wa-thanāʾu ahli jabarūti l-baqāʾ wa-thanāʾu kulli shayʾin fī kulli ḥīn. Iyyākum an taḥtajibū bi-mā khuliqa bayna l-arḍi wa-l-samāʾ an asriʿū ilā Riḍwāni riḍāʾihi wa-lā takūnanna mina l-rāqidīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: My people, feel shame before My beauty! He who has appeared in truth is indeed the Glory of all the worlds, if you are among those endowed with understanding. He is indeed Bahá’u’lláh, and upon Him be the remembrance of God and His praise, and the praise of the inhabitants of the highest assembly, the praise of the inhabitants of the dominion of eternity, and the praise of every thing at every moment. Beware lest you be veiled by anything created between earth and heaven. Hasten to the paradise of His good pleasure, and do not be among those who sleep.
:::

### 685

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قل انّ جماله كان جمالى بالحقّ و انّ نفسه نفسى و كلّما نزّلناه فى البيان قد نزل لأمره المحكم البديع اتّقو اللّه و لاتجادلوا بالّذى اخبرناكم به و بشّرناكم بظهوره و اخذت عهد نفسه قبل عهد نفسى و يشهد بذلك كلّ شیء ان انتم من المنكرين تاللّه بنغمة من نغماته ولدت حقايق كلّ شیء مرّة اخرى و بنغمة اخرى استجذبت افئدة المقرّبين ایّاکم ان تحتجبوا بشىء عن الّذى كان لقائه ذات لقائى و فدى نفسه فى سبيلى كما فديت فى سبيله حبّاً لجماله العزيز المنيع
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul inna jamālahu kāna jamālī bi-l-ḥaqq wa-inna nafsahu nafsī wa-kullamā nazzalnāhu fī al-Bayān qad nazala li-amrihi al-muḥkam al-badīʿ. Ittaqū Allāh wa-lā tujādilū bi-lladhī akhbarnākum bihi wa-bashsharnākum bi-ẓuhūrihi wa-akhadhtu ʿahda nafsihi qabla ʿahda nafsī wa-yashhadu bi-dhālika kull shayʾ in antum min al-munkirīn. Ta-llāh bi-naghma min naghamātihi wulidat ḥaqāʾiq kull shayʾ marra ukhrā wa-bi-naghma ukhrā istujdhibat afʾidat al-muqarrabīn. Iyyākum an taḥtajibū bi-shayʾ ʿan alladhī kāna liqāʾuhu dhāta liqāʾī wa-fadā nafsahu fī sabīlī kamā fadaytu fī sabīlihi ḥubban li-jamālihi al-ʿazīz al-manīʿ.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: His beauty was truly My beauty, and His own Self My Self, and everything We sent down in the Bayán was revealed for His firm and wondrous Cause. Fear God, and do not dispute concerning Him of whom We informed you and whose appearance We announced to you. I took the covenant concerning His Self before the covenant concerning My own Self, and every thing bears witness to this, if you are among those who deny it. By God! Through one of His melodies the realities of all things were born anew, and through another melody the hearts of those brought near were drawn to Him. Beware lest anything veil you from Him, meeting whom was the very essence of meeting Me. He sacrificed Himself in My path, just as I sacrificed Myself in His path, out of love for His mighty, unassailable beauty.
:::

### 686

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قل لولاه ما ركب الحآء بالبآء و ما استقرّ هيكل الهآء على الواو و ما خلق ما كان و ما يكون لو انتم من الشّاعرين و لولاه ما القيت نفسى بين يدى المشركين و ما علّقت بين الهوا تاللّه باشتياقى اليه و شوقى الى نفسه قد حملت ما لا حمله النّبيّين و المرسلين و رضيت كلّ ذلك على نفسى لئلّا يرد عليه ما يحزن به فؤاده الألطف الأرقّ اللّطيف المنيع و وصّيناكم فى كلّ البيان بأن لايحزن احد احداً لعلّ لايرد عليه من حزن و الّا مالى و ذكرى لكم و اشتغالى بكم يا ملأ التّاركين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul lawlāhu mā rukkiba al-Ḥāʾ bi-l-Bāʾ wa-mā istaqarra haykal al-Hāʾ ʿalā al-Wāw wa-mā khuliqa mā kāna wa-mā yakūn law antum min al-shāʿirīn. Wa-lawlāhu mā alqaytu nafsī bayna yaday al-mushrikīn wa-mā ʿulliqtu bayna al-hawā. Ta-llāh bi-ishtiyāqī ilayhi wa-shawqī ilā nafsihi qad ḥamaltu mā lā ḥamalahu al-nabiyyīn wa-l-mursalīn wa-raḍītu kulla dhālika ʿalā nafsī li-allā yarida ʿalayhi mā yaḥzanu bihi fuʾāduhu al-alṭaf al-araqq al-laṭīf al-manīʿ. Wa-waṣṣaynākum fī kull al-Bayān bi-an lā yuḥzina aḥad aḥadan laʿalla lā yarida ʿalayhi min ḥuzn wa-illā mā lī wa-dhikrī lakum wa-ishtighālī bikum yā malaʾ al-tārikīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: Were it not for Him, the Ḥāʾ would not have been joined to the Bāʾ, nor would the form of the Hāʾ have been established upon the Wāw, nor would anything that has been or will be have been created, if you are among those who perceive. Were it not for Him, I would not have cast Myself into the hands of those who associate partners with God, nor would I have been suspended in the air. By God! In My yearning for Him and My longing for His Self, I bore what the Prophets and Messengers did not bear, and willingly accepted all this for Myself, lest anything befall Him that would grieve His most tender, most delicate, gracious, unassailable heart. Throughout the Bayán We enjoined you not to cause anyone sorrow, that perhaps no sorrow might befall Him. Otherwise, what have I to do with mentioning you or concerning Myself with you, O assembly of those who have turned away?
:::

### 687

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انّى ما اردت فى البيان الّا نفسه و لا من الأذکار‌ الّا ذكره و لا من الأسماء الّا اسمه المبارك الأمنع الأقدس الأبدع البديع فو‌عمرى لو ذكرت ذكر الرّبوبيّة ما اردت الّا ربوبيّته على كلّ الأشیآء و ان جرى من قلمى ذكر الالوهيّة ما كان مقصودى الّا اله العالمين و ان جرى من قلمى ذكر المقصود فهو كان مقصودى و كذلك فى المحبوب انّه قد كان محبوبی‌ و محبوب العارفين و ان ذكرت ذكر السّجود ما اردت الّا السّجود لوجهه المتعالى العزيز المنيع و ان اثنيت نفساً ما كان مقصود قلبی‌ الّا ثنآء نفسه و ان امرت النّاس بعمل ما اردت الّا العمل فى رضائه فى يوم ظهوره و بذلك يشهد كلّما نزل علىّ من جبروت ربّی‌ العليم الحكيم و علّقت كلّ شیء بتصديقه و رضائه و انّه لهو الّذى قد كان بنفسه اله العالمين و مقصود القاصدين و انتم لو تدقّون الأبصار لتشهدون مظاهر يفعل ما يشآء فى ظلّه لمن العابدين و انتم قد فعلتم بنفسه ما لا فعل امّة الفرقان بنفسى و لا ملأ اليهود بالرّوح
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-innī mā aradtu fī al-Bayān illā nafsahu wa-lā min al-adhkār illā dhikrahu wa-lā min al-asmāʾ illā ismahu al-mubārak al-amnaʿ al-aqdas al-abdaʿ al-badīʿ. Fa-wa-ʿamrī law dhakartu dhikr al-rubūbiyya mā aradtu illā rubūbiyyatahu ʿalā kull al-ashyāʾ wa-in jarā min qalamī dhikr al-ulūhiyya mā kāna maqṣūdī illā ilāh al-ʿālamīn wa-in jarā min qalamī dhikr al-maqṣūd fa-huwa kāna maqṣūdī wa-kadhālika fī al-maḥbūb innahu qad kāna maḥbūbī wa-maḥbūb al-ʿārifīn wa-in dhakartu dhikr al-sujūd mā aradtu illā al-sujūd li-wajhihi al-mutaʿālī al-ʿazīz al-manīʿ wa-in athnaytu nafsan mā kāna maqṣūd qalbī illā thanāʾ nafsihi wa-in amartu al-nās bi-ʿamal mā aradtu illā al-ʿamala fī riḍāʾihi fī yawm ẓuhūrihi wa-bi-dhālika yashhadu kullamā nazala ʿalayya min jabarūt rabbī al-ʿalīm al-ḥakīm. Wa-ʿallaqtu kulla shayʾ bi-taṣdīqihi wa-riḍāʾihi wa-innahu la-huwa alladhī qad kāna bi-nafsihi ilāh al-ʿālamīn wa-maqṣūd al-qāṣidīn wa-antum law tudiqqūn al-abṣār la-tashhadūn maẓāhir yafʿalu mā yashāʾ fī ẓillihi la-min al-ʿābidīn. Wa-antum qad faʿaltum bi-nafsihi mā lā faʿala ummat al-Furqān bi-nafsī wa-lā malaʾ al-Yahūd bi-l-Rūḥ.
:::

::: {.translation}
In the Bayán I intended none but His Self; by its remembrances, none but His remembrance; and by its names, none but His blessed, most unassailable, most holy, most wondrous, incomparable Name. By My life! If I made mention of lordship, I intended only His lordship over all things. If mention of divinity flowed from My pen, My purpose was none but the God of all worlds. If mention of the Desired One flowed from My pen, He was My Desired One; and likewise with the Beloved: He was My Beloved and the Beloved of those who know. If I made mention of prostration, I intended only prostration before His exalted, mighty, unassailable countenance. If I praised anyone, My heart intended only to praise His Self. If I commanded people to perform a deed, I intended only that it be done for His good pleasure on the day of His appearance. Everything sent down to Me from the dominion of My Lord, the All-Knowing, the All-Wise, bears witness to this. I made everything dependent on His confirmation and good pleasure. He is indeed the One who in His own Self has been the God of all worlds and the Desire of all who seek. If you look closely, you will surely see the Manifestations of “He does whatever He wills” among those who worship in His shadow. Yet you have done to His Self what neither the people of the Qur’an did to Me nor the assembly of the Jews to the Spirit.
:::

### 688

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فآهء آه من حرقة قلبی‌ و حنين نفسى فيما ورد على محبوبی‌ من ملأ المشركين افّ لكم و لوفائكم يا معشر الظّالمين انا خلقنا الوفآء و الأدب لنفسه لعلّ عند ظهوره لا تفعلوا امراً تجزع به حقيقتى و حقايق الأشیآء و انتم تجاوزتم عما حدّد فى كتاب اللّه الملك العلىّ العظيم و خرقتم حجاب الحيا ثمّ ستر الحرمة و عملتم ما يستحيى من ذكره قلم الانشآء بين الأرض و السّمآء
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-āh āh min ḥurqat qalbī wa-ḥanīn nafsī fīmā warada ʿalā maḥbūbī min malaʾ al-mushrikīn. Uff lakum wa-li-wafāʾikum yā maʿshar al-ẓālimīn. Innā khalaqnā al-wafāʾ wa-l-adab li-nafsihi laʿalla ʿinda ẓuhūrihi lā tafʿalū amran tajzaʿu bihi ḥaqīqatī wa-ḥaqāʾiq al-ashyāʾ wa-antum tajāwaztum ʿammā ḥuddida fī kitāb Allāh al-malik al-ʿalī al-ʿaẓīm wa-kharaqtum ḥijāb al-ḥayā thumma sitr al-ḥurma wa-ʿamiltum mā yastaḥyī min dhikrihi qalam al-inshāʾ bayna al-arḍ wa-l-samāʾ.
:::

::: {.translation}
Alas, alas for the burning of My heart and the lamentation of My soul at what has befallen My Beloved at the hands of those who associate partners with God! Shame on you and your faithfulness, O company of wrongdoers! We created faithfulness and courtesy for His sake, so that at His appearance you might not do anything that would cause My reality and the realities of all things to grieve. Yet you have overstepped the bounds set in the Book of God, the King, the Most High, the Most Great. You have torn the veil of modesty and then the covering of reverence, and have done what the Pen of creation is ashamed to mention between earth and heaven.
:::

### 689

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فآهء آه بما ورد منكم على هذا المظلوم الفريد الغريب و لم ادر ما تفعلون به من بعد لا فو‌نفسى العليم بل اعلم و عندى علم كلّ شیء فى لوح جعله اللّه محفوظاً عن انظر المشركين و اخبرناه من قبل بما ورد عليه و يرد ولو انّه قد كان بنفسه عالماً بما فى صدور العالمين و لن يعزب عن علمه من شیء و لا يفوت عن قبضته ما خلق بكلمة من عنده لا اله الّا هو الفرد الباعث المحيى المميت
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-āh āh bi-mā warada minkum ʿalā hādhā al-maẓlūm al-farīd al-gharīb wa-lam adri mā tafʿalūna bihi min baʿd. Lā fa-wa-nafsī al-ʿalīm bal aʿlam wa-ʿindī ʿilm kull shayʾ fī lawḥ jaʿalahu Allāh maḥfūẓan ʿan \[corrupted text\] al-mushrikīn wa-akhbarnāhu min qabl bi-mā warada ʿalayhi wa-yarid wa-law innahu qad kāna bi-nafsihi ʿāliman bi-mā fī ṣudūr al-ʿālamīn wa-lan yaʿzuba ʿan ʿilmihi min shayʾ wa-lā yafūtu ʿan qabḍatihi mā khuliqa bi-kalima min ʿindihi lā ilāha illā huwa al-fard al-bāʿith al-muḥyī al-mumīt.
:::

::: {.translation}
Alas, alas for what you have inflicted on this Wronged One, alone and a stranger! I do not know what you will do to Him hereafter. No, by My all-knowing Self! Rather, I do know, and with Me is the knowledge of all things in a Tablet that God has kept safe from the \[corrupted original text\] of those who associate partners with Him. We told Him beforehand what had befallen Him and what would befall Him, although He Himself knew what lay within the hearts of all the world. Nothing will escape His knowledge, nor will anything created by a word from Him elude His grasp. There is no God but Him, the Unique, the Raiser of the dead, the Giver of life, the Bringer of death.
:::

### 690

::: {.original lang="ar"}
قل يا قوم انّه لهو الّذى لو يريد ان يجعل كلّ من فى السّموات و الأرض حجّة باقية من عنده ليقدر و انّ هذا عنده سهل يسير و انّه لهو الّذى قد خلق رضوان البيان لنفسه و منه بدء كلّ شیء و يعود لو انتم من العالمين و انتم بالّذى كان فى قبضته ملكوت الابداع ما رضيتم ان يسمّى نفسه باسم من الأسمآء بعد الّذى انّها و ملكوتها قد خلقت بأمره العزيز المنيع فآهء آه عن غفلتكم يا ملأ البيان فآهء آه من احتجابكم يا ملأ المشركين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul yā qawm innahu la-huwa alladhī law yurīdu an yajʿala kulla man fī al-samāwāt wa-l-arḍ ḥujja bāqiya min ʿindihi la-yaqdir wa-inna hādhā ʿindahu sahl yasīr. Wa-innahu la-huwa alladhī qad khalaqa Riḍwān al-Bayān li-nafsihi wa-minhu badʾ kull shayʾ wa-yaʿūd law antum min al-ʿālimīn. Wa-antum bi-lladhī kāna fī qabḍatihi malakūt al-ibdāʿ mā raḍītum an yusammiya nafsahu bi-ism min al-asmāʾ baʿda alladhī innahā wa-malakūtahā qad khuliqat bi-amrihi al-ʿazīz al-manīʿ. Fa-āh āh ʿan ghaflatikum yā malaʾ al-Bayān fa-āh āh min iḥtijābikum yā malaʾ al-mushrikīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: My people, He is indeed the One who, if He wished to make everyone in the heavens and on earth an enduring testimony from Him, would have the power to do so. This is easy and effortless for Him. He is indeed the One who created the Paradise of the Bayán for Himself. From Him all things originate and to Him they return, if you are among those who know. Yet you were unwilling that He in whose grasp was the kingdom of creation should call Himself by any name, even though those names and their kingdom were created by His mighty, unassailable command. Alas, alas for your heedlessness, O people of the Bayán! Alas, alas for your veiling, O assembly of those who associate partners with God!
:::

### 691

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و انتم لمّا اسرفتم فى انفسكم و بلغتم الى معارج العرفان بزعمكم تذكرون الوصاية لأحد من اعدائه و تستدلّون بها على اللّه الّذى به شرعت شرايع الأدیان فى الأوّلین‌ و الآخرین و رجعتم الى ما استدلّ به اولو الفرقان بعد الّذى نهيناكم فى ساحته عن كلّ الأذکار‌ الّا بعد اذنه و كان اللّه على ذلك لشهيد و خبير اذا فانظروا فى شأنكم و عرفانكم فافّ لكم و لعقولكم ثمّ درايتكم يا ملأ الأخسرين اما علمتم بانّا طوينا ما عند النّاس و بسطنا بساطاً آخر فتبارك اللّه الملك الباسط العزيز الكريم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-antum lammā asraftum fī anfusikum wa-balaghtum ilā maʿārij al-ʿirfān bi-zaʿmikum tadhkurūna al-waṣāya li-aḥad min aʿdāʾihi wa-tastadillūna bihā ʿalā Allāh alladhī bihi shuriʿat sharāʾiʿ al-adyān fī al-awwalīn wa-l-ākhirīn wa-rajaʿtum ilā mā istadalla bihi ulū al-Furqān baʿda alladhī nahaynākum fī sāḥatihi ʿan kull al-adhkār illā baʿda idhnihi wa-kāna Allāh ʿalā dhālika la-shahīd wa-khabīr. Idhan fa-nẓurū fī shaʾnikum wa-ʿirfānikum fa-uff lakum wa-li-ʿuqūlikum thumma dirāyatikum yā malaʾ al-akhsarīn. A-mā ʿalimtum bi-annā ṭawaynā mā ʿinda al-nās wa-basaṭnā bisāṭan ākhar fa-tabāraka Allāh al-malik al-bāsiṭ al-ʿazīz al-karīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
When you went to excess in your own estimation and, as you imagined, attained the heights of knowledge, you invoked a succession conferred by testament upon one of His enemies, and used it to argue against God, through whom the laws of the religions were ordained among earlier and later generations. You returned to the arguments used by the people of the Qur’an, even though We had forbidden you to make any mention in His presence except with His permission. God is indeed a witness to this and fully informed. Consider, then, your condition and your knowledge! Shame on you, your reason, and your understanding, O assembly of those who have suffered the greatest loss! Did you not know that We rolled up what people possessed and spread out another carpet? Blessed, then, is God, the King, the One who spreads it out, the Almighty, the Generous.
:::

### 692

::: {.original lang="ar"}
قل يا قوم لاتفتروا على نفسى و انّى ما تكلّمت الّا بذكر هذا الظّهور و ثنائه و ما تنفّست الّا بحبّه و ما توجّهت الّا بوجهه المشرق المنير و جعلت البيان و ما نزل فيه ورقة من اوراق حديقة الرّضوان لنفسه المهيمن العزيز القدير ایّاکم ان تغصبوها و ترجعوها الى الّذى اراد سفك دمى مرّه اخرى بما اتّبع النّفس و الهوى و كان من الحاربين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul yā qawm lā taftarū ʿalā nafsī wa-innī mā takallamtu illā bi-dhikr hādhā al-ẓuhūr wa-thanāʾihi wa-mā tanaffastu illā bi-ḥubbihi wa-mā tawajjahtu illā bi-wajhihi al-mushriq al-munīr wa-jaʿaltu al-Bayān wa-mā nazala fīhi waraqa min awrāq ḥadīqat al-Riḍwān li-nafsihi al-muhaymin al-ʿazīz al-qadīr. Iyyākum an taghṣabūhā wa-turjiʿūhā ilā alladhī arāda safka damī marra ukhrā bi-mā ittabaʿa al-nafs wa-l-hawā wa-kāna min al-ḥāribīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: My people, do not fabricate lies about Me. I spoke only in remembrance and praise of this Revelation; I breathed only in love for Him; and I turned only toward His radiant, luminous countenance. I made the Bayán and all that was revealed in it a leaf from the leaves of the garden of Paradise for His Self, the All-Protecting, the Almighty, the All-Powerful. Beware lest you seize it and turn it over to the one who wished to shed My blood once again, because he followed self and desire and was among those who waged war.
:::

### 693

::: {.original lang="ar"}
قد فصّلنا البيان من كلمة ثمّ رجعناه اليها و امرنا الكلمة بان يحضر تلقآء العرش ليشهد خلق قبله و يفرح به نفسه العليم الحكيم اذا فانصفوا هل ينبغى ان يتصرّف فيها صاحبها او دونها فما لكم يا معشر المحتجبين انّا امرنا ملأ البيان بأن يلبسن الحرير و ينظفنّ انفسهم و اثوابهم لئلّا تقع عينه على ما لا يحبّه و كذلك فى كلّ شیء فصّلنا تفصيلاً فى كتاب مبين كلّ ذلك لنفسه لو انتم من المنصفين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qad faṣṣalnā al-Bayān min kalima thumma rajaʿnāhu ilayhā wa-amarnā al-kalima bi-an yaḥḍura tilqāʾ al-ʿarsh li-yashhada khalqa qablahu wa-yafraḥa bihi nafsuhu al-ʿalīm al-ḥakīm. Idhan fa-anṣifū hal yanbaghī an yataṣarrafa fīhā ṣāḥibuhā aw dūnahā fa-mā lakum yā maʿshar al-muḥtajibīn. Innā amarnā malaʾ al-Bayān bi-an yalbasna al-ḥarīr wa-yunaẓẓifunna anfusahum wa-athwābahum li-allā taqaʿa ʿaynuhu ʿalā mā lā yuḥibbuhu wa-kadhālika fī kull shayʾ faṣṣalnā tafṣīlan fī kitāb mubīn kull dhālika li-nafsihi law antum min al-munṣifīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
We unfolded the Bayán from a word, then returned it to that word, and commanded the word to appear before the Throne, that it might witness creation before Him and that His all-knowing, all-wise Self might rejoice in it. Judge fairly, then: should its possessor exercise authority over it, or someone other than it? What is the matter with you, O company of the veiled? We commanded the people of the Bayán to wear silk and to cleanse themselves and their clothes, lest His eyes fall upon anything He dislikes. Likewise, concerning every thing, We set out the details in a clear Book. All this was for His sake, if you are among those who judge fairly.
:::

### 694

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و خلقنا السّموات و الأرض و ما قدّر بينهما لاحبّائه فكيف جماله المشرق العزيز المنير و انتم تمسّكتم بما قدّرناه له و اعترضتم به على محبوبی‌ فما لكم يا ملأ البغضآء و ما يغنيكم اليوم يا معشر المفسدين و انتم اعترضتم عليه و بكلّ ما ظهر من عنده بعد ما وصّيناكم به فى الألواح بأن كلّ من يخطر بباله ذكر اسمه الأعظم البديع يقوم عن مقرّه و يقول سبحان اللّه ذوالملك و الملكوت تسعة عشر مرّة ثمّ سبحان اللّه ذى العزّة و الجبروت تسعة عشر مرّة الى آخر ما نزلناه فى لوح عزّ عظيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-khalaqnā al-samāwāt wa-l-arḍ wa-mā quddira baynahumā li-aḥibbāʾihi fa-kayfa jamāluhu al-mushriq al-ʿazīz al-munīr. Wa-antum tamassaktum bi-mā qaddarnāhu lahu wa-iʿtaraḍtum bihi ʿalā maḥbūbī fa-mā lakum yā malaʾ al-baghḍāʾ wa-mā yughnīkum al-yawm yā maʿshar al-mufsidīn. Wa-antum iʿtaraḍtum ʿalayhi wa-bi-kull mā ẓahara min ʿindihi baʿda mā waṣṣaynākum bihi fī al-alwāḥ bi-anna kulla man yakhṭuru bi-bālihi dhikr ismihi al-aʿẓam al-badīʿ yaqūmu ʿan maqarrihi wa-yaqūlu subḥāna Allāh dhū al-mulk wa-l-malakūt tisʿata ʿashara marra thumma subḥāna Allāh dhī al-ʿizza wa-l-jabarūt tisʿata ʿashara marra ilā ākhir mā nazzalnāhu fī lawḥ ʿizz ʿaẓīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
We created the heavens and the earth and all that was ordained between them for His loved ones—how much more, then, for His radiant, mighty, luminous Beauty! Yet you clung to what We ordained for Him and used it to object to My Beloved. What is the matter with you, O assembly of hatred? What will avail you today, O company of those who spread corruption? You objected to Him and to everything that appeared from Him, even though We had enjoined you in the Tablets that whoever calls to mind His most great and wondrous Name should rise from his seat and say, “Glory be to God, the Possessor of sovereignty and dominion,” nineteen times, and then, “Glory be to God, the Possessor of might and supreme power,” nineteen times, and so on to the end of what We revealed in a Tablet of great glory.
:::

### 695

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انتم كفرتم به و بآياته و ما اكتفيتم بذلك و ما لاحظتم حقوق اللّه فى حقّه و ما راعيتم امر اللّه فى نفسه العلىّ العليم الى ان اعترضتم بكلّ افعاله واحدا بعد واحد و كنتم من المستهزئين و منكم من قال انّه يشرب الچاى و منكم من قال انّه يأكل الطّعام و منكم من اعترض على لباسه بعد الّذى كلّ خيط من خيوطه يشهد بانّه لا اله الّا هو و انّه لمقصود المقرّبين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-antum kafartum bihi wa-bi-āyātihi wa-mā iktafaytum bi-dhālika wa-mā lāḥaẓtum ḥuqūq Allāh fī ḥaqqihi wa-mā rāʿaytum amr Allāh fī nafsihi al-ʿalī al-ʿalīm ilā an iʿtaraḍtum bi-kull afʿālihi wāḥidan baʿda wāḥid wa-kuntum min al-mustahziʾīn. Wa-minkum man qāla innahu yashrabu al-chāy wa-minkum man qāla innahu yaʾkulu al-ṭaʿām wa-minkum man iʿtaraḍa ʿalā libāsihi baʿda alladhī kull khayṭ min khuyūṭihi yashhadu bi-annahu lā ilāha illā huwa wa-innahu la-maqṣūd al-muqarrabīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
You disbelieved in Him and His verses, and were not content with that. You did not regard the rights of God in relation to Him, nor did you observe God’s command concerning His exalted, all-knowing Self, until you objected to all His actions, one after another, and became mockers. Some of you said, “He drinks tea”; some said, “He eats food”; and some objected to His clothing, even though every thread of it bears witness that there is no God but Him and that He is indeed the Desire of those brought near.
:::

### 696

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انّى اشهد بنفسى ما كان عند حضرته فى بعض الأحيان من ثوبين ليبدّل احدهما بالآخر كذلك يشهد لسان صدق عليم و ما كان فى بعض اللّيالى ما يسترزقن به آل اللّه و انّه ستر امره حفظاً لأمر اللّه المحكم المتين بعد الّذى خلق كلّ شیء لنفسه و عنده مفتاح خزاين السّموات و الأرضين افّ لحيائكم يا ملأ البيان تاللّه خجلت من فعلكم و اذاً اتبرّء منكم يا ملأ الشّياطين فآهء آه من ابتلائه بينكم فآهء آه عمّا ورد و يرد عليه فى كلّ حين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-innī ashhadu bi-nafsī mā kāna ʿinda ḥaḍratihi fī baʿḍ al-aḥyān min thawbayn li-yubaddila aḥadahumā bi-l-ākhar kadhālika yashhadu lisān ṣidq ʿalīm. Wa-mā kāna fī baʿḍ al-layālī mā yastarziqna bihi āl Allāh wa-innahu satara amrahu ḥifẓan li-amr Allāh al-muḥkam al-matīn baʿda alladhī khuliqa kull shayʾ li-nafsihi wa-ʿindahu miftāḥ khazāʾin al-samāwāt wa-l-arḍīn. Uff li-ḥayāʾikum yā malaʾ al-Bayān. Ta-llāh khajiltu min fiʿlikum wa-idhan atabarraʾu minkum yā malaʾ al-shayāṭīn. Fa-āh āh min ibtilāʾihi baynakum fa-āh āh ʿammā warada wa-yaridu ʿalayhi fī kull ḥīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
I Myself bear witness that at times He did not possess two garments so that He could change from one into the other. Thus bears witness a truthful, knowing tongue. On some nights the family of God had nothing to sustain them. Yet He concealed His circumstances to safeguard the firm and steadfast Cause of God, even though all things were created for His sake and He holds the key to the treasuries of the heavens and the earth. Shame on your modesty, O people of the Bayán! By God! I am ashamed of your conduct, and I therefore disown you, O assembly of devils! Alas, alas for His affliction among you! Alas, alas for what has befallen Him and befalls Him at every moment!
:::

### 697

::: {.original lang="ar"}
يا قوم فانصفوا ثمّ تفكّروا اقلّ من ان لو انتم فى تلك الحجبات لم اظهرت نفسى و ما ثمر ظهورى يا ملأ المنافقين قد بعثنى اللّه لخرق الأحجاب و تطهيركم لهذا الظّهور و انتم فعلتم به ما يتذرّف به عيناى و عيون المقدّسين قد ابيضّت وجوه ملل القبل من فعلكم لأنكم احجب منهم و اغفل من ملأ التّورية و الزّبور و الانجيل فيا ليت ما ولدت من امّى و ما اظهرت نفسى بينكم يا ملأ الخائبين فو‌الّذى بعثنى بالحقّ احصيت علم كلّ شیء و كلّ ما كنز فى كنائز حفظ اللّه و ما ستر عن انظر العالمين و لكن ما احصيت نفوساً اشقى منكم و ابعد عنكم لانّا بعد ما فصّلناه فى الألواح و ما نصحنا به انفسكم فى كلّ الأوراق ما ظننّا بأن يظهر فى الملك احد ان يعترض على اللّه الّذى فى قبضته ملكوت ملك السّموات و الأرضين اذا تحيّرنا من خلقكم و لم ادر باىّ كلمة خلقتم يا من تحيّر فيكم و من فعلكم افئدة اهل ملأ العالين ثمّ افئدة المخلصين و المقرّبين كذلك قصصنا لك يا عبد فى هذا اللّوح ما تغرّدت به حمامة البيان حينئذ لدى عرش ربّك العزيز الحميد و انّك انت فاقرأ ما نزل فيه ثمّ احفظ لؤلؤ المعانى عن كلّ خائن سارق من ملأ الشّياطين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Yā qawm fa-anṣifū thumma tafakkarū aqall min an law antum fī tilka al-ḥujubāt lam aẓhartu nafsī wa-mā thamar ẓuhūrī yā malaʾ al-munāfiqīn qad baʿathanī Allāh li-kharq al-aḥjāb wa-taṭhīrikum li-hādhā al-ẓuhūr wa-antum faʿaltum bihi mā yatadharrafa bihi ʿaynāya wa-ʿuyūn al-muqaddasīn qad ibyaḍḍat wujūh milal al-qabl min fiʿlikum li-annakum aḥjab minhum wa-aghfal min malaʾ al-Tawriyya wa-al-Zabūr wa-al-Injīl fa-yā layta mā wulidtu min ummī wa-mā aẓhartu nafsī baynakum yā malaʾ al-khāʾibīn fa-wa-alladhī baʿathanī bi-al-ḥaqq aḥṣaytu ʿilm kull shayʾ wa-kull mā kuniza fī kanāʾiz ḥifẓ Allāh wa-mā sutira ʿan anẓar al-ʿālamīn wa-lākin mā aḥṣaytu nufūsan ashqā minkum wa-abʿad ʿankum li-annā baʿda mā faṣṣalnāhu fī al-alwāḥ wa-mā naṣaḥnā bihi anfusakum fī kull al-awrāq mā ẓanannā bi-an yaẓhara fī al-mulk aḥad an yaʿtariḍa ʿalā Allāh alladhī fī qabḍatihi malakūt mulk al-samāwāt wa-al-araḍīn idhan taḥayyarnā min khalqikum wa-lam adri bi-ayy kalima khuliqtum yā man taḥayyara fīkum wa-min fiʿlikum afʾidat ahl malaʾ al-ʿālīn thumma afʾidat al-mukhliṣīn wa-al-muqarrabīn kadhālika qaṣaṣnā laka yā ʿabd fī hādhā al-lawḥ mā tagharradat bihi ḥamāmat al-bayān ḥīnaʾidh ladā ʿarsh rabbika al-ʿAzīz al-Ḥamīd wa-innaka anta fa-iqraʾ mā nuzzila fīhi thumma iḥfaẓ luʾluʾ al-maʿānī ʿan kull khāʾin sāriq min malaʾ al-shayāṭīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
O people, be fair, then reflect. At the very least, had you remained in those veils, I would not have manifested Myself. What is the fruit of My appearance, O assembly of hypocrites? God sent Me to tear away the veils and purify you for this Revelation, yet you have done to Him what makes My eyes and the eyes of the sanctified shed tears. Your conduct has vindicated the peoples of the past, for you are more veiled than they and more heedless than the people of the Torah, the Psalms, and the Gospel. If only My mother had not given birth to Me, and I had not manifested Myself among you, O assembly of the disappointed! By Him who sent Me with the truth! I have encompassed the knowledge of all things, everything treasured in the repositories of God’s keeping, and whatever is concealed from the most discerning of the world’s people. Yet I have not counted any souls more wretched than you or more distant from you. For after all We set forth in detail in the Tablets, and all the counsel We gave you in every page, We did not think that anyone would appear in the world to object to God, in whose grasp is the dominion of the kingdom of the heavens and the earth. Thus We were bewildered at your creation, and I do not know by what word you were created, O you at whom, and at whose conduct, the hearts of the inhabitants of the exalted Assembly, and then the hearts of the sincere and those brought near, are bewildered! Thus, O servant, We have recounted to you in this Tablet what the Dove of Utterance sang at that time before the throne of your Lord, the Almighty, the All-Praised. Read what has been revealed in it, then guard the pearls of meaning from every treacherous thief among the assembly of devils.
:::

### 698

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و ان وجدت من ذى بصر فانشرها امام عينيه ليشهد و يكون من الفائزين لعلّ اولى الأبصار من عبادنا الأخيار يطّلعن بما ورد على جمال المختار من هؤلآء الفجّار الّذين اتّخذوا العجل لانفسهم ربّا من دون اللّه و يسجدونه فى العشىّ و الأبكار و يكونن من الفرحين و انّك انت لا تحزن عمّا ورد علينا ثمّ اصبر كما صبرنا و انّه لخير ناصر و معين ان اذكر ربّك فى اللّيالى و الأیّام ثمّ انطق بثنآء نفسه بين عباده لعلّ بثنائه تحدث نار حبّه فى قلوب المحسنين و كلّ يقومنّ على ثنآء اللّه ربّهم و ربّ ما يرى و ما لايرى و ربّ آبائكم الأوّلین‌ و الحمد للّه ربّ العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-in wajadta min dhī baṣar fa-unshurhā amāma ʿaynayhi li-yashhada wa-yakūna min al-fāʾizīn laʿalla ulī al-abṣār min ʿibādinā al-akhyār yaṭṭaliʿna bi-mā warada ʿalā jamāl al-Mukhtār min hāʾulāʾ al-fujjār alladhīna ittakhadhū al-ʿijl li-anfusihim rabban min dūn Allāh wa-yasjudūnahu fī al-ʿashiyy wa-al-ibkār wa-yakūnanna min al-fariḥīn wa-innaka anta lā taḥzan ʿammā warada ʿalaynā thumma iṣbir kamā ṣabarnā wa-innahu la-khayr nāṣir wa-muʿīn an udhkur rabbaka fī al-layālī wa-al-ayyām thumma inṭiq bi-thanāʾ nafsihi bayna ʿibādihi laʿalla bi-thanāʾihi taḥduthu nār ḥubbihi fī qulūb al-muḥsinīn wa-kull yaqūmanna ʿalā thanāʾ Allāh rabbihim wa-rabb mā yurā wa-mā lā yurā wa-rabb ābāʾikum al-awwalīn wa-al-ḥamdu li-llāh rabb al-ʿālamīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
If you find someone with insight, spread them before his eyes, so that he may witness and be among those who attain their goal. Perhaps those endowed with insight among Our righteous servants will learn what has befallen the Beauty of the Chosen One at the hands of these wicked people, who have taken the calf as their lord instead of God, prostrate themselves before it evening and morning, and rejoice. Do not grieve over what has befallen Us, but be patient as We have been patient. He is indeed the best helper and supporter. Remember your Lord by night and day, then voice His praise among His servants, so that through His praise the fire of His love may arise in the hearts of those who do good, and all may arise to praise God, their Lord and the Lord of all that is seen and unseen, and the Lord of your forefathers. Praise be to God, the Lord of the worlds.
:::

### 699

::: {.original lang="fa"}
هر صاحب بصر و ادراكى از اين آيات مذكوره البتّه بر حقّ و نفس خود هر دو نوحه نمايد امّا بر حقّ منيع چه كه در دست امثال آن ظالمين مبتلى شده بشأنيكه عين ابداع نديده و سمع اختراع نشنيده و امّا بر نفس خود چه كه بشأنيكه بايد بر اين امر بديع قيام نمايد ننموده‌نسئل اللّه بأن يبعث بسلطانه خلقا ليأت بما فات من هؤلآء كه شايد آن نفوس مقدّسه بآنچه لايق و سزاوار اين ظهوراست قيام نمايند من يطوف حول الرّوح يقول لا تستر فاخرق الأحجاب ثمّ اظهر ما كنز فى السّرّ من علم اللّه المهيمن القيّوم و الّذين يطوفن فى حول العقل يقولن ایّاک ایّاک ان اصبر و لاتفش ما يفزع به هياكل المغلّين و تميّز به صدور المشركين ان الق على العباد ما ينبغى لشأنهم و مقامهم ایّاک ان تلق على الرّضيع مقامات البلوغ او على المحروم اسرار حرم اللّه او على الأصمّ نغمات اللّه العزيز المحبوب
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Har ṣāḥeb-e baṣar va edrākī az īn āyāt-e madhkūre albatte bar Ḥaqq va nafs-e khod har do nowḥe namāyad ammā bar Ḥaqq-e manīʿ che ke dar dast-e amthāl-e ān ẓālemīn mobtalā shode be-shaʾnī ke ʿayn-e ebdāʿ nadīde va samʿ-e ekhterāʿ nashenīde va ammā bar nafs-e khod che ke be-shaʾnī ke bāyad bar īn amr-e badīʿ qīyām namāyad nanamūde nasʾalu Allāh bi-an yabʿatha bi-sulṭānihi khalqan li-yaʾta bi-mā fāta min hāʾulāʾ ke shāyad ān nofūs-e moqaddase be-ānche lāyeq va sazāvār-e īn ẓohūr ast qīyām namāyand man yaṭūfu ḥawla al-Rūḥ yaqūlu lā tastur fa-ikhruq al-aḥjāb thumma aẓhir mā kuniza fī al-sirr min ʿilm Allāh al-Muhaymin al-Qayyūm wa-alladhīna yaṭūfna fī ḥawl al-ʿaql yaqūlna iyyāka iyyāka an iṣbir wa-lā tufshi mā yafzaʿu bihi hayākil al-mughillīn wa-tamayyazu bihi ṣudūr al-mushrikīn an alqi ʿalā al-ʿibād mā yanbaghī li-shaʾnihim wa-maqāmihim iyyāka an tulqi ʿalā al-raḍīʿ maqāmāt al-bulūgh aw ʿalā al-maḥrūm asrār ḥaram Allāh aw ʿalā al-aṣamm naghamāt Allāh al-ʿAzīz al-Maḥbūb.
:::

::: {.translation}
Anyone endowed with sight and understanding will surely, on reading these verses, lament both for God and for himself: for the exalted God, because He has been afflicted at the hands of such oppressors in a manner that the eye of creation has never seen and the ear of existence has never heard; and for himself, because he has not arisen to serve this wondrous Cause as he should. We ask God to raise up, through His sovereignty, a people who will make good what these people have failed to do, so that those sanctified souls may arise to do what is fitting and worthy of this Revelation. The one who circles around the Spirit says, “Do not conceal it! Tear away the veils, then reveal what has been secretly treasured of the knowledge of God, the All-Protecting, the Self-Subsisting.” And those who circle around the intellect say, “Beware, beware! Be patient, and do not divulge what would terrify the embodiments of malice and tear apart the breasts of those who associate partners with God. Impart to the servants what befits their condition and station. Beware of imparting the stations of maturity to a suckling infant, or the mysteries of God’s sanctuary to one who is deprived, or the melodies of God, the Almighty, the Beloved, to the deaf.”
:::

### 700

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اى غير منصف غير بصير چرا از شجره اعراض سؤال ننمودى كه چرا نفسى را كه بيست سال باسمش معروف و موسوم بودى و بكلماتش از براى خودشان ثابت نموده‌ حال فتوى بر قتلش داده و عامل شده آنچه را كه احدى عامل نشده و در كلّ حين بمكر جديد در تضييع امرش مشغول و حال آنكه تو و امثال تو كلّ از كلمه او خلق شده و لكن چه ذكر شود كه آنچه گفته شود ابدا در نفس مغلّين و مشركين تأثير ننموده‌و نخواهد نمود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ey gheyr-e monṣef-e gheyr-e baṣīr cherā az shajare-ye eʿrāḍ soʾāl nanamūdī ke cherā nafsī rā ke bīst sāl be-esmash maʿrūf va mowsūm būdī va be-kalemātash az barā-ye khodeshān thābet namūde ḥāl fatvā bar qatl-ash dāde va ʿāmel shode ānche rā ke aḥadī ʿāmel nashode va dar koll-e ḥīn be-makr-e jadīd dar taḍyīʿ-e amrash mashghūl va ḥāl ānke to va amthāl-e to koll az kaleme-ye ū khalq shode va lāken che dhekr shavad ke ānche gofte shavad abadan dar nafs-e moghellīn va moshrekīn taʾthīr nanamūde va nakhāhad namūd.
:::

::: {.translation}
O unjust and undiscerning one! Why did you not ask the tree of aversion why he has now issued a decree for the death of the One by whose name you were known and designated for twenty years, and by whose words they established their own standing? He has done what no one has ever done, and at every moment he is occupied with a new scheme to undermine His Cause, even though you and all those like you were created by His word. But what can be said? Whatever is said has never had, and will never have, any effect on malicious souls and those who associate partners with God.
:::

### 701

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اين بسى واضح است كه اگر نفسى بجذوه از نار حبّ الهى فايز ميشد ابدا باين كلمات مشغول نميگشت و باين اعتراضات بر سلطان اسماء و صفات وارد نمياورد آنچه شبه آن در ابداع ظاهر نشده فسوف يبعثن اللّه خلقا ينتبّهنّ من كلماته و يعرفنّ مراده و يتوجّهنّ اليه و ينقطعنّ عن العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īn basī vāḍeḥ ast ke agar nafsī be-jadhve az nār-e ḥobb-e elāhī fāʾez mīshod abadan be-īn kalemāt mashghūl namīgasht va be-īn eʿterāḍāt bar Solṭān-e asmāʾ va ṣefāt vāred namīāvard ānche shebh-e ān dar ebdāʿ ẓāher nashode fa-sawfa yabʿathanna Allāh khalqan yantabihunna min kalimātihi wa-yaʿrifanna murādahu wa-yatawajjahunna ilayhi wa-yanqaṭiʿunna ʿan al-ʿālamīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
It is abundantly clear that if a soul had attained even a spark of the fire of divine love, he would never have occupied himself with these words or, through these objections, inflicted on the Sovereign of names and attributes what has no precedent in creation. God will assuredly raise up a people who will be awakened by His words, recognize His intent, turn toward Him, and detach themselves from all the worlds.
:::

### 702

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اينكه نوشته كه جواب ميرزا محمّد على و ميرزا ابو الحسن و ديگران را چه بگويم شما قاضى كاينات نبوده و نيستيد قاضى نفس خود باش و فكر خود را كن كه جواب خدا را چه بگوئى جواب خلق آسانست اى بی‌‌شرم بی‌ حيا در جواب مخلوقى چند اظهار تحيّر نموده‌ و ابدا در فكر جواب حقّ نيفتاده حال انصاف ده تو كه از چند نفر مخلوق اظهار شرم و تحيّر از جواب نموده‌ اين عباد در مقرّ عرش اعظم مقاميكه جميع انبیاء و مقرّبين حاضرند جواب چه بگوئيم فاشهد نفسك فى ذلك الموقف ثمّ ملأ البيان كلّهم اجمعين و نقطة الأولی عن يمين العرش يخاطبك و ايّاهم بفارسى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īnke neveshte ke javāb-e Mīrzā Moḥammad ʿAlī va Mīrzā Abu al-Ḥasan va dīgarān rā che begūyam shomā qāḍī-ye kāʾenāt nabūde va nīstīd qāḍī-ye nafs-e khod bāsh va fekr-e khod rā kon ke javāb-e Khodā rā che begūʾī javāb-e khalq āsān ast ey bī-sharm-e bī-ḥayā dar javāb-e makhlūqī chand eẓhār-e taḥayyor namūde va abadan dar fekr-e javāb-e Ḥaqq nayoftāde ḥāl enṣāf de to ke az chand nafar makhlūq eẓhār-e sharm va taḥayyor az javāb namūde īn ʿebād dar maqarr-e ʿarsh-e aʿẓam maqāmī ke jamīʿ-e anbīyā va moqarrabīn ḥāḍerand javāb che begūʾīm fa-ishhad nafsaka fī dhālika al-mawqif thumma malaʾ al-bayān kullahum ajmaʿīn wa-Nuqṭat al-Ūlā ʿan yamīn al-ʿarsh yukhāṭibuka wa-iyyāhum be-fārsī.
:::

::: {.translation}
As for what you wrote, “What answer should I give Mírzá Muḥammad ʿAlí, Mírzá Abu’l-Ḥasan, and the others?”—you have never been, and are not, the judge of all creation. Be the judge of your own self, and consider what answer you will give God. Answering His creatures is easy. O shameless and immodest one! You have expressed bewilderment about answering a few created beings, yet have never given a thought to answering God. Now be fair: you have expressed shame before a few created beings and bewilderment about how to answer them; what answer are we servants to give at the seat of the Most Great Throne, where all the Prophets and those brought near are present? Behold yourself at that gathering, and then the entire assembly of the Bayán, all together, while the Primal Point, at the right hand of the throne, addresses you and them in Persian.
:::

### 703

::: {.original lang="fa"}
ذكر ميشود تا درست ادراك نمائى ميفرمايد اى ملأ بيان آيا بشما خبر ندادم در كلّ الواح كه بعد از من ظهورى ظاهر خواهد شد البتّه كلّ ميگوئيد بلى و نفسك الحقّ در جميع الواح بشارت فرموده و اخذ عهد آن نيّر اعظم را از كلّ فرموده بعد ميفرمايند كه آيا نگفته‌ام كه آن جمال قدم بآيات اللّه ظاهر ميشود و آيا نفرموده‌ام كه طوريّون در آن مقرّ منصعق و ميّت ميشوند و آيا نفرموده‌ام كه اعلى شجره اثبات از ادنى شجره نفى ميشود و آيا نفرموده‌ام كه هر ذى نورى نزد ضياء انوار وجهش مظلم مشاهده ميشود و آيا نفرموده‌ام كه بنفس ظهور احدى جز ذاتش مطّلع نه و آيا نفرموده‌ام در حين ظهور بآنچه در بيان نازل شده از او محتجب نشويد و آيا نفرموده‌ام بحروفات بيان كه اوّل خلق بيانند از آن جمال قدم محروم نمانيد و آيا نفرموده‌ام كلّ بيان ورقه ايست از اوراق جنّت نزد آن شجره احديّت آيا نفرموده‌ام كه او قادر است بر آنكه نفسى را كه اعلى است از كلّ خلق ردّ فرمايد و آيا نفرموده‌ام كه كلّ بيان خلق اويند در ظهور قبل او
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Dhekr mīshavad tā dorost edrāk namāʾī mīfarmāyad ey malaʾ-e Bayān āyā be-shomā khabar nadādam dar koll-e alvāḥ ke baʿd az man ẓohūrī ẓāher khāhad shod albatte koll mīgūʾīd balā wa-nafsika al-Ḥaqq dar jamīʿ-e alvāḥ beshārat farmūde va akhdh-e ʿahd-e ān nayyer-e aʿẓam rā az koll farmūde baʿd mīfarmāyand ke āyā nagofte-am ke ān Jamāl-e Qedam be-āyāt-e Allāh ẓāher mīshavad va āyā nafarmūde-am ke Ṭūrīyūn dar ān maqarr monṣaʿeq va mayyet mīshavand va āyā nafarmūde-am ke aʿlā shajare-ye ethbāt az adnā shajare-ye nafy mīshavad va āyā nafarmūde-am ke har dhī nūrī nazd-e ḍīyā-ye anvār-e vajhash moẓlem moshāhede mīshavad va āyā nafarmūde-am ke be-nafs-e ẓohūr aḥadī joz dhātash moṭṭaleʿ na va āyā nafarmūde-am dar ḥīn-e ẓohūr be-ānche dar Bayān nāzel shode az ū moḥtajeb nashavīd va āyā nafarmūde-am be-ḥorūfāt-e Bayān ke avval-e khalq-e Bayān-and az ān Jamāl-e Qedam maḥrūm namānīd va āyā nafarmūde-am koll-e Bayān varaqe-īst az owrāq-e jannat nazd-e ān shajare-ye aḥadīyyat āyā nafarmūde-am ke ū qāder ast bar ānke nafsī rā ke aʿlā ast az koll-e khalq radd farmāyad va āyā nafarmūde-am ke koll-e Bayān khalq-e ūyand dar ẓohūr-e qabl-e ū.
:::

::: {.translation}
It is recounted so that you may understand correctly. He says, “O assembly of the Bayán! Did I not inform you in all the Tablets that after Me a Revelation would appear?” You will all surely say, “Yes, by Your own true Self! In all the Tablets You gave these glad tidings and received from everyone a covenant concerning that Most Great Luminary.” He then says, “Did I not say that that Ancient Beauty would appear with the verses of God? Did I not say that the people of Sinai would be struck down and die in that presence? Did I not say that the highest tree of affirmation would become one of the lowest trees of negation? Did I not say that every luminous being would be seen as dark before the radiance of the lights of His face? Did I not say that no one but His own Self knows the Revelation itself? Did I not say that, at the time of His appearance, you should not let what has been revealed in the Bayán veil you from Him? Did I not tell the Letters of the Bayán, who are the first of the creation of the Bayán, not to remain deprived of that Ancient Beauty? Did I not say that the whole Bayán is but a leaf among the leaves of paradise before that Tree of Oneness? Did I not say that He is able to reject a soul who is the most exalted of all creation? Did I not say that all the people of the Bayán are His creation in His previous Revelation?”
:::

### 704

::: {.original lang="fa"}
البتّه جميع را تصديق مينمائيد چه كه كلّ در الواح بيان منصوصا نازل و مسطور مع اين وصاياى لايحصى و نصايح محكمه متقنه بچه دليل و برهان باينجمال مبارك سيف جفا كشيده‌ايد و جميع بر هتك حرمتش قيام نموده‌ايد و اراده سفك دم مطهّرش کرده‌‌ايد و از جميع اشطار باسياف نفاق هجوم آورده‌ايد مع آنكه بحجّتى ظاهر شده كه من از قبل بآن ظاهر شده‌ام و هم‌چنين از قبل قبل محمّد رسول اللّه و از قبل قبل قبل روح اگر بگوئيد از كجا اين آيات من عند اللّه است ميگويم بهمان دليل كه آيات مرا ادراك نموده‌ايد كه من عند اللّه است مع آنكه جميع مقرّيد كه اين آيات بديعه در كلّ اقطار منتشر و در كلّ حين بآياتى تكلّم فرموده كه كلّ نزد كلمه آن معدوم بوده و خواهند بود مع‌ذلك شما نفسى را كه محارب با حقّ است او را ربّ اخذ نموده‌ايد بعضى متمسّك شده‌ايد كه من او را ثمره خوانده‌ام مع آنكه در كتاب من نازل كه اگر مشاهده شود بر من غصنى يا ورقى و ثمرى كه سجده ننمايد از براى آن شمس ظهور در يوم ظهور او نيست از من و راجع نميشود بسوى من
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Albatte jamīʿ rā taṣdīq mīnamāʾīd che ke koll dar alvāḥ-e Bayān manṣūṣan nāzel va masṭūr maʿ-e īn vaṣāyā-ye lā yoḥṣā va naṣāyeḥ-e moḥkame-ye motqane be-che dalīl va borhān be-īn Jamāl-e mobārak seyf-e jafā keshīde-īd va jamīʿ bar hatk-e ḥormatash qīyām namūde-īd va erāde-ye safk-e dam-e moṭahharash karde-īd va az jamīʿ-e ashṭār be-asyāf-e nefāq hojūm āvarde-īd maʿ-e ānke be-ḥojjatī ẓāher shode ke man az qabl be-ān ẓāher shode-am va ham-chenīn az qabl-e qabl Moḥammad Rasūl Allāh va az qabl-e qabl-e qabl Rūḥ agar begūʾīd az kojā īn āyāt min ʿind Allāh ast mīgūyam be-hamān dalīl ke āyāt-e marā edrāk namūde-īd ke min ʿind Allāh ast maʿ-e ānke jamīʿ moqerrīd ke īn āyāt-e badīʿe dar koll-e aqṭār montasher va dar koll-e ḥīn be-āyātī takallom farmūde ke koll nazd-e kaleme-ye ān maʿdūm būde va khāhand būd maʿa dhālek shomā nafsī rā ke moḥāreb bā Ḥaqq ast ū rā rabb akhdh namūde-īd baʿḍī motamassek shode-īd ke man ū rā thamare khānde-am maʿ-e ānke dar ketāb-e man nāzel ke agar moshāhede shavad bar man ghoṣnī yā varaqī va thamarī ke sajde nanamāyad az barā-ye ān shams-e ẓohūr dar yowm-e ẓohūr-e ū nīst az man va rājeʿ namīshavad be-sū-ye man.
:::

::: {.translation}
“You will surely acknowledge all of these, for they are all explicitly revealed and recorded in the Tablets of the Bayán. Despite these countless counsels and firm, conclusive admonitions, by what evidence or proof have you drawn the sword of oppression against this blessed Beauty, all arisen to violate His sanctity, sought to shed His pure blood, and attacked Him from every side with the swords of hypocrisy? Yet He has appeared with the very proof with which I appeared before, and with which Muḥammad, the Messenger of God, appeared before that, and the Spirit before that. If you ask, ‘How do we know that these verses are from God?’ I say: by the same evidence through which you recognized that My verses are from God. Moreover, you all acknowledge that these wondrous verses have spread throughout every region, and that at every moment He has uttered verses before a single word of which all have been, and will be, as nothing. Despite this, you have taken as your lord someone who is at war with God. Some of you cling to the fact that I called him a fruit, although it is revealed in My Book that if a branch, a leaf, or a fruit is seen upon Me that does not prostrate itself before that Sun of Revelation on the day of His appearance, it is not of Me and does not return to Me.”
:::

### 705

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و بعضى متمسّك كه من او را مرآت اخذ نموده‌ام مع آنكه صد‌هزار امثال او بنصّ من از يك تجلّى شمس ظاهر و مشرق و حال آنكه امر آن مرآت را هم ندانسته‌ايد بر فرض تسليم كه او آن مرآت باشد شكّى نيست كه بقول من او را مرآت دانسته‌ايد و من منصوصاً فرموده‌ام كه از آنچه نازل شده در كتاب از آن مظهر ربّ الأرباب‌ محجوب نمانيد و هم‌چنين فرموده‌ام كه طوريّون نزد آن ظهور اعظم ميّت و لاشیء ميشوند و صد‌هزار امثال آن مرايا نزد نفسى از آن نفوس طوريّه مشرقه از افق احديّه معدوم صرف بوده و خواهند بود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va baʿḍī motamassek ke man ū rā merʾāt akhdh namūde-am maʿ-e ānke ṣad hezār amthāl-e ū be-naṣṣ-e man az yek tajallī-ye shams ẓāher va moshreq va ḥāl ānke amr-e ān merʾāt rā ham nadāneste-īd bar farḍ-e taslīm ke ū ān merʾāt bāshad shakkī nīst ke be-qowl-e man ū rā merʾāt dāneste-īd va man manṣūṣan farmūde-am ke az ānche nāzel shode dar ketāb az ān maẓhar-e Rabb al-Arbāb maḥjūb namānīd va ham-chenīn farmūde-am ke Ṭūrīyūn nazd-e ān ẓohūr-e aʿẓam mayyet va lā shayʾ mīshavand va ṣad hezār amthāl-e ān marāyā nazd-e nafsī az ān nofūs-e Ṭūrīyye-ye moshreqe az ofoq-e aḥadīyye maʿdūm-e ṣerf būde va khāhand būd.
:::

::: {.translation}
“Some cling to the fact that I designated him a mirror, although, according to My explicit text, a hundred thousand like him appear and shine forth through a single effulgence of the Sun. Yet you have not even understood the matter of that mirror. Even supposing that he is that mirror, there is no doubt that you have recognized him as a mirror because of My words. And I explicitly stated that you should not allow what has been revealed in the Book to veil you from that Manifestation of the Lord of Lords. I also stated that the people of Sinai would become dead and as nothing before that Most Great Revelation. A hundred thousand like those mirrors have been, and will be, sheer nothingness before a single one of those Sinaitic souls shining from the horizon of oneness.”
:::

### 706

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اگر بگوئيد كه اين مرآت هم حال همين دعوى را نموده‌شكّى نيست كه در اين قول كاذب بوده چه كه مخصوص نازل فرموده‌ام كه اگر مرآت دعوى شمسى نمايد نزد شمس واضح است كه او شبحى است از او و از همين بيان من محقّق كه مرآت على زعم شما دعوى شمسى خواهد نمود و همين نفس ادّعاى او در اين ایّام دليل بر كذب او است چه كه بعد از ظهور اشراق شمس احديّه اعتراضاً على نفسه و بغياً على كينونته و استكباراً على ذاته و الحاداً فى امره باين كلمات متكلّم شده و اكثرى از شما هم متابعت او نموده‌ايد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va agar begūʾīd ke īn merʾāt ham ḥāl hamīn daʿvā rā namūde shakkī nīst ke dar īn qowl kādheb būde che ke makhṣūṣ nāzel farmūde-am ke agar merʾāt daʿvā-ye shamsī namāyad nazd-e shams vāḍeḥ ast ke ū shabaḥī ast az ū va az hamīn bayān-e man moḥaqqaq ke merʾāt ʿalā zaʿm-e shomā daʿvā-ye shamsī khāhad namūd va hamīn nafs-e eddeʿā-ye ū dar īn ayyām dalīl bar kedhb-e ū ast che ke baʿd az ẓohūr-e eshrāq-e shams-e aḥadīyye iʿtirāḍan ʿalā nafsihi wa-baghyan ʿalā kaynūnatihi wa-istikbāran ʿalā dhātihi wa-ilḥādan fī amrihi be-īn kalemāt motakallem shode va aktharī az shomā ham motābaʿat-e ū namūde-īd.
:::

::: {.translation}
“If you say that this mirror has now made the same claim, there is no doubt that he has lied in saying this. For I specifically revealed that if a mirror should claim to be the sun, it is clear to the Sun that it is only an image of Him. From this very statement of Mine, it is established that the mirror, as you regard him, would claim to be the sun. His very claim in these days is proof of his falsehood, for after the dawning radiance of the Sun of Oneness appeared, he uttered these words in opposition to His Self, in rebellion against His Being, in arrogance before His Essence, and in impiety toward His Cause. And most of you have followed him.”
:::

### 707

::: {.original lang="ar"}
افّ لكم يا ملأ البيان ثمّ افّ لكم يا ملأ البيان ثمّ افّ لكم يا ملأ البيان ثمّ افّ لكم الى آخر الّذى لا آخر له لانّ من فعلكم ذاب قلبی‌ و احترق كبدى و تشبّك حشائى و تقطّعت اعضائى و تزلزلت اركانى و اقشعرّ جلدى و اهتزّت نفسى و جنّت كينونتى و ضجّ سرّى و حزن ظاهرى و باطنى و اوّلى و آخرى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Uffin lakum yā malaʾa al-Bayān, thumma uffin lakum yā malaʾa al-Bayān, thumma uffin lakum yā malaʾa al-Bayān, thumma uffin lakum ilā ākhiri alladhī lā ākhira lahu, li-anna min fiʿlikum dhāba qalbī wa-iḥtaraqa kabidī wa-tashabbaka ḥashāʾī wa-taqaṭṭaʿat aʿḍāʾī wa-tazalzalat arkānī wa-iqshaʿarra jildī wa-ihtazzat nafsī wa-junnat kaynūnatī wa-ḍajja sirrī wa-ḥazina ẓāhirī wa-bāṭinī wa-awwalī wa-ākhirī.
:::

::: {.translation}
“Shame on you, O people of the Bayān! Again, shame on you, O people of the Bayān! Again, shame on you, O people of the Bayān! Again, shame on you, without end! For because of your deeds My heart has melted, My liver has burned, My entrails have become entangled, My limbs have been torn apart, My frame has been shaken, My skin has shuddered, My soul has trembled, My being has been driven mad, My inmost self has cried out, and My outward and inward being, My beginning and My end, have been overcome with sorrow.”
:::

### 708

::: {.original lang="fa"}
آنچه شما ذكر نموده‌و مينمائيد بمن نسبت ميدهيد و بقول من باو متمسّك شده‌ايد و حجّيت نفس من ببيان ثابت و مخصوص فرموده‌ام ببيان از نفس رحمن محتجب نمانيد لم ادر بعد ذلك باىّ عذر تتمسّكون و باىّ حبل تتشبّثون بامر من ناظر نيستيد و نصح اللّه را نپذيرفتيد نفسى را كه حال محارب باللّه است باسمى از اسماء موسوم نموده‌ بنفس من محاربه و مجادله مينمائيد مع آنكه مظاهر كلّ اسماء را تصريحا فرموده‌ام كه در آن ظهور عزّ تقديس خادمند وظائف چنانچه فرموده‌ام
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ānchih shumā dhikr namūdih va mīnamāyīd bi-man nisbat mīdahīd va bi-qawl-i man bi-ū mutamassik shudih-īd va ḥujjiyyat-i nafs-i man bi-Bayān thābit va makhṣūṣ farmūdih-am bi-Bayān az nafs-i Raḥmān muḥtajib namānīd. Lam adri baʿda dhālika bi-ayyi ʿudhrin tatamassakūna wa-bi-ayyi ḥablin tatashabbathūn. Bi-amr-i man nāẓir nīstīd va nuṣḥ-i Allāh rā napadhīruftīd. Nafsī rā kih ḥāl muḥārib bi-Allāh ast bi-ismī az asmāʾ mawsūm namūdih bi-nafs-i man muḥāribih va mujādilih mīnamāyīd, maʿa ānkih maẓāhir-i kull-i asmāʾ rā taṣrīḥan farmūdih-am kih dar ān ẓuhūr-i ʿizz-i taqdīs khādimand vaẓāʾif, chunānchih farmūdih-am.
:::

::: {.translation}
“What you have mentioned and continue to mention, you attribute to Me, and it is on the strength of My words that you have clung to him. The authority of My own Self is established through the Bayān, and I have specifically stated that you must not let the Bayān veil you from the Person of the All-Merciful. I do not know, after this, what excuse you will cling to or what cord you will grasp. You pay no heed to My command and have not accepted God’s counsel. You have designated a soul who is now at war with God by one of the names, and you wage war and dispute with My own Self, even though I have explicitly stated that the manifestations of all the names are servants in their duties in that Revelation of sanctified glory, as I have stated:”
:::

### 709

::: {.original lang="ar"}
ان اقول انّه واحد فذلك اسم من اسمائه وان اقول انّه سبّوح فظهر ذلك الاسم اسم من اسمائه و ان اقول انّه قدّوس فهو الّذى يتجلّى بذلك الاسم بامثاله و ان اقول انّه عزيز فكلّ عزيز ساجد لعلوّ عزّته و ان اقول انّه محبوب فكلّ محبوب قد شغف فى حبّ عرفانه و جلال عزّته و ان اقول انّه مهيمن فهو الّذى من يستدل يوم ظهوره قد جعله اللّه مهيمنا على كلّ شیء بأمره و ان اقول انّه قيّوم فذلك مظهر احد من قوّام بساط احديّته فتعالى تعالى ذكره
:::

::: {.transliteration}
In aqūlu innahu wāḥidun fa-dhālika ismun min asmāʾihi wa-in aqūlu innahu subbūḥun fa-ẓahara dhālika al-ismu ismun min asmāʾihi wa-in aqūlu innahu quddūsun fa-huwa alladhī yata jallā bi-dhālika al-ismi bi-amthālihi wa-in aqūlu innahu ʿazīzun fa-kullu ʿazīzin sājidun li-ʿuluwwi ʿizzatihi wa-in aqūlu innahu maḥbūbun fa-kullu maḥbūbin qad shaghifa fī ḥubbi ʿirfānihi wa-jalāli ʿizzatihi wa-in aqūlu innahu muhayminun fa-huwa alladhī man yastadillu yawma ẓuhūrihi qad jaʿalahu Allāhu muhayminan ʿalā kulli shayʾin bi-amrihi wa-in aqūlu innahu qayyūmun fa-dhālika maẓharu aḥadin min quwwāmi bisāṭi aḥadiyyatihi fa-taʿālā taʿālā dhikruhu.
:::

::: {.translation}
“If I say that He is One, that is one of His names; and if I say that He is All-Glorious, that name appears as one of His names; and if I say that He is Most Holy, He is the One who reveals Himself through that name to those like Him. If I say that He is Mighty, every mighty one prostrates before the loftiness of His might; and if I say that He is Beloved, every beloved one is consumed with love for the recognition of Him and the majesty of His might. If I say that He is All-Protecting, He is the One who, by His command, causes God to make whoever adduces proof on the day of His appearance a protector over all things. If I say that He is Self-Subsisting, that is the manifestation of one of those who stand upon the expanse of His oneness. Exalted, exalted be His remembrance!”
:::

### 710

::: {.original lang="fa"}
ثمّ تعالى تعالى شأنه كه معنى پارسى آن اينست كه اگر بگويم او واحد است اين واحد يكى از اسماء او بوده اگر بگويم او سبّوح است محل ظهور اين اسم اسمى از اسماء او بوده اگر بگويم او قدّوس است او است آنچنان نفسيكه تجلّى فرموده و ميفرمايد باين اسم بامثال او و اگر بگويم او عزيز است هر عزيزى ساجد است از براى علوّ عزّت او و اگر بگويم او محبوب است هر محبوبی‌ شقّ نموده‌ پرده قلب خود را در دوستى و محبّت او و اگر بگويم او مهيمن است او است آن سلطانيكه هر نفسى استدلال نمايد بدليل او در يوم ظهور او بتحقيق ميگرداند او را خدا مهيمن بر كلّ شیء بامر او و اگر بگويم او قيّوم است پس آن مظهر يكى از قائمين بساط احديّت او است مع آنكه باين تصريح جميع اسماء حسنى را از خدّام درگهش ذكر نمودم و آن جوهر مقصود و طلعت موعود را از كلّ مقدّس و منزّه و مبرّا مع‌ذلك اسمى از كتاب من اخذ نموده‌ايد و بآن اسم تشبّث نموده‌وارد آورده‌ايد آنچه را كه هيچ ملّتى از قبل وارد نياورده
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Thumma taʿālā taʿālā shaʾnuhu, kih maʿnī-yi pārsī-yi ān īn ast kih agar bigūyam ū vāḥid ast īn vāḥid yakī az asmāʾ-i ū būdih, agar bigūyam ū subbūḥ ast maḥall-i ẓuhūr-i īn ism ismī az asmāʾ-i ū būdih, agar bigūyam ū quddūs ast ū ast ānchunān nafsī kih tajallī farmūdih va mīfarmāyad bi-īn ism bi-amthāl-i ū, va agar bigūyam ū ʿazīz ast har ʿazīzī sājid ast az barā-yi ʿuluvv-i ʿizzat-i ū, va agar bigūyam ū maḥbūb ast har maḥbūbī shaqq namūdih pardih-yi qalb-i khud rā dar dūstī va maḥabbat-i ū, va agar bigūyam ū muhaymin ast ū ast ān sulṭānī kih har nafsī istidlāl namāyad bi-dalīl-i ū dar yawm-i ẓuhūr-i ū bi-taḥqīq mīgardānad ū rā Khudā muhaymin bar kull-i shayʾ bi-amr-i ū, va agar bigūyam ū qayyūm ast pas ān maẓhar yakī az qāʾimīn-i bisāṭ-i aḥadiyyat-i ū ast. Maʿa ānkih bi-īn taṣrīḥ jamīʿ-i asmāʾ-i ḥusnā rā az khuddām-i dargahash dhikr namūdam va ān jawhar-i maqṣūd va ṭalʿat-i mawʿūd rā az kull muqaddas va munazzah va mubarrā, maʿa dhālik ismī az kitāb-i man akhdh namūdih-īd va bi-ān ism tashabbuth namūdih vārid āvardih-īd ānchih rā kih hīch millatī az qabl vārid nayāvardih.
:::

::: {.translation}
“And exalted, exalted be His station!” Its meaning in Persian is this: “If I say that He is One, this One is one of His names. If I say that He is All-Glorious, the locus of the manifestation of this name is one of His names. If I say that He is Most Holy, He is that very Person who has revealed and continues to reveal Himself through this name to those like Him. If I say that He is Mighty, every mighty one prostrates before the loftiness of His might. If I say that He is Beloved, every beloved one has torn the veil of his own heart in affection and love for Him. If I say that He is All-Protecting, He is that Sovereign by whose command God assuredly makes every soul who adduces His proof on the day of His appearance a protector over all things. If I say that He is Self-Subsisting, that manifestation is one of those who stand upon the expanse of His oneness.” “Although I thus explicitly described all the most beautiful names as servants at His threshold, and that desired Essence and promised Countenance as sanctified, exalted, and free from them all, you have nevertheless taken a name from My Book, clung to that name, and inflicted what no religious community has ever inflicted before.”
:::

### 711

::: {.original lang="fa"}
كذلك نطق لسان اللّه الملك المقتدر العلىّ العظيم اين بيانات نقطه اولى روح ما سواه فداه آيا نفسى قادر است بر جواب لا و اللّه بل جميع منفعل و خجل و شرمساريم چه كه نفوسيكه مقبل شده‌اند على ما هو عليه بشرايط اقبال قيام ننموده‌اند و نفوس معرضين معلوم كه چه ارتكاب نموده‌ و مينمايند مع آنكه بنصّ نقطه اولى جميع اسماء حسنى از مهيمن و قیّوم و فوق آن و دون آن جميع نفوسى هستند كه در امر اين ظهور بديع ببيّنه خود اين ظهور استدلال نمايند ديگر ملاحظه كن شأن نفوسيكه ببيان و قلم در اثبات اين ظهور اعظم استدلال نموده‌و نوشته‌اند آنچه را كه بر آن قلوب مجرّده القا شده تاللّه انّهم من اعلى الخلق و ابهاهم بحيث ما سبقهم احد من قبل و لن يسبقهم نفس من الآخرین
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Kadhālika naṭaqa lisānu Allāhi al-Maliki al-Muqtadiri al-ʿAliyyi al-ʿAẓīm. Īn bayānāt-i Nuqṭih-yi Ūlā rūḥ-i mā sivāh fidāh āyā nafsī qādir ast bar javāb? Lā wa-Allāh, bal jamīʿ munfaʿil va khajil va sharmsārīm, chih kih nufūsī kih muqbil shudih-and ʿalā mā huwa ʿalayhi bi-sharāyiṭ-i iqbāl qiyām nanamūdih-and va nufūs-i muʿriḍīn maʿlūm kih chih irtikāb namūdih va mīnamāyand. Maʿa ānkih bi-naṣṣ-i Nuqṭih-yi Ūlā jamīʿ-i asmāʾ-i ḥusnā az Muhaymin va Qayyūm va fawq-i ān va dūn-i ān jamīʿ nufūsī hastand kih dar amr-i īn ẓuhūr-i badīʿ bi-bayyin ih-yi khud-i īn ẓuhūr istidlāl namāyand. Dīgar mulāḥiẓih kun shaʾn-i nufūsī kih bi-bayān va qalam dar ithbāt-i īn ẓuhūr-i aʿẓam istidlāl namūdih va nivishtih-and ānchih rā kih bar ān qulūb-i mujarradih ilqā shudih. Ta-Allāhi innahum min aʿlā al-khalqi wa-abhāhum bi-ḥaythu mā sabaqahum aḥadun min qablu wa-lan yasbiqahum nafsun mina al-ākhirīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Thus has spoken the Tongue of God, the King, the All-Powerful, the Most High, the Most Great. These are the words of the Primal Point—may the soul of all else be sacrificed for Him. Is any soul capable of answering them? No, by God! Rather, we are all abashed, ashamed, and embarrassed, for those souls who have turned toward Him have not fulfilled the conditions of turning toward Him as they truly require, while it is evident what the souls who turn away have perpetrated and continue to perpetrate. Yet, according to the explicit text of the Primal Point, all the most beautiful names, from the All-Protecting and the Self-Subsisting to those above and below them, are all souls who establish the truth of this wondrous Revelation by the proof of this Revelation itself. Consider, then, the station of those souls who, through speech and writing, have adduced proofs establishing this Most Great Revelation and have written what has been cast upon those detached hearts. By God, they are among the most exalted and most glorious of creation, such that no one before them has surpassed them, nor will any soul among those to come surpass them.
:::

### 712

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اى نفس امّاره چرا بذكر آن نفوس مشغول شدى و اظهار تحيّر در جواب نمودى و تنبّه ننمودى از فعل نفوسى كه در سبيل اين امر جان دادند و فعل هر يك در اثبات اين ظهور ابدع امنع برهانى بود واضح و حجّتى لائح بين السّموات و الأرضين از جمله محبوب الشّهداء جناب آقا سيّد اسمعيل زواره كه بدست خود حبّاً لهذا الظّهور سر فدا نمود و هيچ نفسى در زهد و تقوى و ورع و فضل و علم او باللّه منكر نبوده از فعل چنين نفسى مهتدى نشدى و ذكر نفوسى كه حال معلوم نيست كه در چه صراط قائمند بين يدى العرش فرستاده و لعلّ اللّه يؤيّدهم على امره و ينقطعهم عنك و عن امثالك و يجعلهم من المخلصين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ay nafs-i ammārih chirā bi-dhikr-i ān nufūs mashghūl shudī va iẓhār-i taḥayyur dar javāb namūdī va tanabbuh nanamūdī az fiʿl-i nufūsī kih dar sabīl-i īn amr jān dādand va fiʿl-i har yak dar ithbāt-i īn ẓuhūr-i abdaʿ-i amnaʿ burhānī būd vāḍiḥ va ḥujjatī lāʾiḥ bayna al-samāwāti wa-al-araḍīn. Az jumlih Maḥbūb al-Shuhadā Janāb-i Āqā Siyyid Ismāʿīl-i Zavārih kih bi-dast-i khud ḥubban li-hādhā al-ẓuhūr sar fidā namūd va hīch nafsī dar zuhd va taqvā va varaʿ va faḍl va ʿilm-i ū bi-Allāh munkir nabūdih. Az fiʿl-i chunīn nafsī muhtadī nashudī va dhikr-i nufūsī kih ḥāl maʿlūm nīst kih dar chih ṣirāṭ qāʾimand bayna yaday al-ʿarsh firistādih, va laʿalla Allāha yuʾayyiduhum ʿalā amrihi wa-yanqaṭiʿuhum ʿanka wa-ʿan amthālika wa-yajʿalahum mina al-mukhliṣīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
O commanding self, why did you occupy yourself with mentioning those souls and express bewilderment at answering, yet take no heed of the deeds of souls who gave their lives in the path of this Cause? The deed of each was a clear proof and a shining testimony, between the heavens and the earths, establishing this most wondrous, most unassailable Revelation. Among them was the Beloved of Martyrs, Āqā Siyyid Ismāʿīl of Zavārih, who sacrificed his life by his own hand out of love for this Revelation. No soul denied his asceticism, piety, devoutness, learning, or knowledge of God. You were not guided by the deed of such a soul, but sent before the Throne an account of souls whose present path is unknown. May God strengthen them in His Cause, detach them from you and those like you, and make them among the sincere.
:::

### 713

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بارى لازم شد كه تفصيل جناب سيّد شهيد عليه بهآء اللّه و عليه عزّ اللّه و عليه نور اللّه و عليه كبريآء اللّه و عليه سرّ اللّه و عليه عظمة اللّه و عليه ضيآء اللّه و عليه ثنآء اللّه و ثنآء كلّ شیء و ثنآء العالمين در اينمقام ذكر شود كه شايد مطّلع شوى بر آن نفوسى كه نقطه بيان جلّ اقتداره خبر فرموده كه قبل از ظهور آن شمس احديّه بنار حبّش مشتعل شوند چنانچه مخاطباً لظهور بعد ميفرمايند كه مضمون پارسى آن اين است قوله عزّ اعزازه اگر چه عباد كلّ از تو محجوب بوده و خواهند بود و لكن از براى تو عبادى هم خواهد خلق شد كه قبل از ظهور تو بنار محبّت تو مشتعل گردند چنانچه سيّد مذكور قبل از ظهور مشتعل شده و البتّه امثال آن نفس هم ظاهر خواهند شد و لو انتم و امثالكم تنكرون او تكفرون حكايت آن شهيد آنكه وارد عراق شدند و جوار بيت اعظم بيت آقا محمّد رضا عليه بهآء اللّه منزل و مقرّ گرفتند اسم مذكور از حضرت ابهى مستدعى شده كه وقتى از اوقات ببيت او تشريف ببرند چند يوم تأخير افتاد و در جواب توقّف فرمودند تا آنكه يومى از ایّام قبول فرموده و بآن مقرّ تشريف بردند و جناب مذكور بقدر استطاعت خود مجلسى آراست و چند سينى از مركّبات و ميوه و حلويات بحضور آورد اذاً توجّه وجه اللّه الى وجه الّذى استشهد فى سبيله و خاطبه تعال و كلّ ما حضر بين يديك من الآء اللّه و نعمائه
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bārī lāzim shud kih tafṣīl-i Janāb-i Siyyid-i shahīd, ʿalayhi bahāʾu Allāh wa-ʿalayhi ʿizzu Allāh wa-ʿalayhi nūru Allāh wa-ʿalayhi kibriyāʾu Allāh wa-ʿalayhi sirru Allāh wa-ʿalayhi ʿaẓamatu Allāh wa-ʿalayhi ḍiyāʾu Allāh wa-ʿalayhi thanāʾu Allāh wa-thanāʾu kulli shayʾin wa-thanāʾu al-ʿālamīn, dar īn maqām dhikr shavad kih shāyad muṭṭaliʿ shavī bar ān nufūsī kih Nuqṭih-yi Bayān jalla iqtidāruhu khabar farmūdih kih qabl az ẓuhūr-i ān shams-i aḥadiyyih bi-nār-i ḥubbash mushtaʿil shavand. Chunānchih mukhāṭiban li-ẓuhūr-i baʿd mīfarmāyand kih maḍmūn-i pārsī-yi ān īn ast, qawluhu ʿazza iʿzāzuhu: agar chih ʿibād kull az tu maḥjūb būdih va khvāhand būd va lākin az barā-yi tu ʿibādī ham khvāhad khalq shud kih qabl az ẓuhūr-i tu bi-nār-i maḥabbat-i tu mushtaʿil gardand. Chunānchih Siyyid-i madhkūr qabl az ẓuhūr mushtaʿil shudih va al-battih amthāl-i ān nafs ham ẓāhir khvāhand shud, wa-law antum wa-amthālukum tunkirūna aw takfurūn. Ḥikāyat-i ān shahīd ānkih vārid-i ʿIrāq shudand va jivār-i Bayt-i Aʿẓam bayt-i Āqā Muḥammad Riḍā ʿalayhi bahāʾu Allāh manzil va maqarr giriftand. Ism-i madhkūr az Ḥaḍrat-i Abhā mustadʿī shudih kih vaqtī az awqāt bi-bayt-i ū tashrīf bibarand. Chand yawm taʾkhīr uftād va dar javāb tavaqquf farmūdand tā ānkih yawmī az ayyām qabūl farmūdih va bi-ān maqarr tashrīf burdand va Janāb-i madhkūr bi-qadr-i istiṭāʿat-i khud majlisī ārāst va chand sīnī az murakkabāt va mīvih va ḥalaviyyāt bi-ḥuḍūr āvard. Idhan tawajjaha wajhu Allāhi ilā wajhi alladhī istushhida fī sabīlihi wa-khāṭabahu taʿāl wa-kul mā ḥaḍara bayna yadayka min ālāʾi Allāhi wa-naʿmāʾihi.
:::

::: {.translation}
It has therefore become necessary to recount here the story of the martyred Siyyid—upon him be the glory of God, the might of God, the light of God, the grandeur of God, the mystery of God, the greatness of God, the radiance of God, the praise of God, the praise of all things, and the praise of the worlds—so that perhaps you may learn of those souls of whom the Point of the Bayān—glorious is His power—foretold that, before the appearance of that Sun of Oneness, they would be set ablaze with the fire of His love. Thus, addressing the subsequent Manifestation, He says, in words whose substance in Persian is as follows—His words, exalted be His honor: “Although the servants have all been, and will remain, veiled from You, yet servants will also be created for You who, before Your appearance, will be set ablaze with the fire of Your love.” Thus the aforementioned Siyyid was set ablaze before the Revelation, and others like that soul will assuredly appear, even though you and those like you deny or disbelieve. The story of that martyr is this: he arrived in Iraq and took up residence near the Most Great House, in the house of Āqā Muḥammad Riḍā—upon him be the glory of God. The aforementioned person requested that the Most Glorious One visit his house at some time. Several days passed, and He deferred His reply until one day He accepted and went to that dwelling. The aforementioned Siyyid arranged a gathering according to his means and brought into His presence several trays of citrus fruits, other fruit, and sweets. Then the Face of God turned toward the face of him who was martyred in His path and addressed him: “Come and eat what has been set before you of God’s favors and bounties.”
:::

### 714

::: {.original lang="fa"}
انّه تكلّم بين يدى اللّه بخضوع و خشوع و صريخ و انابة و قال اريد من بديع مواهبك بأن ترزقنى من نعمائك الرّوحانيّة اذا اشتعل وجه الرّوح ثمّ قال تعال يا عبد و امر بجلوسه امام وجهه ثمّ تكلّم لسان اللّه بكلمات يترشّح منها رشحات المعانى على كلّ ما كان و ما يكون و انّى لم اقدر ان اصفها او اذكرها و لم ادر ما انفق عليه يد العناية من نعمائه المكنونة الرّوحانيّة بحيث استجذبت منها نفسه و روحه و كينونته و ذاته و اخذته غلبات الشّوق على شأن غفل عن نفسه و عن كلّ من فى السّموات و الأرضين فتوجّه بسرّه و جهره الى محبوب العالمين الى ان انتهى المجلس و رجع الرّوح الى مقرّه
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Innahu takallama bayna yaday Allāhi bi-khuḍūʿin wa-khushūʿin wa-ṣarīkhin wa-inābatin wa-qāla urīdu min badīʿi mawāhibika bi-an tarzuqanī min naʿmāʾika al-rūḥāniyyah. Idhan ishtaʿala wajhu al-Rūḥi thumma qāla taʿāl yā ʿabd wa-amara bi-julūsihi amāma wajhihi thumma takallama lisānu Allāhi bi-kalimātin yatarashshaḥu minhā rashaḥātu al-maʿānī ʿalā kulli mā kāna wa-mā yakūn wa-innī lam aqdir an aṣifahā aw adhkurahā wa-lam adri mā anfaqa ʿalayhi yadu al-ʿināyati min naʿmāʾihi al-maknūnati al-rūḥāniyyati bi-ḥaythu istajdh ab at minhā nafsuhu wa-rūḥuhu wa-kaynūnatuhu wa-dhātuhu wa-akhadhat-hu ghalabātu al-shawqi ʿalā shaʾnin ghafala ʿan nafsihi wa-ʿan kulli man fī al-samāwāti wa-al-araḍīn fa-tawajjaha bi-sirrihi wa-jahrihi ilā Maḥbūbi al-ʿālamīn ilā an intahā al-majlisu wa-rajaʿa al-Rūḥu ilā maqarrihi.
:::

::: {.translation}
He spoke before God with humility, reverence, cries, and supplication, saying, “I desire, from Your wondrous gifts, that You grant me a share of Your spiritual bounties.” Then the face of the Spirit blazed, and He said, “Come, O servant,” and bade him sit before His face. Then the Tongue of God spoke words from which drops of meaning rained upon all that has been and will be. I could neither describe nor recount them, nor do I know what hidden spiritual bounties the hand of providence bestowed upon him, such that his soul, his spirit, his being, and his essence were enraptured by them. The overpowering force of longing seized him so completely that he became oblivious to himself and to all who are in the heavens and the earths. Inwardly and outwardly he turned toward the Beloved of the worlds, until the gathering ended and the Spirit returned to His dwelling.
:::

### 715

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و لكن انّه بعد استماع كلمات اللّه و ما ذاق عمّا اراد ما شهد احد فى نفسه سكوناً و قراراً و قضت عليه ایّام معدودات و فى كلّ حين يزداد شوقه و يشتدّ شغفه باللّه بارئه الى ان حضر فى فجر يوم من الأیّام و كنس بعمامته فنآء البيت و رجع و اخذ سكّيناً و تجنّب عن العباد و خرج عن المدينة الى ورد شاطى الشّط قام مقبلاً الى البيت بيد اخذ لحاه و بيد آخر قطع حنجره حبّاً للّه المقتدر المهيمن القيّوم اذا ارتفع بين النّاس ضوضآء و ارتفعت الصّياح من كلّ النّفوس و اجتمعوا فى حوله خلق كثير و راوا بانّ السّكين كان بيده و وضع يده على صدره فتحيّر بذلك كلّ الوجود ثمّ اهل ملأ الأعلی ثمّ اهل مداين الكبريا ثمّ اهل ملكوت الأسماء و جبروت البقآء و كلّهم صلّوا عليه و كبّروا على وجهه و نزلوا عليه و طافوا فى حوله و استنشقوا روايح حبّه و انّى لو اذكر ما ظهر فى ذلك اليوم انّك لن تقبل و لن تستطيع ان تعرف و كان اللّه على ما اقول شهيد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-lākin innahu baʿda istimāʿi kalimāti Allāhi wa-mā dhāqa ʿammā arāda mā shahida aḥadun fī nafsihi sukūnan wa-qarāran wa-qaḍat ʿalayhi ayyāmun maʿdūdātun wa-fī kulli ḥīnin yazdādu shawquhu wa-yashtaddu shaghafuhu bi-Allāhi bāriʾihi ilā an ḥaḍara fī fajri yawmin mina al-ayyāmi wa-kanasa bi-ʿimāmatihi fināʾa al-bayti wa-rajaʿa wa-akhadha sikkīnan wa-tajannaba ʿani al-ʿibādi wa-kharaja ʿani al-madīnati ilā wardi shāṭiʾi al-shaṭṭi qāma muqbilan ilā al-bayti bi-yadin akhadha liḥāhu wa-bi-yadin ākhar qaṭaʿa ḥanjarahu ḥubban li-Allāhi al-Muqtadiri al-Muhaymini al-Qayyūm. Idhan irtafaʿa bayna al-nāsi ḍawḍāʾun wa-irtafaʿati al-ṣiyāḥu min kulli al-nufūsi wa-ijtamaʿū fī ḥawlihi khalqun kathīrun wa-raʾaw bi-anna al-sikkīna kāna bi-yadihi wa-waḍaʿa yadahu ʿalā ṣadrihi fa-taḥayyara bi-dhālika kullu al-wujūdi thumma ahlu malaʾi al-aʿlā thumma ahlu madāyini al-kibriyā thumma ahlu malakūti al-asmāʾi wa-jabarūti al-baqāʾi wa-kulluhum ṣallaw ʿalayhi wa-kabbarū ʿalā wajhihi wa-nazalū ʿalayhi wa-ṭāfū fī ḥawlihi wa-istanshaqū rawāʾiḥa ḥubbihi wa-innī law adhkuru mā ẓahara fī dhālika al-yawmi innaka lan taqbala wa-lan tastaṭīʿa an taʿrifa wa-kāna Allāhu ʿalā mā aqūlu shahīd.
:::

::: {.translation}
But after he had heard the words of God and tasted what he had desired, no one saw any calm or repose in him. A few days passed, and at every moment his longing increased and his ardent love for God, his Maker, grew more intense, until one day he came at dawn and swept the courtyard of the House with his turban. He returned, took a knife, withdrew from the people, and left the city for a watering place on the riverbank. He stood facing the House, grasped his beard with one hand, and with the other cut his throat out of love for God, the All-Powerful, the All-Protecting, the Self-Subsisting. Then an uproar arose among the people, cries went up from every soul, and a great crowd gathered around him. They saw that the knife was in his hand and that he had placed his hand upon his breast. All existence was astonished at this, as were the people of the Concourse on High, the inhabitants of the cities of grandeur, and the inhabitants of the kingdom of names and the dominion of eternity. They all offered prayers for him, proclaimed God’s greatness before his face, descended upon him, circled around him, and inhaled the fragrances of his love. Were I to recount what appeared on that day, you would neither accept it nor be able to comprehend it. God is witness to what I say.
:::

### 716

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بلسان پارسى ذكر ميشود كه سيّد مذكور بعد از ورود حضرت ابهى غذاى روحانى طلب نموده ‌فرمودند بيا و در مقابل بنشين بعد از جلوس بياناتى فرمودند فو‌اللّه سكر خمر معانى كلمات الهيّه چنان جذبش نمود كه از خود و كونين غافل گشت و اگر عالمين اراده نمايند كه تفصيل آنمجلس را ذكر كنند و يا بوصف آن كوثر معانى كه از بحر بيان طلعت لايزالى جارى شد مشغول شوند البتّه خود را عاجز مشاهده نمايند و بشأنى كلمات اللّه در قلب مقبل الى اللّه مؤثّر افتاد كه جميع اركانش بنار محبّت الهى مشتعل و ديگر حقّ عالم است كه باو چه عنايت شد قد ذاق ما لاعرفه احد الّا اللّه العليم الخبير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bi-lisān-i pārsī dhikr mīshavad kih Siyyid-i madhkūr baʿd az vurūd-i Ḥaḍrat-i Abhā ghadhā-yi rūḥānī ṭalab namūdih, farmūdand biyā va dar muqābil binishīn. Baʿd az julūs bayānātī farmūdand, fa-wa-Allāh sukr-i khamr-i maʿānī-yi kalimāt-i ilāhiyyih chunān jadhbash namūd kih az khud va kawnayn ghāfil gasht va agar ʿālamayn irādih namāyand kih tafṣīl-i ān majlis rā dhikr kunand va yā bi-vaṣf-i ān kawthar-i maʿānī kih az baḥr-i bayān-i ṭalʿat-i lā-yazālī jārī shud mashghūl shavand al-battih khud rā ʿājiz mushāhidih namāyand. Va bi-shaʾnī kalimāt-i Allāh dar qalb-i muqbil ilā Allāh muʾaththir uftād kih jamīʿ-i arkānash bi-nār-i maḥabbat-i ilāhī mushtaʿil va dīgar Ḥaqq ʿālim ast kih bi-ū chih ʿināyat shud. Qad dhāqa mā lā ʿarafahu aḥadun illā Allāhu al-ʿAlīmu al-Khabīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
It is recounted in Persian that, after the arrival of the Most Glorious One, the aforementioned Siyyid asked for spiritual food. He said, “Come and sit before Me.” After he had seated himself, He spoke certain words. By God, the intoxication of the wine of meanings in the divine words so enraptured him that he became oblivious to himself and to both worlds. If both worlds sought to recount the details of that gathering or to describe that Kawthar of meanings which flowed from the ocean of the utterance of the eternal Countenance, they would assuredly find themselves powerless. The words of God so affected the heart of him who had turned toward God that his entire frame was set ablaze with the fire of divine love. God alone knows what was bestowed upon him. He tasted what no one has known except God, the All-Knowing, the All-Aware.
:::

### 717

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و بعد مجلس منقضى شده جمال ابهى تشريف بردند و لكن آن سيّد در كلّ حين بشأن بديع ظاهر و بشأنى حبّ اللّه اخذش نمود كه بالأخره‌ از اكل و شرب منقطع شد و مدّتى باينحالت بوده تا آنكه در يومى اشعارى در مدح اللّه گفته و باصحاب داده و الان موجود اگر نفسى ملاحظه نمايد از اشتعال كينونت آن ساذج قدس مطّلع ميشود تا آنكه يومى از ایّام در اوّل فجر برخواسته و به بيت اعظم توجّه نمود و بعمامه خود فناء اطهر بيت را جاروب نموده‌و بعد رفته تيغى اخذ نمود و ببيت آقا محمّد رضا هم رفته و ديدنى نمود و بمقرّ قربانگاه دوست شتافت منقطعاً عن كلّ من فى السّموات و الأرضين و در آن حين توجّه جميع ملائكه عالين در حولش بوده و با او بقربانگاه توجّه نمودند تا آنكه در خارج مدينه قرب شط مقابل بيت بدست خود حنجر مبارك خود را قطع نمود شوقاً لحبّ ربّه و شغفاً فى ودّه و طلباً لوصاله و راضياً لقضائه و مقبلاً الى حرم وصله
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va baʿd majlis munqaḍī shude Jamāl-i Abhā tashrīf burdand va lākin ān siyyid dar kull-i ḥīn bi-shaʾn-i badīʿ ẓāhir va bi-shaʾnī ḥubb-i Allāh akhdhash namūd kih bi'l-ākhirih az akl va shurb munqaṭiʿ shud va muddatī bi-īn ḥālat būde tā ānkih dar yawmī ashʿārī dar madḥ-i Allāh gufte va bi-aṣḥāb dāde va al-ān mawjūd agar nafsī mulāḥiẓih namāyad az ishtiʿāl-i kaynūnat-i ān sādhij-i quds muṭṭaliʿ mīshavad tā ānkih yawmī az ayyām dar avval-i fajr bar-khāste va bi-Bayt-i Aʿẓam tavajjuh namūd va bi-ʿammāmiy-i khud fanā-yi aṭhar-i bayt rā jārūb namūde va baʿd rafte tīghī akhdh namūd va bi-bayt-i Āqā Muḥammad Riḍā ham rafte va dīdanī namūd va bi-maqarr-i qurbāngāh-i Dūst shitāft munqaṭiʿan ʿan kulli man fī al-samāwāti wa'l-araḍīn va dar ān ḥīn tavajjuh-i jamīʿ-i malāʾikiy-i ʿāllīn dar ḥawlash būde va bā ū bi-qurbāngāh tavajjuh namūdand tā ānkih dar khārij-i madīnih qurb-i shaṭṭ muqābil-i bayt bi-dast-i khud ḥanjar-i mubārak-i khud rā qaṭʿ namūd shawqan li-ḥubbi rabbihi wa-shaghafan fī wuddihi wa-ṭalaban li-wiṣālihi wa-rāḍiyan li-qaḍāʾihi wa-muqbilan ilā ḥarami waṣlihi.
:::

::: {.translation}
Afterward, the gathering ended and the Most Glorious Beauty departed. But that Siyyid manifested a wondrous state at every moment, and the love of God so seized him that he eventually ceased eating and drinking. He remained in this condition for a time, until one day he composed verses in praise of God and gave them to the companions. They still exist, and anyone who reads them will become aware of the fire that consumed the very being of that embodiment of holiness. Then, one day, he arose at the first light of dawn and turned toward the Most Great House. With his turban he swept the most pure courtyard of the House, and afterward went and took a blade. He also went to the house of Āqā Muḥammad Riḍā and paid a visit, then hastened to the place of sacrifice for the Beloved, detached from all who are in the heavens and the earths. At that moment, all the exalted angels were gathered around him, their attention fixed upon him, and they went with him toward the place of sacrifice. Outside the city, near the river, facing the House, he cut his blessed throat with his own hand, out of longing for the love of his Lord, passionate devotion to Him, and a desire for reunion with Him, content with His decree and turning toward the sanctuary of reunion with Him.
:::

### 718

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و بعد در مدينه اين امر شهرت نمود بشأنيكه كلّ استماع نمودند و تفنگچى باشى با جمعى از عرب و عجم توجّه بآن مقرّ اطهر نموده ‌مشاهده نمودند كه آن هيكل مقدّس خوابيده و تيغ در دستش و باينحالت جان فدا نموده ‌بعد از ملاحظه كلّ متحيّر شده و همان فعل سبب شد كه چند نفر از اعدا از افعال خود نادم شده بحبّ الهى فايز شدند و در هيچ عصرى چنين امرى واقع نشد حال ملاحظه كن كه اسم اين نفس مبارك هم اسمعيل بوده و لكن اين اسمعيل از قربانگاه دوست زنده برنگشت و جان در رهش ايثار نمود فو‌اللّه اين فعل حجّت است بر كلّ من فى السّموات و الأرض و لكن تو نيابی‌ و امثال تو نيابند تو را چه باين عوالم تو برو و ذكر وصايت مجعوله كن و در آنمقام تحقيق كن و رساله بنويس
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va baʿd dar madīnih īn amr shuhrat namūd bi-shaʾnī kih kull istimāʿ namūdand va tufangchī-bāshī bā jamʿī az ʿarab va ʿajam tavajjuh bi-ān maqarr-i aṭhar namūde mushāhidih namūdand kih ān haykal-i muqaddas khābīde va tīgh dar dastash va bi-īn ḥālat jān fidā namūde baʿd az mulāḥiẓih kull mutaḥayyir shude va hamān fiʿl sabab shud kih chand nafar az aʿdā az afʿāl-i khud nādim shude bi-ḥubb-i ilāhī fāʾiz shudand va dar hīch ʿaṣrī chunīn amrī vāqiʿ nashud ḥāl mulāḥiẓih kun kih ism-i īn nafs-i mubārak ham Ismāʿīl būde va lākin īn Ismāʿīl az qurbāngāh-i Dūst zindih bar-nagasht va jān dar rahash īthār namūd fa-wa'llāh īn fiʿl ḥujjat ast bar kulli man fī al-samāwāti wa'l-arḍ va lākin tu nayābī va amthāl-i tu nayāband tu rā chih bi-īn ʿavālim tu biraw va dhikr-i viṣāyat-i majʿūlih kun va dar ān maqām taḥqīq kun va risālih binivīs.
:::

::: {.translation}
Afterward, news of this event spread through the city until everyone had heard it. The chief of the musketeers, with a group of Arabs and Persians, went to that most pure spot and saw that sacred figure lying there, the blade in his hand, having sacrificed his life in this manner. All who saw him were astonished, and this very deed caused several of his enemies to repent of their actions and attain the love of God. In no age had such a thing occurred. Now consider that the name of this blessed soul was also Ishmael, but this Ishmael did not return alive from the place of sacrifice for the Beloved: he gave his life in His path. By God, this deed is a proof to all who are in the heavens and on earth, but you do not comprehend it, nor do those like you. What have you to do with these realms? Go and speak of a fabricated successorship; investigate that matter and write a treatise.
:::

### 719

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و هم‌چنين نفوس ديگر كه در اين ظهور جان داده‌اند و تا مقرّ قربانگاه بذكر محبوب ناطق بوده‌اند ذكر اين نفوس را كه مثل شموس مشرقه ما‌بين ناس مشرق و مضئ‌اند بغضاً على اللّه ننموده‌ و مينويسى كه جواب فلان و فلان را چه بگويم قد خسر الّذينهم كفروا بآيات اللّه و اتّبعوك و امثالك فى الدّنيا و الآخرة و انّ النّار مثويهم فبئس مثوى المنكرين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va hamchunīn nufūs-i dīgar kih dar īn ẓuhūr jān dāde-and va tā maqarr-i qurbāngāh bi-dhikr-i Maḥbūb nāṭiq būde-and dhikr-i īn nufūs rā kih mithl-i shumūs-i mushriqih mā-bayn-i nās mushriq va muḍīʾ-and bughḍan ʿalā Allāh nanamūde va mīnivīsī kih javāb-i fulān va fulān rā chih bigūyam qad khasira alladhīnahum kafarū bi-āyāti Allāh wa-ttabaʿūka wa-amthālaka fī al-dunyā wa'l-ākhirah wa-inna al-nāra mathwāhum fa-biʾsa mathwā al-munkirīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Likewise, there are other souls who have given their lives in this Revelation and continued to speak in remembrance of the Beloved until they reached the place of sacrifice. Out of hatred for God, you have made no mention of these souls, who shine resplendent among the people like rising suns, and you write, “What answer should I give to this person and that?” Those who have disbelieved in the verses of God and followed you and your like have indeed suffered loss in this world and the next. The Fire is their dwelling place: how wretched is the dwelling of the deniers!
:::

### 720

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اينكه نوشته كه چه جواب گويم كه فلانيها هر روز بيكى ميچسبند و يكى را حقّ ميدانند و باطل مينمايند اين حقّيكه ذكر نموده ‌لازال خلق بوده بقميصى از قمايص اسماء مفتخر شد و بعد از طغيان و غرور و اعراض آن قميص از او اخذ شده خذ زمام القلم لانّ بما جرى منه يلعنك اهل ممالك القدم و يشهد بذلك لسان اللّه الصّادق النّاطق الأمين ميفرمايد طوريّون در كرّه اخرى عند رشح من ذلك النّور المهيمن الحمرا ميّت و لاشیء ميشوند تو تازه ذكر مينمائى كه چگونه ميشود مرآتى على زعم تو باطل شود و يا ثمره ساقط گردد منصوص است كه بسا شجره اثبات كه در ظهور بعد باعراض از شجره نفى ميشود و تو حال بيك ثمره بزعم خود چسبيده و متمسّك شده لو يكون ثمرة حقيقيّة باعراضها سقطت عن سدرة الالهيّة و رجعت الى اوّل مقرّها فى النّار
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īnkih nivishte kih chih javāb gūyam kih fulānīhā har rūz bi-yikī mīchasband va yakī rā ḥaqq mīdānand va bāṭil mīnamāyand īn ḥaqqī kih dhikr namūde lāzāl khalq būde bi-qamīṣī az qamāyiṣ-i asmāʾ muftakhir shud va baʿd az ṭughyān va ghurūr va iʿrāḍ ān qamīṣ az ū akhdh shude khudh zimāma al-qalam li-anna bi-mā jarā minhu yalʿanuka ahlu mamāliki al-qidam wa-yashhadu bi-dhālika lisānu Allāhi al-ṣādiqu al-nāṭiqu al-amīn mīfarmāyad Ṭūriyyūn dar karrih-yi ukhrā ʿinda rashḥin min dhālika al-nūri al-muhaymini al-ḥamrā mayyit va lā-shayʾ mīshavand tu tāzih dhikr mīnamāʾī kih chigūnih mīshavad mirʾātī ʿalā zaʿm-i tu bāṭil shavad va yā thamarah sāqiṭ gardad manṣūṣ ast kih basā shajariy-i ithbāt kih dar ẓuhūr-i baʿd bi-iʿrāḍ az shajariy-i nafy mīshavad va tu ḥāl bi-yik thamarah bi-zaʿm-i khud chasbīde va mutamassik shude law yakūnu thamaratan ḥaqīqiyyatan bi-iʿrāḍihā saqaṭat ʿan sidrati al-ilāhiyyah wa-rajaʿat ilā awwali maqarrihā fī al-nār.
:::

::: {.translation}
As for what you have written, “What answer should I give, when these people attach themselves to someone new every day, regard someone as true, and then declare him false?”—this one whom you have called true has always been a created being. He was honored with one of the garments of the names, and after his rebellion, pride, and turning away, that garment was taken from him. Rein in your pen, for because of what has flowed from it, the inhabitants of the realms of eternity curse you. To this bears witness the truthful, speaking, trustworthy Tongue of God. He says that, in another cycle, the people of Sinai become dead and as nothing at a sprinkling from that all-protecting crimson Light. Yet you now ask how a mirror, as you suppose him to be, can become false, or a fruit can fall. It is expressly stated that many a tree of affirmation, through turning away in the next Revelation, becomes a tree of negation. Yet now you have attached yourself to and held fast to what you imagine to be a fruit. Even if it were a true fruit, by turning away it would fall from the divine Lote-Tree and return to its original abode in the Fire.
:::

### 721

::: {.original lang="fa"}
در اينمقام يك بيان از نقطه بيان و طلعت رحمن و نفس سبحان روح من فى ممالك الأكوان و الامكان فداه ذكر ميشود كه شايد حيا نمائى و دست تعدّى بسرادق علم و عرفان الهى دراز ننمائى اگر چه تو و امثال تو عند اللّه از محرومين محسوب و لكن وجه بيان بمقرّبين بوده و خواهد بود قال و قوله الحقّ و اجعل اللّهمّ تلك الشّجرة كلّها لها لتظهرن ما فيها ثمرات ما قد خلق اللّه فيها لمن قد اراد اللّه ان يظهر به ما اراد فانّنى انا و عزّتك ما اردت ان يكون على تلك الشّجرة من غصن و لا ورق و لا ثمر لن يسجد له يوم ظهوره و لا يسبّحك به بما ينبغى لعلوّ علوّ ظهوره و سموّ سموّ بطونه و ان شهدت يا الهى علىّ من غصن او ورق او ثمر لم يسجد له يوم ظهوره فاقطعه اللّهمّ عن تلك الشّجرة فانّه لم يكن منّى و لايرجع الىّ انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Dar īn maqām yik bayān az Nuqṭiy-i Bayān va Ṭalʿat-i Raḥmān va Nafs-i Subḥān rūḥu man fī mamāliki al-akwāni wa'l-imkān fidāh dhikr mīshavad kih shāyad ḥayā namāʾī va dast-i taʿaddī bi-surādiq-i ʿilm va ʿirfān-i ilāhī dirāz nanamāʾī agar chih tu va amthāl-i tu ʿinda Allāh az maḥrūmīn maḥsūb va lākin vajh-i bayān bi-muqarrabīn būde va khvāhad būd qāla wa-qawluhu al-ḥaqq wa-jʿal allāhumma tilka al-shajarata kullahā lahā li-taẓharanna mā fīhā thamarātu mā qad khalaqa Allāhu fīhā li-man qad arāda Allāhu an yuẓhira bihi mā arād fa-innanī anā wa-ʿizzatika mā aradtu an yakūna ʿalā tilka al-shajarati min ghuṣnin wa-lā waraqin wa-lā thamarin lan yasjuda lahu yawma ẓuhūrihi wa-lā yusabbiḥaka bihi bi-mā yanbaghī li-ʿuluwwi ʿuluwwi ẓuhūrihi wa-sumūwwi sumūwwi buṭūnihi wa-in shahidta yā ilāhī ʿalayya min ghuṣnin aw waraqin aw thamarin lam yasjud lahu yawma ẓuhūrihi fa-qṭaʿhu allāhumma ʿan tilka al-shajarah fa-innahu lam yakun minnī wa-lā yarjiʿu ilayya intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
Here an utterance of the Point of the Bayān, the Countenance of the All-Merciful and the Person of the All-Glorious—may the souls of all who dwell in the realms of existence and contingency be sacrificed for Him—is cited, so that perhaps you may feel shame and not stretch out a hand of aggression toward the pavilion of divine knowledge and recognition. Although you and your like are numbered among the deprived in God’s sight, the utterance has been, and will remain, addressed to those who are near to Him. He said, and His word is truth: “Make, O God, that Tree wholly hers, so that the fruits of what God has created within it may appear within it for Him through whom God has willed to manifest what He has willed. For I, by Your might, have not desired that there should be upon that Tree any branch, leaf, or fruit that will not bow down before Him on the day of His appearance, or glorify You through Him as befits the loftiest heights of His manifestation and the most exalted sublimity of His concealment. And if, O my God, You should behold upon Me any branch, leaf, or fruit that does not bow down before Him on the day of His appearance, cut it off, O God, from that Tree, for it is not of Me and does not return to Me.” End of quotation.
:::

### 722

::: {.original lang="fa"}
نفسى فداه و روحى فداه و سرّى فداه و ظاهرى فداه و باطنى فداه و الملك و الملكوت فداه و القدرة و اللّاهوت فداه و العزّ و الياقوت فداه و الظّهور و النّاسوت فداه و ما خلق فى ممالك القدم فداه لانّه روحى فداه ما تحرّك قلمه الّا فى هذا الذّكر البديع و هذا الظّهور المتباذخ المنيع و هذا العلوّ المتعالى الرّفيع و هذه الشّمس المشرقة المنير و هذا الأمر الظّاهر الباهر العزيز المنيع قدرى تفكّر كن كه چه ميفرمايد آن نقطه وجود و جمال معبود ميفرمايد اى پروردگار من اراده نکرده‌ام اينكه باقى بماند بر اين شجر از غصن و ورق و ثمرى كه ساجد نشود از براى او يوم ظهور او و تسبيح ننمايد تو را بآن مظهر ظهور بآنچه سزاوار است از براى علوّ علوّ ظهور او و سموّ سموّ بطون او و ميفرمايد اگر مشاهده نمودى تو اى پروردگار من بر من از غصن و ورق و ثمرى كه ساجد نشود از براى او يوم ظهور او پس قطع كن او را اى پروردگار از اين شجره بدرستيكه او نبوده است از من و راجع نميشود بسوى من
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Nafsī fidāh wa-rūḥī fidāh wa-sirrī fidāh wa-ẓāhirī fidāh wa-bāṭinī fidāh wa'l-mulku wa'l-malakūtu fidāh wa'l-qudratu wa'l-lāhūtu fidāh wa'l-ʿizzu wa'l-yāqūtu fidāh wa'l-ẓuhūru wa'l-nāsūtu fidāh wa-mā khuliqa fī mamāliki al-qidami fidāh li-annahu rūḥī fidāh mā taḥarraka qalamuhu illā fī hādhā al-dhikri al-badīʿ wa-hādhā al-ẓuhūri al-mutabādhikhi al-manīʿ wa-hādhā al-ʿuluwwi al-mutaʿālī al-rafīʿ wa-hādhihi al-shamsi al-mushriqati al-munīr wa-hādhā al-amri al-ẓāhiri al-bāhiri al-ʿazīzi al-manīʿ qadrī tafakkur kun kih chih mīfarmāyad ān Nuqṭiy-i Vujūd va Jamāl-i Maʿbūd mīfarmāyad ay Parvardigār-i man irādih nakarde-am īnkih bāqī bimānad bar īn shajar az ghuṣn va varaq va thamarī kih sājid nashavad az barā-yi ū yawm-i ẓuhūr-i ū va tasbīḥ nanamāyad tu rā bi-ān maẓhar-i ẓuhūr bi-ānchih sazāvār ast az barā-yi ʿuluvv-i ʿuluvv-i ẓuhūr-i ū va sumuvv-i sumuvv-i buṭūn-i ū va mīfarmāyad agar mushāhidih namūdī tu ay Parvardigār-i man bar man az ghuṣn va varaq va thamarī kih sājid nashavad az barā-yi ū yawm-i ẓuhūr-i ū pas qaṭʿ kun ū rā ay Parvardigār az īn shajarih bi-durustī kih ū nabūde ast az man va rājiʿ namīshavad bi-sū-yi man.
:::

::: {.translation}
May my self be sacrificed for Him, and my soul be sacrificed for Him, and my inmost secret be sacrificed for Him, and my outward being be sacrificed for Him, and my inward being be sacrificed for Him; may the earthly kingdom and the heavenly kingdom be sacrificed for Him, and power and the divine realm be sacrificed for Him, and glory and ruby be sacrificed for Him, and manifestation and the human realm be sacrificed for Him, and all that has been created in the realms of eternity be sacrificed for Him. For He—may my soul be sacrificed for Him—moved His pen only in celebration of this wondrous Remembrance, this supremely exalted and unassailable Revelation, this transcendent and lofty height, this radiant, shining Sun, and this manifest, resplendent, mighty, inviolable Cause. Reflect a little on what that Point of Existence and Beauty of the Adored One says. He says, “O my Lord, I have not desired that there should remain upon this Tree any branch, leaf, or fruit that does not bow down before Him on the day of His appearance, and does not glorify You through that Manifestation of revelation as befits the loftiest heights of His manifestation and the most exalted sublimity of His concealment.” And He says, “If, O my Lord, You should behold upon Me any branch, leaf, or fruit that does not bow down before Him on the day of His appearance, then cut it off, O Lord, from this Tree. Truly, it has not been of Me and does not return to Me.”
:::

### 723

::: {.original lang="fa"}
قدرى تفكّر نما ثمره شجره حقيقت در ظهور قبل آن است كه كلّ اهل بيان در ظلّ اين شجره ساكن شوند اين بوده اصل مقصود از آنچه تقدير شد در شجره قبل حال هر نفسى بآنمقام فايز شد از اثمار و افنان و اغصان و ما قدّر لها مذكور و من دون آن ساقط و مقطوع حال قدرى نوحه نما بر ثمره كه من دون اللّه اخذ نموده ‌و اگر ثمرهء حقيقى باشد بنصّ نقطه بيان كه ميفرمايد اگر حقّ را در يوم ظهور تصديق ننمايد از من نبوده و نخواهد بود مع اين بيان واضح لايح آشكار تعجّب مينمائيد كه چگونه ميشود ثمره باطل گردد و يا ساقط شود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qadrī tafakkur namā thamarah-yi shajariy-i ḥaqīqat dar ẓuhūr-i qabl ān ast kih kull-i ahl-i Bayān dar ẓill-i īn shajarih sākin shavand īn būde aṣl-i maqṣūd az ānchih taqdīr shud dar shajariy-i qabl ḥāl har nafsī bi-ān maqām fāʾiz shud az athmār va afnān va aghṣān va mā quddira lahā madhkūr va min dūn-i ān sāqiṭ va maqṭūʿ ḥāl qadrī nawḥih namā bar thamarah kih min dūni Allāh akhdh namūde va agar thamarah-yi ḥaqīqī bāshad bi-naṣṣ-i Nuqṭiy-i Bayān kih mīfarmāyad agar Ḥaqq rā dar yawm-i ẓuhūr taṣdīq nanamāyad az man nabūde va nakhvāhad būd maʿ-i īn bayān-i vāḍiḥ-i lāyiḥ-i āshkār taʿajjub mīnamāyīd kih chigūnih mīshavad thamarah bāṭil gardad va yā sāqiṭ shavad.
:::

::: {.translation}
Reflect a little. The fruit of the Tree of Truth in the former Revelation is that all the people of the Bayān should dwell beneath the shade of this Tree. This was the essential purpose of all that was ordained in the former Tree. Now, whoever has attained that station is numbered among its fruits, twigs, branches, and whatever has been ordained for it; anyone else is fallen and cut off. Now lament a little for the fruit that has taken hold of something other than God. Even if it is a true fruit, the Point of the Bayān expressly says, “If it does not acknowledge the True One on the day of His appearance, it has not been, and will not be, of Me.” Despite this clear, evident, manifest utterance, you wonder how a fruit can become false or fall!
:::

### 724

::: {.original lang="fa"}
حال عظمت امر اللّه را مشاهده كن و شأن خود و مرشدت را بگو اى طفل دبستان جهل هنوز بالغ نشده چه كه اگر بالغ بودى باين كلمات مشغول نميشدى فافّ لك و بما عندك و بما استدللت به و بما تكون مسروراً به اليوم بالغين آنانند كه بمظهر ربّ العالمين عارف شده و بر اعراش تمكين و وقار متمكّن نزد تو و امثال تو بسيار مشكل است خرق اين حجبات و لكن از براى حقّ جلّ ثنائه نفوسى هست كه بنفحاتش جميع احجاب را خرق نمايند و ايشانند آن نفوسى كه كلّ نفس ايشان مهيمن است بر كلّ اهل بيان و هم‌چنين كلمات ايشان و افعال ايشان و عرفان ايشان چنانچه نقطه بيان ميفرمايد كه نطفه يكساله ظهور بعد اقوى است از كلّ من فى البيان و اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو كه اگر در همين بيان نقطه بيان تفكّر نمايند جميع از كلّ من فى السّموات و الأرض و از روح و نفس و ذات خود منقطع شده بشطر احديّه توجّه نمايند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ḥāl ʿaẓamat-i Amr-i Allāh rā mushāhidih kun va shaʾn-i khud va murshidat rā bigū ay ṭifl-i dabistān-i jahl hanūz bāligh nashude chih kih agar bāligh būdī bi-īn kalimāt mashghūl namīshudī fa-uffin laka wa-bi-mā ʿindaka wa-bi-mā istad­lalta bihi wa-bi-mā takūnu masrūran bihi al-yawm bālighīn ānānand kih bi-Maẓhar-i Rabb-i ʿālamīn ʿārif shude va bar aʿrāsh-i tamkīn va vaqār mutamakkin nazd-i tu va amthāl-i tu bisyār mushkil ast kharq-i īn ḥujubāt va lākin az barā-yi Ḥaqq jalla thanāʾuhu nufūsī hast kih bi-nafaḥātash jamīʿ-i aḥjāb rā kharq namāyand va īshānand ān nufūsī kih kull-i nafs-i īshān muhaymin ast bar kull-i ahl-i Bayān va hamchunīn kalimāt-i īshān va afʿāl-i īshān va ʿirfān-i īshān chinānchih Nuqṭiy-i Bayān mīfarmāyad kih nuṭfih-yi yiksālih-yi ẓuhūr-i baʿd aqvā ast az kulli man fī al-Bayān wa'llāhi alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa kih agar dar hamīn bayān-i Nuqṭiy-i Bayān tafakkur namāyand jamīʿ az kulli man fī al-samāwāti wa'l-arḍ va az rūḥ va nafs va dhāt-i khud munqaṭiʿ shude bi-shaṭr-i Aḥadiyyih tavajjuh namāyand.
:::

::: {.translation}
Now behold the greatness of the Cause of God and the standing of yourself and your guide. Say: O child in the school of ignorance, you have not yet reached maturity, for had you matured, you would not have occupied yourself with these words. Shame on you, on what you possess, on what you have adduced as proof, and on what delights you today! The mature are those who have recognized the Manifestation of the Lord of the worlds and are established upon the thrones of steadfastness and dignity. For you and your like, tearing through these veils is exceedingly difficult. Yet God—exalted be His praise—has souls who, through His breaths, tear through every veil. These are the souls each one of whom holds sway over all the people of the Bayān, as do their words, their deeds, and their recognition. Thus the Point of the Bayān says that the year-old embryo of the next Revelation is mightier than all who are in the Bayān. By God, besides whom there is no god, if they reflected upon this very utterance of the Point of the Bayān, they would all detach themselves from everyone in the heavens and on earth, and from their own souls, selves, and beings, and turn toward the One.
:::

### 725

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اين كلمه بسيار بزرگ است لو انتم تتفكّرون چه اگر امر عظيم نباشد چگونه چنين بيان از منزل بيان ظاهر ميشد اذا نشهد بأن صدق اللّه العلىّ العظيم چه كه اگر اقوى از كلّ خلق نباشد نميتواند اين سبحات اوهام را خرق نمايد و اين اصنام كبيره را بقوّه خليل آفاق‌ بشكند كجا است مقام اين عباد و مقام عباد قبل هؤلآء عباد يصلين عليهم اهل ملأ الأعلی ثمّ حقايق الأشیآء و لكن انتم لا تشعرون
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īn kalimih bisyār buzurg ast law antum tatafakkarūn chih agar amr ʿaẓīm nabāshad chigūnih chunīn bayān az Munzil-i Bayān ẓāhir mīshud idhan nashhadu bi-anna ṣadaqa Allāhu al-ʿaliyyu al-ʿaẓīm chih kih agar aqvā az kull-i khalq nabāshad namītavānad īn subuḥāt-i awhām rā kharq namāyad va īn aṣnām-i kabīrih rā bi-quvvih-yi Khalīl-i āfāq bishikanad kujā ast maqām-i īn ʿibād va maqām-i ʿibād-i qabl hāʾulāʾi ʿibādun yuṣallīna ʿalayhim ahlu malaʾi al-aʿlā thumma ḥaqāʾiqu al-ashyāʾ wa-lākin antum lā tashʿurūn.
:::

::: {.translation}
This utterance is exceedingly momentous, if you would reflect. For if the Cause were not mighty, how could such an utterance have appeared from the Revealer of the Bayān? Thus We testify that God, the Most High, the Most Great, has spoken the truth. For unless one is mightier than all creation, one cannot tear through these veils of vain imaginings or shatter these mighty idols through the power of the Friend of all the worlds. How far apart are the station of these servants and that of the servants of former times! These are servants upon whom the inhabitants of the Concourse on High, and then the realities of all things, invoke blessings, but you do not perceive.
:::

### 726

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و اينكه بقلم غلّ و افترا نوشته كه بعضى مردم نسبت عصيان بجمال ابهى ميدهند و نوشته آنچه قلم حيا مينمايد از ذكر آن كلّما ذكرت كذب صراح جميع اين كلمات را آن ملقى كذّاب بتو القا نموده‌ و نوشته و الّذى تكلّم بذلك افترى على اللّه المهيمن القيّوم اذا يخاطبك ملائكة التّقديس من فردوس الأعظم و يقول يا ايّها المشرك صه لسانك بقطرة من ابحر تقديسه خلقنا و بعثنا و جعلنا اللّه مطهّراً عن دلالة غيره و منزّها عن ذكر ما سواه و اذا نسبّحنه و نقدسنه فى هذا المقرّ الأعظم العظيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va īnkih bi-qalam-i ghill va iftirā nivishte kih baʿḍī mardum nisbat-i ʿiṣyān bi-Jamāl-i Abhā mīdihand va nivishte ānchih qalam ḥayā mīnamāyad az dhikr-i ān kullu mā dhakarta kadhibun ṣurāḥ jamīʿ-i īn kalimāt rā ān mulqī-yi kadhdhāb bi-tu ilqā namūde va nivishte wa'lladhī takallama bi-dhālika iftarā ʿalā Allāhi al-muhaymini al-qayyūm idhan yukhāṭibuka malāʾikatu al-taqdīsi min Firdawsi al-Aʿẓam wa-yaqūlu yā ayyuhā al-mushriku ṣah lisānaka bi-qaṭratin min abḥuri taqdīsihi khuliqnā wa-buʿithnā wa-jaʿalanā Allāhu muṭahharan ʿan dalālati ghayrihi wa-munazzahan ʿan dhikri mā siwāhu wa-idhan nusabbiḥannahu wa-nuqaddisannahu fī hādhā al-maqarri al-aʿẓami al-ʿaẓīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
As for what you have written with the pen of malice and slander, that some people accuse the Most Glorious Beauty of disobedience, and your having written what the pen is ashamed to mention: everything you have said is an outright lie. That lying prompter has prompted you with all these words and written them. Whoever spoke thus has fabricated a lie against God, the All-Protecting, the Self-Subsisting. Now the angels of holiness address you from the Most Great Paradise, saying, “O you who associate partners with God, silence your tongue! From a drop of the oceans of His holiness we were created and raised up, and God has made us pure of the guidance of anyone other than Him and sanctified us from the mention of all besides Him. Thus we assuredly glorify Him and proclaim His holiness in this most great and mighty abode.”
:::

### 727

::: {.original lang="fa"}
ثمّ يخاطبك ملائكة التّنزيه من جنّة الأعلی و يقولنّ خذ قلمك يا ايّها المشرك باللّه تاللّه بهبوب من ارياح تنزيهه قد بعثنا و خلقنا و اذا ننزهنّه و نسبّحنه و نقدسنه فى هذا المقام الّذى جعله اللّه مطهّراً عن ذكرك و ثنائك و عرفانك و عرفان العالمين ثمّ يخاطبك ملائكة التّجريد فى جنّة الأبهی و يقولن فاستحى يا ايّها المعرض عن اللّه قد خلقنا اللّه من ابحر تجريده و انقطعنا عن كلّ ذكر دون ذكره و اذا نسير فى هذه الجنّة الأعظم و نذكرنه و نحمدنه فى كلّ بكور و اصيل
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Thumma yukhāṭibuka malāʾikat al-tanzīh min jannat al-Aʿlā wa-yaqulna khudh qalamaka yā ayyuhā al-mushrik bi-llāh ta-llāh bi-hubūb min aryāḥ tanzīhihi qad buʿithnā wa-khuliqnā wa-idhan nunazzihannahu wa-nusabbiḥannahu wa-nuqaddisannahu fī hādhā al-maqām alladhī jaʿalahu Allāh muṭahharan ʿan dhikrika wa-thanāʾika wa-ʿirfānika wa-ʿirfān al-ʿālamīn thumma yukhāṭibuka malāʾikat al-tajrīd fī jannat al-Abhā wa-yaqulna fa-staḥi yā ayyuhā al-muʿriḍ ʿan Allāh qad khalaqanā Allāh min abḥur tajrīdihi wa-nqaṭaʿnā ʿan kull dhikr dūna dhikrihi wa-idhan nasīr fī hādhihi al-jannat al-aʿẓam wa-nadhkurannahu wa-naḥmadannahu fī kull bukūr wa-aṣīl.
:::

::: {.translation}
Then the angels of transcendence address you from the Most Exalted Paradise, saying, “Take up your pen, O you who associate partners with God! By God, through a breath from the winds of His transcendence we were raised up and created. Thus we proclaim His transcendence, glorify Him, and declare His holiness in this station, which God has purified of your mention, your praise, your recognition, and the recognition of all the worlds.” Then the angels of detachment address you in the All-Glorious Paradise, saying, “Be ashamed, O you who turn away from God! God has created us from the oceans of His detachment, and we have severed ourselves from every mention but His. Thus we walk in this Most Great Paradise, remembering and praising Him every morning and evening.”
:::

### 728

::: {.original lang="ar"}
ثمّ يخاطبك اهل جنّة الأمر و يقولن يا ايّها الغافل عن ذكر اللّه و المحارب بنفسه انّا خلقنا بامر الّذى جرى من قلمه العزيز البديع و انّه لهو الّذى بأمره رقم قلم الأعلی على الألواح كلّما اراد و انّه لهو الحاكم على ما يريد انّه لا يسئل عمّا فعل و ما سواه يسئلون لو انت من العالمين انّه لهو المختار فى نفسه يفعل ما يشآء بسلطانه ليس لأحد ان يعترض عليه و انّما الاعتراض يرجع الى نفسك الشّقىّ البعيد ما احصينا احجب منك من ملل القبل تاللّه بنار غلّك اشتعلت نار السّعير خف عن اللّه و لاتنسب اليه ما يأمرك نفسك و هويك و لاتكن من المشركين تاللّه يشهد بتقديسه كلّ الذّرّات ثمّ بتنزيهه كلّ الأشیآء و بتجريده اهل ملأ اعلى و بتوحيد ذاته اهل مداين البقآء انّه لو يحكم لنفس الشّرك حكم التّوحيد يقدر بسلطانه المقتدر القدير و لو يريد ان يبدّل ذنوب الممكنات بكلمة من عنده ليكون قادراً بأمره و انّما العجز شأنك و شأن امثالك يا ايّها الّذى جعلت نفسك محروماً عن نفحات اللّه فى هذه الأیّام الأبدع البديع
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Thumma yukhāṭibuka ahl jannat al-amr wa-yaqulna yā ayyuhā al-ghāfil ʿan dhikr Allāh wa-l-muḥārib bi-nafsihi innā khuliqnā bi-amr alladhī jarā min qalamihi al-ʿazīz al-badīʿ wa-innahu la-huwa alladhī bi-amrihi raqama qalam al-Aʿlā ʿalā al-alwāḥ kullamā arāda wa-innahu la-huwa al-ḥākim ʿalā mā yurīd innahu lā yusʾalu ʿammā faʿala wa-mā siwāhu yusʾalūn law anta min al-ʿālimīn innahu la-huwa al-mukhtār fī nafsihi yafʿalu mā yashāʾ bi-sulṭānihi laysa li-aḥad an yaʿtariḍa ʿalayhi wa-innamā al-iʿtirāḍ yarjiʿu ilā nafsika al-shaqiyy al-baʿīd mā aḥṣaynā aḥjab minka min milal al-qabl ta-llāh bi-nār ghillika ishtaʿalat nār al-saʿīr khaf ʿan Allāh wa-lā tansub ilayhi mā yaʾmuruka nafsuka wa-hawāka wa-lā takun min al-mushrikīn ta-llāh yashhadu bi-taqdīsihi kull al-dharrāt thumma bi-tanzīhihi kull al-ashyāʾ wa-bi-tajrīdihi ahl malaʾ aʿlā wa-bi-tawḥīd dhātihi ahl madāʾin al-baqāʾ innahu law yaḥkumu li-nafs al-shirk ḥukm al-tawḥīd yaqdiru bi-sulṭānihi al-muqtadir al-qadīr wa-law yurīdu an yubaddila dhunūb al-mumkināt bi-kalima min ʿindihi la-yakūnu qādiran bi-amrihi wa-innamā al-ʿajz shaʾnuka wa-shaʾn amthālika yā ayyuhā alladhī jaʿalta nafsaka maḥrūman ʿan nafaḥāt Allāh fī hādhihi al-ayyām al-abdaʿ al-badīʿ.
:::

::: {.translation}
Then the inhabitants of the Paradise of the Command address you, saying, “O you who are heedless of the remembrance of God and wage war against His own Self! We were created by a command that flowed from His mighty, wondrous Pen. He is indeed the One at whose command the Most Exalted Pen inscribed on the Tablets whatever He desired. He is indeed the Ruler over whatever He wills. He is not questioned about what He does, while all besides Him are questioned, if you are among those who know. He indeed chooses freely in His own right, doing whatever He wishes through His sovereignty. No one has the right to object to Him; any objection only turns back upon your own wretched, wayward self. We have counted none among the religious communities of the past more veiled than you. By God, the fire of your malice has kindled the fire of hell! Fear God, and do not attribute to Him what your own self and desires dictate to you, and do not be among those who associate partners with Him. By God, every atom bears witness to His holiness, all things to His transcendence, the inhabitants of the Concourse on High to His detachment, and the inhabitants of the cities of eternity to the oneness of His Essence. If He were to pronounce belief in His oneness upon unbelief itself, He would have the power through His all-compelling, all-powerful sovereignty. If He wished to transform the sins of all contingent beings with a word from Himself, He would assuredly have the power through His command. Powerlessness belongs only to you and those like you, O you who have deprived yourself of the breaths of God in these most wondrous days.”
:::

### 729

::: {.original lang="fa"}
افٍّ لك و لعرفانك اما عرفت بأن الحكم يظهر منه و لايرجع اليه حكم احد و انّه لهو الأمر فى ازل الازال و لايجرى عليه امر احد لانّ كلّ فقراء عنده و خلقوا بقوله العزيز البديع هل ينبغى لورقة الّتى سقطت من السّدرة و اصفرّت من هوآء نفسها يعترض على سدرة الّتى ينطق كلّ ورقة منها بانّه لا اله الّا هو العزيز المتعالى العليم الحكيم هل ينبغى للعدم بأن يعترض على سلطان القدم او يقنّن له قوانين نفسه لا فو‌نفسه العلىّ العظيم اذاً اسمع قولى ثمّ استغفر بدوام عمرك لعلّ اللّه يغفرك و يطهّرك عمّا ابتليت به و ينقطعك عن نفسك و هويك و يقرّبك الى ما هو خير لك عن ملكوت ملك السّموات و الأرضين فو‌اللّه ما اردت فيما ذكرت الّا تضييع امر اللّه و نسئل اللّه بأن يضيّعك ثمّ الّذين ايّدوك على ما فعلت و ارتكبت و انّه لعلى كلّ شیء قدير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Uffin laka wa-li-ʿirfānika a-mā ʿarafta bi-anna al-ḥukm yaẓharu minhu wa-lā yarjiʿu ilayhi ḥukm aḥad wa-innahu la-huwa al-amr fī azal al-āzāl wa-lā yajrī ʿalayhi amr aḥad li-anna kull fuqarāʾ ʿindahu wa-khuliqū bi-qawlihi al-ʿazīz al-badīʿ hal yanbaghī li-waraqa allatī saqaṭat min al-sidra wa-ṣfarrat min hawāʾ nafsihā yaʿtariḍ ʿalā sidra allatī yanṭiqu kull waraqa minhā bi-annahu lā ilāha illā huwa al-ʿAzīz al-Mutaʿālī al-ʿAlīm al-Ḥakīm hal yanbaghī li-l-ʿadam bi-an yaʿtariḍa ʿalā sulṭān al-qidam aw yuqannina lahu qawānīn nafsihi lā fa-wa-nafsihi al-ʿaliyy al-ʿaẓīm idhan ismaʿ qawlī thumma istaghfir bi-dawām ʿumrika laʿalla Allāh yaghfiruka wa-yuṭahhiruka ʿammā ibtulīta bihi wa-yanqaṭiʿuka ʿan nafsika wa-hawāka wa-yuqarribuka ilā mā huwa khayr laka ʿan malakūt mulk al-samāwāt wa-l-arḍīn fa-wa-llāh mā aradta fīmā dhakarta illā taḍyīʿ amr Allāh wa-nasʾalu Allāh bi-an yuḍayyiʿaka thumma alladhīna ayyadūka ʿalā mā faʿalta wa-rtakabta wa-innahu la-ʿalā kull shayʾ qadīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
Shame on you and your understanding! Have you not recognized that judgment proceeds from Him, while no one’s judgment applies to Him? He is indeed the Command from all eternity, and no one’s command holds sway over Him, for all are destitute before Him and were created by His mighty, wondrous word. Is it fitting for a leaf that has fallen from the Lote Tree and yellowed through the air of its own self to object to a Tree whose every leaf proclaims that there is no God but Him, the Almighty, the Most Exalted, the All-Knowing, the All-Wise? Is it fitting for nothingness to object to the Sovereign of eternity, or to prescribe its own laws for Him? No, by His own exalted, mighty Self! Listen, then, to My words, and seek forgiveness throughout your life, that God may perhaps forgive you, purify you of what has afflicted you, detach you from your self and desires, and bring you near to what is better for you than sovereignty over the heavens and the earth. By God, in what you have said you intended only to bring the Cause of God to ruin. We ask God to bring you to ruin, and those who supported you in what you have done and committed. He indeed has power over all things.
:::

### 730

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اين عبد را ملجأ نموده‌ اگر جواب ذكر نشود بيم آنست كه بعضى از نفوس ضعيفه باين كلمات جعليّه از حقّ محروم مانند و اگر ذكر شود و اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو فطرت اصليّه راضى نميشود كه از ذكر اللّه غافل شود و بكلمات مشركين توجّه نمايد و لكن چه چاره تكليف اينست آنچه گفته‌ايد جواب ذكر شودلعلّ آن مجعولات ما بين عباد و سلطان يوم ميعاد حجاب نگردد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Īn ʿabd rā muljaʾ namūdeh agar javāb dhekr nashavad bīm ān ast keh baʿżī az nofūs-e żaʿīfeh be-īn kalemāt-e jaʿlīyyeh az Ḥaqq maḥrūm mānand va agar dhekr shavad va-llāh alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa feṭrat-e aṣlīyyeh rāżī nemīshavad keh az dhekr-e Allāh ghāfel shavad va be-kalemāt-e moshrekīn tavajjoh namāyad va lāken cheh chāreh taklīf īn ast āncheh gofteh-īd javāb dhekr shavad laʿall ān majʿūlāt mā beyn-e ʿebād va Solṭān-e yowm-e mīʿād ḥejāb nagardad.
:::

::: {.translation}
You have left this servant no choice: if no answer is given, there is a fear that some weak souls may be deprived of the True One through these fabricated words. Yet if an answer is given—by God, besides whom there is no other god—one’s innate nature is unwilling to become heedless of the remembrance of God and turn its attention to the words of those who associate partners with Him. But what can be done? The duty is to answer what you have said, so that those fabrications may not become a veil between His servants and the Sovereign of the Day of Promise.
:::

### 731

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و از اين كلمات كه بتو القا نموده‌مقصودى نداشته مگر آنكه بعضى نفوس را از شطر فردوس منع نمايند و عباد را بدام كلمات صيد كنند در دوازده سنه توقّف در عراق جميع ميدانند كه چه مقدار جدّ و جهد فرموده‌اند تا آنكه بعضى فواحش را از ما بين اين طايفه برداشتند و اگر هم نعوذ باللّه بعضى مرتكب شده‌اند در ستر بوده فو‌اللّه يا غافل مطّلع نيستى كه بر چه مقرّى اين اعتراضات نموده ‌لو تعرف لتهلك نفسك فى الحين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va az īn kalemāt keh be-to elqā namūdeh maqṣūdī nadāshteh magar ānkeh baʿżī nofūs rā az shaṭr-e ferdows manʿ namāyand va ʿebād rā be-dām-e kalemāt ṣeyd konand dar davāzdah saneh tavaqqof dar ʿErāq jamīʿ mīdānand keh cheh meqdār jedd o jahd farmūdeh-and tā ānkeh baʿżī favāḥesh rā az mā beyn-e īn ṭāʾefeh bardāshtand va agar ham naʿūdhu bi-llāh baʿżī mortakeb shodeh-and dar setr būdeh fa-wa-llāh yā ghāfel moṭṭaleʿ nīstī keh bar cheh maqarrī īn eʿterāżāt namūdeh law taʿrif la-tahlika nafsuka fī al-ḥīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
In prompting you with these words, he had no purpose but to keep some souls from turning toward Paradise and to catch His servants in the snare of words. Everyone knows how strenuously He exerted Himself during His twelve years’ residence in Iraq, until He eliminated certain shameful practices from among this community. And if some did commit them—God forbid—it was in secret. By God, O heedless one, you do not know against what station you have raised these objections! If you knew, you would perish that very instant.
:::

### 732

::: {.original lang="fa"}
علّت و سبب اعظم كدورت جمال ابهى از ميرزا يحيى و اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو اين بوده كه در حرم نقطه اولى روح ما سواه فداه تصرّف نمود با اينكه در كلّ كتب سماوى حرام است و بی‌‌شرمى او بمقامى رسيده كه مخصوص زوجات خود را در مكتوبات خود حرام نموده‌ مع‌ذلك دست تعدّى و خيانت بحرم مظهر مليك علام گشوده فافّ له و لوفائه و كاش بنفس خود قناعت مينمود بلكه او را بعد از ارتكاب خود وقف مشركين نمود و جميع اهل بيان شنيده و ميدانند سيّئات او را بايد از معاشرين او سؤال نمود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
ʿEllat va sabab-e aʿẓam-e kodūrat-e Jamāl-e Abhā az Mīrzā Yaḥyā va-llāh alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa īn būdeh keh dar ḥaram-e Noqṭeh-ye Ūlā rūḥ-e mā sevāh fadāh taṣarrof namūd bā īnkeh dar koll-e kotob-e samāvī ḥarām ast va bī-sharmī-ye ū be-maqāmī resīdeh keh makhṣūṣ-e zowjāt-e khod rā dar maktūbāt-e khod ḥarām namūdeh maʿa-dhālek dast-e taʿaddī va khīyānat be-ḥaram-e Maẓhar-e Malīk-e ʿAllām goshūdeh fa-uffin lahu wa-li-wafāʾihi va kāsh be-nafs-e khod qanāʿat mīnamūd balkeh ū rā baʿd az ertekāb-e khod vaqf-e moshrekīn namūd va jamīʿ-e ahl-e Bayān shenīdeh va mīdānand sayyeʾāt-e ū rā bāyad az moʿāsherīn-e ū soʾāl namūd.
:::

::: {.translation}
The chief reason and greatest cause of the All-Glorious Beauty’s displeasure with Mīrzā Yaḥyā—by God, besides whom there is no other god—was that he took possession of the wife of the Primal Point, may the souls of all besides Him be sacrificed for Him, although this is forbidden in all the heavenly Books. His shamelessness reached such a point that, while he specifically forbade marriage to his own wives in his writings, he nevertheless stretched out the hand of transgression and betrayal toward the wife of the Manifestation of the all-knowing King. Shame on him and his faithfulness! If only he had confined himself to his own act; instead, after committing it himself, he made her available to those who associate partners with God. All the people of the Bayān have heard and know of this. His associates should be asked about his misdeeds.
:::

### 733

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و از اينها گذشته عجب در اينست كه همين فقره كه نوشته دليلى است واضح و برهانى است قاطع بر حقّیّت اين امر و تو هنوز مستشعر نشده نفسى را كه خود تو ميدانى كه از اهل علم و زهد نبوده و از عرفا و ارباب عمايم محسوب نه و بقول تو با امثال مشير الدّوله معاشر بوده و بعد يكمرتبه كوثر معانى الهيّه من غير جهات از او جارى و شموس حكمت ربانيّه از افق اراده‌اش مشرق و مضئ اى بی‌ انصاف اين مقامى است فوق كلّ مقام لو تكون من المنصفين اين فضل اكبر را حقير شمرده و بخيال خود اين كلمات را بجهت اغواى ناس ذكر كرده قد اخطات يا ايّها المجرم العاصى هر عاقل بصيرى كه بشنود البتّه در امر اللّه ثابت‌تر و مستقيم‌تر شده و خواهد شد
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va az īnhā godhashteh ʿajab dar īn ast keh hamīn faqreh keh neveshteh dalīlī ast vāżeḥ va borhānī ast qāṭeʿ bar ḥaqqīyyat-e īn Amr va to hanūz mostashʿer nashodeh nafsī rā keh khod-e to mīdānī keh az ahl-e ʿelm va zohd nabūdeh va az ʿorafā va arbāb-e ʿamāyem maḥsūb nah va be-qowl-e to bā amthāl-e Moshīr al-Dowleh moʿāsher būdeh va baʿd yek-martabeh kowthar-e maʿānī-ye elāhīyyeh min ghayr-e jahāt az ū jārī va shomūs-e ḥekmat-e rabbānīyyeh az ofoq-e erādeh-ash moshreq va możīʾ ey bī-enṣāf īn maqāmī ast fowq-e koll-e maqām law takūnu min al-munṣifīn īn fażl-e akbar rā ḥaqīr shemordeh va be-khīyāl-e khod īn kalemāt rā be-jehat-e eghvā-ye nās dhekr kardeh qad akhṭaʾta yā ayyuhā al-mujrim al-ʿāṣī har ʿāqel-e baṣīrī keh beshnavad albatteh dar Amr-e Allāh thābet-tar va mostaqīm-tar shodeh va khvāhad shod.
:::

::: {.translation}
Beyond all this, what is astonishing is that the very passage he has written is clear evidence and conclusive proof of the truth of this Cause, yet you have still not perceived it. You yourself know that this Person was not one of the learned or the ascetics, nor counted among the mystics and the turbaned clergy, and that, according to you, He associated with the likes of Moshīr al-Dowleh. Then, all at once, the heavenly stream of divine meanings flows from Him, without dependence on any source, and the suns of divine wisdom rise and shine from the horizon of His will. O unfair one! This is a station above every station, if you are among the fair-minded. You have belittled this greatest favor and, as you imagine, spoken these words to lead people astray. You have erred, O sinful transgressor! Every discerning person of reason who hears them has certainly become, and will become, firmer and more steadfast in the Cause of God.
:::

### 734

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بارى فكر ديگر براى خود نموده‌كه اين وساوس در انفس خنّاسيّه اثر نمايد نه در انفس رحمانيّه قلوب كدره محدوده شايد باينكلمات كذبه نالايقه از ذكر سلطان احديّه غافل شوند و لكن انفس مجرّده بجان بشطر رحمن توجّه نمايند حال از تو ميپرسم اگر نفسى از مابين قومى كه ابدا معروف بعلم نبوده و باسم فضل و عدل مابين ناس مشهور نه برخيزد و بجواهر كلمات اللّه ناطق شود چنانچه شنيده و ميشنويد اين نفس اعظم است و يا نفسيكه در ميانه اهل علم تربيت شود شكّى نيست كه اوّل ارجح بوده چه كه او بصرف قدرت الهيّه ظاهر
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bārī fekr-e dīgar barā-ye khod namūdeh keh īn vasāves dar anfos-e khannāsīyyeh athar namāyad nah dar anfos-e raḥmānīyyeh qolūb-e kadereh-ye maḥdūdeh shāyad be-īn kalemāt-e kadhebeh-ye nālāyeqeh az dhekr-e Solṭān-e Aḥadīyyeh ghāfel shavand va lāken anfos-e mojarradeh be-jān be-shaṭr-e Raḥmān tavajjoh namāyand ḥāl az to mīporsam agar nafsī az mā beyn-e qowmī keh abadan maʿrūf be-ʿelm nabūdeh va be-esm-e fażl va ʿadl mā beyn-e nās mashhūr nah barkhīzad va be-javāher-e kalemāt-e Allāh nāṭeq shavad chenāncheh shenīdeh va mīshenavīd īn nafs aʿẓam ast va yā nafsī keh dar mīyāneh-ye ahl-e ʿelm tarbīyat shavad shakkī nīst keh avval arjaḥ būdeh cheh keh ū be-ṣerf-e qodrat-e elāhīyyeh ẓāher.
:::

::: {.translation}
In any case, devise another plan for yourself, for these insinuations affect souls given to whispering evil, not souls that belong to the All-Merciful. Clouded, constrained hearts may become heedless of the remembrance of the Sovereign of Oneness through these false, unworthy words, but detached souls turn wholeheartedly toward the All-Merciful. Now I ask you: if someone arises from among a people who have never been known for learning or renowned among others for excellence and justice, and gives voice to the gems of God’s words, as you have heard and continue to hear, is this person greater, or someone educated among the learned? There is no doubt that the former is superior, for He has appeared solely through divine power.
:::

### 735

::: {.original lang="fa"}
خوب است كه حقّ جلّ اجلاله از لسان خود شما كلماتى فرموده كه متبصّرين را در معرفت امثال آن نفوس كافى بوده و خواهد بود لازال حقّ محلّ اينگونه اعتراضات بوده چنانچه بروح اللّه اعتراض نمودند كه با خاطئين و عشارين مجالس و مؤانس است فو‌اللّه بر اين ظهور مع وصاياى نقطه بيان جلّ اعزازه بلايائى وارد شده كه بر احدى از مظاهر قبل وارد نشده بلاياى اوّلين و آخرين معادله نمينمايد با همين قرطاس نجسه كه بساحت اقدس ارسال داشته با آنكه از هيچ امرى مطّلع نبوده و نيستى و محض هوى و مجرّد نفس تكلّم نموده‌ و اين از رزايائى است كه مشهود شده و لكن بلايائى بر اين ظهور وارد كه احدى محصى آن نه الّا اللّه
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Khūb ast keh Ḥaqq jalla ijlāluhu az lesān-e khod-e shomā kalemātī farmūdeh keh motabaṣṣerīn rā dar maʿrefat-e amthāl-e ān nofūs kāfī būdeh va khvāhad būd lā yazāl Ḥaqq maḥall-e īngūneh eʿterāżāt būdeh chenāncheh be-Rūḥ Allāh eʿterāż namūdand keh bā khāṭeʾīn va ʿashshārīn mojāles va moʾānes ast fa-wa-llāh bar īn Ẓohūr maʿa vaṣāyā-ye Noqṭeh-ye Bayān jalla iʿzāzuhu balāyāʾī vāred shodeh keh bar aḥadī az Maẓāher-e qabl vāred nashodeh balāyā-ye avvalīn va ākherīn moʿādeleh nemīnamāyad bā hamīn qerṭās-e najeseh keh be-sāḥat-e aqdas ersāl dāshteh bā ānkeh az hīch amrī moṭṭaleʿ nabūdeh va nīstī va maḥż-e havā va mojarrad-e nafs takallom namūdeh va īn az razāyāʾī ast keh mashhūd shodeh va lāken balāyāʾī bar īn Ẓohūr vāred keh aḥadī moḥṣī-ye ān nah illā Allāh.
:::

::: {.translation}
It is well that the True One—exalted be His glory—has spoken through your own tongue words that have been, and will be, sufficient for the discerning to recognize souls such as these. The True One has always been the object of such objections, just as they objected to the Spirit of God for sitting and associating with sinners and tax collectors. By God, despite the counsels of the Point of the Bayān—exalted be His honor—afflictions have befallen this Revelation that have befallen none of the Manifestations of the past. The afflictions of the first and the last do not equal this very defiled sheet that you have sent to the Most Holy Court, although you have had, and still have, no knowledge of any of these matters, and have spoken out of sheer desire and self alone. This is one of the calamities that have been witnessed, yet afflictions have befallen this Revelation that no one but God can count.
:::

### 736

::: {.original lang="fa"}
چنانچه در توقيع جناب جود عليه بهآء اللّه يك آيه نازل كه و اللّه كبد اهل آفاق‌ را گداخته قوله جلّ كبريائه انّك رأيتنى و عاشرت معى و عرفت بحر سكونى و جبل اصطبارى فكّر ما اقامنى على الصّيحة بين السّموات و الأرضين و لكن چه فايده كه آيات الهى بر تو القا نموده مثل آن است كه عندليبی‌ از براى كر تغنّى نمايد نسئل اللّه بأن يطهّر الأرض من رجسك و رجس الّذينهم كانوا معك و انّه لمجيب دعوة السّايلين قدرت آن قدر معلوم شده كه بقول اخبث ناس و ادناهم از حقّ معرض شده و بشجره نفس و هوى متمسّك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Chenāncheh dar towqīʿ-e Janāb-e Jūd ʿalayhi bahāʾ Allāh yek āyeh nāzel keh va-llāh kabed-e ahl-e āfāq rā godākhteh qawluhu jalla kibriyāʾuhu innaka raʾaytanī wa-ʿāsharta maʿī wa-ʿarafta baḥr sukūnī wa-jabal iṣṭibārī fakkir mā aqāmanī ʿalā al-ṣayḥa bayna al-samāwāt wa-l-arḍīn va lāken cheh fāyedeh keh āyāt-e elāhī bar to elqā namūdeh methl-e ān ast keh ʿandalībī az barā-ye kar taghannī namāyad nasʾalu Allāh bi-an yuṭahhira al-arḍ min rijsika wa-rijs alladhīnahum kānū maʿaka wa-innahu la-mujīb daʿwat al-sāʾilīn qadrat ān qadr maʿlūm shodeh keh be-qowl-e akhbath-e nās va adnāhom az Ḥaqq moʿreż shodeh va be-shajareh-ye nafs va havā motamassek.
:::

::: {.translation}
Thus, in the Tablet to Jināb-i-Jūd—upon him be the glory of God—a verse was revealed that, by God, has melted the hearts of the people of every land. He says—exalted be His majesty—“You have seen Me, associated with Me, and known the ocean of My calm and the mountain of My patience. Consider what has made Me raise My cry between the heavens and the earth.” But what use is there in conveying divine verses to you? It is like a nightingale singing to someone deaf. We ask God to cleanse the earth of your defilement and the defilement of those who were with you. He indeed answers the prayers of those who ask. Your worth has become clear to this extent: at the word of the vilest and most abject of people, you have turned away from the True One and clung to the tree of self and desire.
:::

### 737

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ديگر نوشته بودى كه در مجلسها صحبت ميشود كه جمال ابهى بناى فساد و فتنه گذاشته‌اند و مشهور شده كه اوّل برادرش را قائم و پنهان كرده باسم او نانى پخت حالا او را در كرده ميخواهند آجيل بخورند انتهى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va dīgar neveshteh būdī keh dar majleshā ṣoḥbat mīshavad keh Jamāl-e Abhā banā-ye fasād va fetneh godhāshteh-and va mashhūr shodeh keh avval barādarash rā qāʾem va penhān kardeh be-esm-e ū nānī pokht ḥālā ū rā dar kardeh mīkhvāhand ājīl bokhorand intahā.
:::

::: {.translation}
You had also written, “It is being said in gatherings that the All-Glorious Beauty has set about fomenting corruption and discord. It has become common talk that He first set up His brother as the Qāʾim and hid him away, baking bread for Himself in his name; now He has cast him out and wants to eat nuts.” End of quotation.
:::

### 738

::: {.original lang="fa"}
لعن اللّه من القاك و لعن اللّه من كذب و افترى ثمّ بغى و اطغى ثمّ كفر و اشقى و اللّه بسيار ناس را احمق يافته جميع ميدانند كه ایشان حسب الأمر دولت ايران به عراق تشريف آوردند و ميرزا يحيى بعد از مقدمه ارض طاء فرار نموده‌به عراق آمد قل ان يا ايّها المشرك انّ الّذى انفق روحه فى سبيل اللّه و كان بين يدى النّاس و ورد عليه فى كلّ حين سهام القضا ما لم يحصيها احد الّا اللّه الملك العليم الخبير و قام عليه اكثر النّاس فى ایّام الّتى كان فى العراق و فى كلّ يوم ينادى منهم بأن يأخذوه و يرسلوه الى ارض الطّاء و منهم من قال فسوف يغرقونه فى الشّط و منهم من قال ينفيه الدّولة و كان اللّه على ذلك لشهيد و عليم و بكت عليه عيون كلّ الأشیآء بما مسّته البأسآء و الضرآء و انّك كتبت ما كتبت الا لعنة اللّه على الكاذبين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Laʿana Allāhu man alqāka wa-laʿana Allāhu man kadhaba wa-iftarā thumma baghā wa-aṭghā thumma kafara wa-ashqā. Va-Allāh, bisyār nās rā aḥmaq yāftih. Jamīʿ mīdānand kih īshān ḥasb al-amr-i dawlat-i Īrān bih ʿIrāq tashrīf āvardand va Mīrzā Yaḥyā baʿd az muqaddamih-yi Arḍ-i Ṭāʾ farār nimūdih bih ʿIrāq āmad. Qul an yā ayyuhā al-mushrik, inna alladhī anfaqa rūḥahu fī sabīli Allāh wa-kāna bayna yaday al-nās wa-warada ʿalayhi fī kulli ḥīn sihāmu al-qaḍāʾ mā lam yuḥṣihā aḥad illā Allāhu al-Maliku al-ʿAlīmu al-Khabīr, wa-qāma ʿalayhi aktharu al-nās fī ayyām allatī kāna fī al-ʿIrāq, wa-fī kulli yawm yunādī minhum bi-an yaʾkhudhūhu wa-yursilūhu ilā arḍ al-Ṭāʾ, wa-minhum man qāla fa-sawfa yughriqūnahu fī al-shaṭṭ, wa-minhum man qāla yanfīhi al-dawlah, wa-kāna Allāhu ʿalā dhālika la-shahīd wa-ʿalīm. Wa-bakat ʿalayhi ʿuyūnu kulli al-ashyāʾ bi-mā massathu al-baʾsāʾ wa-al-ḍarrāʾ, wa-innaka katabta mā katabta. Alā laʿnatu Allāhi ʿalā al-kādhibīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
May God curse the one who prompted you, and may God curse the one who lied and fabricated, then acted unjustly and led others into transgression, then disbelieved and brought misery. By God, he has found people very foolish. Everyone knows that He came to Iraq at the command of the government of Iran, while Mīrzā Yaḥyā fled after the incident in the Land of Ṭā and came to Iraq. Say: O idolater! The One who expended His life in the path of God was in full view of the people, and at every moment the arrows of fate rained upon Him in numbers that no one but God, the King, the All-Knowing, the All-Informed, could count. Most of the people rose against Him during His days in Iraq. Every day some called for Him to be seized and sent to the Land of Ṭā; some said, “They will drown Him in the river”; and others said, “The government will exile Him.” God indeed witnessed and knew all this. The eyes of all things wept for Him because of the suffering and adversity that afflicted Him, yet you wrote what you wrote. Surely God’s curse rests upon the liars.
:::

### 739

::: {.original lang="fa"}
كلّ اشیآء شاهد و گواهند كه در سنين توقّف در عراق ابدا اميد جان نبود و در كلّ حين ببلاياى جديده مبتلا و مع‌ذلك امثال آن نفوس رذليّه ذكر نان و آجيل مينمايند و ملاحظه كن كه چه قدر از عقل ظاهره محروم شده و اللّه هر نفسى كلماتت را ملاحظه نمايد قهر حقّ را ظاهر و آشكار در تو مشاهده مينمايد سبحان اللّه نفسيكه عاجز است دو كلمه پارسى را بعبارات حسنه تحرير نمايد اعترض على الّذى بارادة منه خلق قلم الأعلی و ظهر منه الصّرير الّذى به استجذبت قلوب ما كان و ما يكون افّ لك و بما ظهر منك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Kull-i ashyāʾ shāhid va guvāhand kih dar sinīn-i tavaqquf dar ʿIrāq abadan umīd-i jān nabūd va dar kull-i ḥīn bih-balāyā-yi jadīdih mubtalā, va maʿa dhālik amthāl-i ān nufūs-i radhīliyyih dhikr-i nān va ājīl mīnamāyand. Va mulāḥiẓih kun kih chih qadr az ʿaql-i ẓāhirih maḥrūm shudih. Va-Allāh, har nafsī kalimātat rā mulāḥiẓih namāyad qahr-i Ḥaqq rā ẓāhir va āshkār dar tu mushāhidih mīnamāyad. Subḥān Allāh, nafsī kih ʿājiz ast du kalimih-yi pārsī rā bih-ʿibārāt-i ḥasanih taḥrīr namāyad, iʿtaraḍa ʿalā alladhī bi-irādatin minhu khuliqa Qalamu al-Aʿlā wa-ẓahara minhu al-ṣarīru alladhī bihi istujdhibat qulūbu mā kāna wa-mā yakūn. Uffin laka wa-bi-mā ẓahara minka.
:::

::: {.translation}
All things bear witness and testify that during the years of residence in Iraq there was never any hope of survival, and at every moment new afflictions arose. Yet the likes of those vile souls speak of bread and nuts. Consider how utterly bereft of ordinary reason you have become. By God, anyone who reads your words sees God’s wrath plainly and manifestly in you. Glory be to God! Someone unable to write two words of Persian in a graceful manner has objected to the One by whose will the Most Exalted Pen was created and from whom came the sound of its writing, through which the hearts of all that has been and will be were drawn. Shame on you and on what has proceeded from you!
:::

### 740

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و لكن از اين مردم غافل بعيد نيست كه همين كلمات تو را بر كلمات حقّ ترجيح دهند چنانچه سنين لانهاية لهاعجل را بر حقّ ترجيح داده و پرستيده‌اند و حال هم بآن مشغولند بسيار حيف است كه انسان باينگونه كلمات نالايقه تكلّم نمايد چه كه كلمات حاكيند از نفس انسانى لذا كلمات اهل منظر اكبر مزيّن است بطراز ادب نسئل اللّه بأن لا يجعلنا عريّا من هذا الثّوب الّذى به يظهر قدر الانسان بين ملأ الأكوان و امتيازه عن الحيوان ثمّ نسئله بأن يقرّبنا عليه و ينقطعنا عن دونه و يطهّرنا عن روايح الوهم و التّقليد و يجعلنا من الّذين قالوا اللّه ربّنا ثمّ استقاموا و ما منعهم استهزاء الخلايق اجمعين و لاشماتة الغافلين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va-lākin az īn mardum-i ghāfil baʿīd nīst kih hamīn kalimāt-i tu rā bar kalimāt-i Ḥaqq tarjīḥ dihand, chunānchih sinīn lā nihāyata lahā ʿijl rā bar Ḥaqq tarjīḥ dādih va parastīdih-and va ḥāl ham bi-ān mashghūland. Bisyār ḥayf ast kih insān bi-īngūnih kalimāt-i nālāyiqih takallum namāyad, chih kih kalimāt ḥākī-and az nafs-i insānī. Lidhā kalimāt-i ahl-i Manẓar-i Akbar muzayyan ast bih-ṭirāz-i adab. Nasʾalu Allāha bi-an lā yajʿalanā ʿariyyan min hādhā al-thawb alladhī bihi yaẓharu qadru al-insān bayna malaʾ al-akwān wa-imtiyāzuhu ʿan al-ḥayawān. Thumma nasʾaluhu bi-an yuqarribanā ʿalayhi wa-yanqaṭiʿanā ʿan dūnihi wa-yuṭahhiranā ʿan rawāʾiḥ al-wahm wa-al-taqlīd wa-yajʿalanā min alladhīna qālū Allāhu rabbunā thumma istaqāmū wa-mā manaʿahum istihzāʾu al-khalāʾiq ajmaʿīn wa-lā shamātatu al-ghāfilīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Yet it would not be surprising if these heedless people preferred these very words of yours to the words of the True One, just as for endless years they have preferred the calf to the True One and worshipped it, and are still doing so. It is a great pity for a human being to utter such unworthy words, for words reflect the human soul. Thus the words of the people of the Most Great View are adorned with the ornament of courtesy. We ask God not to leave us stripped of this robe, through which human worth becomes manifest among all created beings, as does the distinction between humans and animals. Then we ask Him to draw us near to Him, detach us from all besides Him, purify us of the odors of delusion and imitation, and make us among those who said, “God is our Lord,” and then stood firm, undeterred by the mockery of all creatures or the gloating of the heedless.
:::

### 741

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اللّهمّ يا الهى فافتح ابصار هؤلآء ليروك ظاهراً بين خلقك و مشرقاً فى مملكتك و انّك يا الهى لو فتحت ابصارهم ما ابتليت باستهزائهم و احجار ظنونهم و سهام اوهامهم كما فتحت ابصار احبّائك و عرفتهم ما لاعرفته دونهم و انّك لو كشفت الحجبات لهم كما كشفت عن وجوههم ما احتجبوا و ما اعترضوا فلمّا سترت عن هؤلآء و كشفت لاحبّائك لذا ارتفع ضجيج الغافلين من بريّتك و صريخ المتوهّمين من اهل مملكتك اذا اسئلك بنفسك بأن تكشف لهم حجبات الّتى منعتهم عن عرفانك و عرفان مظهر نفسك ليجمعنّ كلّ على شاطى بحر توحيدك و مقرّ عزّ تقديسك و تفريدك و انّك انت على ما تشآء قدير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Allāhumma yā ilāhī, fa-ftaḥ abṣāra hāʾulāʾ li-yarawka ẓāhiran bayna khalqika wa-mushriqan fī mamlakatika. Wa-innaka yā ilāhī law fataḥta abṣārahum mā ibtulīta bi-istihzāʾihim wa-aḥjāri ẓunūnihim wa-sihāmi awhāmihim, kamā fataḥta abṣāra aḥibbāʾika wa-ʿarraftahum mā lā ʿarafathu dūnahum. Wa-innaka law kashafta al-ḥujubāt lahum kamā kashafta ʿan wujūhihim mā iḥtajabū wa-mā iʿtaraḍū. Fa-lammā satarta ʿan hāʾulāʾ wa-kashafta li-aḥibbāʾika lidhā irtafaʿa ḍajīju al-ghāfilīn min bariyyatika wa-ṣarīkhu al-mutawahhimīn min ahli mamlakatika. Idhan asʾaluka bi-nafsika bi-an takshifa lahum ḥujubāt allatī manaʿathum ʿan ʿirfānika wa-ʿirfāni maẓhari nafsika li-yajmaʿanna kullun ʿalā shāṭiʾi baḥri tawḥīdika wa-maqarri ʿizzi taqdīsika wa-tafrīdika. Wa-innaka anta ʿalā mā tashāʾ qadīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
O God, my God! Open the eyes of these people, that they may see You manifest among Your creatures and shining in Your kingdom. My God, had You opened their eyes, You would not have been afflicted by their mockery, the stones of their suspicions, and the arrows of their imaginings, just as You opened the eyes of Your loved ones and made known to them what no others knew. Had You lifted the veils for these people as You lifted them from the faces of Your loved ones, they would not have remained veiled or raised objections. But because You concealed Yourself from these and revealed Yourself to Your loved ones, the clamor of the heedless among Your creatures and the cries of the deluded among the people of Your kingdom have risen. I therefore ask You by Your own Self to lift for them the veils that have kept them from recognizing You and the Manifestation of Your Self, so that all may gather on the shore of the ocean of Your oneness and at the seat of the glory of Your holiness and singleness. You indeed have power over whatever You will.
:::

### 742

::: {.original lang="fa"}
آنانكه ذكر نموده‌اند كه ايشان نان باسم او درست نموده ‌و اللّه خجالت ميبرم از ذكر چنين نفوس بی‌‌ادب رذلى و آن خود سيّد محمّد خبيث است اين اذكار اذكار اولى النّجابه نبوده و نخواهد بود و هر نفسى كه چنين كلمه تكلّم نموده‌ مثل آنست كه كسى بگويد شمس از ظلمت مستنير شده و يا عندليب از زاغ تغنّى آموخته و يا قطعهء ياقوت از حجر كسب ضيا و لون كرده چه فايده كه آن غافل مطّلع نيست و نفوسى كه مابين بوده جميع را تكذيب نموده‌اند كه مبادا حرف صدقى بميان آيد و ناس بشنوند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ānān kih dhikr nimūdih-and kih īshān nān bih-ism-i ū durust nimūdih—va-Allāh khijālat mībaram az dhikr-i chunīn nufūs-i bī-adab-i radhilī—va ān khud-i Siyyid Muḥammad-i khabīth ast. Īn adhkār adhkār-i ulī al-najābih nabūdih va nakhvāhad būd, va har nafsī kih chunīn kalimih takallum nimūdih mithl-i ānast kih kasī bigūyad shams az ẓulmat mustanīr shudih va yā ʿandalīb az zāgh taghannī āmūkhtih va yā qiṭʿih-yi yāqūt az ḥajar kasb-i ḍiyā va lawn kardih. Chih fāʾidih kih ān ghāfil muṭṭaliʿ nīst, va nufūsī kih mābayn būdih jamīʿ rā takdhīb nimūdih-and kih mabādā ḥarf-i ṣidqī bih-miyān āyad va nās bishnavand.
:::

::: {.translation}
Those who have stated that He made bread in his name—by God, I am ashamed to mention such vile, ill-mannered souls—and it is that wicked Siyyid Muḥammad himself. Such remarks have never been, nor will they ever be, the remarks of noble people. Anyone who has uttered such a statement is like someone saying that the sun has been illumined by darkness, that the nightingale has learned to sing from the crow, or that a ruby has acquired its radiance and color from a stone. But what use is it? That heedless one is unaware, and they have branded as liars all those who were present, lest a truthful word be uttered and the people hear it.
:::

### 743

::: {.original lang="fa"}
سيّد محمّدى كه و اللّه العظيم افتخار مينمود كه در حضور مبارك بايستد حال آمده و اينگونه مفتريات نسبت بحقّ داده حمد خدا را كه اين عباد بغير حقّ و راستى تكلّم ننموده‌ و نخواهيم نمود و دين بدنيا مبادله ننموده‌ايم و از حقّ چشم نپوشيده‌ايم جميع شكر مينمايند كه بايمان باللّه در اين ظهور فايز شده‌اند و اين عبد ناطق يا ليتنى ما ولدت من امّى و لو ولدت ما رضعت و لو رضعت ما اشدّ ظهرى فيا ليت كنت من الفاقدين در هر نفسى كه اقلّ من ذرّ حبّ اللّه باشد راضى نشده و نخواهد شد كه چنين امور مشاهده نمايد الى اللّه فوضنا الأمر و عليه توكّلنا و نسئل من بدايع جوده بأن يوفّقنا على الاقرار بوحدانيّته و الاعتراف بفردانيّته و ينقطعنا عن دونه و انّه لعلى كلّ شیء قدير ثمّ نسئله باسم الّذى به فصّل بين الحقّ و الباطل بأن يوفّقك على ذكره و عرفان مظهر نفسه و يطهّرك عن اشارات هؤلآء الكاذبين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Siyyid Muḥammadī kih va-Allāh al-ʿAẓīm iftikhār mīnamūd kih dar ḥuḍūr-i mubārak bāyistad ḥāl āmadih va īngūnih muftariyāt nisbat bih-Ḥaqq dādih. Ḥamd-i Khudā rā kih īn ʿibād bih-ghayr-i ḥaqq va rāstī takallum nanimūdih va nakhvāhīm nimūd va dīn bih-dunyā mubādilih nanimūdih-īm va az Ḥaqq chashm napūshīdih-īm. Jamīʿ shukr mīnamāyand kih bih-īmān bi-Allāh dar īn ẓuhūr fāʾiz shudih-and va īn ʿabd nāṭiq: yā laytanī mā wulidtu min ummī wa-law wulidtu mā raḍiʿtu wa-law raḍiʿtu mā ushidda ẓahrī fa-yā layta kuntu min al-fāqidīn. Dar har nafsī kih aqall-i min dharr ḥubb Allāh bāshad rāḍī nashudih va nakhvāhad shud kih chunīn umūr mushāhidih namāyad. Ilā Allāhi fawwaḍnā al-amr wa-ʿalayhi tawakkalnā wa-nasʾalu min badāʾiʿi jūdihi bi-an yuwaffiqanā ʿalā al-iqrār bi-waḥdāniyyatihi wa-al-iʿtirāf bi-fardāniyyatihi wa-yanqaṭiʿanā ʿan dūnihi wa-innahu la-ʿalā kulli shayʾ qadīr. Thumma nasʾaluhu bi-ismi alladhī bihi fuṣṣila bayna al-ḥaqq wa-al-bāṭil bi-an yuwaffiqaka ʿalā dhikrihi wa-ʿirfāni maẓhari nafsihi wa-yuṭahhiraka ʿan ishārāti hāʾulāʾ al-kādhibīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Siyyid Muḥammad, who, by God the Almighty, used to take pride in standing in the blessed presence, has now come forward and attributed such fabrications to the True One. Praise be to God that we servants have spoken nothing but truth and honesty, and never will speak otherwise. We have not exchanged faith for worldly gain, nor have we turned our eyes away from the True One. All give thanks that they have attained faith in God in this Revelation, while this servant says: “If only I had not been born of my mother! And if I had been born, had not been suckled; and if I had been suckled, my back had not been strengthened. If only I had been among those lost!” No soul possessing even less than a mote of the love of God has ever been, or ever will be, content to witness such things. To God we have committed the matter, and in Him we have placed our trust. We ask, from the wonders of His bounty, that He enable us to affirm His unity and acknowledge His singleness, and detach us from all besides Him. He indeed has power over all things. Then we ask Him, by the Name through which truth was distinguished from falsehood, to enable you to remember Him and recognize the Manifestation of His Self, and to purify you of the insinuations of these liars.
:::

### 744

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فو‌اللّه الّذى لا اله الّا هو بلايائى در اين ارض وارد كه احدى قادر بر احصاى آن نه بكرّات فرموده‌اند آنچه در سجن و تحت سلاسل و اغلال بوده‌ام و در دست مشركين مبتلا بشأنيكه ديار بديار برده‌اند و سر و پاى برهنه از محلّ بمحلّ كشيده‌اند هيچكدام از بلا محسوب نه اعظم بليّه كه در ابداع شبه نداشته و نخواهد داشت آن است كه حقّ بدست ظالمى كه باسم عدل معروف است مبتلا شود چه كه آن بی‌انصاف اعتمادا على حمقاء الأرض لايخاف و لايبالى يفعل ما يأمره النّفس و الهوى چنانچه مشاهده ميشود نفسى را كه آن همه تربيت و حفظ نمودم بعد استكباراً على اللّه و اعراضاً منه و اعتراضاً عليه وارد آورده آنچه را هيچ ظالمى وارد نياورده و علّت اين ظلم اطمينان از عباد غافلين بوده چه كه اگر موقن بود باينكه ناس صاحب بصرند و اعمالش را تصديق نمينمايند بچنين اعمال ارتكاب نمينمود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-Allāh alladhī lā ilāha illā huwa, balāyāʾī dar īn arḍ vārid kih aḥadī qādir bar iḥṣā-yi ān nah. Bih-karrāt farmūdih-and: ānchih dar sijn va taḥt-i salāsil va aghlāl būdih-am va dar dast-i mushrikīn mubtalā, bih-shaʾnī kih diyār bih-diyār burdih-and va sar va pāy barahnih az maḥall bih-maḥall kashīdih-and, hīchkudām az balā maḥsūb nah. Aʿẓam baliyyih kih dar ibdāʿ shibh nadāshtih va nakhvāhad dāsht ān ast kih Ḥaqq bih-dast-i ẓālimī kih bih-ism-i ʿadl maʿrūf ast mubtalā shavad, chih kih ān bī-inṣāf iʿtimādan ʿalā ḥumaqāʾ al-arḍ lā yakhāfu wa-lā yubālī yafʿalu mā yaʾmuruhu al-nafs wa-al-hawā. Chunānchih mushāhidih mīshavad nafsī rā kih ān hamih tarbiyat va ḥifẓ nimūdam baʿd istikbāran ʿalā Allāh wa-iʿrāḍan minhu wa-iʿtirāḍan ʿalayhi vārid āvardih ānchih rā hīch ẓālimī vārid nayāvardih. Va ʿillat-i īn ẓulm iṭmīnān az ʿibād-i ghāfilīn būdih, chih kih agar mūqin būd bi-īnkih nās ṣāḥib-i baṣarand va aʿmālash rā taṣdīq namīnamāyand bih-chunīn aʿmāl irtikāb namīnimūd.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, besides whom there is no other god, afflictions have befallen us in this land that no one can count. He has repeatedly said: “All that I suffered in prison, in chains and fetters, and at the hands of the idolaters, who took Me from land to land and dragged Me, bareheaded and barefoot, from place to place—none of this counts as affliction. The greatest affliction, which has never had and will never have its like in creation, is for the True One to fall into the hands of an oppressor known for justice. For that unjust man, relying on the fools of the earth, has neither fear nor concern, and does whatever self and desire command him.” As can be seen, the person whom I nurtured and protected so much afterward, out of arrogance toward God, aversion to Him, and opposition to Him, inflicted what no oppressor had ever inflicted. The cause of this oppression was his confidence in the heedless servants, for had he been certain that the people possessed discernment and would not endorse his deeds, he would not have committed such acts.
:::

### 745

::: {.original lang="fa"}
لازال باكثرى از عباد هر قدر عنايت بيشتر شده بيشتر بكفران قيام نموده‌اند حكايت شيطان از قبل ذكر شد كه در هر يك از سموات باسمى معروف و در ملكوت اعلى بكمال وصف موصوف و قرنها در قيام و ركوع و قعود و سجود بوده و بعد چنان شد كه بر مراصد جالس و عباد را از شطر رحمن منع مينمود و كاش انفس مشركه در اين ایّام باين مقدار كفايت مينمودند لا فو‌الّذى نفسى بيده لن يسكن عطش بغضهم الّا بشرب دمى و كان الشّيطان استعاذ بين يدى الرّحمن منهم و من اعمالهم و لكن النّاس هم لا يفقهون و لا يشعرون
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Lā yazāl bi-aktharī az ʿibād har qadr ʿināyat bīshtar shudih bīshtar bih-kufrān qiyām nimūdih-and. Ḥikāyat-i shayṭān az qabl dhikr shud kih dar har yak az samāvāt bih-ismī maʿrūf va dar malakūt-i aʿlā bih-kamāl-i vaṣf mawṣūf va qarnhā dar qiyām va rukūʿ va quʿūd va sujūd būdih, va baʿd chunān shud kih bar marāṣid jālis va ʿibād rā az shaṭr-i Raḥmān manʿ mīnamūd. Va kāsh anfus-i mushrikih dar īn ayyām bi-īn miqdār kifāyat mīnamūdand. Lā fa-wa-alladhī nafsī bi-yadihi lan yaskuna ʿaṭashu bughḍihim illā bi-shurbi damī, wa-kāna al-shayṭānu istaʿādha bayna yaday al-Raḥmān minhum wa-min aʿmālihim, wa-lākin al-nāsu hum lā yafqahūn wa-lā yashʿurūn.
:::

::: {.translation}
It has always been the case with most servants that the more favor they have received, the more they have risen in ingratitude. The story of Satan was mentioned earlier: he was known by a name in each of the heavens, was described in the most perfect terms in the kingdom on high, and for centuries stood, bowed, sat, and prostrated himself in worship. Yet afterward he came to sit in ambush, keeping the servants from turning toward the All-Merciful. If only the idolatrous souls in these days had contented themselves with that much! No, by Him in whose hand is my soul, the thirst of their hatred will never be quenched except by drinking my blood. Satan himself has sought refuge before the All-Merciful from them and their deeds, but the people neither understand nor perceive.
:::

### 746

::: {.original lang="fa"}
معلوم نشد كه مقصود از آجيل كه از قلم نحست جارى شده چه بوده هرگز اشیآء فانيه و زخارف دنيويه در ميان نبوده گويا مقصود دراهمى كه در هر شهر از باب عالى مخصوص خدّام ميفرستاده‌اند بوده اگر اينست حال كه راجع بمشرك باللّه شده و بمحبوب خود فايز شدند افّ لهم و لحيائهم و لوفائهم از باب اللّه منقطع شده بهر بابی‌ توجّه نموده‌و التجا نموده‌اند و از جمال قدم شكايت کرده‌‌اند تا آنكه بمطلوب خود رسيدند خوب حقّ يافتى محكم متمسّك شو كه شايد بمتابعت آن نفوس باسفل النّيران وارد شوى
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Maʿlūm nashud kih maqṣūd az ājīl kih az qalam-i naḥsat jārī shudih chih būdih. Hargiz ashyāʾ-i fāniyih va zakhārif-i dunyaviyyih dar miyān nabūdih. Gūyā maqṣūd darāhimī kih dar har shahr az Bāb-i ʿĀlī makhṣūṣ-i khuddām mīfiristādih-and būdih. Agar īnast, ḥāl kih rājiʿ bih-mushrik bi-Allāh shudih va bih-maḥbūb-i khud fāʾiz shudand. Uffin lahum wa-li-ḥayāʾihim wa-li-wafāʾihim. Az bāb Allāh munqaṭiʿ shudih bih-har bābī tavajjuh nimūdih va iltijā nimūdih-and va az Jamāl-i Qidam shikāyat kardih-and tā ānkih bih-maṭlūb-i khud rasīdand. Khūb ḥaqq yāftī, muḥkam mutamassik shaw kih shāyad bih-mutābiʿat-i ān nufūs bih-asfal-i nīrān vārid shavī.
:::

::: {.translation}
It is not clear what was meant by the nuts that flowed from your ill-omened pen. Perishable things and worldly vanities were never at issue. Apparently, the reference was to the sums of money that the Sublime Porte sent in each city specifically for the attendants. If that is what was meant, these have now passed to the one who associates partners with God, and they have attained their beloved. Shame on them, their sense of shame, and their fidelity! Having cut themselves off from God’s door, they have turned to every door, sought refuge there, and complained of the Ancient Beauty until they attained their object. What a fine truth you have found! Cling firmly to it, that perhaps, by following those souls, you may enter the lowest depths of the fires.
:::

### 747

::: {.original lang="fa"}
آىغافل نفوس رذيله كه باطّلاع نفس ملحدت مخصوص زخارف چه مقدار ذلّت نموده‌اند و تضييع امر کرده‌اند مع‌ذلك چنين نفوس را حقّ دانسته و از حقّى كه ابدا اعتنا بنفسى نفرموده بلكه خدّامش اعتنا نداشته‌اند معرض شده لعن اللّه من شهد برهان اللّه و انكره و عرف تنزيهه عمّا سواه و اعرض عنه
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ay ghāfil, nufūs-i radhīlih kih bi-iṭṭilāʿ-i nafs-i mulḥidat makhṣūṣ-i zakhārif chih miqdār dhillat nimūdih-and va taḍyīʿ-i Amr kardih-and, maʿa dhālik chunīn nufūs rā ḥaqq dānistih va az Ḥaqqī kih abadan iʿtinā bih-nafsī nafarmūdih balkih khuddāmash iʿtinā nadāshtih-and muʿriḍ shudih. Laʿana Allāhu man shahida burhāna Allāh wa-ankarahu wa-ʿarafa tanzīhahu ʿammā siwāhu wa-aʿraḍa ʿanhu.
:::

::: {.translation}
O heedless one! As your own impious self knows, those vile souls have abased themselves to such a degree solely for worldly vanities, and have dishonored the Cause. Yet you have regarded such souls as true and turned away from the True One, who has never paid heed to anyone—indeed, even His attendants have paid them no heed. May God curse the one who witnessed God’s proof and denied it, and recognized His transcendence above all besides Him yet turned away from Him.
:::

### 748

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اى ملأ بيان اعتراضات اين مردود كه بالقاى ميرزا يحيى و سيّد محمّد نوشته مخصوص ذكر شد تا بدانيد كه چه مقدار ضرّ وارد شده و ادراك نمائيد نوحه و ندبه نقطه اولى را بر ظهور آخر و آن جمال مبارك چون مطّلع بوده‌اند بر نفوس مشركه كه چه خواهند نمود لذا در جميع بيان بوصاياى لايحصى كلّ را وصيّت فرموده‌اند و بشأنى تأكيد فرموده‌اند كه فوق آن ممكن نه چنانچه از قلم اعلى نازل كه جميع بكمال تقديس و تنزيه خود را مقدس و منزّه نمايند و هم‌چنين لباس و اسباب بيت را كه مباد لحاظ اللّه در حين ظهور بر شیء غير محبوب افتد و بهمان قدر سبب حزن قلب اطهر گردد با اين وصايا شأن اهل بيان را ملاحظه نمائيد كه مخصوص رسائل رديّه نوشته و بمقرّ عرش فرستاده‌اند اين بيان اولو الأفئدة و اولو العزّة و اولو الوفا را كافى است
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ay malaʾ-i Bayān, iʿtirāḍāt-i īn mardūd kih bih-ilqā-yi Mīrzā Yaḥyā va Siyyid Muḥammad nivishtih makhṣūṣ dhikr shud tā bidānīd kih chih miqdār ḍurr vārid shudih va idrāk namāyīd nawḥih va nudbih-yi Nuqṭih-yi Ūlā rā bar Ẓuhūr-i Ākhar. Va ān Jamāl-i Mubārak chūn muṭṭaliʿ būdih-and bar nufūs-i mushrikih kih chih khvāhand nimūd, lidhā dar jamīʿ-i Bayān bih-vaṣāyā-yi lā yuḥṣā kull rā vaṣiyyat farmūdih-and va bih-shaʾnī taʾkīd farmūdih-and kih fawq-i ān mumkin nah. Chunānchih az Qalam-i Aʿlā nāzil kih jamīʿ bih-kamāl-i taqdīs va tanzīh khud rā muqaddas va munazzah namāyand va hamchunīn libās va asbāb-i bayt rā, kih mabād liḥāẓ Allāh dar ḥīn-i ẓuhūr bar shayʾ-i ghayr-i maḥbūb uftad va bih-hamān qadr sabab-i ḥuzn-i qalb-i aṭhar gardad. Bā īn vaṣāyā shaʾn-i ahl-i Bayān rā mulāḥiẓih namāyīd kih makhṣūṣ rasāʾil-i raddiyyih nivishtih va bih-maqarr-i ʿarsh firistādih-and. Īn bayān ulū al-afʾidih va ulū al-ʿizzih va ulū al-wafā rā kāfī ast.
:::

::: {.translation}
O people of the Bayān! The objections that this rejected one wrote at the prompting of Mīrzā Yaḥyā and Siyyid Muḥammad have been specifically mentioned so that you may know how much harm has been inflicted and understand the Primal Point’s lamentation and mourning over the later Revelation. Since that blessed Beauty knew what the idolatrous souls would do, He admonished everyone throughout the Bayān with countless counsels, emphasizing them to a degree beyond which nothing is possible. Thus it was revealed by the Most Exalted Pen that all should sanctify and purify themselves with the utmost holiness and purity, and likewise their clothing and household furnishings, lest at the time of the Revelation God’s gaze fall upon anything displeasing and thereby cause even that much sorrow to His most pure heart. In light of these counsels, consider the condition of the people of the Bayān: they have deliberately written treatises of refutation and sent them to the seat of the throne. This statement suffices for those possessed of understanding, honor, and fidelity.
:::

### 749

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فو‌اللّه وارد شده آنچه بر احدى از مظاهر قبل وارد نشده و با جميع بلايا و رزايا و محن كه وارد شده شاكر و صابريم و ابدا حزنى نه و لكن از تضييع امر اللّه قلب در احتراق است قسم بحقّ كه بر جميع لازم است نوحه و ندبه بر امر الهى چه كه بشانى امر اللّه را تضييع نموده‌اند كه فاسقه ارض را خير النّسا ناميده اند ملاحظه كنيد كه چگونه بطلان اين قوم را حقّ ظاهر فرمود فو‌اللّه بهمين فعل بر كلّ حجّت تمام شد چه كه اكثرى آن فاسقه را ميشناسند و بر احوالش مطّلعند و از آن خير النّسا خير الرّجال را عارف شويد يعنى آن نفسى كه او را سيّده نساء نوشته فو‌اللّه لعنه كلّ الذّرّات و لكن هو ما استشعر فى نفسه و يكون من الفرحين بی‌‌شرميش بمقامى رسيده كه زوجات خود را خير النّسا ناميده و حرم نقطه اولى را تصرّف نموده ‌و بخشيده فويل لهم من عذاب يوم عظيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-llāh vārid shudih ānchih bar aḥadī az maẓāhir-i qabl vārid nashudih va bā jamīʿ-i balāyā va razāyā va miḥan kih vārid shudih shākir va ṣābirīm va abadan ḥuznī nah va lākin az taḍyīʿ-i Amr Allāh qalb dar iḥtirāq ast. Qasam bi-Ḥaqq kih bar jamīʿ lāzim ast nawḥih va nudbih bar Amr-i Ilāhī chih kih bi-shaʾnī Amr Allāh rā taḍyīʿ namūdih-and kih fāsiqiy-i arḍ rā khayr al-nisāʾ nāmīdih-and. Mulāḥiẓih kunīd kih chigūnih buṭlān-i īn qawm rā Ḥaqq ẓāhir farmūd. Fa-wa-llāh bi-hamīn fiʿl bar kull ḥujjat tamām shud chih kih aktharī ān fāsiqih rā mīshināsand va bar aḥvālash muṭṭaliʿand va az ān khayr al-nisāʾ khayr al-rijāl rā ʿārif shavīd yaʿnī ān nafsī kih ū rā sayyidiy-i nisāʾ nivishtih. Fa-wa-llāh laʿanahu kull al-dharrāt wa lākin huwa mā istashʿara fī nafsihi wa yakūnu min al-fariḥīn. Bī-sharmīsh bi-maqāmī rasīdih kih zawjāt-i khud rā khayr al-nisāʾ nāmīdih va ḥaram-i Nuqṭiy-i Ūlā rā taṣarruf namūdih va bakhshīdih. Fa-waylun lahum min ʿadhābi yawmin ʿaẓīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
By God, what has befallen Us has befallen none of the Manifestations of the past. Yet despite all the afflictions, calamities, and ordeals that have befallen Us, We remain thankful and patient, with no sorrow whatsoever. But Our heart burns over the dishonoring of the Cause of God. By the True One, everyone must lament and mourn for the divine Cause, for they have so dishonored the Cause of God that they have called a depraved woman of the earth “the best of women.” Consider how the True One has exposed the falsity of these people. By God, through this act alone the proof against all has been made complete, for most people know that depraved woman and are acquainted with her circumstances. And through that “best of women,” recognize the “best of men”—namely, the person who has described her as the foremost of women. By God, every atom has cursed him, yet he remains unaware within himself and is among those who rejoice. His shamelessness has reached such a point that he has called his own wives “the best of women,” and has taken possession of the wife of the Primal Point and given her away. Woe to them, then, for the punishment of a tremendous day!
:::

### 750

::: {.original lang="ar"}
در اينمقام اين آيات ابدع احلى من لسان اللّه العلى الأبهی نازل هذا ما نزل حينئذ من جبروت عزّ عليّا يا قوم فاعلموا بانّا اصطفينا امّ نقطة الأولی و انّها قد كانت من خيرة الاماء لدى العرش مذكوراً و حرّم اطلاق هذا الاسم على غيرها كذلك رقم من قلم الأعلی فى لوح القضا الّذى كان فى كنائز عصمة ربّك محفوظا و انّها لخير النّسا و بعدها تطلق على ضلع النّقطة الّتى ما خرجت عن حصن العصمة و ما مسّتها ايدى الخائنين و كذلك كان الأمر مقضيّا و الّتى خانت انّها خرجت عن النّقطة و قطعت نسبتها من اللّه الّذى قدّر كلّ امر فى لوح مبينا قل انّ المشركين ظنّوا بانّا اردنا ان ننسخ ما نزل على نقطة البيان
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Dar īn maqām īn āyāt-i abdaʿ-i aḥlā min lisān Allāh al-ʿAlī al-Abhā nāzil: Hādhā mā nazala ḥīnaʾidhin min jabarūti ʿizzin ʿaliyyā. Yā qawm fa-iʿlamū bi-annā iṣṭafaynā umma Nuqṭati al-Ūlā wa innahā qad kānat min khīrati al-imāʾ ladā al-ʿarsh madhkūrā. Wa ḥurrima iṭlāqu hādhā al-ism ʿalā ghayrihā. Kadhālika ruqima min Qalami al-Aʿlā fī Lawḥi al-Qaḍā alladhī kāna fī kanāʾizi ʿiṣmati rabbika maḥfūẓā. Wa innahā la-khayru al-nisāʾ wa baʿdahā tuṭlaqu ʿalā ḍilʿi al-Nuqṭah allatī mā kharajat ʿan ḥiṣni al-ʿiṣmah wa mā massathā aydī al-khāʾinīn. Wa kadhālika kāna al-amru maqḍiyyā. Wa allatī khānat innahā kharajat ʿan al-Nuqṭah wa qaṭaʿat nisbatāhā min Allāh alladhī qaddara kulla amrin fī lawḥin mubīnā. Qul inna al-mushrikīn ẓannū bi-annā aradnā an nansakha mā nazala ʿalā Nuqṭati al-Bayān.
:::

::: {.translation}
At this point these wondrous, most sweet verses were revealed from the tongue of God, the Most High, the All-Glorious: “This is what has now descended from the dominion of lofty glory. O people, know that We have chosen the mother of the Primal Point, and she has been recorded before the Throne as among the choicest of handmaidens. Applying this name to anyone other than her has been forbidden. Thus has it been inscribed by the Most Exalted Pen in the Tablet of Decree, preserved within the treasuries of your Lord’s unfailing protection. She is indeed the best of women, and after her this designation applies to the wife of the Point who has not left the stronghold of purity and whom the hands of the treacherous have not touched. Thus has the matter been decreed. As for the one who acted treacherously, she has departed from the Point and severed her relationship with God, who has ordained all things in a clear Tablet. Say: The idolaters have imagined that We intended to abrogate what was revealed to the Point of the Bayān.”
:::

### 751

::: {.original lang="ar"}
قل فو‌ربّی‌ الرّحمن لو نريد كما ظنّوا ليس لأحد ان يعترض على اللّه الّذى خلق كلّ شیء بأمر من عنده و انّه كان على كلّ شیء قديرا و كلّما نريد هو ما اراد اللّه و ما يظهر منّى هو ما ظهر منه و يشهد بذلك كلّ موحّد عليماً و لكن اللّه اراد بهذا الظّهور ان يثبت ما نزل من عند نقطة البيان و يضع احكامه على اعناق الفراعنة من ملأ الطّغيان و كان نفسه الحقّ على ذلك شهيدا و انّا اردنا ان نفدى نفسنا فى سبيله كما فدى نفسه فى سبيلى اتّقوا اللّه يا قوم و لاتفتروا على الّذى به اشرقت شمس البيان و ظهر حكمه بين الخلايق جميعاً فسوف نثبت احكامه و نبرهن آثاره فى الأرض بقدرة و سلطان مبيناً
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul fa-wa-rabbī al-Raḥmān law nurīdu kamā ẓannū laysa li-aḥadin an yaʿtariḍa ʿalā Allāh alladhī khalaqa kulla shayʾin bi-amrin min ʿindihi wa innahu kāna ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīrā. Wa kullamā nurīdu huwa mā arāda Allāh wa mā yaẓharu minnī huwa mā ẓahara minhu wa yashhadu bi-dhālika kullu muwaḥḥidin ʿalīmā. Wa lākin Allāh arāda bi-hādhā al-ẓuhūr an yuthbita mā nazala min ʿindi Nuqṭati al-Bayān wa yaḍaʿa aḥkāmahu ʿalā aʿnāqi al-farāʿinah min malaʾi al-ṭughyān wa kāna nafsuhu al-Ḥaqq ʿalā dhālika shahīdā. Wa innā aradnā an nafdī nafsanā fī sabīlihi kamā fadā nafsahu fī sabīlī. Ittaqū Allāh yā qawm wa lā taftarū ʿalā alladhī bihi ashraqat shamsu al-Bayān wa ẓahara ḥukmuhu bayna al-khalāʾiqi jamīʿā. Fa-sawfa nuthbitu aḥkāmahu wa nubarhinu āthārahu fī al-arḍ bi-qudratin wa sulṭānin mubīnā.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: By my Lord, the All-Merciful, if We wished to do as they have imagined, no one would have the right to object to God, who created all things through a command from Himself. He is indeed powerful over all things. Whatever We wish is what God has wished, and whatever appears from Me is what has appeared from Him. Every knowledgeable believer in His oneness bears witness to this. But through this Revelation God has intended to confirm what was revealed by the Point of the Bayān and to place His laws upon the necks of the Pharaohs among the hosts of tyranny. His own Self, the True One, bears witness to this. We have intended to sacrifice Ourself in His path, just as He sacrificed Himself in My path. Fear God, O people, and do not fabricate lies against Him through whom the Sun of the Bayān has shone and His decree has appeared among all created beings. We will assuredly establish His laws and demonstrate the truth of His writings on earth with power and manifest authority.
:::

### 752

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اليوم خير النّسا امّ نقطه اولى است و حرام شده اطلاق اين اسم بر اماء اللّه و هم‌چنين اذن داده شده اطلاق اين اسم بعدها بر ضلع نقطه كه در فارس ساكنند و از حصن عصمت ربّانى خارج نشده‌اند و حرمة اللّه را رعايت نموده‌ و دست خائنين بذيل عصمتش نرسيده فو‌نفسى الحقّ او است بتول عذرا و حرم اعلى و عصمت كبرى ان اخدموها يا احبّائى بصدق مبين لانّها بقيّة اللّه بينكم ان انتم من العارفين نسئل اللّه بأن يستقيمها على ما هى عليه و يعصمها عن مسّ الهاتكين الّذين تحرّكهم ارياح النّفس و الهوى كيف یشآء اولئك هم فى ضلال مبين و بأن يثبتها على هذا الأمر و انّه على كلّ شیء قدير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Al-yawm khayr al-nisāʾ umm-i Nuqṭiy-i Ūlā ast va ḥarām shudih iṭlāq-i īn ism bar imāʾ Allāh va hamchunīn idhn dādih shudih iṭlāq-i īn ism baʿdahā bar ḍilʿ-i Nuqṭih kih dar Fārs sākinand va az ḥiṣn-i ʿiṣmat-i rabbānī khārij nashudih-and va ḥurmat Allāh rā riʿāyat namūdih va dast-i khāʾinīn bi-dhayl-i ʿiṣmatash narisīdih. Fa-wa-nafsī al-Ḥaqq ū ast Batūl-i ʿAdhrā va Ḥaram-i Aʿlā va ʿIṣmat-i Kubrā. An ikhdumūhā yā aḥibbāʾī bi-ṣidqin mubīn li-annahā baqiyyatu Allāh baynakum in antum min al-ʿārifīn. Nasʾalu Allāh bi-an yastaqīmahā ʿalā mā hiya ʿalayhi wa yaʿṣimahā ʿan massi al-hātikīn alladhīna tuḥarrikuhum aryāḥu al-nafs wa al-hawā kayfa yashāʾ. Ulāʾika hum fī ḍalālin mubīn. Wa bi-an yuthbitahā ʿalā hādhā al-amr wa innahu ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
Today the best of women is the mother of the Primal Point, and applying this name to the handmaidens of God has been forbidden. Permission has likewise been given to apply this name after her to the wife of the Point who resides in Fārs, who has not left the stronghold of divine purity, who has observed the sanctity of God, and whose robe of purity the hands of the treacherous have not reached. By My own Self, the True One, she is the chaste Virgin, the Most Exalted Consort, and the Most Great Purity. Serve her, O My loved ones, with manifest sincerity, for she is what remains of God among you, if you are among those who understand. We ask God to keep her steadfast in her present state and to protect her from the touch of those who violate sanctity, whom the winds of self and desire move as they please. They are indeed in manifest error. And We ask Him to establish her firmly in this Cause. He is powerful over all things.
:::

### 753

::: {.original lang="fa"}
يا قوم انّى ما اردت فيما اقول نفسى بل نفس اللّه ان انتم من المنصفين و نلقى عليكم ما اراد ربّكم العلىّ العظيم حرمت حرم اللّه بر كلّ لازم در جميع احوال رعايتشان محبوب بوده و هم‌چنين نفوسيكه نفس الرّحمن از مابين آن نفوس ظاهر شده عزّزوهم و وقّروهم يا قوم و لاتكوننّ من الغافلين و جميع اين فضل محقّق مادام كه حبل نسبت منقطع نشود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Yā qawm innī mā aradtu fīmā aqūlu nafsī bal nafsa Allāh in antum min al-munṣifīn wa nulqī ʿalaykum mā arāda rabbukum al-ʿAlī al-ʿAẓīm. Ḥurmat-i ḥaram-i Allāh bar kull lāzim dar jamīʿ-i aḥvāl riʿāyatishān maḥbūb būdih va hamchunīn nufūsī kih Nafs-i Raḥmān az mābayn-i ān nufūs ẓāhir shudih. ʿAzzizūhum wa waqqirūhum yā qawm wa lā takūnanna min al-ghāfilīn. Va jamīʿ-i īn faḍl muḥaqqaq mādām kih ḥabl-i nisbat munqaṭiʿ nashavad.
:::

::: {.translation}
O people, in what I say I have not intended My own self, but the Self of God, if you judge fairly. We convey to you what your Lord, the Most High, the Almighty, has willed. Respect for the family of God is incumbent upon all; showing them consideration in every circumstance has been deemed desirable, as has showing consideration to those from whose midst the Person of the All-Merciful has appeared. Honor and revere them, O people, and do not be among the heedless. All this bounty holds true so long as the bond of relationship is not severed.
:::

### 754

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انت تعلم يا الهى بانّى احبّ هؤلآء و كلّ ما نسب الى نفسك وَ اَجد منهم نفحات قميص رحمانيّتك وفوحات ثوب عزّك و مواهبك و اشتاق لقائهم و الاجتماع معهم و المؤانسة بهم اذا اسئلك يا الهى باسم الّذى جعلته سلطان الأسماء بين الأرض و السّمآء و به كسّرتَ اصنام النّفس و الهوى و به غسّلت العارفين و المشتاقين و طهّرتهم عن روايح ما سواك فى ملكوت الانشآء بأن تشتعل فى صدور هؤلآء مشاعل حبّك ليهتدى بها اهل مملكتك الّذينهم غفلوا عن ذكرك و ثنائك و بعدوا عن شاطى قربك و لقائك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa anta taʿlamu yā ilāhī bi-annī uḥibbu hāʾulāʾ wa kulla mā nusiba ilā nafsika wa ajidu minhum nafaḥāti qamīṣi raḥmāniyyatika wa fawaḥāti thawbi ʿizzika wa mawāhibika wa ashtāqu liqāʾahum wa al-ijtimāʿa maʿahum wa al-muʾānasata bihim. Idhan asʾaluka yā ilāhī bi-ismi alladhī jaʿaltahu sulṭāna al-asmāʾ bayna al-arḍ wa al-samāʾ wa bihi kassarta aṣnāma al-nafs wa al-hawā wa bihi ghassalta al-ʿārifīn wa al-mushtāqīn wa ṭahhartahum ʿan rawāʾiḥi mā siwāka fī malakūti al-inshāʾ bi-an tashtaʿila fī ṣudūri hāʾulāʾ mashāʿilu ḥubbika li-yahtadiya bihā ahlu mamlakatika alladhīnahum ghafalū ʿan dhikrika wa thanāʾika wa baʿudū ʿan shāṭiʾi qurbika wa liqāʾika.
:::

::: {.translation}
You know, O my God, that I love these souls and all that is related to Your own Self. From them I perceive the fragrances of the shirt of Your all-mercifulness and the sweet scents of the robe of Your glory and Your gifts, and I long to meet them, to gather with them, and to enjoy their companionship. I therefore ask You, O my God, by the Name that You have made sovereign over all names between earth and heaven, through which You have shattered the idols of self and desire, and through which You have washed those who know You and long for You, purifying them from the scents of all besides You in the kingdom of creation, to kindle the torches of Your love in the hearts of these souls, so that through them the inhabitants of Your realm may be guided—those who have neglected Your remembrance and praise and have strayed far from the shore of nearness to You and meeting with You.
:::

### 755

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فيا الهى لاتمنعهم عمّا ظهر بينهم و لاتحرمهم عمّا رشحت فى تلك الأیّام من سحاب رحمتك و غمام فضلك ثمّ اسمعهم يا الهى فى كلّ حين نغماتك و الحانك الّتى ارتفعت عن مقرّ عرش وحدانيّتك و كرسىّ عزّ فردانيّتك ثمّ اقبل منهم يا الهى ما ترك عنهم فى ایّامك الّتى فيها اشرقت شمس جمالك عن افق مشيّتك و كان ان يمشى بينهم سلطان الرّسل باقتدارك و عظمتك و انت ترى يا الهى بانّ البكا منعنى حينئذ عن ذكرك و ثنائك و ثنآء الّذين نسبتهم الى مظهر نفسك بما خطر ببالى ذكر محبوبی‌ و مقصودى و رجائى و ذكر ایّامه و شئوناته
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-yā ilāhī lā tamnaʿhum ʿammā ẓahara baynahum wa lā taḥrimhum ʿammā rashaḥta fī tilka al-ayyām min saḥābi raḥmatika wa ghamāmi faḍlika. Thumma asmiʿhum yā ilāhī fī kulli ḥīnin naghamātika wa alḥānaka allatī irtafaʿat ʿan maqarri ʿarshi waḥdāniyyatika wa kursiyyi ʿizzi fardāniyyatika. Thumma iqbal minhum yā ilāhī mā turika ʿanhum fī ayyāmika allatī fīhā ashraqat shamsu jamālika ʿan ufuqi mashīʾatika wa kāna an yamshiya baynahum Sulṭānu al-Rusul bi-iqtidārika wa ʿaẓamatika. Wa anta tarā yā ilāhī bi-anna al-bukāʾ manaʿanī ḥīnaʾidhin ʿan dhikrika wa thanāʾika wa thanāʾi alladhīna nasabtahum ilā maẓhari nafsika bi-mā khaṭara bi-bālī dhikru maḥbūbī wa maqṣūdī wa rajāʾī wa dhikru ayyāmihi wa shuʾūnātihi.
:::

::: {.translation}
O my God, do not keep them from what has appeared among them, and do not deprive them of what You have showered in these days from the clouds of Your mercy and Your grace. Let them hear, O my God, at every moment, Your melodies and songs that have risen from the seat of the throne of Your oneness and the seat of the glory of Your singleness. Accept from them, O my God, what they have left behind in Your days, in which the Sun of Your beauty has shone from the horizon of Your will and the Sovereign of the Messengers has walked among them through Your might and grandeur. You see, O my God, that weeping has now prevented me from remembering and praising You and from praising those whom You have related to the Manifestation of Your own Self, for there has come to my mind the remembrance of my Beloved, my Desire, and my Hope, and the remembrance of His days and His ways.
:::

### 756

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فو‌عزّتك يا الهى بنفسى ضيع اسم الوفآء بين الأرض و السّمآء لانّ محبوبی‌ فدى نفسه فى سبيلك و انّى اكون موجوداً فى مملكتك بين بريّتك مع انّك انت تعلم يا الهى بانّى فى كلّ حين احبّ ان انفق روحى و نفسى فى سبيله و فى كلّ آن انتظر هذا و لكن لم ادر باىّ جهة منعت عمّا اردت فو‌عزّتك اذاً انقطع الصّبر منّى حبّاً للقائك و طلباً لوصالك و لاتفرح نفسى الّا حين الّذى تشاهد وجهى محمرّاً بدمى و كلّما القيت نفسى بين يدى الأعدا انّك حفظتنى بسلطان مشيّتك و كلّما اودعت جسدى تحت ايادى اولى البغضآء انت عصمتنى بقدرتك و قوّتك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā ilāhī bi-nafsī ḍuyyiʿa ismu al-wafāʾ bayna al-arḍ wa al-samāʾ li-anna maḥbūbī fadā nafsahu fī sabīlika wa innī akūnu mawjūdan fī mamlakatika bayna bariyyatika maʿa annaka anta taʿlamu yā ilāhī bi-annī fī kulli ḥīnin uḥibbu an unfiqa rūḥī wa nafsī fī sabīlihi wa fī kulli ānin antaẓiru hādhā wa lākin lam adri bi-ayyi jihatin muniʿtu ʿammā aradtu. Fa-wa-ʿizzatika idhan inqaṭaʿa al-ṣabru minnī ḥubban li-liqāʾika wa ṭalaban li-wiṣālika wa lā tafraḥu nafsī illā ḥīna alladhī tushāhidu wajhī muḥmarran bi-damī. Wa kullamā alqaytu nafsī bayna yaday al-aʿdāʾ innaka ḥafiẓtanī bi-sulṭāni mashīʾatika wa kullamā awdaʿtu jasadī taḥta ayādī ulī al-baghḍāʾ anta ʿaṣamtanī bi-qudratika wa quwwatika.
:::

::: {.translation}
By Your glory, O my God, through me the very name of faithfulness has been lost between earth and heaven, for my Beloved sacrificed Himself in Your path, while I remain alive in Your realm among Your creatures. Yet You know, O my God, that at every moment I long to offer up my spirit and my life in His path, and at every instant I await this. But I do not know why I have been prevented from attaining what I desired. By Your glory, my patience has now come to an end through love of meeting You and longing for union with You. My soul will rejoice only when You behold my face reddened with my blood. Whenever I have cast myself into the hands of my enemies, You have preserved me through the sovereignty of Your will; and whenever I have placed my body beneath the hands of those possessed of hatred, You have protected me through Your power and might.
:::

### 757

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فلمّا جعلتنى محروماً عمّا اردته فى سبيلك قرّبنى الى ارض الّتى استوى عليها محبوبی‌ و محبوب العالمين ومقصودى و مقصود العارفين لاستأنس بها و اقبّل ترابها و اجد منها روايح قدسك و نفحات رحمتك لعلّ بذلك تسكن نفسى من اضطرابها و روحى من احتراقها و جسدى من اهتزازه و استغفرك يا الهى عن كلّ ذلك لانّه حینئذ يكون حيّاً فى الأفق الأبهی يشهد و يرى و بذلك تشهد نفسى و روحى و ذاتى و قلمى و لسانى و ظاهرى و باطنى و اوّلى و آخرى لا اله الّا انت العزيز المتعالى المقتدر المهيمن العليم الحكيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-lammā jaʿaltanī maḥrūman ʿammā aradtuhu fī sabīlika qarribnī ilā arḍi allatī istawā ʿalayhā maḥbūbī wa maḥbūbu al-ʿālamīn wa maqṣūdī wa maqṣūdu al-ʿārifīn li-astaʾnisa bihā wa uqabbila turābahā wa ajida minhā rawāʾiḥa qudsika wa nafaḥāti raḥmatika laʿalla bi-dhālika taskunu nafsī min iḍṭirābihā wa rūḥī min iḥtirāqihā wa jasadī min ihtizāzihi. Wa astaghfiruka yā ilāhī ʿan kulli dhālika li-annahu ḥīnaʾidhin yakūnu ḥayyan fī al-Ufuqi al-Abhā yashhadu wa yarā wa bi-dhālika tashhadu nafsī wa rūḥī wa dhātī wa qalamī wa lisānī wa ẓāhirī wa bāṭinī wa awwalī wa ākhirī. Lā ilāha illā anta al-ʿAzīz al-Mutaʿālī al-Muqtadir al-Muhaymin al-ʿAlīm al-Ḥakīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
Since You have deprived me of what I desired in Your path, bring me near to the land upon which my Beloved and the Beloved of all worlds, my Desire and the Desire of those who know You, once dwelt, so that I may find solace in it, kiss its dust, and perceive from it the fragrances of Your holiness and the breezes of Your mercy. Perhaps through this my soul may be stilled from its agitation, my spirit from its burning, and my body from its trembling. I ask Your forgiveness, O my God, for all this, for He is even now alive in the All-Glorious Horizon, witnessing and seeing. To this bear witness my soul, my spirit, my being, my pen, my tongue, my outer and inner self, my beginning and my end. There is no God but You, the Almighty, the Most Exalted, the All-Powerful, the All-Protecting, the All-Knowing, the All-Wise.
:::

### 758

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بدانيد ايقوم كه اين غلام رحمن در جميع احيان اراده‌اش آن بوده كه آنچه از ظهور قبلش نقطه بيان روح من فى الأكوان فداه نازل شده ثابت نمايد حركت ننموده‌ام مگر برضاى او چنانچه او حركت نفرمود مگر برضاى اين غلام مع آنكه كلّ آنچه از اين مشيّت ظاهر شود نفس مشيّت و اراده او بوده و كفى بنفسه شهيداً و لكن مشركين بيان گمان نموده‌اند و در باديه‌هاى مهلكه ظنّ مشى کرده‌اند چنانچه نسبت داده‌اند كه اين غلام گفته كه نقطه بيان از يكحرف من خلق شده لا و اللّه آنچه نازل شده منزل حقّ تعالى سلطنته و تعالى قدرته و تعالى عظمته و تعالى اقتداره و تعالى عزّه و تعالى رفعته و تعالى شأنه و تعالى بهائه و تعالى امره بوده و خواهد بود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bidānīd ay qawm kih īn Ghulām-i Raḥmān dar jamīʿ-i aḥyān irādih-ash ān būdih kih ānchih az ẓuhūr-i qablash Nuqṭiy-i Bayān rūḥu man fī al-akwān fidāhu nāzil shudih thābit namāyad. Ḥarakat nanamūdih-am magar bi-riḍā-yi ū chunānchih ū ḥarakat nafarmūd magar bi-riḍā-yi īn Ghulām maʿa ānkih kull-i ānchih az īn Mashiyyat ẓāhir shavad nafs-i mashiyyat va irādiy-i ū būdih wa kafā bi-nafsihi shahīdā. Va lākin mushrikīn-i Bayān gumān namūdih-and va dar bādiyih-hā-yi muhlikiy-i ẓann mashy kardih-and chunānchih nisbat dādih-and kih īn Ghulām guftih kih Nuqṭiy-i Bayān az yik ḥarf-i man khalq shudih. Lā wa-llāh ānchih nāzil shudih munzil Ḥaqq taʿālā salṭanatuhu wa taʿālā qudratuhu wa taʿālā ʿaẓamatuhu wa taʿālā iqtidāruhu wa taʿālā ʿizzuhu wa taʿālā rifʿatuhu wa taʿālā shaʾnuhu wa taʿālā bahāʾuhu wa taʿālā amruhu būdih va khwāhad būd.
:::

::: {.translation}
Know, O people, that this Youth of the All-Merciful has at all times intended to establish whatever was revealed by His previous Manifestation, the Point of the Bayān—may the souls of all in existence be sacrificed for Him. I have acted only in accordance with His good pleasure, just as He acted only in accordance with the good pleasure of this Youth. Moreover, whatever appears from this Will has been His very will and purpose, and His own Self is sufficient as a witness. But the idolaters of the Bayān have indulged in conjecture and wandered through the deadly wildernesses of supposition, even alleging that this Youth has said that the Point of the Bayān was created from a single letter of Mine. No, by God! Whatever has been revealed, its Revealer has been and will be the True One—exalted be His sovereignty, exalted be His power, exalted be His grandeur, exalted be His might, exalted be His glory, exalted be His loftiness, exalted be His station, exalted be His splendor, and exalted be His Cause.
:::

### 759

::: {.original lang="fa"}
بگوئيد اى بي‌شرمهاى ارض آنچه در اين ظهور نازل بعينه همان كلمات نقطه اوّليّه بوده و خواهد بود و اين غلام لازال جز عبوديّت صرفه دوست نداشته فو‌الّذى نفسى بيده عبوديّت محبوب جانم بوده بشأنيكه كلّما اشاهد موقفاًمن مواقف الأرض احبّ ان اخرّ عليه سجّدا للّه محبوبی‌ و محبوب العارفين فيا ليت على كلّ ذرّة من ترابها سجدت للّه ربّی‌ و ربّ العالمين و اينكه در الواح ذكر مقامات عاليه شده ناظراً الى امر اللّه و شأنه و عزّه و اجلاله بوده چنانچه نقطهء بيان فرموده ‌انّه ينطق فى كلّ شیء بانّى انا اللّه لا اله الّا انا ان يا خلقى ايّاى فاعبدون و اگر نظر باينمقام نبود فو‌نفسه المحبوب ما ذكرت الّا العبوديّة الصّرفة للّه الحقّ كذلك كان الأمر و لكن النّاس هم لا يشعرون
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Bigūyīd ay bī-sharmhā-yi arḍ ānchih dar īn ẓuhūr nāzil bi-ʿaynihi hamān kalimāt-i Nuqṭiy-i Avvaliyyih būdih va khwāhad būd va īn Ghulām lā yazāl juz ʿubūdiyyat-i ṣirfih dūst nadāshtih. Fa-wa-alladhī nafsī bi-yadihi ʿubūdiyyat maḥbūb-i jānam būdih bi-shaʾnī kih kullamā ushāhidu mawqifan min mawāqifi al-arḍ uḥibbu an akhirra ʿalayhi sujjadan li-llāh maḥbūbī wa maḥbūbi al-ʿārifīn. Fa-yā layta ʿalā kulli dharratin min turābihā sajadtu li-llāh rabbī wa rabbi al-ʿālamīn. Va īnkih dar alvāḥ dhikr-i maqāmāt-i ʿāliyih shudih nāẓiran ilā Amr Allāh wa shaʾnihi wa ʿizzihi wa ijlālihi būdih chunānchih Nuqṭiy-i Bayān farmūdih innahu yanṭiqu fī kulli shayʾin bi-annī anā Allāh lā ilāha illā anā an yā khalqī iyyāya fa-uʿbudūn. Va agar naẓar bi-īn maqām nabūd fa-wa-nafsihi al-Maḥbūb mā dhakartu illā al-ʿubūdiyyata al-ṣirfata li-llāh al-Ḥaqq. Kadhālika kāna al-amr wa lākin al-nāsu hum lā yashʿurūn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: O shameless ones of the earth! Whatever is revealed in this Revelation has been and will be precisely the words of the Primal Point, and this Youth has always loved nothing but pure servitude. By Him in whose hand is my soul, servitude has been the beloved of my heart, to such a degree that whenever I behold any spot on earth, I long to fall prostrate upon it before God, my Beloved and the Beloved of those who know Him. Would that upon every atom of its dust I had prostrated myself before God, my Lord and the Lord of all worlds! The exalted stations mentioned in the Tablets have been spoken of with regard to the Cause of God, His station, His glory, and His majesty, just as the Point of the Bayān has said: “He speaks in all things, saying, ‘I am God; there is no God but Me. O My creation, worship Me alone.’” Were it not with regard to this station, then by His own beloved Self, I would have spoken of nothing but pure servitude to God, the True One. Such is the matter, but the people do not perceive it.
:::

### 760

::: {.original lang="fa"}
در اينمقام مناجاتى كه مخصوص يكى از احبّا از سماء عزّ ابهى نازل ذكر ميشود تا كلّ عارف شوند كه در جميع مراتب اكمل از كلّ مظاهر ظاهر شده‌اند حتّى در مقام عبوديّت
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Dar īn maqām munājātī kih makhṣūṣ-i yikī az aḥibbā az samāʾ-i ʿizz-i Abhā nāzil dhikr mīshavad tā kull ʿārif shavand kih dar jamīʿ-i marātib akmal az kull-i maẓāhir ẓāhir shudih-and ḥattā dar maqām-i ʿubūdiyyat.
:::

::: {.translation}
At this point a prayer revealed from the heaven of all-glorious majesty especially for one of the loved ones is cited, so that all may recognize that He has appeared in every degree more perfect than all the Manifestations, even in the station of servitude.
:::

### 761

::: {.original lang="ar"}
سبحانك اللّهمّ يا الهى تشهد السن الممكنات على سلطنتك و اقتدارك و على فقرى و افتقارى عند ظهورات غنائك اذا يا الهى فانظر هذا العاصى الّذى لم يزل كان ناظراً الى شطر غفرانك و قلبه متوجّهاً الى افق فضلك و مواهبك و انّى يا الهى من اوّل يوم الّذى خلقتنى بامرك و احييتنى من نسماءت جود رحمانيّتك ما توجّهت الى احد دونك و قمت الى مقابلة الأعدآء لسلطنتك و اقتدارك و دعوت الكلّ الى شاطى بحر توحيدك و سماء عزّ تفريدك و ما اردت فى ایّامى حفظ نفسى من طغاة خلقك بل اعلآء ذكرك بين بريّتك و بذلك ورد علىّ ما لا حمله احد من خلقك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Subḥānaka Allāhumma yā ilāhī, tashhadu alsunu al-mumkināti ʿalā salṭanatika wa-iqtidārika wa-ʿalā faqrī wa-iftiqārī ʿinda ẓuhūrāti ghināʾika. Idhan yā ilāhī fa-nẓur hādhā al-ʿāṣī alladhī lam yazal kāna nāẓiran ilā shaṭri ghufrānika wa-qalbuhu mutawajjihan ilā ufuqi faḍlika wa-mawāhibika. Wa-innī yā ilāhī min awwali yawmin alladhī khalaqtanī bi-amrika wa-aḥyaytanī min nasamāʾāti jūdi raḥmāniyyatika mā tawajjahtu ilā aḥadin dūnaka wa-qumtu ilā muqābalati al-aʿdāʾi li-salṭanatika wa-iqtidārika wa-daʿawtu al-kulla ilā shāṭiʾi baḥri tawḥīdika wa-samāʾi ʿizzi tafrīdika. Wa-mā aradtu fī ayyāmī ḥifẓa nafsī min ṭughāti khalqika bal iʿlāʾa dhikrika bayna bariyyatika wa-bi-dhālika warada ʿalayya mā lā ḥamalahu aḥadun min khalqika.
:::

::: {.translation}
Glory be to You, O God, my God! The tongues of all contingent beings testify to Your sovereignty and power, and to my poverty and need before the manifestations of Your wealth. Look, then, O my God, upon this sinner, who has always gazed toward Your forgiveness, his heart turned toward the horizon of Your grace and Your gifts. O my God, from the very first day when You created me by Your command and brought me to life through the breezes of Your all-merciful generosity, I have turned to no one but You. I arose to confront the enemies for the sake of Your sovereignty and power, and summoned everyone to the shore of the ocean of Your oneness and the heaven of the glory of Your singleness. Throughout my days, I have sought not to protect myself from the tyrants among Your creatures, but to exalt Your remembrance among Your creation. Because of this, there has befallen me what none of Your creatures has borne.
:::

### 762

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و كم من ایّام يا الهى كنت فريداً بين المذنبين من عبادك و كم من ليالى يا محبوبی‌ كنت اسيراً بين الغافلين من خلقك و فى موارد البأسآء و الضّرّآء كنت ناطقاً بثنآء نفسك بين سمائك و ارضك و ذاكراً ببدايع ذكرك فى ملكوت امرك و خلقك و لو انّ كلّ ما ظهر منّى لاينبغى لسلطان عزّ وحدانيّتك و لايليق لشأنك و اقتدارك فو‌عزّتك يا محبوبی‌ لم اجد لنفسى وجوداً تلقآء مدين عزّك و كلّما اريد ان اثنى نفسك بثنآء يمنعنى فؤادى لانّ دونك لم يقدر ان يطير فى هواء ملكوت قربك او ان يصعد الى سماء جبروت لقائك فو‌عزّتك اشاهد بانّى لو اسجد لكفّ من التّراب الى آخر الّذى لا آخر له لنسبته الى اسمك الصّانع لا أجد نفسى بعيداً عن التّقرّب اليه و اشاهد بأنّ عملى لا ينبغى له بل كان محدوداً بحدودات نفسى و لو اخدم احداً من عبادك بحيث اقوم بين يديه بدوام ملكوتك و بقآء جبروتك لنسبته الى اسمك الخالق فو‌عزّتك لأجد نفسى مقصّراً عن ادآء خدمته و محروماً عمّا يليق له لانّ فى هذا المقام لا يرى الّا نسبتهم الى اسمائك و صفاتك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-kam min ayyāmin yā ilāhī kuntu farīdan bayna al-mudhnibīna min ʿibādika wa-kam min layālin yā maḥbūbī kuntu asīran bayna al-ghāfilīna min khalqika. Wa-fī mawāridi al-baʾsāʾi wa-l-ḍarrāʾi kuntu nāṭiqan bi-thanāʾi nafsika bayna samāʾika wa-arḍika wa-dhākiran bi-badāʾiʿi dhikrika fī malakūti amrika wa-khalqika. Wa-law anna kulla mā ẓahara minnī lā yanbaghī li-sulṭāni ʿizzi waḥdāniyyatika wa-lā yalīqu li-shaʾnika wa-iqtidārika, fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā maḥbūbī lam ajid li-nafsī wujūdan tilqāʾa madīni ʿizzika. Wa-kullamā urīdu an uthniya nafsaka bi-thanāʾin yamnaʿunī fuʾādī li-anna dūnaka lam yaqdir an yaṭīra fī hawāʾi malakūti qurbika aw an yaṣʿada ilā samāʾi jabarūti liqāʾika. Fa-wa-ʿizzatika ushāhidu bi-annī law asjudu li-kaffin mina al-turābi ilā ākhiri alladhī lā ākhira lahu li-nisbatihi ilā ismika al-Ṣāniʿi lā ajidu nafsī baʿīdan ʿani al-taqarrubi ilayhi wa-ushāhidu bi-anna ʿamalī lā yanbaghī lahu bal kāna maḥdūdan bi-ḥudūdāti nafsī. Wa-law akhdumu aḥadan min ʿibādika bi-ḥaythu aqūmu bayna yadayhi bi-dawāmi malakūtika wa-baqāʾi jabarūtika li-nisbatihi ilā ismika al-Khāliqi fa-wa-ʿizzatika la-ajidu nafsī muqaṣṣiran ʿan adāʾi khidmatihi wa-maḥrūman ʿammā yalīqu lahu li-anna fī hādhā al-maqāmi lā yurā illā nisbatuhum ilā asmāʾika wa-ṣifātika.
:::

::: {.translation}
How many days, O my God, I was alone among the sinful among Your servants, and how many nights, O my Beloved, I was a captive among the heedless among Your creatures! Amid hardship and adversity, I spoke Your praise between Your heaven and Your earth, and proclaimed the wonders of Your remembrance in the kingdom of Your command and creation. Although everything that has proceeded from me is unworthy of the sovereignty of Your glorious oneness and unbefitting Your station and power, yet, by Your glory, O my Beloved, I have found no existence of my own before the city of Your glory. Whenever I wish to offer You praise, my heart restrains me, for no one other than You can soar in the atmosphere of the kingdom of Your nearness or ascend to the heaven of the dominion of Your presence. By Your glory! I see that, were I to prostrate myself before a handful of dust until the end that has no end, because of its relationship to Your name, the Maker, I would not consider myself far from drawing near to it. I see that my deed would be unworthy of it, being confined instead within the limits of my own self. Were I to serve one of Your servants, standing before him for as long as Your kingdom endures and Your dominion remains, because of his relationship to Your name, the Creator, then, by Your glory, I would find myself falling short in serving him and deprived of what befits him, for in this station nothing is seen but their relationship to Your names and attributes.
:::

### 763

::: {.original lang="ar"}
انّ الّذى كان شأنه ذلك كيف يقدر ان يذكر الّذى باشارة من اصبعه خلقت الأسمآء و ملكوتها و الصّفات و جبروتها و باشارة اخرى ركّبت الكاف بالنّون و ظهر منها ما عجز عن عرفانه اعلى افئدة المقرّبين من اصفيائك و ابهى مشاعر المخلصين من اودّائك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Inna alladhī kāna shaʾnuhu dhālika kayfa yaqdiru an yadhkura alladhī bi-ishāratin min iṣbaʿihi khuliqati al-asmāʾu wa-malakūtuhā wa-l-ṣifātu wa-jabarūtuhā wa-bi-ishāratin ukhrā rukkibati al-kāfu bi-l-nūni wa-ẓahara minhā mā ʿajaza ʿan ʿirfānihi aʿlā afʾidati al-muqarrabīna min aṣfiyāʾika wa-abhā mashāʿiri al-mukhliṣīna min awiddāʾika.
:::

::: {.translation}
How can one whose condition is such make mention of Him at a gesture of whose finger the names and their kingdom, and the attributes and their dominion, were created, and at another gesture of whom the letter kāf was joined to the letter nūn, and from this appeared that which the loftiest hearts of those drawn near among Your chosen ones, and the most radiant faculties of the sincere among Your loved ones, are powerless to comprehend?
:::

### 764

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فو‌عزّتك يا محبوبی‌ صرت متحيّراً فى مظاهر صنعك و مطالع قدرتك و اشاهد نفسى عاجزاً عن عرفان ادنى آيتك و كيف عرفان نفسك اذاً اسئلك يا الهى باسمك الّذى به طيّرت العاشقين فى هوآء ارادتك و اهتديت به المشتاقين الى رضوان قربك و وصالك بأن تهبّ من رضوان عنايتك روايح الاطمينان على المضطرّين من احبّائك فى تلك الأیّام الّتى احاطتهم ارياح الافتتان من كلّ الجهات بحيث اضطربت النّفوس من سطوة قضائك و تزلزلت اركان الوجود عمّا نزل عليهم من سمآء تقديرك و بلغت اضطرابهم الى مقام تكاد ان تخمد فى مشكوة قلوبهم سراج حبّك و ذكرك و انّك انت المقتدر على ما تشآء و انّك انت الغفور الكريم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā maḥbūbī ṣirtu mutaḥayyiran fī maẓāhiri ṣunʿika wa-maṭāliʿi qudratika wa-ushāhidu nafsī ʿājizan ʿan ʿirfāni adnā āyatika wa-kayfa ʿirfāni nafsika. Idhan asʾaluka yā ilāhī bi-ismika alladhī bihi ṭayyarta al-ʿāshiqīna fī hawāʾi irādatika wa-ihtadayta bihi al-mushtāqīna ilā riḍwāni qurbika wa-wiṣālika bi-an tahubba min riḍwāni ʿināyatika rawāʾiḥu al-iṭmiʾnāni ʿalā al-muḍṭarrīna min aḥibbāʾika fī tilka al-ayyāmi allatī aḥāṭathum aryāḥu al-iftitāni min kulli al-jihāti bi-ḥaythu iḍṭarabati al-nufūsu min saṭwati qaḍāʾika wa-tazalzalat arkānu al-wujūdi ʿammā nazala ʿalayhim min samāʾi taqdīrika wa-balaghat iḍṭirābuhum ilā maqāmin takādu an takhmuda fī mishkāti qulūbihim sirāju ḥubbika wa-dhikrika. Wa-innaka anta al-Muqtadiru ʿalā mā tashāʾu wa-innaka anta al-Ghafūru al-Karīmu.
:::

::: {.translation}
By Your glory, O my Beloved! I am bewildered by the manifestations of Your handiwork and the dawning places of Your power. I see myself powerless to know even Your least sign; how much less can I know Your own Self! I therefore ask You, O my God, by Your name through which You have made the lovers soar in the atmosphere of Your will and guided those who yearn to the paradise of Your nearness and reunion with You, to let the fragrances of assurance waft from the paradise of Your care over those of Your loved ones who are in distress, in these days when the winds of trial have surrounded them from every direction. Souls have been shaken by the force of Your decree, and the pillars of existence have trembled at what has descended upon them from the heaven of Your ordainment. Their agitation has reached such a degree that the lamp of Your love and remembrance is almost extinguished in the niche of their hearts. You indeed have power over whatever You will, and You are indeed the Ever-Forgiving, the Generous.
:::

### 765

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فيا الهى و سيّدى تسمع ضجيج محبّيك و صريخهم من كلّ الأقطار بما ورد عليهم من الّذين كانت قلوبهم محروماً عن نفحات حبّك و ليس لهم من معين ليعينهم و لا من ناصر لينصرهم و كذلك ليس لاعدائهم من مانع ليمنعهم عن ضرّ هؤلآء لذا يفعلون ما يريدون و يعملون ما يشاؤن اذا فانصر يا الهى ببديع نصرك احبّائك الّذين ما استنصروا من غيرك و ما توجّهوا الى دونك و كانت عيونهم منتظرة لبدايع مواهبك و الطافك ثمّ ارحمهم يا الهى ببدايع رحمتك ثمّ ادخلهم فى حصن حمايتك و عنايتك و انّك انت الّذى يا الهى لم تزل كنت مأمن الخائفين و ملجأ المضطرّين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-yā ilāhī wa-sayyidī tasmaʿu ḍajīja muḥibbīka wa-ṣarīkhahum min kulli al-aqṭāri bi-mā warada ʿalayhim mina alladhīna kānat qulūbuhum maḥrūman ʿan nafaḥāti ḥubbika wa-laysa lahum min muʿīnin li-yuʿīnahum wa-lā min nāṣirin li-yanṣurahum wa-kadhālika laysa li-aʿdāʾihim min māniʿin li-yamnaʿahum ʿan ḍarri hāʾulāʾi li-dhā yafʿalūna mā yurīdūna wa-yaʿmalūna mā yashāʾūna. Idhan fa-nṣur yā ilāhī bi-badīʿi naṣrika aḥibbāʾaka alladhīna mā istanṣarū min ghayrika wa-mā tawajjahū ilā dūnika wa-kānat ʿuyūnuhum muntaẓiratan li-badāʾiʿi mawāhibika wa-alṭāfika. Thumma irḥamhum yā ilāhī bi-badāʾiʿi raḥmatika thumma adkhilhum fī ḥiṣni ḥimāyatika wa-ʿināyatika wa-innaka anta alladhī yā ilāhī lam tazal kunta maʾmana al-khāʾifīna wa-maljaʾa al-muḍṭarrīna.
:::

::: {.translation}
O my God and my Lord! You hear the lamentation of those who love You and their cries from every region over what has befallen them at the hands of those whose hearts are deprived of the breaths of Your love. They have no helper to assist them and no supporter to come to their aid. Nor is there anyone to restrain their enemies from harming them; thus they do whatever they desire and act as they please. Aid, then, O my God, with Your wondrous assistance, Your loved ones who have sought help from none but You and turned to no one besides You, whose eyes have awaited the wonders of Your gifts and Your favors. Have mercy on them, O my God, through the wonders of Your mercy, and bring them into the stronghold of Your protection and care. You, O my God, have always been the refuge of the fearful and the shelter of those in distress.
:::

### 766

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اسئلك بأن لاتحرم هؤلآء الضّعفآء عن بدايع جودك و افضالك و لاتدعهم بين ايدى الّذين ما خلقت كينوناتهم الّا من نار غضبك و قهرك و ما وجدوا روايح الرّحم و الانصاف و غرّتهم الدّنيا بغرورها الى شأن انكروا برهانك و اشركوا بنفسك و كفروا بآياتك و سفكوا دم احبّائك و امنائك فو‌عزّتك يا محبوبی‌ ارتكبوا ما لم يرتكبه احد من قبل و بذلك استحقّوا غضبك و سياط قهرك خذهم بسلطانك ثمّ سلّط عليهم من لا يرحمهم الّا بأن يرجعوا اليك و يدخلوا فى ظلّ عنايتك و يتوبوا اليك و انّك انت لم تزل كنت قادراً و لاتزال تكون مقتدراً و انّك انت المقتدر المتعالى العادل الحكيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Asʾaluka bi-an lā taḥrima hāʾulāʾi al-ḍuʿafāʾa ʿan badāʾiʿi jūdika wa-ifḍālika wa-lā tadaʿhum bayna aydī alladhīna mā khalaqta kaynūnātihim illā min nāri ghaḍabika wa-qahrika wa-mā wajadū rawāʾiḥa al-raḥmi wa-l-inṣāfi wa-gharrathumu al-dunyā bi-ghurūrihā ilā shaʾnin ankarū burhānaka wa-ashrakū bi-nafsika wa-kafarū bi-āyātika wa-safakū dama aḥibbāʾika wa-umanāʾika. Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā maḥbūbī irtakabū mā lam yartakibhu aḥadun min qablu wa-bi-dhālika istaḥaqqū ghaḍabaka wa-siyāṭa qahrika. Khudhhum bi-sulṭānika thumma salliṭ ʿalayhim man lā yarḥamuhum illā bi-an yarjiʿū ilayka wa-yadkhulū fī ẓilli ʿināyatika wa-yatūbū ilayka. Wa-innaka anta lam tazal kunta qādiran wa-lā tazālu takūnu muqtadiran wa-innaka anta al-Muqtadiru al-Mutaʿālī al-ʿĀdilu al-Ḥakīmu.
:::

::: {.translation}
I ask You not to deprive these weak ones of the wonders of Your generosity and bounty, and not to leave them in the hands of those whose beings You created from nothing but the fire of Your wrath and Your subduing might. They have never sensed the fragrances of compassion and fairness, and the world has so beguiled them with its deceptions that they have denied Your proof, associated partners with You, disbelieved in Your signs, and shed the blood of Your loved ones and Your trusted ones. By Your glory, O my Beloved! They have committed what no one before them has committed, and have thereby deserved Your wrath and the scourges of Your subduing might. Seize them through Your sovereignty, and set over them one who will show them no mercy unless they return to You, enter beneath the shadow of Your care, and turn to You in repentance. You have always been powerful and will forever be mighty. You are indeed the All-Powerful, the Most Exalted, the Just, the All-Wise.
:::

### 767

::: {.original lang="ar"}
سبحانك اللّهمّ يا الهى فانصر هذا المظلوم الّذى ابتلى بين يدى الظّالمين من خلقك و المشركين من اعدائك بعد الّذى ما تنفّس الّا باذنك و امرك قد كنت يا الهى راقداً على مهد السّكون مرّت علىّ ارياح فضلك و الطافك و ايقظتنى بها بسلطانك و مواهبك و اقمتنى بين عبادك بثنآء نفسك و اعلآء كلمتك اذا اعترض علىّ اكثر بريّتك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Subḥānaka Allāhumma yā ilāhī fa-nṣur hādhā al-Maẓlūma alladhī ibtuliya bayna yaday al-ẓālimīna min khalqika wa-l-mushrikīna min aʿdāʾika baʿda alladhī mā tanaffasa illā bi-idhnika wa-amrika. Qad kuntu yā ilāhī rāqidan ʿalā mahdi al-sukūni marrat ʿalayya aryāḥu faḍlika wa-alṭāfika wa-ayqaẓtanī bihā bi-sulṭānika wa-mawāhibika wa-aqamtanī bayna ʿibādika bi-thanāʾi nafsika wa-iʿlāʾi kalimatika idhan iʿtaraḍa ʿalayya aktharu bariyyatika.
:::

::: {.translation}
Glory be to You, O God, my God! Aid this Wronged One who has been afflicted at the hands of the unjust among Your creatures and those among Your enemies who associate partners with You, even though he has never drawn a breath except by Your permission and command. I was asleep, O my God, in the cradle of stillness. The winds of Your grace and favors passed over me, and through them You awakened me by Your sovereignty and Your gifts. You raised me up among Your servants to praise You and exalt Your word. Then most of Your creatures opposed me.
:::

### 768

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فو‌عزّتك يا الهى ما ظننت فى حقّهم ما ظهر منهم بعد الّذى انّك بشّرتهم بهذا الظّهور فى صحايف امرك و الواح قضائك و ما نزلت من عندك كلمة الّا و قد اخذت بها عهد هذا الغلام من خلقك و بريّتك اذاً صرت متحيّراً يا الهى و لم ادر ما افعل بين هؤلآء و كلّما اصمت عن بدايع ذكرك ينطقنى الرّوح بين سمائك و ارضك و كلّما اسكن يهتزّنى ما تهبّ عن يمين مشيّتك و ارادتك و اجد نفسى كورقة الّتى تحركها ارياح قضائك و تذهبها كيف تشآء بامرك و اذنك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā ilāhī mā ẓanantu fī ḥaqqihim mā ẓahara minhum baʿda alladhī innaka bashshartahum bi-hādhā al-ẓuhūri fī ṣaḥāʾifi amrika wa-alwāḥi qaḍāʾika wa-mā nazalat min ʿindika kalimatun illā wa-qad akhadhta bihā ʿahda hādhā al-ghulāmi min khalqika wa-bariyyatika. Idhan ṣirtu mutaḥayyiran yā ilāhī wa-lam adri mā afʿalu bayna hāʾulāʾi wa-kullamā aṣmutu ʿan badāʾiʿi dhikrika yunṭiqunī al-Rūḥu bayna samāʾika wa-arḍika wa-kullamā askunu yahtazzunī mā tahubbu ʿan yamīni mashīʾatika wa-irādatika wa-ajidu nafsī ka-waraqatin allatī tuḥarrikuhā aryāḥu qaḍāʾika wa-tudhhibuhā kayfa tashāʾu bi-amrika wa-idhnika.
:::

::: {.translation}
By Your glory, O my God! I had never expected from them what they have shown, after You had given them the glad tidings of this Revelation in the scriptures of Your Cause and the Tablets of Your decree. Not a word has descended from You through which You have not taken from Your creatures and Your creation a covenant concerning this Youth. I am therefore bewildered, O my God, and do not know what to do among these people. Whenever I fall silent concerning the wonders of Your remembrance, the Spirit makes me speak between Your heaven and Your earth. Whenever I am still, what blows from the right hand of Your purpose and will stirs me. I find myself like a leaf moved by the winds of Your decree and carried wherever You will, by Your command and permission.
:::

### 769

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و بما ظهر منّى يوقن كلّ بصير بانّ الأمر ليس بيدى بل بيدك و لم يكن زمام الاختيار فى قبضتى بل فى قبضتك و اقتدارك مع‌ذلك يا الهى اجتمعوا علىّ اهل مملكتك و ينزلن فى كلّ حين ما تفزع به حقايق اصفيائك و امنائك اذا اسئلك يا الهى باسمك الّذى به اهتديت العاشقين الى كوثر فضلك و الطافك و استجذبت المشتاقين الى رضوان قربك و لقائك بأن تفتح ابصار بريّتك ليشهدن فى هذا الظّهور ظهور عزّ فردانيّتك و طلوع انوار وجهك و جمالك ثمّ طهّرهم يا الهى من الظّنون و الأوهام ليجدن روايح التّقديس من قميص ظهورك و امرك لعلّ لايردنّ علىّ ما تمنع به انفسهم من نفحات شئون رحمانيّتك فى ایّام ظهور مظهر نفسك و مطلع امرك و لايرتكبن ما تجعل به ذواتهم مستحقّاً لظهورات قهرك و غضبك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-bi-mā ẓahara minnī yūqinu kullu baṣīrin bi-anna al-amra laysa bi-yadī bal bi-yadika wa-lam yakun zimāmu al-ikhtiyāri fī qabḍatī bal fī qabḍatika wa-iqtidārika. Maʿa dhālika yā ilāhī ijtamaʿū ʿalayya ahlu mamlakatika wa-yunazzilunna fī kulli ḥīnin mā tafzaʿu bihi ḥaqāʾiqu aṣfiyāʾika wa-umanāʾika. Idhan asʾaluka yā ilāhī bi-ismika alladhī bihi ihtadayta al-ʿāshiqīna ilā kawthari faḍlika wa-alṭāfika wa-istajdhabta al-mushtāqīna ilā riḍwāni qurbika wa-liqāʾika bi-an taftaḥa abṣāra bariyyatika li-yashhadanna fī hādhā al-ẓuhūri ẓuhūra ʿizzi fardāniyyatika wa-ṭulūʿa anwāri wajhika wa-jamālika. Thumma ṭahhirhum yā ilāhī mina al-ẓunūni wa-l-awhāmi li-yajidanna rawāʾiḥa al-taqdīsi min qamīṣi ẓuhūrika wa-amrika laʿalla lā yuridunna ʿalayya mā tamnaʿu bihi anfusahum min nafaḥāti shuʾūni raḥmāniyyatika fī ayyāmi ẓuhūri maẓhari nafsika wa-maṭlaʿi amrika wa-lā yartakibanna mā tajʿalu bihi dhawātuhum mustaḥaqqan li-ẓuhūrāti qahrika wa-ghaḍabika.
:::

::: {.translation}
Through what has proceeded from me, every discerning person knows with certainty that the matter is not in my hands but in Yours, and that the reins of choice are not in my grasp but in Your grasp and power. Nevertheless, O my God, the people of Your realm have gathered against me, and at every moment they bring down upon me what terrifies the inmost beings of Your chosen ones and Your trusted ones. I therefore ask You, O my God, by Your name through which You have guided the lovers to the heavenly river of Your grace and favors, and drawn those who yearn to the paradise of Your nearness and presence, to open the eyes of Your creatures so that in this Revelation they may witness the manifestation of the glory of Your singleness and the dawning of the lights of Your countenance and beauty. Purify them, O my God, of conjectures and delusions, that they may sense the fragrances of holiness from the garment of Your Revelation and Your Cause. Perhaps they will not inflict upon me what would deprive their own souls of the breaths of the expressions of Your all-merciful grace in the days of the appearance of the Manifestation of Your Self and the Dawning Place of Your Cause, nor commit what would make their own beings deserving of the manifestations of Your subduing might and wrath.
:::

### 770

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انت تعلم يا الهى بانّى كنت بين ملأ البيان كاَحد منهم و عاشرت معهم بالشّوق و الاشتياق و دعوتهم الى نفسك فى العشىّ و الاشراق ببدايع وحيك و الهامك و ورد علىّ منهم ما عجزت عن ذكره سكّان مداين انشائك فو‌عزّتك يا محبوبی‌ ما اصبحت الّا و قد صرت هدفا لسهام غلّهم و ما امسيت الّا و قد ورد علىّ رماح بغضهم و مع ما جعلتنى عالماً بما فى انفسهم و قادراً عليهم سترت و صبرت ناظراً الى ميقاتك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-anta taʿlamu yā ilāhī bi-annī kuntu bayna malaʾi al-bayāni ka-aḥadin minhum wa-ʿāshartu maʿahum bi-l-shawqi wa-l-ishtiyāqi wa-daʿawtuhum ilā nafsika fī al-ʿashiyyi wa-l-ishrāqi bi-badāʾiʿi waḥyika wa-ilhāmika wa-warada ʿalayya minhum mā ʿajazat ʿan dhikrihi sukkānu madāʾini inshāʾika. Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā maḥbūbī mā aṣbaḥtu illā wa-qad ṣirtu hadafan li-sihāmi ghillihim wa-mā amsaytu illā wa-qad warada ʿalayya rimāḥu bughḍihim wa-maʿa mā jaʿaltanī ʿāliman bi-mā fī anfusihim wa-qādiran ʿalayhim satartu wa-ṣabartu nāẓiran ilā mīqātika.
:::

::: {.translation}
You know, O my God, that I lived among the people of the Bayān as one of them, associated with them with ardent longing, and summoned them to You at evening and at dawn through the wonders of Your revelation and inspiration. Yet there has befallen me at their hands what the inhabitants of the cities of Your creation are powerless to recount. By Your glory, O my Beloved! No morning came without my becoming a target for the arrows of their malice, and no evening came without the spears of their hatred striking me. Although You had made me aware of what was within them and given me power over them, I concealed it and remained patient, looking toward Your appointed time.
:::

### 771

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فلمّا جاء الوعد و تمّت الميقات حركت ذيل السّتر اقلّ من ان يحصى اذاً فزع من فى جبروت الأمر و الخلق الّا الّذين خلقتهم من نار حبّك و هوآء شوقك و مآء عنايتك و تراب فضلك اولئك يصلّين عليهم اهل ملأ الأعلی و سكّان مداين البقآء فلك الحمد يا الهى بما عصمت الموحّدين و اهلكت المشركين و فصّلت بين الكلّ بكلمة اخرى الّتى خرجت من فم مشيّتك و ظهرت من قلم ارادتك و بذلك اعترض علىّ عباد الّذينهم خلقوا بكلمة امرك و بعثوا بارادتك و بلغوا فى الاعراض الى مقام كفروا بك و بآياتك و حاربوا بنفسك
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-lammā jāʾa al-waʿdu wa-tammat al-mīqātu ḥarraktu dhayla al-sitri aqalla min an yuḥṣā idhan faziʿa man fī jabarūti al-amri wa-l-khalqi illā alladhīna khalaqtahum min nāri ḥubbika wa-hawāʾi shawqika wa-māʾi ʿināyatika wa-turābi faḍlika. Ulāʾika yuṣallīna ʿalayhim ahlu malaʾi al-aʿlā wa-sukkānu madāʾini al-baqāʾi. Fa-laka al-ḥamdu yā ilāhī bi-mā ʿaṣamta al-muwaḥḥidīna wa-ahlakta al-mushrikīna wa-faṣṣalta bayna al-kulli bi-kalimatin ukhrā allatī kharajat min fami mashīʾatika wa-ẓaharat min qalami irādatika. Wa-bi-dhālika iʿtaraḍa ʿalayya ʿibādun alladhīnahum khuliqū bi-kalimati amrika wa-buʿithū bi-irādatika wa-balaghū fī al-iʿrāḍi ilā maqāmin kafarū bika wa-bi-āyātika wa-ḥārabū bi-nafsika.
:::

::: {.translation}
When the promise came and the appointed time was fulfilled, I moved the hem of the veil by an immeasurably small degree. Then all who dwell in the dominion of command and creation were terrified, except those whom You had created from the fire of Your love, the air of longing for You, the water of Your care, and the dust of Your grace. Upon them the people of the Concourse on high and the inhabitants of the cities of eternity invoke blessings. Praise be to You, O my God, for protecting those who affirm Your oneness, destroying those who associate partners with You, and distinguishing everyone from one another through another word that issued from the mouth of Your purpose and appeared from the Pen of Your will. Because of this, servants who had been created by the word of Your command and raised up by Your will opposed me. Their rejection reached such a degree that they disbelieved in You and Your signs and waged war against Your own Self.
:::

### 772

::: {.original lang="fa"}
فو‌عزّتك يا محبوبی‌ لن يقدر القلم ان يذكر ما ورد منهم على مظهر امرك و مطلع وحيك و مشرق الهامك فلك الحمد فى كلّ ذلك و انّى فو‌عزّتك يا الهى قد كنت مشتاقاً لما قدّر فى سماء قضائك و ملكوت تقديرك لانّ ما يرد علىّ فى سبيلك هو محبوب ذاتى و مقصود نفسى و هذا لم يكن الّا بحولك و قوّتك انا الّذى يا الهى بحبّك استغنيت عن كلّ من فى السّموات و الأرض و به لن اجزع و لو يرد علىّ ضرّ العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā maḥbūbī lan yaq dira al-qalamu an yadhkura mā warada minhum ʿalā maẓhari amrika wa-maṭlaʿi waḥyika wa-mashriqi ilhāmika. Fa-laka al-ḥamdu fī kulli dhālika wa-innī fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā ilāhī qad kuntu mushtāqan li-mā quddira fī samāʾi qaḍāʾika wa-malakūti taqdīrika li-anna mā yaridu ʿalayya fī sabīlika huwa maḥbūbu dhātī wa-maqṣūdu nafsī wa-hādhā lam yakun illā bi-ḥawlika wa-quwwatika. Anā alladhī yā ilāhī bi-ḥubbika istaghnaytu ʿan kulli man fī al-samāwāti wa-l-arḍi wa-bihi lan ajzaʿa wa-law yaridu ʿalayya ḍurru al-ʿālamīna.
:::

::: {.translation}
By Your glory, O my Beloved! The Pen can never recount what has befallen the Manifestation of Your Cause, the Dawning Place of Your revelation, and the Dayspring of Your inspiration at their hands. Praise be to You in all of this! By Your glory, O my God, I have longed for what has been ordained in the heaven of Your decree and the kingdom of Your ordainment, for whatever befalls me in Your path is the beloved of my being and the desire of my soul. This has come about only through Your might and power. I am the one, O my God, who through Your love has become independent of all who are in the heavens and on earth. Through it I shall never be dismayed, even should the affliction of all the worlds befall me.
:::

### 773

::: {.original lang="ar"}
فيا ليت كان حينئذ حين الّذى فيه يسفك دمى على وجه الأرض بين يديك و تشهدنى على حالة الّتى بها شهدت المقرّبين من عبادك و المصطفين من خيرة خلقك فلك الحمد يا الهى على ما قضيت بسلطان قضائك و تقضى بتقديرك و امضائك اسئلك يا محبوبی‌ باسمك الّذى به رفعت اعلام امرك و اشرقت انوار وجهك بأن تنزل علىّ و على المخلصين من عبادك كلّ خير قدّرته فى الألواح ثمّ اجعل لنا مقعد صدق عندك يا من بيدك ملكوت كلّ شیء و انّك انت المقتدر العزيز الرّحمن
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Fa-yā layta kāna ḥīnaʾidhin ḥīna alladhī fīhi yusfaku damī ʿalā wajhi al-arḍi bayna yadayka wa-tashhadunī ʿalā ḥālatin allatī bihā shahidta al-muqarrabīna min ʿibādika wa-al-muṣṭafayna min khīrati khalqika fa-laka al-ḥamdu yā ilāhī ʿalā mā qaḍayta bi-sulṭāni qaḍāʾika wa-taqḍī bi-taqdīrika wa-imḍāʾika asʾaluka yā maḥbūbī bi-smika alladhī bihi rafaʿta aʿlāma amrika wa-ashraqat anwāru wajhika bi-an tunazzila ʿalayya wa-ʿalā al-mukhliṣīna min ʿibādika kulla khayrin qaddartahu fī al-alwāḥi thumma ijʿal lanā maqʿada ṣidqin ʿindaka yā man bi-yadika malakūtu kulli shayʾin wa-innaka anta al-Muqtadiru al-ʿAzīzu al-Raḥmān.
:::

::: {.translation}
If only this were the hour when my blood is shed upon the face of the earth before You, and You behold me in the condition in which You beheld those of Your servants who are near to You and the chosen ones among the best of Your creation. Praise be to You, O my God, for what You have decreed through the sovereignty of Your judgment and what You decree through Your ordainment and sanction. I ask You, O my Beloved, by Your name through which You have raised the banners of Your Cause and the lights of Your countenance have shone, to send down upon me and upon the sincere among Your servants every good thing You have ordained in the Tablets. Then appoint for us a seat of truth in Your presence, O You in whose hand is the dominion of all things. You are indeed the All-Powerful, the Almighty, the All-Merciful.
:::

### 774

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اميد چنان است كه از فضل سبحانى در اين ربيع روحانى كلّ بخلع انسانى فايز شوند و اثواب خلقهء عتيقهء رثيثه باليه را باثواب جديده الهيّه تبديل نمايند و كلّ بر امر حقّ بمنتهاى استطاعت و قدرت خود قائم شوند و اهل بهاء جناح يكديگر باشند از براى طيران كلّ در اين هواى روحانى و فضاى قدس نورانى و بغير ما قدّره اللّه تكلّم ننمايند و بغير رضاى او مشى نكنند و بر امرى تكلّم ننمايند مگر باذن اللّه و بادراك خود در معانى كلمات الهيّه اكتفا ننمايند چه كه غير اللّه بر معانى كلمات خود على ما هى عليها مطّلع نه چنانچه بعضى من غير اذن نسبت باغصان شجره الهيّه بعضى سخنها گفته‌اند كه عند‌اللّه مرضىّ نبوده چه كه اينگونه بيانات سبب فساد و اختلاف در امر است مخصوص در اين ایّام كه اكثرى از معرضين منتظرند كه فسادى در امر احداث شود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Umīd chunān ast kih az faḍl-i subḥānī dar īn rabīʿ-i rūḥānī kull bi-khilaʿ-i insānī fāʾiz shavand va athvāb-i khaliqih-yi ʿatīqih-yi rathīthih-yi bāliyih rā bi-athvāb-i jadīdih-yi ilāhiyyih tabdīl namāyand va kull bar amr-i Ḥaqq bi-muntahā-yi istiṭāʿat va qudrat-i khud qāʾim shavand va ahl-i Bahāʾ janāḥ-i yakdīgar bāshand az barā-yi ṭayarān-i kull dar īn havā-yi rūḥānī va faḍā-yi quds-i nūrānī va bi-ghayr-i mā qaddarahu Allāh takallum nanamāyand va bi-ghayr-i riḍā-yi ū mashy nakunand va bar amrī takallum nanamāyand magar bi-idhn-i Allāh va bi-idrāk-i khud dar maʿānī-yi kalimāt-i ilāhiyyih iktifā nanamāyand chih kih ghayr-i Allāh bar maʿānī-yi kalimāt-i khud ʿalā mā hiya ʿalayhā muṭṭaliʿ nah chunānchih baʿḍī min ghayr-i idhn nisbat bi-aghṣān-i shajariy-i ilāhiyyih baʿḍī sukhanhā guftih-and kih ʿinda Allāh marḍī nabūdih chih kih īngūnih bayānāt sabab-i fasād va ikhtilāf dar amr ast makhṣūṣ dar īn ayyām kih aktharī az muʿriḍīn muntaẓirand kih fasādī dar amr iḥdāth shavad.
:::

::: {.translation}
The hope is that, through divine grace, all may attain the robes of humanity in this spiritual springtime, exchange their old, worn, threadbare, and tattered garments for new, divine garments, and arise to uphold the Cause of the True One to the utmost of their ability and power. May the people of Bahāʾ be wings for one another, so that all may soar in this spiritual atmosphere and this luminous expanse of holiness. May they speak only what God has ordained, walk only in accordance with His good pleasure, and speak of no matter except with God's permission. They should not content themselves with their own understanding of the meanings of the divine words, for none but God knows the meanings of His own words as they truly are. Thus, some have, without permission, said certain things concerning the branches of the divine Tree that have not been pleasing to God, for such statements cause corruption and dissension in the Cause, especially in these days when most of those who turn away are waiting for some corruption to arise in the Cause.
:::

### 775

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اتّقوا اللّه يا قوم و لاتكوننّ من المتجاوزين ان اذكروا ما امرناكم به لا بما امركم انفسكم و اهوائكم اتّقوا اللّه و كونوا من المتّقين انا انطقناه حين الّذى قضت من عمره ستّة سنين متواليات ليكون دليلاً على هذا النّبأ الأعظم العظيم حقّ او را ناطق فرمود تا دليل باشد بر امرش نفوسى كه بچنين كلمات تكلّم نموده ‌از عظمت اين امر غافل شده‌اند لأنّه لو يريد ان ينطق كلّ شیء ليقدر و انّه لعلى كلّ شیء قدير قبل از الف ل ايظهر غير من ظهر كذلك نزل الأمر فى اوّل هذا الظّهور لو انتم من العارفين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ittaqū Allāha yā qawmu wa-lā takūnanna mina al-mutajāwizīn in udhkurū mā amarnākum bihi lā bi-mā amarakum anfusukum wa-ahwāʾukum ittaqū Allāha wa-kūnū mina al-muttaqīn innā anṭaqnāhu ḥīna alladhī qaḍat min ʿumrihi sittatu sinīna mutawāliyātin li-yakūna dalīlan ʿalā hādhā al-nabaʾi al-aʿẓami al-ʿaẓīm Ḥaqq ū rā nāṭiq farmūd tā dalīl bāshad bar amrash nufūsī kih bi-chunīn kalimāt takallum namūdih az ʿaẓamat-i īn amr ghāfil shudih-and li-annahu law yurīdu an yunṭiqa kulla shayʾin la-yaqdiru wa-innahu la-ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr qabl az alf \[corrupted text\] yaẓharu ghayru man ẓahara kadhālika nazala al-amru fī awwali hādhā al-ẓuhūri law antum mina al-ʿārifīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Fear God, O people, and do not be among those who transgress. Remember what We have commanded you, not what your own selves and desires have commanded you. Fear God and be among the God-fearing. We caused him to speak when six successive years of his life had passed, that he might be a proof of this most great and mighty Announcement. The True One caused him to speak so that he might be a proof of His Cause. Those who have spoken such words have become heedless of the greatness of this Cause, for if He wishes to cause all things to speak, He is able to do so, and He indeed has power over all things. Before a thousand, \[corrupted original text\] anyone other than the One who has appeared appears. Thus was the command sent down at the beginning of this Revelation, if you are among those who understand.
:::

### 776

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و قد بعث اللّه و سوف يبعث لهذا الأمر ادلّاء ينطقن عنه و يتوجّهنّ فى كلّ حين اليه و لايتحرّكنّ الّا بعد اذنه اولئك لا يبدلنّ نغمة من نغماتى بكلّ من فى السّموات و الأرضين اولئك ادلّائى فى الأرض و اصفيائى فى البلاد و امنائى بين العباد عليهم رحمتى و بهائى و ذكرى و ثنائى و هم عباد مكرمون
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-qad baʿatha Allāhu wa-sawfa yabʿathu li-hādhā al-amri adillāʾa yanṭiqna ʿanhu wa-yatawajjahnna fī kulli ḥīnin ilayhi wa-lā yataḥarrakna illā baʿda idhnihi ulāʾika lā yubaddilna naghmatan min naghamātī bi-kulli man fī al-samāwāti wa-al-araḍīn ulāʾika adillāʾī fī al-arḍi wa-aṣfiyāʾī fī al-bilādi wa-umanāʾī bayna al-ʿibādi ʿalayhim raḥmatī wa-bahāʾī wa-dhikrī wa-thanāʾī wa-hum ʿibādun mukramūn.
:::

::: {.translation}
God has raised up, and will raise up, guides for this Cause who speak on His behalf, turn toward Him at all times, and make no move without His permission. They will not exchange a single one of My melodies for all who are in the heavens and on earth. They are My guides on earth, My chosen ones in the lands, and My trusted ones among the servants. Upon them rest My mercy, My glory, My remembrance, and My praise. They are honored servants.
:::

### 777

::: {.original lang="fa"}
آنقدر معلوم بوده كه الى حين تفصيل اين ظهور ابدع ابهى ذكر نشده لو يذكر ليشهدنّ الكلّ بانّه لهو الّذى ما سبقه احد من قبل و لن يسبقه احد من الآخرین و من يدّعى قبل الألف انّه افترى على اللّه لانّ بذلك يفسد الأمر و لا يستقرّ هيكل المشيّة على عرش عزّ عظيم در اوّل اين ظهور منيع در اينمقام آياتى نازل و بعضى از آن در بعضى از الواح مذكور ان اشهدوها لتستقرّوا على الأمر و تكوننّ من الثّابتين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Ānqadr maʿlūm būdih kih ilā ḥīn tafṣīl-i īn ẓuhūr-i abdaʿ-i abhā dhikr nashudih law yudhkaru la-yashhadanna al-kullu bi-annahu la-huwa alladhī mā sabaqahu aḥadun min qablu wa-lan yasbiqahu aḥadun mina al-ākhirīn wa-man yaddaʿī qabla al-alfi innahu iftarā ʿalā Allāhi li-anna bi-dhālika yafsudu al-amru wa-lā yastaqirru haykalu al-mashīʾati ʿalā ʿarshi ʿizzin ʿaẓīm dar avval-i īn ẓuhūr-i manīʿ dar īn maqām āyātī nāzil va baʿḍī az ān dar baʿḍī az alvāḥ madhkūr in ishhadūhā li-tastaqirrū ʿalā al-amri wa-takūnanna mina al-thābitīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Let this much be known: until now, the details of this most wondrous, most glorious Revelation have not been set forth. Were they set forth, all would surely testify that He is the One whom no one before Him has surpassed and whom no one among those to come will surpass. Whoever makes a claim before the thousand has fabricated a lie against God, for this corrupts the Cause, and the Temple of the Will cannot be established upon a throne of mighty glory. At the beginning of this exalted Revelation, verses were revealed on this subject, and some of them are recorded in certain Tablets. Consider them, that you may stand firm in the Cause and be among the steadfast.
:::

### 778

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و ديگر معلوم بوده كه مقصود از وادى نبيل كه در الواح ذكر شده نفس اين ظهور اعظم بوده و خواهد بود و وادى آن ارض قدسى است كه فوق طبقات جنان خلق شده و لايقدر ان يرد عليها الّا اهل البهآء تاللّه انّهم اهل وادى النّبيل و وادى العظمة و وادى الاستقلال و وادى الجلال و وادى الاقتدار و وادى العزّة و وادى البقآء و وادى التّقديس و وادى التّنزيه و وادى الكبريا و غير اين نفوس از وادى نبيل خارج و در تيه نفس و هوى متحيّر و مبتلى و كينونة النّبيل حينئذ يتبرّء منهم و من اعمالهم و افعالهم و ما يظهر منهم و بذلك يشهد كلّ شیء ان انتم تعلمون
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va dīgar maʿlūm būdih kih maqṣūd az vādī-yi Nabīl kih dar alvāḥ dhikr shudih nafs-i īn ẓuhūr-i aʿẓam būdih va khvāhad būd va vādī ān arḍ-i qudsī ast kih fawq-i ṭabaqāt-i jinān khalq shudih va lā yaqdiru an yarida ʿalayhā illā ahlu al-Bahāʾ ta-Allāhi innahum ahlu wādī al-Nabīli wa-wādī al-ʿaẓamati wa-wādī al-istiqlāli wa-wādī al-jalāli wa-wādī al-iqtidāri wa-wādī al-ʿizzati wa-wādī al-baqāʾi wa-wādī al-taqdīsi wa-wādī al-tanzīhi wa-wādī al-kibriyā va ghayr-i īn nufūs az vādī-yi Nabīl khārij va dar tīh-i nafs va havā mutaḥayyir va mubtalā va kaynūnatu al-Nabīli ḥīnaʾidhin yatabarraʾu minhum wa-min aʿmālihim wa-afʿālihim wa-mā yaẓharu minhum wa-bi-dhālika yashhadu kullu shayʾin in antum taʿlamūn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Furthermore, let it be known that what is meant by the Valley of Nabīl mentioned in the Tablets has been, and will be, this Most Great Revelation itself. That valley is the holy land created above the levels of paradise, and none but the people of Bahāʾ can enter it. By God, they are the people of the Valley of Nabīl, the Valley of Grandeur, the Valley of Independence, the Valley of Majesty, the Valley of Power, the Valley of Might, the Valley of Eternity, the Valley of Sanctification, the Valley of Transcendence, and the Valley of Glory. All others are outside the Valley of Nabīl, bewildered and afflicted in the wilderness of self and desire. The very being of Nabīl then disavows them, their works, their deeds, and whatever proceeds from them. To this all things bear witness, if you know.
:::

### 779

::: {.original lang="fa"}
ایّاکم يا قوم ان تحرفوا كلمات اللّه عن مواضعها ان اشهدوا بما شهد اللّه ثمّ كونوا اخوانا على سرر متقابلين ان اتّحدوا على شأن لايجد احد بينكم روايح الاختلاف و باتّحادكم يظهر امر اللّه بين بريّته و تثبت آثاره بين عباده و تبرهن انواره بين العالمين اميد چنان است كه كلّ بكلمه جامعه مجتمع شده بذكر و ثناى حقّ مشغول شوند و بكمال انقطاع در ارض ظاهر گردند و بشأنى بنار حبّ الهى مشتعل شوند كه كلّ بحرارت آن مشتعل شده بشطر قدس ناظر گردند
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Iyyākum yā qawmu an tuḥarrifū kalimāti Allāhi ʿan mawāḍiʿihā in ishhadū bi-mā shahida Allāhu thumma kūnū ikhwānan ʿalā sururin mutaqābilīn in ittaḥidū ʿalā shaʾnin lā yajidu aḥadun baynakum rawāʾiḥa al-ikhtilāfi wa-bi-ittiḥādikum yaẓharu amru Allāhi bayna bariyyatihi wa-tathbutu āthāruhu bayna ʿibādihi wa-tubarhanu anwāruhu bayna al-ʿālamīn umīd chunān ast kih kull bi-kalimiy-i jāmiʿih mujtamiʿ shudih bi-dhikr va thanā-yi Ḥaqq mashghūl shavand va bi-kamāl-i inqiṭāʿ dar arḍ ẓāhir gardand va bi-shaʾnī bi-nār-i ḥubb-i ilāhī mushtaʿil shavand kih kull bi-ḥarārat-i ān mushtaʿil shudih bi-shaṭr-i quds nāẓir gardand.
:::

::: {.translation}
Beware, O people, lest you distort the words of God from their proper places. Bear witness to what God has witnessed, and be brothers seated upon couches facing one another. Unite in such a way that no one can detect among you the scents of discord. Through your unity, the Cause of God will become manifest among His creatures, its traces will be established among His servants, and its lights will be demonstrated among the peoples of the world. The hope is that all may gather around the all-embracing Word, occupy themselves with the remembrance and praise of the True One, and appear on earth in perfect detachment. May they be so ablaze with the fire of divine love that all may be kindled by its heat and turn their gaze toward the realm of holiness.
:::

### 780

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و آنچه از آيات الهى ادراك نشود از معدن و مبدء آن سؤال نمايند مقصود از اينكلمه آنكه مباد در معنى كلمات مابين احبّاى الهى اختلاف شود و بدانند كه كلمات الهيّه كلّ از نقطه واحده ظاهر و باو راجع ایّاکم ان تشهدوا الاختلاف فيهنّ اگرچه بظاهر مختلف نازل شود در باطن بكلمه واحده و نقطه واحده راجع و منتهى چنانچه در بعضى مقام ذكر شده كه احدى بمعنى كلمات الهى مطّلع نه الّا اللّه شكّى نيست كه اين قول حقّ است چه كه حرفى از حروفات منزله در هر عالمى از عوالم لايتناهى اثر مخصوصى و معانى مخصوصه باقتضاى آن عالم داشته و خواهد داشت و هم‌نين حروفات و كلمات الهيّة هر يك كنز علم لدنّى بوده وخواهد بود و ما اطّلع بما كنز فيهنّ الّا اللّه احدى قادر بر عرفان آن على ما ينبغى لها نبوده و نخواهد بود
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va ānchih az āyāt-i ilāhī idrāk nashavad az maʿdan va mabdaʾ-i ān suʾāl namāyand maqṣūd az īn kalimih ānkih mabād dar maʿnī-yi kalimāt mābayn-i aḥibbā-yi ilāhī ikhtilāf shavad va bidānand kih kalimāt-i ilāhiyyih kull az nuqṭiy-i vāḥidih ẓāhir va bi-ū rājiʿ iyyākum an tashhadū al-ikhtilāfa fīhinna agarchih bi-ẓāhir mukhtalif nāzil shavad dar bāṭin bi-kalimiy-i vāḥidih va nuqṭiy-i vāḥidih rājiʿ va muntahī chunānchih dar baʿḍī maqām dhikr shudih kih aḥadī bi-maʿnī-yi kalimāt-i ilāhī muṭṭaliʿ nah illā Allāh shakkī nīst kih īn qawl ḥaqq ast chih kih ḥarfī az ḥurūfāt-i munazzalih dar har ʿālamī az ʿavālim-i lā-yatanāhī athar-i makhṣūṣī va maʿānī-yi makhṣūṣih bi-iqtiḍā-yi ān ʿālam dāshtih va khvāhad dāsht va \[corrupted text\] ḥurūfāt va kalimāt-i ilāhiyyih har yak kanz-i ʿilm-i ladunnī būdih va khvāhad būd wa-mā iṭṭalaʿa bi-mā kuniza fīhinna illā Allāh aḥadī qādir bar ʿirfān-i ān ʿalā mā yanbaghī lahā nabūdih va nakhvāhad būd.
:::

::: {.translation}
Whatever they do not understand of the divine verses, they should ask about from their mine and source. The purpose of this statement is that no disagreement over the meaning of the words should arise among the loved ones of God, and that they should know that the divine words all proceed from a single point and return to it. Beware lest you perceive discord among them. Although outwardly they may be revealed in differing forms, inwardly they return and lead to a single word and a single point. Thus, in certain passages it has been stated that no one knows the meaning of the divine words except God. There is no doubt that this statement is true, for a single letter among the revealed letters has had, and will have, a particular effect and particular meanings in each of the infinite worlds, according to the requirements of that world. And \[corrupted original text\] the divine letters and words have each been, and will be, a treasury of knowledge bestowed by God. None but God has known what is treasured within them. No one has been, or will be, capable of knowing them as they deserve to be known.
:::

### 781

::: {.original lang="fa"}
و هم‌چنين در مقامى ذكر شده كه كلّ آيات الهى را درك مينمايند چه كه اگر صاحب اينمقام نبودند حجّيت آيات مبرهن نميشد اين دو بيان مختلفند بر حسب ظاهر و لكن نزد متبصّرين و صاحبان ابصر حديده معلومست كه مقصود از آنكه فرموده كلّ ادراك مينمايند على قدرهم و مقدارهم بوده لا على قدر و مقدار ما نزل من لدى اللّه المقتدر المهيمن القيّوم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Va hamchunīn dar maqāmī dhikr shudih kih kull āyāt-i ilāhī rā dark mīnamāyand chih kih agar ṣāḥib-i īn maqām nabūdand ḥujjiyyat-i āyāt mubarhan namīshud īn du bayān mukhtalifand bar ḥasab-i ẓāhir va lākin nazd-i mutabaṣṣirīn va ṣāḥibān-i abṣār-i ḥadīdih maʿlūm ast kih maqṣūd az ānkih farmūdih kull idrāk mīnamāyand ʿalā qadrihim wa-miqdārihim būdih lā ʿalā qadri wa-miqdāri mā nazala min ladā Allāhi al-Muqtadiri al-Muhaymini al-Qayyūm.
:::

::: {.translation}
Likewise, in another passage it has been stated that all understand the divine verses, for if they did not possess this capacity, the authority of the verses as proof could not be demonstrated. These two statements differ outwardly, but to those endowed with insight and keen vision it is clear that the statement that all understand means according to their own capacity and measure, not according to the capacity and measure of what has been sent down from God, the All-Powerful, the All-Protecting, the Self-Subsisting.
:::

### 782

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اليوم نفوسيكه در هتك حرمت بيان ساعيند چنانچه ديده و شنيده‌ايد آن نفوس نظر بحماقت مريدين خود ادّعاى امر نموده‌اند لعن اللّه على الّذين تجاوزوا عن حدود البيان و هتكوا حرمة اللّه و نقضوا ميثاقه و كفروا بنقطة الأولى و محبوبه و مقصوده الّذى ظهر باسمه الأبهی بين الأرض و السّمآء و منه استضآء افئدة المقرّبين و صدور المخلصين و لكن قد اخطاؤا ما توهّموا بحول اللّه و قوّته حصن امر بيد قدرت حفظ خواهد شد و انّه لعلى كلّ شیء قدير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Al-yawm nufūsī kih dar hatk-i ḥurmat-i Bayān sāʿīand chunānchih dīdih va shinīdih-īd ān nufūs naẓar bi-ḥamāqat-i murīdīn-i khud iddiʿā-yi amr namūdih-and laʿnu Allāhi ʿalā alladhīna tajāwazū ʿan ḥudūdi al-Bayāni wa-hatakū ḥurmata Allāhi wa-naqaḍū mīthāqahu wa-kafarū bi-Nuqṭati al-Ūlā wa-maḥbūbihi wa-maqṣūdihi alladhī ẓahara bi-smihi al-Abhā bayna al-arḍi wa-al-samāʾi wa-minhu istaḍāʾa afʾidatu al-muqarrabīna wa-ṣudūru al-mukhliṣīn va lākin qad akhṭaʾū mā tavahhamū bi-ḥawl-i Allāh va quvvat-i ū ḥiṣn-i amr bi-yad-i qudrat ḥifẓ khvāhad shud wa-innahu la-ʿalā kulli shayʾin qadīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
Today, those who strive to violate the sanctity of the Bayān, as you have seen and heard, have put forward claims to a Cause in view of the foolishness of their followers. God's curse be upon those who have transgressed the bounds of the Bayān, violated the sanctity of God, broken His covenant, and disbelieved in the Primal Point and in His Beloved and His Desired One, who has appeared in His name, the All-Glorious, between earth and heaven, and from whom the hearts of those brought near and the breasts of the sincere have received light. But they have been mistaken in what they imagined. Through God's power and His might, the fortress of the Cause will be guarded by the hand of power. He indeed has power over all things.
:::

### 783

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و فى آخر القول غرّدت ورقآء الأمر على افنان سدرة عزّ رفيع و يقول يا ملأ البيان اتّقوا اللّه و لاتفسدوا فى الأرض بعد اصلاحها و لاترتكبوا الفحشآء طهّروا انفسكم عن كلّ ما حرّم فى كتاب اللّه العلىّ العظيم ایّاکم ان تسفكوا الدّمآء و الّذى سفك انّه ليس منّى و كان اللّه برئ منه و هذا ما نزل فى اوّل هذا الظّهور من ملكوت ربّكم الرّحمن الرّحيم
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-fī ākhiri al-qawli gharradat warqāʾu al-amri ʿalā afnāni sidrati ʿizzin rafīʿin wa-yaqūlu yā malaʾa al-Bayāni ittaqū Allāha wa-lā tufsidū fī al-arḍi baʿda iṣlāḥihā wa-lā tartakibū al-faḥshāʾa ṭahhirū anfusakum ʿan kulli mā ḥurrima fī kitābi Allāhi al-ʿAliyyi al-ʿAẓīm iyyākum an tasfikū al-dimāʾa wa-alladhī safaka innahu laysa minnī wa-kāna Allāhu barīʾan minhu wa-hādhā mā nazala fī awwali hādhā al-ẓuhūri min malakūti rabbikumu al-Raḥmāni al-Raḥīm.
:::

::: {.translation}
At the close of this discourse, the Dove of the Cause sang upon the branches of the Tree of lofty glory, saying: “O people of the Bayān, fear God, and do not spread corruption on earth after it has been set right, nor commit indecency. Purify yourselves of everything forbidden in the Book of God, the Most High, the Most Great. Beware lest you shed blood. Whoever has shed blood is not of Me, and God disavows him.” This is what was sent down at the beginning of this Revelation from the kingdom of your Lord, the All-Merciful, the Compassionate.
:::

### 784

::: {.original lang="ar"}
ایّاکم ان ترتكبوا ما يكرهه عقولكم و افئدتكم اتّقوا اللّه يا ملأ المؤمنين ان انقطعوا عن الدّنيا و ما فيها و لاتصرّفوا فى اموال النّاس الّا بعد اذنهم كذلك نزلنا من قبل و حينئذ من لدن عزيز جميل كونوا امنآء اللّه فى البلاد بحيث لو تمرّنّ على مداين الذّهب لن ترتدّ ابصاركم اليها كذلك ينبغى لكم يا ملأ الموحّدين ان انصروا ربّكم الرّحمن باعمالكم ليجدنّ منكم روايح الحقّ عباد اللّه بين السّموات و الأرضين تخلّقوا يا قوم باخلاق اللّه و لاترتكبوا ما تضيع به حرمة مظهر نفسه بين خلقه كذلك وصّاكم اللّه فى الواح عزّ حفيظ لا تتعرّضوا باحد و لا تجادلوا بنفس ان وجدتم من مقبل ذكّروه بكلمة الأعظم و ان وجدتم من معرض فاعرضوا عنه ثمّ اقبلوا الى اللّه ربّكم و انّه يكفيكم عن العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Iyyākum an tartakibū mā yakrahuhu ʿuqūlukum wa-afʾidatukum ittaqū Allāha yā malaʾa al-muʾminīn in inqaṭiʿū ʿani al-dunyā wa-mā fīhā wa-lā taṣarrafū fī amwāli al-nāsi illā baʿda idhnihim kadhālika nazzalnā min qablu wa-ḥīnaʾidhin min ladun ʿazīzin jamīl kūnū umanāʾa Allāhi fī al-bilādi bi-ḥaythu law tamurrunna ʿalā madāʾini al-dhahabi lan tartadda abṣārukum ilayhā kadhālika yanbaghī lakum yā malaʾa al-muwaḥḥidīn in unṣurū rabbakumu al-Raḥmāna bi-aʿmālikum li-yajidanna minkum rawāʾiḥa al-Ḥaqqi ʿibādu Allāhi bayna al-samāwāti wa-al-araḍīn takhallaqū yā qawmu bi-akhlāqi Allāhi wa-lā tartakibū mā taḍīʿu bihi ḥurmatu maẓhari nafsihi bayna khalqihi kadhālika waṣṣākumu Allāhu fī alwāḥi ʿizzin ḥafīẓ lā tataʿarraḍū bi-aḥadin wa-lā tujādilū bi-nafsin in wajadtum min muqbilin dhakkirūhu bi-kalimati al-aʿẓami wa-in wajadtum min muʿriḍin fa-aʿriḍū ʿanhu thumma aqbilū ilā Allāhi rabbikum wa-innahu yakfīkum ʿani al-ʿālamīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Beware lest you commit what your minds and hearts abhor. Fear God, O company of believers. Detach yourselves from the world and all that is in it, and do not dispose of people's property without their permission. Thus have We sent down before and now, from One who is Mighty and Beautiful. Be God's trusted ones in the lands, such that, were you to pass through cities of gold, your eyes would not turn toward them. Such should be your conduct, O company of those who affirm His oneness. Aid your Lord, the All-Merciful, through your deeds, so that God's servants throughout the heavens and the earth may sense from you the fragrances of the True One. Adorn yourselves, O people, with the attributes of God, and do not commit what would diminish the honor of the Manifestation of His own Self among His creatures. Thus has God counseled you in Tablets of preserving might. Do not assail anyone or dispute with any soul. If you find someone receptive, remind him through the word of the Most Great; and if you find someone who turns away, turn away from him, then turn toward God, your Lord. He will indeed suffice you against all the peoples of the world.
:::

### 785

::: {.original lang="fa"}
ان اتّحدوا يا احبّائى ثمّ اجتمعوا على شريعة امرى و لا تكوننّ من المختلفين و انّ اقربكم الى اللّه اخشاكم و اخشعكم لو انتم من العارفين تاللّه الحقّ لو انتم تظلمون احبّ عندى من ان تظلموا على احد و هذا من سجيّتى و احسن خصالى لو انتم من الموقنين ان اصبروا يا احبّائى فى البأسآء و الضّرّآء و ان يظلمكم من ظالم فارجعوا حكمه الى اللّه الّذى بيده ملكوت كلّ شیء و انّه لهو المقتدر على ما یشآء و انّه هو اشدّ المنتقمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
In ittaḥidū yā aḥibbāʾī thumma ijtamiʿū ʿalā sharīʿati amrī wa-lā takūnanna mina al-mukhtalifīn wa-inna aqrabakum ilā Allāhi akhshākum wa-akhshaʿukum law antum mina al-ʿārifīn ta-Allāhi al-Ḥaqqi law antum tuẓlamūna aḥabbu ʿindī min an taẓlimū ʿalā aḥadin wa-hādhā min sajiyyatī wa-aḥsani khiṣālī law antum mina al-mūqinīn in iṣbirū yā aḥibbāʾī fī al-baʾsāʾi wa-al-ḍarrāʾi wa-in yaẓlimkum min ẓālimin fa-arjiʿū ḥukmahu ilā Allāhi alladhī bi-yadihi malakūtu kulli shayʾin wa-innahu la-huwa al-Muqtadiru ʿalā mā yashāʾu wa-innahu huwa ashaddu al-muntaqimīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Unite, O My loved ones, and gather around the law of My Cause. Do not be among those who disagree. The nearest of you to God are those who most fear Him and are most humble before Him, if you are among those who understand. By God, the True One, that you should suffer injustice is dearer to Me than that you should wrong anyone. This is of My nature and among My finest attributes, if you are among those who are certain. Be patient, O My loved ones, in hardship and adversity. If an oppressor wrongs you, leave judgment upon him to God, in whose hand is the dominion of all things. He indeed has power to do whatever He wills, and He is the most severe of avengers.
:::

### 786

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و انّا وصّيناكم فى اكثر الألواح بأن لا تتعرّضوا بأحد و انتم فعلتم ما رجع ضرّه الى سدرة عزّ رفيع يا قوم اتّقوا اللّه و لاتجاوزوا عمّا امرتم به فى الألواح و انّ هذا خير لكم عمّا عندكم لو انتم من العارفين ان اجتنبوا من الّذينهم كفروا و اشركوا باللّه و جادلوا بآياته و حاربوا بنفسه العلىّ العظيم ثمّ اصبروا كما صبرنا و لاتحاربوا مع احد من المشركين توكّلوا فى كلّ الأمور على اللّه و انّه ينصرنى كما نصرنى اوّل مرّة اذ كنت فى السّجن تحت السّلاسل و الأغلال و نصرنى بالحقّ بجنود السّموات و الأرضين الى ان اخرجنى عنه بسلطان مبين فى قبضته ملكوت كلّ شیء ينصر من یشآء كيف یشآء و انّه لهو المقتدر القدير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-innā waṣṣaynākum fī akthar al-alwāḥ bi-an lā tataʿarraḍū bi-aḥad wa-antum faʿaltum mā rajaʿa ḍarruhu ilā sidrat ʿizz rafīʿ. Yā qawm ittaqū Allāh wa-lā tatajāwazū ʿammā umirtum bihi fī al-alwāḥ wa-inna hādhā khayr lakum ʿammā ʿindakum law antum min al-ʿārifīn. An ijtanibū min alladhīnahum kafarū wa-ashrakū bi-Allāh wa-jādalū bi-āyātihi wa-ḥārabū bi-nafsihi al-ʿAlī al-ʿAẓīm. Thumma iṣbirū kamā ṣabarnā wa-lā tuḥāribū maʿa aḥad min al-mushrikīn. Tawakkalū fī kull al-umūr ʿalā Allāh wa-innahu yanṣurunī kamā naṣaranī awwal marra idh kuntu fī al-sijn taḥta al-salāsil wa-al-aghlāl wa-naṣaranī bi-al-ḥaqq bi-junūd al-samāwāt wa-al-arḍīn ilā an akhrajanī ʿanhu bi-sulṭān mubīn. Fī qabḍatihi malakūt kull shayʾ yanṣur man yashāʾ kayfa yashāʾ wa-innahu la-huwa al-Muqtadir al-Qadīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
We have counseled you in most of the Tablets not to assail anyone, yet you have done what has brought harm upon the Tree of lofty glory. O people, fear God and do not transgress what you have been commanded in the Tablets. This is indeed better for you than what you possess, if you are among those who understand. Avoid those who have disbelieved, associated partners with God, disputed His verses, and made war against His own exalted and mighty Self. Then be patient as We have been patient, and do not wage war against any of those who associate partners with God. Put your trust in God in all matters. He will indeed aid Me as He aided Me the first time, when I was in prison under chains and fetters. He aided Me in truth with the hosts of the heavens and the earth until He brought Me out of it with manifest authority. In His grasp is the dominion of all things. He aids whomever He wills, however He wills. He is indeed the All-Powerful, the Omnipotent.
:::

### 787

::: {.original lang="ar"}
ایّاکم يا قوم ان تتمسّكوا بالأسمآء و تعترضوا على الّذى خلقها بامر من عنده لا اله الّا هو المقتدر العالم الحكيم قل انّه خلق الأسماء كما خلق كلّ شیء ان انتم من العالمين كلّ ذى قدرة عاجز عند سلطان قدرته و كلّ ذى علم جاهل لدى علمه و كلّ ذى غنآء فقير لدى بابه الّذى فتح على وجه الخلايق اجمعين ایّاکم ان يصدّنكم الأسماء عن موجدها تجنّبوا عن الّذين تمسّكوا بها و كانوا عليها لمن العاكفين قل انّ النّبی‌ من سمع نبأى و آمن بنفسى و الرّسول من بلّغ رسالاتى و الأمام من قام امام وجهى وفاز بأیّامى و الولىّ من دخل حصن ولايتى و انقطع عن سوائى و الوصىّ من وصّى نفسه ثمّ العباد بحبّی‌ و ذكرى و ثنائى كذلك اشرقت شمس البيان عن افق مشيّة ربّكم الرّحمن فى هذا الرّضوان المقدّس الممتنع المتعالى المنيع و الحمد للّه محبوبی‌ و محبوب العارفين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Iyyākum yā qawm an tatamassakū bi-al-asmāʾ wa-taʿtariḍū ʿalā alladhī khalaqahā bi-amr min ʿindihi lā ilāha illā huwa al-Muqtadir al-ʿĀlim al-Ḥakīm. Qul innahu khalaqa al-asmāʾ kamā khalaqa kull shayʾ in antum min al-ʿālimīn. Kull dhī qudra ʿājiz ʿinda sulṭān qudratihi wa-kull dhī ʿilm jāhil ladā ʿilmihi wa-kull dhī ghināʾ faqīr ladā bābihi alladhī fataḥa ʿalā wajh al-khalāʾiq ajmaʿīn. Iyyākum an yaṣuddannakum al-asmāʾ ʿan mūjidihā tajannabū ʿan alladhīna tamassakū bihā wa-kānū ʿalayhā la-min al-ʿākifīn. Qul inna al-nabī man samiʿa nabaʾī wa-āmana bi-nafsī wa-al-rasūl man ballagha risālātī wa-al-imām man qāma amāma wajhī wa-fāza bi-ayyāmī wa-al-walī man dakhala ḥiṣn wilāyatī wa-inqaṭaʿa ʿan siwāʾī wa-al-waṣī man waṣṣā nafsahu thumma al-ʿibād bi-ḥubbī wa-dhikrī wa-thanāʾī. Kadhālika ashraqat shams al-bayān ʿan ufuq mashīʾat rabbikum al-Raḥmān fī hādhā al-Riḍwān al-muqaddas al-mumtaniʿ al-mutaʿālī al-manīʿ wa-al-ḥamd li-llāh maḥbūbī wa-maḥbūb al-ʿārifīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
Beware, O people, lest you cling to names and object to the One who created them by a command from Himself. There is no God but Him, the All-Powerful, the All-Knowing, the All-Wise. Say: He created the names just as He created all things, if you are among those who know. Everyone endowed with power is helpless before the sovereignty of His power; everyone endowed with knowledge is ignorant before His knowledge; and everyone endowed with wealth is poor at His door, which He has opened to all created beings. Beware lest the names keep you from their Creator. Shun those who have clung to them and remained devoted to them. Say: The prophet is the one who has heard My tidings and believed in My own Self; the messenger is the one who has conveyed My messages; the imam is the one who has stood before My face and attained My days; the guardian is the one who has entered the stronghold of My guardianship and detached himself from all but Me; and the appointed successor is the one who has enjoined upon himself, and then upon the servants, love for Me, remembrance of Me, and praise of Me. Thus has the sun of utterance shone from the horizon of the will of your Lord, the All-Merciful, in this sanctified, inaccessible, exalted, and impregnable Paradise. Praise be to God, My Beloved and the Beloved of those who know Him.
:::

### 788

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و اذا نخاطب الّذى افترى على اللّه و اعترض عليه و ارسل الى مقرّ القدس اوراق النّاريّة و ذكر فيها ما احترقت عنها اكباد الأصفیا‌ء و المقرّبين لعلّ يستيقظ عن نوم الغفلة و يتوجّه الى شطر القدس مقرّ اللّه المقتدر العزيز العليم و لو انّه اتى بذنب اثقل عن ثقل السّموات و الأرضين و لكن لمّا تموّجت ابحر الفضل فى تلك الأیّام لو يتوب و يرجع لعلّ ان يغفره اللّه برحمته الّتى سبقت العالمين
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-idhā nukhāṭib alladhī iftarā ʿalā Allāh wa-iʿtaraḍa ʿalayhi wa-arsala ilā maqarr al-quds awrāq al-nāriyya wa-dhakara fīhā mā iḥtaraqat ʿanhā akbād al-aṣfiyāʾ wa-al-muqarrabīn laʿalla yastayqiẓ ʿan nawm al-ghafla wa-yatawajjaha ilā shaṭr al-quds maqarr Allāh al-Muqtadir al-ʿAzīz al-ʿAlīm. Wa-law innahu atā bi-dhanb athqal ʿan thiqal al-samāwāt wa-al-arḍīn wa-lākin lammā tamawwajat abḥur al-faḍl fī tilka al-ayyām law yatūb wa-yarjaʿ laʿalla an yaghfirahu Allāh bi-raḥmatihi allatī sabaqat al-ʿālamīn.
:::

::: {.translation}
And now We address the one who has fabricated lies against God, objected to Him, and sent fiery pages to the seat of holiness, setting down in them what has burned the hearts of the chosen ones and those brought near, so that he may awaken from the sleep of heedlessness and turn toward the holy region, the seat of God, the All-Powerful, the Almighty, the All-Knowing. Although he has committed a sin heavier than the weight of the heavens and the earth, yet, since the oceans of grace have surged in these days, if he repents and returns, perhaps God will forgive him through His mercy, which has preceded all the worlds.
:::

### 789

::: {.original lang="ar"}
قل ان يا ايّها الغافل لو تسمع من هذا العبد فاعمل بما نذكرك به لتكون من الفائزين طهّر نفسك عن غير اللّه ثمّ قل بسم اللّه و باللّه و غسل بالمآء و بعد فراغك قل يا الهى و محبوبی‌ كما طهّرت ظاهرى من هذا المآء طهّر قلبی‌ و فؤادى عن النّفس و الهوى لاعرفك بنفسك و انقطع عن العالمين ثمّ ضع وجهك على التّراب خضّعاً للّه ربّ الأرباب‌ قل يا الهى و سيّدى اسئلك باسمك الّذى به ظهر الزّلزال فى قبائل الأرض و السّمآء و ارتفع الضّجيج بين ملأ الانشآء و اضطربت انفس المريبين و حقايق الغافلين بأن تغفرلى جريراتى الّتى ما شهدت عين الابداع شبهها فو‌عزّتك يا محبوبی‌ قد جئتك بذنب لا يعادله ذنوب من خلق بقولك الابدع البديع
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Qul in yā ayyuhā al-ghāfil law tasmaʿ min hādhā al-ʿabd fa-iʿmal bi-mā nadhkuruka bihi li-takūna min al-fāʾizīn. Ṭahhir nafsaka ʿan ghayr Allāh thumma qul bi-sm Allāh wa-bi-Allāh wa-ghassil bi-al-māʾ wa-baʿda farāghika qul yā ilāhī wa-maḥbūbī kamā ṭahharta ẓāhirī min hādhā al-māʾ ṭahhir qalbī wa-fuʾādī ʿan al-nafs wa-al-hawā li-aʿrifaka bi-nafsika wa-anqaṭiʿa ʿan al-ʿālamīn. Thumma ḍaʿ wajhaka ʿalā al-turāb khuḍḍaʿan li-llāh rabb al-arbāb qul yā ilāhī wa-sayyidī asʾaluka bi-ismika alladhī bihi ẓahara al-zilzāl fī qabāʾil al-arḍ wa-al-samāʾ wa-irtafaʿa al-ḍajīj bayna malaʾ al-inshāʾ wa-iḍṭarabat anfus al-murībīn wa-ḥaqāʾiq al-ghāfilīn bi-an taghfira lī jarīrātī allatī mā shahidat ʿayn al-ibdāʿ shibhahā. Fa-wa-ʿizzatika yā maḥbūbī qad jiʾtuka bi-dhanb lā yuʿādiluhu dhunūb man khuliqa bi-qawlika al-abdaʿ al-badīʿ.
:::

::: {.translation}
Say: O heedless one, if you will listen to this servant, act upon what We tell you, so that you may be among those who attain their goal. Purify yourself of all but God, then say, “In the name of God and by God,” and wash with water. When you have finished, say, “O my God and my Beloved, just as You have cleansed my outward being with this water, cleanse my heart and my inmost being of self and desire, so that I may know You through Your own Self and detach myself from all the worlds.” Then place your face upon the dust in humility before God, the Lord of lords, and say, “O my God and my Master, I ask You by Your name, through which the earthquake has appeared among the tribes of earth and heaven, the clamor has risen among the company of creation, and the souls of the doubters and the realities of the heedless have been shaken, to forgive my transgressions, the like of which the eye of creation has never witnessed. By Your might, O my Beloved, I have come to You with a sin that cannot be equaled by the sins of those created through Your most wondrous, incomparable word.
:::

### 790

::: {.original lang="fa"}
اذا فارحم على هذا العاصى ثمّ البسنى ثوب الغفران و طهّرنى من تعيّنات البشر و وجّهنى الى منظرك الأكبر بحيث لايبقى فى صدرى الّا بدايع عرفانك و لا فى قلبی‌ الّا ظهورات حبّك و لا من وجهى الّا نضرة رضوانك و انّك انت المقتدر على ما تشآء و انّك انت المهيمن المقتدر العزيز القدير يا الهى هذا عاصى قد سرع الى مدين غفرانك و هذا المسكين قد تمسّك باذيال ردآء غنائك و استغنائك اى ربّ لاتحرمنى عمّا عندك ثمّ اجعلنى خالصاً لوجهك و خاضعاً عند ظهورات انوار عزّ فردانيّتك و انّك لم تزل كنت ذوالفضل القديم و تكون على كلّ شیء قدير
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Idhan fa-irḥam ʿalā hādhā al-ʿāṣī thumma albisnī thawb al-ghufrān wa-ṭahhirnī min taʿayyunāt al-bashar wa-wajjihnī ilā manẓarika al-akbar bi-ḥaythu lā yabqā fī ṣadrī illā badāʾiʿ ʿirfānika wa-lā fī qalbī illā ẓuhūrāt ḥubbika wa-lā min wajhī illā naḍrat riḍwānika wa-innaka anta al-Muqtadir ʿalā mā tashāʾ wa-innaka anta al-Muhaymin al-Muqtadir al-ʿAzīz al-Qadīr. Yā ilāhī hādhā ʿāṣī qad saraʿa ilā madīn ghufrānika wa-hādhā al-miskīn qad tamassaka bi-adhyāl ridāʾ ghināʾika wa-istighnāʾika. Ay rabb lā taḥrimnī ʿammā ʿindaka thumma ijʿalnī khāliṣan li-wajhika wa-khāḍiʿan ʿinda ẓuhūrāt anwār ʿizz fardāniyyatika wa-innaka lam tazal kunta dhū al-faḍl al-qadīm wa-takūn ʿalā kull shayʾ qadīr.
:::

::: {.translation}
Then have mercy on this sinner, clothe me in the robe of forgiveness, purify me of human limitations, and turn me toward Your Most Great Countenance, so that nothing may remain in my breast but the wonders of the knowledge of You, nor in my heart but the manifestations of Your love, nor shine from my face but the radiance of Your good pleasure. You are indeed powerful to do whatever You will, and You are the All-Protecting, the All-Powerful, the Almighty, the Omnipotent. O my God, this is a sinner who has hastened to the city of Your forgiveness, and this poor one has clung to the hem of the robe of Your wealth and self-sufficiency. O Lord, do not deprive me of what is with You. Then make me wholly devoted to You and humble before the manifestations of the lights of the glory of Your singleness. You have ever been the Possessor of ancient grace, and You are powerful over all things.”
:::

### 791

::: {.original lang="ar"}
و نسئل اللّه بذلك يفتح بصراك و يعرّفك ما لا عرفته من قبل و يعلّمك ما تجعل به غنيّا عن دونه و عنده علم السّموات و الأرض و انّه قد كان على كلّ شیء محيط
:::

::: {.transliteration}
Wa-nasʾal Allāh bi-dhālika yaftaḥ baṣarāka wa-yuʿarrifaka mā lā ʿaraftahu min qabl wa-yuʿallimaka mā tujʿal bihi ghaniyyan ʿan dūnihi wa-ʿindahu ʿilm al-samāwāt wa-al-arḍ wa-innahu qad kāna ʿalā kull shayʾ muḥīṭ.
:::

::: {.translation}
And We ask God, through this, to open your eyes, make known to you what you did not know before, and teach you that through which you may be made independent of all but Him. With Him is the knowledge of the heavens and the earth, and He indeed encompasses all things.
:::

